      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "10": {"synopsis":"The extension ROM's entry points after the \"EXOS_ROM\" header: $C00A is the action entry\nEXOS calls with C = the action code, $C00D and $C010 are entries for other code (the\nfunction dispatcher is $C010).","comment":"Action entry: C = the action code"},
        "13": {"comment":"Second entry: goes to $1C9F"},
        "16": {"comment":"EXDOS function call: A = the function number"},
        "19": {"synopsis":"Action entry (EXOS calls it with C = the action code, B, DE its parameters, IY = the RAM\nEXOS gave this ROM, page 1 = that RAM's segment).\n1. Adds $80 to IY, so IY-$80..IY+$7F reach the first 256 bytes of the workspace.\n2. Action 7 (RAM allocation) asks for the workspace (ACT7_RAM). Nothing else is done while\n   page 1 holds segment 0 (no RAM yet), and only action 8 (initialise, INIT_ACTION) runs\n   before bit 7 of IY-$37 marks the initialisation done.\n3. Action 1 (cold start) goes to ACT1_COLD, 2 (command string) to $2BF1, 3 (help string)\n   to $2B5E, 4 (EXOS variable) to ACT4_VAR.\n4. Action 5 (explain error code, B = the code) takes codes $95-$BF (messages 0-$2A) and\n   $CF (message $2B), unless EXDOS variable $50 (IY-$4E) is not 0; the message is built\n   by MSG_TO_BUFFER and handed back with C = 0, B = $FF, DE = its address.\nAny other action returns with C unchanged, so EXOS offers it to the next extension."},
        "20": {"comment":"IY + $80: the middle of the workspace's first 256 bytes"},
        "23": {"comment":"IY = workspace + $80"},
        "26": {"comment":"A = the action code"},
        "27": {"comment":"Action 7 (RAM allocation)?"},
        "31": {"comment":"A = page 1's segment, the RAM EXOS gave this ROM"},
        "34": {"comment":"No RAM yet? Leave the action"},
        "36": {"comment":"Action 8 (initialise)?"},
        "41": {"comment":"Initialised (bit 7 of IY-$37)? Else leave the action"},
        "46": {"comment":"Action 1 (cold start)?"},
        "50": {"comment":"Action 2 (command string)?"},
        "54": {"comment":"Action 3 (help string)?"},
        "58": {"comment":"Action 4 (EXOS variable)?"},
        "61": {"comment":"Action 5 (explain error code)? Others: leave"},
        "63": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $50 not 0? Leave the explaining to others"},
        "67": {"comment":"B = the error code: $CF?"},
        "70": {"comment":"Error $CF has message $2B"},
        "74": {"comment":"Codes $95-$BF have messages 0-$2A"},
        "77": {"comment":"Below $95? Not ours"},
        "78": {"comment":"Above $BF? Not ours"},
        "81": {"synopsis":"Action 5: builds message A in the workspace and hands it back to EXOS.","comment":"DE = the copy, A = its length"},
        "84": {"comment":"Empty message? Leave the action (C = 5)"},
        "86": {"comment":"C = 0: action taken; B = $FF, DE = the text"},
        "90": {"synopsis":"Action 7 (RAM allocation): asks for $07D4 bytes of RAM with B = 1, and takes the action\n(C = 0).","comment":"C = 0: taken; B = 1"},
        "93": {"comment":"DE = $07D4: the bytes of RAM wanted"},
        "97": {"synopsis":"Action 4 (an EXOS variable from 40 up, E = its number; B = 0 read, 1 write, 2 toggle,\nD = the value to write).\n1. Variable $90: kept by EXDOS only when EXOS has none (IY+$6A = $FF, set at INIT_ACTION);\n   its value is IY+$69.\n2. Variables $40-$63 are EXDOS's own: the bytes IY-$5E to IY-$3B ($40 is EXDOS's\n   segment, $47 the current drive).\nOthers are left for the next extension (C unchanged). VAR_ACCESS does the access and\ntakes the action.","comment":"E = the variable's number"},
        "98": {"comment":"Variable $90?"},
        "102": {"comment":"Does EXDOS keep variable $90 (IY+$6A = $FF)?"},
        "107": {"comment":"No: EXOS has it, leave the action"},
        "108": {"comment":"A = the access: 0 read, 1 write, 2 toggle"},
        "109": {"comment":"HL = IY+$69, variable $90's byte"},
        "119": {"synopsis":"Variables $40-$63: HL = IY-$5E + (number - $40); then VAR_ACCESS.","comment":"Index from variable $40"},
        "122": {"comment":"Below $40? Not ours"},
        "123": {"comment":"Above $63? Not ours"},
        "126": {"comment":"C = the index"},
        "127": {"comment":"A = the access"},
        "130": {"comment":"HL = IY + index"},
        "134": {"comment":"- $5E: variable $40 is at IY-$5E"},
        "138": {"synopsis":"Reads, writes or toggles the variable byte at HL as the access code in A asks (0 read,\n1 write, 2 toggle), then returns its value in D with A = 0 and C = 0 (action taken).","comment":"Access 0 (read)?"},
        "142": {"comment":"Access 1 (write)?"},
        "144": {"comment":"Toggle: D = the byte inverted"},
        "147": {"synopsis":"Writes D to the variable byte, then reads it back.","comment":"Store the new value"},
        "148": {"synopsis":"Returns the variable's value: D = the byte at HL, A = 0, C = 0 (action taken).","comment":"D = the variable's value"},
        "149": {"comment":"A = 0, no error"},
        "150": {"comment":"C = 0: action taken"},
        "152": {"synopsis":"Copies message A into the workspace as a counted text. Pages segment + 1 (EXDOS's second\npage) into page 1 and takes the message table whose address is at $4002 when EXOS\nvariable $90 is 0, else the one at $4000. Each entry is a length byte and the text; every\n\"\\\" in the text becomes CR LF. The copy at IY+$5DB is the length, the text and a 0.\nEntry: A = the message number; IY = the workspace.\nExit: DE = the copy (IY+$5DB); A = its length; page 1 restored.\nChanges: A, DE.\nKeeps: F, BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "154": {"comment":"E = the message number"},
        "155": {"comment":"Keep page 1's segment"},
        "158": {"comment":"A = this ROM's segment (page 3)"},
        "160": {"comment":"The next segment: EXDOS's second page"},
        "161": {"comment":"In page 1"},
        "164": {"comment":"HL = the table at ($4002)"},
        "167": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90"},
        "173": {"comment":"D = its value"},
        "174": {"comment":"Variable $90 = 0? Keep the table at ($4002)"},
        "178": {"comment":"Else the table at ($4000)"},
        "181": {"synopsis":"Walks the table at HL to entry E (each entry a length byte and its text).","comment":"E = the message number"},
        "182": {"comment":"B = entry counter, D = 0 for the length"},
        "186": {"synopsis":"Skips one entry per pass until the counter in B reaches the message number in A.","comment":"This entry?"},
        "189": {"comment":"Next entry number"},
        "190": {"comment":"E = this entry's length"},
        "191": {"comment":"Skip the text"},
        "192": {"comment":"And the length byte"},
        "195": {"synopsis":"Copies the entry at HL to the buffer at IY+$5DB, after its length byte.","comment":"BC = the entry"},
        "197": {"comment":"A = its length"},
        "201": {"comment":"HL = the buffer, IY+$5DB"},
        "205": {"comment":"Keep the buffer's address for the length"},
        "206": {"comment":"E = characters to copy + 1, D = the copy's length"},
        "208": {"comment":"+ 1 for the first DEC E"},
        "209": {"synopsis":"Copies one character, ends when the count in E runs out.","comment":"Next buffer byte"},
        "210": {"comment":"Next text character"},
        "211": {"comment":"All copied?"},
        "215": {"comment":"\"\\\"? It stands for a new line"},
        "219": {"comment":"Copy the character"},
        "222": {"synopsis":"Writes CR LF for a \"\\\": the copy grows by one byte.","comment":"CR"},
        "225": {"comment":"LF"},
        "227": {"comment":"One more byte in the copy"},
        "230": {"synopsis":"Ends the copy with a 0, writes its length in front, restores page 1 and returns\nA = the length, DE = the copy.","comment":"A 0 after the text (E = 0)"},
        "231": {"comment":"HL = the copy's start"},
        "232": {"comment":"Its length byte"},
        "233": {"comment":"Page 1's segment as it was"},
        "236": {"comment":"A = the copy's length"},
        "237": {"comment":"DE = the copy"},
        "242": {"synopsis":"Reads a workspace word: DE = the word at IY + the signed byte that follows the CALL, and\nreturns past that byte.\nEntry: the byte after the CALL = an offset from IY (-128 to 127); IY = the workspace.\nExit: DE = the word at IY + the offset.\nChanges: DE.\nKeeps: AF, BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "243": {"comment":"E = the inline byte"},
        "244": {"comment":"Return past it"},
        "247": {"comment":"HL = IY, the caller's HL kept on the stack"},
        "250": {"comment":"D = the byte's sign"},
        "254": {"comment":"HL = IY + the offset"},
        "255": {"comment":"DE = the word there"},
        "261": {"synopsis":"Returns the character that separates the names in a path (the callers look for it in a\nname): \"\\\" ($5C) when EXOS variable $90 is not 0, \"'\" ($27) when it is 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the separator.\nChanges: A.\nKeeps: F, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "264": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90"},
        "270": {"comment":"D = its value"},
        "271": {"comment":"Variable $90 = 0?"},
        "275": {"comment":"Not 0: \"\\\""},
        "279": {"synopsis":"Variable $90 is 0: the separator is \"'\".","comment":"\"'\""},
        "281": {"synopsis":"Returns the separator in A with the caller's flags, BC and DE.","comment":"The caller's flags"},
        "282": {"comment":"A = the separator"},
        "286": {"synopsis":"Action 1 (cold start), once (bit 6 of IY-$37): sets bits 6 and 3 of IY-$37, then has\nANNOUNCE_DRIVES offer \"EXDOS E:\", \"EXDOS F:\", \"EXDOS B:\" and \"EXDOS A:\" to the\nextensions. C stays 1, so the other extensions get the action too.","comment":"A = EXDOS's flags"},
        "289": {"comment":"Cold start done before?"},
        "292": {"comment":"Mark it done; bit 3 also set"},
        "298": {"comment":"Offer the drive commands"},
        "301": {"comment":"Room for a longer call"},
        "314": {"synopsis":"Action 8 (initialise).\n1. Makes DISK the default device (EXOS 19, type 1); clears the error hook's segment\n   (IY-$3A), IY-$80 and IY-$20; sets EXDOS variables $4B and $4C and IY+$2E to $FF.\n2. Already initialised (bit 7 of IY-$37)? The rest is REINIT's.\n3. First time: variable $47 (the current drive) becomes 1, variables $46 and $53 $FF,\n   IY+$2E $FE; keeps page 0's segment (IY+$2C) and EXDOS's segment (IY+$2F and\n   variable $40).\n4. Copies the 72 bytes at $04BD (RAM_FARCALL, RAM_SEGCALL and two device descriptors) to\n   IY+$01ED and patches them: both CALL $0000s call the copy's JP (HL), and EXDOS's\n   segment goes into the page-3 restore and both descriptors' table segments.\n5. Asks for 3 sector buffers and links the DISK device and the buffers (LINK_DISK_DEV);\n   maps every drive to itself (FN26_MAP_DRIVE with B = 0).\n6. Adds the built-in units: 4 driven by $1FD3 (records from IY+$2BB) and, when that worked,\n   makes drive 2 a copy of drive 1 (FN25_COPY_DRIVE); then 1 driven by $1005 (record at\n   IY+$441). Both are in this segment, IX = IY for them.\nGoes on at INIT_LAST_UNIT.","comment":"DE = \"DISK\", the default device's name"},
        "317": {"comment":"C = the device type"},
        "321": {"comment":"No error hook (its segment = 0)"},
        "331": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "332": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $4B = $FF"},
        "335": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $4C = $FF"},
        "341": {"comment":"Initialised before?"},
        "346": {"comment":"Yes: only relink and restart"},
        "349": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $47 (current drive) = 1"},
        "352": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $46 = $FF"},
        "355": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $53 = $FF"},
        "358": {"comment":"IY+$2E = $FE"},
        "361": {"comment":"Page 0's segment"},
        "366": {"comment":"EXDOS's segment (page 3)"},
        "371": {"comment":"Is EXDOS variable $40"},
        "377": {"comment":"Workspace kept twice for later"},
        "379": {"comment":"DE = IY+$01ED, where the RAM code goes"},
        "384": {"comment":"HL = the code and descriptors to copy"},
        "388": {"comment":"72 bytes"},
        "393": {"comment":"IX = the copy"},
        "395": {"comment":"Page 3's segment the copy puts back"},
        "398": {"comment":"HL = the copy's JP (HL) ($04D4's copy)"},
        "402": {"comment":"RAM_FARCALL's CALL goes to it"},
        "408": {"comment":"RAM_SEGCALL's CALL goes to it"},
        "414": {"comment":"The second descriptor's table segment"},
        "417": {"comment":"The DISK descriptor's table segment"},
        "420": {"comment":"3 sector buffers wanted"},
        "424": {"comment":"Link DISK and the buffers"},
        "427": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "429": {"comment":"Every drive mapped to itself"},
        "432": {"comment":"IX = IY, the workspace for the units' driver"},
        "434": {"comment":"DE = the driver routine ($1FD3)"},
        "437": {"comment":"Its segment: this ROM"},
        "439": {"comment":"4 units, records from HL (IY+$2BB)"},
        "444": {"comment":"Drive 2 = a copy of drive 1, if the units were added"},
        "450": {"comment":"HL = IX = IY"},
        "454": {"comment":"HL = IY+$43E: one more unit's block"},
        "458": {"comment":"DE = the driver routine ($1005)"},
        "463": {"comment":"1 unit"},
        "465": {"synopsis":"Adds the last built-in unit (ADD_UNITS), then checks that EXOS has variable $90: if it\nhas not, EXDOS keeps it itself (IY+$6A = $FF), with the value $FF (IY+$69).","comment":"Add the unit"},
        "471": {"comment":"Assume EXOS has variable $90"},
        "475": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90"},
        "481": {"comment":"Exists? EXOS keeps it"},
        "483": {"comment":"No: EXDOS answers for it (ACT4_VAR)"},
        "487": {"comment":"Its value: $FF"},
        "491": {"synopsis":"Marks the initialisation done (bit 7 of IY-$37)."},
        "494": {"comment":"Initialised"},
        "498": {"synopsis":"Offers the command \"EXDOS\" + $FF to the extensions (EXOS 26) until none takes it; each\none that does hands back B = a segment and DE = a block of units, added by\nFN24_ADD_DRIVER.","comment":"DE = the command \"EXDOS\" + $FF"},
        "503": {"comment":"Nobody took it? Done"},
        "505": {"comment":"Add the units it gave"},
        "510": {"synopsis":"First initialisation done: announces \"EXDOS\" + $FC with A = 0.","comment":"DE = the command \"EXDOS\" + $FC"},
        "513": {"comment":"A = 0 for EXDOS_STATE_RST"},
        "514": {"synopsis":"Resets EXDOS's drive state (EXDOS_STATE_RST with A), offers the command at DE to the\nextensions (EXOS 26) and leaves action 8 to the others (C = 8)."},
        "515": {"comment":"Reset the state"},
        "519": {"comment":"Offer the command"},
        "521": {"comment":"C = 8: the other extensions get action 8 too"},
        "545": {"synopsis":"Action 8 again (EXDOS initialised before).\n1. Keeps bits 7, 6, 2 and 1 of IY-$37.\n2. Links the DISK device and the buffers again unless the device for drive A answers\n   (RELINK_DEVICES), and the drive letter devices.\n3. Calls function 1 of every driver block in the chain at IY+$1E (REINIT_DRV_LP).","comment":"Keep bits 7, 6, 2, 1 of the flags"},
        "550": {"comment":"Relink the devices"},
        "553": {"comment":"Keep B (1: nothing relinked)"},
        "554": {"comment":"A = the first driver block's segment"},
        "557": {"comment":"HL = its address"},
        "563": {"synopsis":"Calls function 1 of each driver block in the chain (link: segment, address in the block's\nfirst 3 bytes; segment 0 ends it), then frees the scratch buffer (FN30_SCRATCH_BUF with\nA = B = 0) and announces \"EXDOS\" + $FB with A = the B kept at REINIT.","comment":"Page the block in"},
        "566": {"comment":"HL = its first unit record"},
        "569": {"comment":"Driver function 1"},
        "575": {"comment":"A = the next block's segment"},
        "577": {"comment":"HL = its address"},
        "582": {"comment":"Another block?"},
        "584": {"comment":"B = 0, A = 0: release"},
        "585": {"comment":"Free the scratch buffer"},
        "588": {"comment":"DE = the command \"EXDOS\" + $FB"},
        "591": {"comment":"A = the B kept at REINIT"},
        "594": {"synopsis":"Checks whether the device for drive A answers (QUERY_DRIVE_DEV); if it does, returns with\nB = 1. Otherwise links the DISK device and the buffers again (LINK_DISK_DEV) and goes on\nat RELINK_LETTERS (B = 0).\nEntry: IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z; B = 1 when nothing was linked, 0 when the devices were linked again.\nError: none (a failed link is not reported).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL' (RELINK_LET_DEV works in the alternate set).\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"Drive A"},
        "599": {"comment":"B = 1: nothing relinked"},
        "601": {"comment":"Device A answers? Done"},
        "602": {"comment":"Link DISK and the buffers again"},
        "605": {"synopsis":"Makes sure every drive from 26 down to 1 that has a unit has its letter device\n(ENSURE_DRIVE_DEV); a unit record with byte +9 not 0 gets 1 there.","comment":"From drive 26 down"},
        "607": {"synopsis":"One drive: maps it to its unit and pages the unit's record in.","comment":"A = the drive"},
        "608": {"comment":"HL = its unit's slot"},
        "611": {"comment":"A = the slot's segment"},
        "613": {"comment":"No unit? Next drive"},
        "615": {"comment":"Page the record in"},
        "617": {"comment":"DE = the record's address"},
        "621": {"comment":"Its byte +9"},
        "627": {"comment":"0? Keep it"},
        "629": {"comment":"Else 1"},
        "631": {"synopsis":"Links drive B's letter device unless it answers.","comment":"A = the drive"},
        "632": {"comment":"Keep B, the loop counter"},
        "633": {"comment":"Link the letter device if needed"},
        "637": {"synopsis":"Next drive; A = 0 when all are done."},
        "639": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "641": {"synopsis":"Links the DISK device (the descriptor copied to IY+$01FB) with EXOS 21, empties the buffer\nlist, then links the buffer device \".\" with as many sector buffers as IY+$21 asks\n(LINK_DRIVE_DEV), falling back to 3 when the RAM is not there.\nEntry: IY = the workspace; IY+$21 = the buffers wanted.\nExit: Z when the buffers were linked; IY+$21 = their count.\nError: NZ and carry when not even 3 buffers could be linked.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IY+$21-$27.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"HL = IY+$229, 3 below the second descriptor's copy"},
        "648": {"comment":"Kept for LINK_DRIVE_DEV"},
        "654": {"comment":"HL - 14: the DISK descriptor's DD_TYPE"},
        "659": {"comment":"No device RAM"},
        "664": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "665": {"comment":"No buffers in the list"},
        "671": {"comment":"IY+$24/$25 high byte = 0: no recent buffer"},
        "674": {"comment":"B = the buffers wanted"},
        "677": {"synopsis":"Links the buffer device with B buffers; when that fails and B was 4 or more, tries once\nmore with 3.","comment":"None linked yet"},
        "681": {"comment":"The device's name: \".\""},
        "684": {"comment":"Link it with B buffers"},
        "688": {"comment":"Linked? Done"},
        "690": {"comment":"Fewer than 4 asked? Fail (carry)"},
        "693": {"comment":"Try with 3"},
        "697": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 27: adds sector buffers until there are B (at most 10). Asking for fewer\nthan there are changes nothing.\nEntry: B = the buffers wanted; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0; B = the buffers there are.\nError: A = $F7 with carry for more than 10; a failed link's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"More than 10 buffers?"},
        "700": {"comment":"Error $F7"},
        "703": {"comment":"B = how many more are wanted"},
        "708": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "710": {"comment":"None? Done"},
        "712": {"comment":"The buffer device \".\""},
        "714": {"comment":"More wanted: link them"},
        "717": {"synopsis":"Returns B = the number of buffers (IY+$21).","comment":"B = the buffers there are"},
        "721": {"synopsis":"Maps a drive to its unit: A = the byte at IY+$2A0 + drive (0 for a drive above 26), and\nHL = that unit's slot (UNIT_SLOT).\nEntry: A = the drive (1-26); IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the unit's number; HL = its slot (segment, then the record's address).\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"Above 26?"},
        "725": {"comment":"Taken as 0"},
        "726": {"synopsis":"Reads the drive's entry in the map at IY+$2A0 and finds the slot of the unit it names."},
        "730": {"comment":"HL = the map, IY+$2A0"},
        "735": {"comment":"HL = the drive's entry"},
        "739": {"comment":"A = its unit"},
        "741": {"comment":"HL = the unit's slot"},
        "744": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "747": {"synopsis":"Pages a unit's record in: A = the unit, its slot gives the segment (put in page 1) and the\nrecord's address.\nEntry: A = the unit (1-26); IY = the workspace.\nExit: page 1 = the record's segment (also in A); DE = the record's address; HL = the\nslot's address high byte.\nError: Z (A = 0) when the slot is empty.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; page 1.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY.","comment":"HL = the unit's slot"},
        "750": {"comment":"A = its segment"},
        "752": {"comment":"No unit? Z"},
        "753": {"comment":"Page the record in"},
        "756": {"comment":"DE = the record's address"},
        "760": {"synopsis":"Finds a unit's slot: HL = IY+$24F + 3 x unit (a unit above 26 is taken as 0). A slot is the\nsegment of the unit's record (0: no unit) and the record's address.\nEntry: A = the unit; IY = the workspace.\nExit: HL = the slot.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY.","comment":"Above 26?"},
        "764": {"comment":"Taken as 0"},
        "765": {"synopsis":"HL = IY+$24F + 3 x A.","comment":"A = unit x 3"},
        "771": {"comment":"HL = the slot table (unit 1 at IY+$252)"},
        "780": {"synopsis":"Asks whether the device named after drive A answers: builds the name \"<letter>:\" (counted)\nat IY+$6D1 and opens it in query mode (OPEN_QUERY).\nEntry: A = the drive (1-26); IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0; Z when the open ended with status $F9 or $F8.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"A = the drive's letter"},
        "782": {"comment":"HL = IY+$6D3, the name's end"},
        "789": {"comment":"\":\""},
        "792": {"comment":"E = the letter (L after the swap: bit 7 clear, open)"},
        "793": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "795": {"comment":"The name's length: 2"},
        "797": {"comment":"DE = the name"},
        "798": {"comment":"Open it in query mode"},
        "801": {"comment":"Status $F9?"},
        "804": {"comment":"Z when the status was $F8"},
        "806": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "809": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 23: opens a channel to \"DISK:\" in query mode, passing BC to the device in\nIY+$6B/$6C; falls into OPEN_QUERY.","comment":"DE = \"DISK:\""},
        "812": {"comment":"BC for the device"},
        "818": {"synopsis":"Opens a channel (OPEN_FREE_CHAN) with bit 0 of IY-$37 set while it runs, so EXDOS's own\ndevices know the open is a query.\nEntry: DE = the device name (counted); L bit 7 = 0; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the last status, flags from OR A; DE = the word at IY+$6B; B = IY+$6D.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H.","comment":"Query mode on"},
        "822": {"synopsis":"Opens a channel to the name at DE on the first free channel number from 0 up: EXOS 1\n(open), or EXOS 2 (create) when entered at $0339, which sets bit 7 of L. Status $F9 moves\non to the next number; any other error closes the channel. Ends with bit 0 of IY-$37\nclear, B = IY+$6D and DE = the word at IY+$6B.\nEntry: DE = the name (counted); L = flags; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the status, flags from OR A; H = the channel tried last; DE = the word at\nIY+$6B; B = IY+$6D.\nError: A = the error's status (NZ); $F9 when every number was taken.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H; bit 7 of L.","comment":"Open (bit 7 of L clear)"},
        "824": {"comment":"Its bytes CB FD: SET 7,L, the create entry $0339"},
        "827": {"comment":"From channel 0"},
        "829": {"synopsis":"Tries channel H: EXOS 1 (open) or, when bit 7 of L is set, EXOS 2 (create).","comment":"A = the channel"},
        "831": {"comment":"Create?"},
        "837": {"comment":"Its bytes F7 02: EXOS 2 (create), the entry at $0346"},
        "841": {"comment":"Opened? Done"},
        "843": {"comment":"Status $F9: the channel number is taken?"},
        "847": {"comment":"Try the next number"},
        "850": {"comment":"All taken: give up with $F9"},
        "852": {"synopsis":"Any other error: closes channel H and keeps the error's status."},
        "853": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "857": {"synopsis":"Leaves query mode and returns B = IY+$6D, DE = the word at IY+$6B, A = the status.","comment":"Query mode off"},
        "861": {"comment":"B = IY+$6D"},
        "864": {"synopsis":"DE = the word at IY+$6B; returns with flags from OR A.\nEntry: A; IY = the workspace.\nExit: DE = the word at IY+$6B; flags from A.\nChanges: F, DE.\nKeeps: A, BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"DE = (IY+$6B)"},
        "868": {"synopsis":"Returns with the flags from A (IY_WORD_INLINE comes back here past its byte).","comment":"Flags from A, carry clear"},
        "876": {"synopsis":"Makes sure drive A has its letter device: when the query of \"<letter>:\" ends with status\n$F9 or $F8 nothing is done; otherwise the device named after the letter is linked with no\nbuffers (LINK_DRIVE_DEV).\nEntry: A = the drive (1-26); IY = the workspace.\nExit: Z, A = 0 when the device answered or was linked.\nError: NZ, A = the status when the link failed.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"Does the device answer?"},
        "879": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to do"},
        "880": {"comment":"C = the letter, the device's name"},
        "882": {"synopsis":"Links a device whose name is the one character in C, with RAM for B sector buffers of $20B\nbytes and a header (B x $20B + 14 bytes), from the descriptor template 3 bytes above the\naddress at IY+$26. The template's 9 bytes are then copied below the device's RAM (whose\naddress is at IY+$6B), IY+$26 points 3 below the copy, and the two bytes under it hold the\nworkspace's distance (IY - copy - 1). With B not 0 the buffers are linked into the list at\nIY+$22 (LINK_BUF_LOOP).\nEntry: B = the buffers; C = the name; IY = the workspace.\nExit: Z, A = 0 when linked; IY+$21 counts the buffers linked.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS 21's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IY+$21-$27."},
        "883": {"comment":"A = the name"},
        "884": {"comment":"$FE03 + $20B = $000E: the header"},
        "887": {"comment":"+ $20B per buffer"},
        "890": {"comment":"B + 1 additions"},
        "891": {"synopsis":"Adds $20B per buffer.","comment":"+ one buffer"},
        "894": {"comment":"BC = the RAM wanted"},
        "896": {"comment":"DE = (IY+$26)"},
        "900": {"synopsis":"Second half of LINK_DRIVE_DEV: links the device, then copies its descriptor below its RAM.","comment":"DE = the template's DD_TYPE"},
        "903": {"comment":"HL = the name's character"},
        "907": {"comment":"The device's name"},
        "908": {"comment":"Link it, BC bytes of RAM"},
        "910": {"comment":"B = the buffers"},
        "911": {"comment":"Failed? Return its status"},
        "912": {"comment":"A = the buffers"},
        "913": {"comment":"DE = (IY+$6B): the device's RAM"},
        "916": {"comment":"The 9 bytes below it"},
        "920": {"comment":"Copy the descriptor there"},
        "925": {"comment":"HL = IY - the copy - 1"},
        "928": {"comment":"DE = that distance, HL = below the copy"},
        "931": {"comment":"IY+$26 = 3 below the copy"},
        "938": {"comment":"The distance below that"},
        "941": {"comment":"No buffers?"},
        "944": {"synopsis":"Puts one buffer ($20C bytes below the last) at the head of the buffer list.","comment":"HL = the next buffer, $20C lower"},
        "948": {"comment":"DE = (IY+$22), the list's head"},
        "952": {"synopsis":"Second half of LINK_BUF_LOOP: the buffer becomes the head, its link the old head.","comment":"The new head"},
        "958": {"comment":"Its link: the old head"},
        "961": {"comment":"One more buffer"},
        "964": {"comment":"More?"},
        "968": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 24: adds the units of a driver. The block at DE (in segment B, read in page\n1) holds the number of units, the driver's routine address and its segment, then room\nfor a record of $60 bytes per unit; ADD_UNITS builds the records over it.\nEntry: B = the block's segment; DE = its address; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z when the block has no units; else as ADD_UNITS.\nError: Z when there are no units (nothing added).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; page 1.","comment":"Page the block in"},
        "971": {"comment":"IX = the block's address: the driver's IY"},
        "974": {"comment":"In page 1"},
        "979": {"comment":"A = the number of units"},
        "981": {"comment":"None? Done"},
        "982": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "985": {"comment":"DE = the driver's routine"},
        "989": {"comment":"A = the driver's segment"},
        "991": {"synopsis":"Adds C units of a driver.\n1. For each unit, writes a record ($60 bytes, the first at HL + 3): +0 the segment for\n   page 1 (B), +1/+2 the driver's IY (IX), +3 its segment (A), +4/+5 its routine (DE),\n   +6 the unit's number within the driver (from 0), +7 and +8 the drive given to it,\n   +9 = 0, +$1F = $FF.\n2. Gives it the first free drive from 1 to 26: the drive's slot gets the record's segment\n   and address (interrupts off while it is written), and the letter device is linked\n   (ENSURE_DRIVE_DEV). A unit gets no drive when all 26 are taken.\n3. Links the block at the head of the chain at IY+$1E-$20 (its first 3 bytes get the old\n   head) and calls the driver's function 0 for its first unit (DRV_CALL_FF).\nEntry: HL = the block; C = the units; DE = the routine; A = the driver's segment; B = the\nblock's segment; IX = the value the driver gets in IY; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the status of driver function 0, flags from OR A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF'; page 1.","comment":"A' = 0: the first unit's number"},
        "994": {"comment":"The block's address in page 1"},
        "998": {"comment":"Keep the block's start"},
        "999": {"comment":"The first record at +3"},
        "1002": {"synopsis":"Writes one unit's record and looks for a free drive for it."},
        "1005": {"comment":"+0: the segment for page 1"},
        "1006": {"comment":"BC = the driver's IY"},
        "1012": {"comment":"+1/+2: the driver's IY"},
        "1016": {"comment":"+3: the driver's segment"},
        "1018": {"comment":"+4/+5: the routine"},
        "1022": {"comment":"+6: the unit's number in the driver"},
        "1024": {"comment":"Next unit's number"},
        "1027": {"comment":"Keep +7, where the drive goes"},
        "1030": {"comment":"+9 = 0"},
        "1032": {"comment":"+ $16"},
        "1036": {"comment":"+$1F = $FF"},
        "1038": {"comment":"26 drives"},
        "1040": {"comment":"HL = drive 1's slot, IY+$252"},
        "1047": {"comment":"DE = the record's +7"},
        "1048": {"synopsis":"Looks for the first drive whose slot is empty.","comment":"A = the slot's segment"},
        "1050": {"comment":"Empty? This drive"},
        "1053": {"comment":"Next slot"},
        "1057": {"comment":"None free: no drive for the unit"},
        "1059": {"synopsis":"Gives the unit drive 27 - B: writes it in the record (+7 and +8) and the record's segment\nand address in the drive's slot, then links the drive's letter device.","comment":"A = the drive's number"},
        "1062": {"comment":"Record +7"},
        "1064": {"comment":"And +8"},
        "1065": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "1066": {"comment":"No interrupts while the slot changes"},
        "1067": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "1069": {"comment":"A = the record's segment"},
        "1071": {"comment":"The slot's address"},
        "1076": {"comment":"The slot's segment"},
        "1078": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "1079": {"comment":"Link its letter device if needed"},
        "1082": {"synopsis":"Next record ($60 bytes on); after the last, links the block into the chain at IY+$1E and\ncalls driver function 0.","comment":"HL = this record"},
        "1083": {"comment":"The next record"},
        "1092": {"comment":"One unit fewer"},
        "1095": {"comment":"HL = IY+$1E, the chain's head"},
        "1102": {"comment":"DE = the block"},
        "1104": {"comment":"Its first 3 bytes = the old head"},
        "1109": {"comment":"BC = the block"},
        "1111": {"comment":"The head = the block's address"},
        "1115": {"comment":"And segment (page 1)"},
        "1118": {"comment":"HL = the first record's +8"},
        "1122": {"comment":"B = its drive"},
        "1123": {"comment":"HL = the first record"},
        "1124": {"comment":"Driver function 0"},
        "1125": {"synopsis":"Calls a driver function (DRIVER_CALL) with C = $FF, so page 1 holds segment $FF during\nthe call, and IX = IY + $C4A1.","comment":"IX = IY + $C4A1"},
        "1134": {"comment":"Segment $FF for page 1"},
        "1136": {"synopsis":"Calls a unit's driver through the RAM copy of RAM_FARCALL. The unit's record gives: +0 the\nvalue for B', +1/+2 for IY, +3 the segment for page 3, +4/+5 the routine, +6 the value\nfor C.\n1. Keeps IX, IY, HL, the alternate set and AF'; IY = the RAM code (IY+$01ED), whose\n   page-1 restore gets page 1's segment and whose page-3 load the record's segment.\n2. Pages segment C into page 1 and jumps to RAM_FARCALL with the routine in HL, the\n   record's IY on the stack and A' = the entry A.\n3. RAM_FARCALL returns to DRV_CALL_RET with the driver's status in A'.\nEntry: A = the function code; HL = the unit's record; C = the segment for page 1; DE for\nthe driver; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the driver's status, flags from OR A ($E5 when SOFT_IRQ_CHECK finds $20); BC, DE\nas the driver left them; pages 1 and 3 restored.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "1141": {"comment":"Swap to keep the alternates and A' = A"},
        "1146": {"comment":"Keep AF' (the caller's)"},
        "1148": {"comment":"Keep DE"},
        "1149": {"comment":"IY = the RAM code"},
        "1154": {"comment":"Page 1's segment, restored after the call"},
        "1159": {"comment":"A = record +0"},
        "1162": {"comment":"Into B'"},
        "1164": {"comment":"DE = record +1/+2: the driver's IY"},
        "1168": {"comment":"For RAM_FARCALL's POP IY"},
        "1169": {"comment":"Record +3: the driver's segment"},
        "1170": {"comment":"Into the RAM code's page-3 load"},
        "1174": {"comment":"DE = record +4/+5: the routine"},
        "1178": {"comment":"A = the segment for page 1"},
        "1179": {"comment":"C = record +6"},
        "1180": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "1182": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "1183": {"comment":"To the RAM copy of RAM_FARCALL"},
        "1185": {"synopsis":"The return from a driver call: A = the driver's status (or $E5), the caller's AF', BC',\nDE', HL', HL, IY and IX back, flags from OR A.","comment":"$20 pending? A' = $E5"},
        "1188": {"comment":"The caller's AF'"},
        "1189": {"comment":"A = the status"},
        "1200": {"comment":"Flags from the status"},
        "1202": {"synopsis":"Checks $BFF2 (EXOS 2.1's FLAG_SOFT_IRQ) for $20: if it is there, A' = $E5 and Z.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Z and A' = $E5 when $BFF2 holds $20; NZ otherwise, A' unchanged.\nChanges: AF, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A = the pending software interrupt"},
        "1205": {"comment":"$20?"},
        "1208": {"comment":"Status $E5 instead"},
        "1211": {"comment":"Z"},
        "1213": {"synopsis":"Code copied to IY+$01ED at INIT_ACTION and run there (the operands at +4, +9, +$0D and\n+$11 are patched): DRIVER_CALL's far call. Pops the driver's IY and the caller's DE,\npages the driver's segment into page 3, calls the routine in HL with A = the function\ncode, restores pages 1 and 3 and goes back to DRV_CALL_RET with the status in A'.","comment":"IY = the driver's IY"},
        "1215": {"comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "1216": {"comment":"The driver's segment (patched)"},
        "1218": {"comment":"Into page 3"},
        "1220": {"comment":"A = the function code"},
        "1221": {"comment":"Call HL (patched to the copy's JP (HL))"},
        "1224": {"comment":"A' = the status"},
        "1225": {"comment":"Page 1's segment (patched)"},
        "1229": {"comment":"EXDOS's segment (patched)"},
        "1231": {"comment":"Back into page 3"},
        "1233": {"comment":"Back in EXDOS"},
        "1236": {"synopsis":"The copy's JP (HL): both copied CALLs come here.","comment":"To the routine"},
        "1237": {"synopsis":"Also run in the copy (IY+$0205, called at $0F0C): calls DE with segment A in page 3 and\nA = IY+$2A, then puts EXDOS's segment (EXDOS variable $40) back in page 3.","comment":"Segment A into page 3"},
        "1239": {"comment":"A = IY+$2A for the routine"},
        "1242": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "1243": {"comment":"Call it (patched to the copy's JP (HL))"},
        "1246": {"comment":"B = its result"},
        "1247": {"comment":"EXDOS's segment"},
        "1252": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "1285": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function call (entry $C010): runs function A (1-30) from the table at $0550 with the\ncaller's BC, DE, HL.\n1. Keeps the alternate BC, DE, HL and AF', page 1's segment (IY+$2D) and SP (IY+$28, for\n   the error handler's abandon), clears IY+$48.\n2. Enters the function through FUNC_JUMP with A = 0; it returns to FUNC_RETURN.\nEntry: A = the function; BC, DE, HL its parameters; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the status, flags from OR A; BC, DE, HL as the function left them; page 1, BC',\nDE', HL' and AF' restored.\nError: A = $B0 (NZ) for function 0 or above 30.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Above 30?"},
        "1289": {"comment":"Use the alternate set; the caller's in the other"},
        "1290": {"comment":"Keep the caller's alternates"},
        "1293": {"comment":"BC = the function x 2"},
        "1297": {"comment":"A' = the function x 2"},
        "1298": {"comment":"Keep the caller's AF'"},
        "1299": {"comment":"Keep page 1's segment"},
        "1304": {"comment":"IY+$48 = 0"},
        "1307": {"comment":"HL = SP"},
        "1310": {"comment":"Kept for an abandoned call"},
        "1316": {"comment":"HL = the function's table entry"},
        "1320": {"comment":"DE = the function's address"},
        "1323": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "1324": {"comment":"Enter it; it returns to FUNC_RETURN"},
        "1327": {"synopsis":"The return from an EXDOS function (also where the error handler abandons one, with the\nstack put back): restores page 1, checks $BFF2, restores the caller's AF', BC', DE', HL',\nclears bit 1 of IY-$37 and IY-$80, and returns A = the status with flags from OR A.","comment":"A' = the status"},
        "1328": {"comment":"Page 1 as it was"},
        "1333": {"comment":"$20 pending? Status $E5"},
        "1336": {"comment":"The caller's AF'"},
        "1337": {"comment":"A = the status"},
        "1343": {"comment":"Clear bit 1 of the flags"},
        "1347": {"comment":"IY-$80 = 0"},
        "1351": {"comment":"Flags from the status"},
        "1353": {"synopsis":"Jumps to DE with the caller's BC, DE, HL back in the main set.\nEntry: DE = the address (alternate set active).\nExit: none: it jumps.\nChanges: the main and alternate sets swap.","comment":"The address as the return"},
        "1354": {"comment":"The caller's registers"},
        "1355": {"comment":"To the function"},
        "1356": {"synopsis":"Function 0 or a number above 30: A = $B0, NZ.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = $B0; NZ, carry clear.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Status $B0"},
        "1422": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 28: maps drive 5 (E:) to itself (FN26_MAP_DRIVE), selects it and drops its\nbuffers (SELECT_DROP), calls its driver with A = $FF (DRIVER_CALL, C = 5); with B not 0\ngoes on at $05BC.\nEntry: B = the parameter; DE; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z when B is 0; else as $05BC.\nError: NZ, A = the status from selecting the drive or from the driver.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Drive 5"},
        "1425": {"comment":"B = C = 5: drive 5 to itself"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Select it, drop its buffers"},
        "1433": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1435": {"comment":"Driver function $FF"},
        "1441": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1442": {"comment":"B = 0? Done"},
        "1446": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 29 (table word at $058A): prepares drive C, has its unit's driver run request\n8, then writes a fresh file system: FAT entries 0 and 1, every other FAT entry 0, and an\nemptied root directory.\n1. $0608 selects the drive (B = 2) and drops its buffers; DE is handed on to it.\n2. Driver request 8 through $0470, with C = the caller's page-1 segment (IY+$2D); an answer\n   of $BD becomes error $AF (Invalid drive).\n3. INIT_FS_FAT writes the FAT and clears the directory (function 28 joins there too).\nEntry: C = the drive number; DE = handed to $0608; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code (from $0608, the driver or the drive select).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Select drive C (B = 2) and drop its buffers"},
        "1449": {"comment":"No such drive or no disk?"},
        "1451": {"comment":"Request 8 to the unit's driver"},
        "1453": {"comment":"C = the caller's page-1 segment, saved by $0505"},
        "1460": {"comment":"Request done?"},
        "1462": {"comment":"Answer $BD?"},
        "1465": {"comment":"Then error $AF (Invalid drive)"},
        "1468": {"synopsis":"Writes a fresh FAT for drive C and clears its root directory: FAT[0] = $F00 + the media byte\n(record+$1D), FAT[1] = $FFF, then FAT[2] up to the last cluster 0 (INIT_FS_CLEAR). Function\n28 ($05A4) joins here too.","comment":"HL = the drive's record (paged into page 1)"},
        "1471": {"comment":"Drive selected?"},
        "1473": {"comment":"Keep the record twice: the second slot gets the media byte"},
        "1479": {"comment":"C = the media byte at record+$1D"},
        "1480": {"comment":"BC = $0F00 + media byte, the value of FAT entry 0"},
        "1482": {"comment":"H = media byte, kept on the stack for the end"},
        "1484": {"comment":"DE = 0: cluster 0"},
        "1485": {"comment":"FAT[0] = $F00 + media byte"},
        "1488": {"comment":"Cluster 1"},
        "1489": {"comment":"B >= $10 writes $FFF"},
        "1492": {"comment":"FAT[1] = $FFF"},
        "1495": {"synopsis":"Sets every FAT entry from cluster 2 on to 0 (free) up to the last cluster (record+$16 holds\nthe cluster count + 2), then clears the root directory's sectors (record+$12 up to\nrecord+$14 - 1) through DIR_CLEAR_SECS when the media byte is below $FE, and writes the\ndrive's changed buffers back ($0BAD).","comment":"Next cluster"},
        "1499": {"comment":"FAT[DE] = 0: free"},
        "1503": {"comment":"HL = the word at record+$16, the cluster limit"},
        "1511": {"comment":"The last cluster is limit - 1"},
        "1512": {"comment":"Was that the last one?"},
        "1517": {"comment":"Record+$12: the root directory's first sector"},
        "1525": {"comment":"DE = record+$14: the sector after it (the data area)"},
        "1530": {"comment":"L = the directory's sector count"},
        "1532": {"comment":"A = the media byte saved at $05CB"},
        "1533": {"comment":"Below $FE?"},
        "1537": {"comment":"DE = the directory's last sector"},
        "1538": {"comment":"Clear the directory, last sector first"},
        "1541": {"comment":"Write back the drive's changed buffers"},
        "1544": {"synopsis":"Selects drive C (SELECT_DRIVE with B = 2: its changed buffers written back), drops its\nbuffers (BUF_DROP_DRIVE) and resets the record (+9 = 0, +$1E = $FF at $0DE6).\nEntry: C = the drive; DE; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL = the drive's record; IX = DE.\nError: NZ, A = the status from SELECT_DRIVE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "1546": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "1548": {"comment":"Select the drive"},
        "1552": {"comment":"IX = the caller's DE"},
        "1555": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1556": {"comment":"Drop its buffers"},
        "1559": {"comment":"Reset the record"},
        "1562": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 14 (table word at $056C): writes back the changed buffers of drive B (0: the\ndefault drive at IY-$57; $FF: every drive). With C nonzero it then drops those buffers and\nmarks every unit for a disk check ($025D).\nEntry: B = the drive number (0 default, $FF all); C = nonzero to drop the buffers too.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = $AF (Invalid drive), NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IY."},
        "1563": {"comment":"Drive $FF?"},
        "1566": {"comment":"Drive 0?"},
        "1569": {"comment":"Then the default drive"},
        "1572": {"synopsis":"Looks drive A up ($02D1); a drive without a unit is error $AF (Invalid drive).","comment":"A = the drive's unit, 0 for none"},
        "1576": {"comment":"Unit found?"},
        "1578": {"comment":"Error $AF: Invalid drive"},
        "1581": {"synopsis":"Writes back the changed buffers of unit A ($FF: all, $0BAE), then, when C is nonzero, drops\nthem ($0BBE) and has every unit's disk checked again ($025D).","comment":"B = the unit, $FF for all"},
        "1582": {"comment":"Write back the unit's changed buffers"},
        "1585": {"comment":"C = 0: done?"},
        "1588": {"comment":"Drop the unit's buffers"},
        "1591": {"comment":"Recheck every unit's disk"},
        "1594": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 21 (table word at $057A): the free space of drive B. Reads every FAT entry\nfrom cluster 2 to the last one and counts the zero ones.\nEntry: B = the drive number; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL = the free clusters; DE = the clusters in all; B = 1 + the byte at\nrecord+$0A; C = the record's segment; IX = record+8.\nError: A = an error code from the drive select ($AF Invalid drive), NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"C = the drive"},
        "1595": {"comment":"HL = the drive's record"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Selected?"},
        "1600": {"comment":"IX = the record"},
        "1603": {"comment":"DE = record+$16: the cluster limit (count + 2)"},
        "1609": {"comment":"Kept on the stack for the loop's test"},
        "1610": {"comment":"Start at cluster 2"},
        "1613": {"comment":"BC = 0: the free count (D = 0)"},
        "1615": {"synopsis":"Reads the FAT entry of cluster DE and counts it in BC when it is 0."},
        "1616": {"comment":"DE = FAT[DE]"},
        "1619": {"comment":"Free cluster?"},
        "1623": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "1624": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next cluster until the limit, then builds the results."},
        "1625": {"comment":"Next cluster"},
        "1626": {"comment":"HL = the limit, the record on the stack"},
        "1627": {"comment":"Limit reached?"},
        "1630": {"comment":"HL = the record again"},
        "1633": {"comment":"HL = the free clusters"},
        "1635": {"comment":"DE = the limit"},
        "1636": {"comment":"DE = the clusters in all (limit - 2)"},
        "1641": {"comment":"IX = record+8"},
        "1643": {"comment":"C = the segment in page 1, the record's"},
        "1646": {"comment":"B = 1 + the byte at record+$0A"},
        "1652": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 20 (table word at $0578): a map of the drives that exist. For drives 26 (Z)\ndown to 1 (A) it shifts a 1 into DE:HL when the drive has a unit with a segment, so drive A\nends in bit 0 and Z in bit 25.\nEntry: A = 0 (as $0505 calls it); IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; DE:HL = the drive map.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, HL'.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY.","comment":"DE:HL = 0"},
        "1656": {"comment":"Drives 26 down to 1"},
        "1658": {"synopsis":"Shifts in the bit of drive B."},
        "1659": {"comment":"The lookup's HL and DE are the alternates"},
        "1660": {"comment":"HL = the drive's unit entry"},
        "1663": {"comment":"A = its segment"},
        "1664": {"comment":"Carry when the segment is nonzero"},
        "1667": {"comment":"Shift the bit into DE:HL"},
        "1731": {"synopsis":"DISK's interrupt entry (table word at $068D). Counts down every unit's disk-change timer\n(the byte at record+9) by one, down to 2, then counts down the byte at IY-$5F; when that\nreaches 0 it goes on at $1C9F with B = 0.\nEntry: IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = the IY-$5F count.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IY, DE'; page 1.\nKeeps: C, IX."},
        "1734": {"comment":"HL = IY+$0252: 26 unit entries, 3 bytes each"},
        "1741": {"comment":"26 units"},
        "1743": {"synopsis":"Takes the next unit entry: segment, then the record's address."},
        "1745": {"comment":"No unit here?"},
        "1748": {"comment":"Page the unit's segment into page 1"},
        "1750": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "1753": {"comment":"Back to the entry's address byte"},
        "1754": {"comment":"DE = record+9, the disk-change timer"},
        "1761": {"synopsis":"Counts the unit's timer down by one while it is 3 or more."},
        "1762": {"comment":"Carry when below 3"},
        "1764": {"comment":"Minus 1 only when 3 or more"},
        "1767": {"synopsis":"Next unit; after the last, counts down IY-$5F.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "1771": {"comment":"A = the count at IY-$5F"},
        "1774": {"comment":"Already 0?"},
        "1780": {"comment":"Not 0 yet?"},
        "1781": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "1785": {"synopsis":"The special function entry of both devices (table words at $06A3 and $06BD). B selects:\n$10 writes the channel's buffer and finishes its file (DSK_SPEC_FLUSH); $F0 is EXOS 24\n(allocate segment) and $F1 EXOS 25 (free segment), passed on; any other code is error $EA.\nEntry: A = the channel number; B = the function code; IX = the channel's RAM; IY = the\ndevice's pointer; C, DE for EXOS 24/25.\nExit: A = 0, Z, or EXOS 24/25's results.\nError: NZ, A = $EA for an unknown code, or the error of the work done.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "1788": {"comment":"Keep the channel number in A'"},
        "1790": {"comment":"Code $10?"},
        "1794": {"comment":"Code $F0?"},
        "1798": {"comment":"Code $F1?"},
        "1799": {"comment":"Any other: error $EA"},
        "1802": {"comment":"EXOS 25 (free segment), the caller's registers as they are"},
        "1805": {"synopsis":"Special function $F0: EXOS 24 (allocate segment) with the caller's registers."},
        "1808": {"synopsis":"Special function $10: makes the channel current, then writes its buffer and runs function\n$0D (CHAN_COMMIT).","comment":"A = the channel number again"},
        "1809": {"comment":"Make it the current channel"},
        "1812": {"synopsis":"When Z: writes the channel's waiting bytes (CHAN_FLUSH_WR); then runs function $0D on the\ncurrent control block (the call close makes).\nEntry: F: Z to go on (NZ returns at once); IX = the channel's RAM; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "1816": {"comment":"DE = the control block"},
        "1819": {"comment":"Function $0D"},
        "1821": {"synopsis":"Runs EXDOS function A through the entry at $0505 and keeps IX.\nEntry: A = the function number; the function's own registers; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: the function's results: A = 0, Z on success.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "1823": {"synopsis":"Runs EXDOS function A, then takes IX back from the stack (pushed by the caller)."},
        "1826": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "1829": {"synopsis":"The drive-letter device's initialise entry (table word at $06BF): stores IX at IY+$6B.\nEntry: IX, IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: IY = EXDOS's base; HL = IX.\nChanges: F, HL, IY, DE'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, IX."},
        "1834": {"synopsis":"DISK's initialise entry (table word at $06A5): no channel is current any more.\nEntry: IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: IY = EXDOS's base.\nChanges: F, BC, HL, IY, DE'.\nKeeps: A, DE, IX."},
        "1839": {"synopsis":"The close and destroy entry of both devices (table words at $0693, $0695, $06AD and $06AF):\nwrites the channel's waiting bytes, runs function $0D on its file and leaves no channel\ncurrent.\nEntry: A = the channel number; IX = its RAM; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($E4 for a channel whose open did not complete).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "1845": {"synopsis":"IY+$0720 = 0: no channel's block is at IY+$0724 any more."},
        "1855": {"synopsis":"DISK's open entry (table word at $068F); create enters one byte on (table word at $0691, the\n$B7 inside LD H,$B7: OR A), so carry is 1 for open, 0 for create. When bit 0 of IY-$37 is\nset, it only allocates (word at IY+$6B) + 1 bytes of channel RAM and notes it (IY+$6B = its\npointer - 1, IY+$6D = the segment in page 1). Otherwise OPEN_CHAN_FILE.\nEntry: A = the channel number; DE = the counted file name; C = the drive number; IX; IY =\nthe device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates; page 1.","comment":"Open: carry 1"},
        "1856": {"comment":"Hides OR A at $0741: create, carry 0"},
        "1858": {"comment":"A', F' = the channel number and open/create"},
        "1862": {"comment":"Allocate-only mode?"},
        "1868": {"comment":"DE = the word at IY+$6B"},
        "1872": {"comment":"EXOS 27: allocate channel RAM"},
        "1877": {"comment":"The segment in page 1: the RAM's"},
        "1883": {"synopsis":"IY+$6B = IX.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "1893": {"synopsis":"The drive-letter device's open entry (table word at $06A9); create enters one byte on\n($06AB, the $B7 of LD H,$B7: OR A). The drive comes from the device's name: C = the letter\nat IY+8\n- $40. With bit 0 of IY-$37 set it does nothing (A = 0); otherwise OPEN_CHAN_FILE.\nEntry: A = the channel number; DE = the counted file name; IX; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z, or A = 0 and NZ when bit 0 of IY-$37 is set.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Open: carry 1"},
        "1894": {"comment":"Hides OR A at $0767: create, carry 0"},
        "1896": {"comment":"A', F' = the channel number and open/create"},
        "1897": {"comment":"The device name's letter"},
        "1900": {"comment":"C = the drive number (A = 1)"},
        "1907": {"comment":"Allocate-only mode: nothing to open?"},
        "1912": {"synopsis":"Opens or creates the file named by DE on channel A, drive C.\n1. EXOS 27 allocates $0134 bytes of channel RAM: the 256-byte buffer at IX-$0134, the\n   control block's copy at IX-$34, the counts at IX-4..IX-2 and the open mark at IX-1.\n2. The channel is made current and the name's end is marked with a 0.\n3. Function 1 takes the path apart into the block at IY+$06A1 (drive at IY+$06A8); a\n   nonzero C back is error $A8 (Invalid pathname string).\n4. Create runs function 6; open runs function 4, after putting \"START\" (or \"EXDOS.INI\"\n   when bit 4 of IY-$37 is set) into the block when B comes back with bits 3 and 4 clear.\n5. An open file whose attribute byte (control block +$13) has bit 2 set is error $A1\n   (Invalid file attributes), unless bit 5 of IY-$37 is set.\n6. Function $0C, then the open mark becomes $FF."},
        "1913": {"comment":"The size of the channel RAM"},
        "1916": {"comment":"EXOS 27: allocate channel RAM"},
        "1919": {"comment":"A = the channel number from A'"},
        "1924": {"comment":"Make the new channel current"},
        "1927": {"comment":"HL = the counted name"},
        "1931": {"comment":"HL = the name's first character"},
        "1933": {"comment":"HL = the name's end"},
        "1934": {"comment":"End the name with a 0"},
        "1935": {"comment":"Default-drive mode?"},
        "1941": {"comment":"Then the drive at IY-$56"},
        "1944": {"synopsis":"Sets up the path block and runs function 1 on the name."},
        "1947": {"comment":"HL = IY+$06A8"},
        "1951": {"comment":"The drive"},
        "1954": {"comment":"IY+$06A7 = 0"},
        "1959": {"comment":"IY+$06A1 = $FF"},
        "1961": {"comment":"DE = IY+$06A1, the path block"},
        "1962": {"comment":"HL = the name's first character"},
        "1964": {"comment":"Function 1: take the path apart"},
        "1971": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1972": {"comment":"C nonzero?"},
        "1973": {"comment":"Then error $A8: Invalid pathname string"},
        "1978": {"comment":"A = the channel, F: carry for open"},
        "1979": {"comment":"Function 6: create"},
        "1981": {"comment":"Create?"},
        "1983": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 of B both clear?"},
        "1988": {"comment":"EXDOS.INI wanted?"},
        "1992": {"comment":"\"EXDOS   INI\""},
        "1997": {"comment":"\"START\""},
        "2000": {"synopsis":"Copies the 11-byte default name to the path block +8.","comment":"DE = the path block +8"},
        "2010": {"synopsis":"A = 4: function 4, the open."},
        "2012": {"synopsis":"Runs function A (4 or 6) with the control block, the path block and the name, then checks\nthe attribute.","comment":"DE = the control block"},
        "2015": {"comment":"BC = the control block too"},
        "2017": {"comment":"DE = the path block"},
        "2018": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "2019": {"comment":"Function 4 (open) or 6 (create)"},
        "2022": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "2023": {"comment":"Attributes left unchecked?"},
        "2029": {"comment":"HL = the control block +$13: the attribute byte"},
        "2033": {"comment":"Attribute bit 2 set?"},
        "2035": {"comment":"Then error $A1: Invalid file attributes"},
        "2038": {"synopsis":"Function $0C, then marks the channel open.","comment":"HL = the path block"},
        "2039": {"comment":"DE = the control block"},
        "2041": {"comment":"Function $0C"},
        "2046": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "2047": {"comment":"Open mark: $FF"},
        "2051": {"synopsis":"DE = IY+$0724: the current channel's control block.\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: DE = IY+$0724.\nChanges: F, DE.\nKeeps: A, BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2061": {"synopsis":"HL = IX-$0134: the start of the channel's 256-byte buffer.\nEntry: IX = the channel's RAM.\nExit: HL = the buffer; BC = $FECC.\nChanges: F, BC, HL.\nKeeps: A, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2063": {"synopsis":"HL = IX-$0134 + C: byte C of the channel's buffer.\nEntry: C = the index; IX = the channel's RAM.\nExit: HL = the byte's address; BC = $FECC.\nChanges: F, BC, HL.\nKeeps: A, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2074": {"synopsis":"DE = IY+$074C, the current file's 4-byte position; HL = IY+$073B, its 4-byte length (both in\nthe control block at IY+$0724).\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: DE = the position; HL = the length.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, IX, IY."},
        "2087": {"synopsis":"Gives back the bytes read ahead and not taken: the count at IX-2 is subtracted from the\nfile's position at IY+$074C (a borrow goes into its high word) and set to 0.\nEntry: IX = the channel's RAM; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0; IX-2 = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"A = the bytes read ahead"},
        "2091": {"comment":"None?"},
        "2092": {"comment":"DE = the position"},
        "2096": {"comment":"HL = its low word"},
        "2100": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "2102": {"comment":"None read ahead from now on"},
        "2106": {"comment":"Low word minus the count"},
        "2112": {"comment":"No borrow?"},
        "2113": {"comment":"The high word"},
        "2118": {"comment":"Borrow from it"},
        "2123": {"synopsis":"Writes the bytes waiting in the channel's buffer to its file: the count at IX-4 (0: none)\ngoes to function $10 with the buffer at IX-$0134 and the control block at IY+$0724.\nEntry: IX = the channel's RAM; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z (also when nothing was waiting).\nError: NZ, A = the error of function $10.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"A = the bytes waiting"},
        "2126": {"comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "2128": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "2131": {"synopsis":"Writes BC bytes from the channel's buffer: DE = the control block, the waiting count\ncleared, then function $10 with IX = the buffer (the channel's IX kept on the stack)."},
        "2135": {"comment":"No bytes waiting from now on"},
        "2139": {"comment":"HL = the channel's buffer"},
        "2143": {"comment":"IX = the buffer, the channel's IX on the stack"},
        "2146": {"comment":"Function $10: write bytes"},
        "2151": {"synopsis":"The read character entry of both devices (table words at $0697 and $06B1). Takes the next\nbyte of the channel's buffer; an empty buffer is filled first: the waiting writes go out,\nthen function $0F reads up to 256 bytes into it.\nEntry: A = the channel number; IX = its RAM; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z; B = the byte.\nError: NZ, A = the error code; A = $E4 (with Z) when nothing was left to read.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, all alternates.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Keep the channel number in A'"},
        "2152": {"comment":"Bytes left in the buffer?"},
        "2159": {"comment":"Make the channel current"},
        "2162": {"comment":"Write the waiting bytes first"},
        "2166": {"comment":"DE = the control block"},
        "2169": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "2173": {"comment":"IX = the buffer, the channel's IX on the stack"},
        "2175": {"comment":"Up to 256 bytes"},
        "2178": {"comment":"Function $0F: read bytes"},
        "2185": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "2187": {"comment":"Read in part ($E4)?"},
        "2190": {"synopsis":"Starts on a freshly filled buffer: BC = the bytes read."},
        "2191": {"comment":"Nothing read?"},
        "2192": {"comment":"Error $E4"},
        "2195": {"comment":"Index 0"},
        "2199": {"comment":"A = the count (0 for 256)"},
        "2200": {"synopsis":"Takes the byte at the buffer's index and counts it.","comment":"One byte fewer left"},
        "2204": {"comment":"C = the index"},
        "2210": {"comment":"B = the byte"},
        "2211": {"comment":"Next index"},
        "2216": {"synopsis":"The write character entry of both devices (table words at $069B and $06B5). Gives back any\nbytes read ahead, puts B into the channel's buffer, and writes the buffer when it holds 256.\nEntry: A = the channel number; B = the byte; IX = its RAM; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Make the channel current"},
        "2221": {"comment":"Give back the bytes read ahead"},
        "2224": {"comment":"C = the bytes waiting: the index"},
        "2231": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "2233": {"comment":"One more waiting"},
        "2236": {"comment":"Fewer than 256?"},
        "2237": {"comment":"Write all 256"},
        "2243": {"synopsis":"The read block entry of both devices (table words at $0699 and $06B3): DSK_BLOCK with\nfunction $0F (read bytes).\nEntry: A = the channel number; BC = the byte count; DE = the address; IX = its RAM; IY = the\ndevice's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z, or $E4 when the file ended first; BC = the bytes not read; DE = the address\nafter the last byte; IX = the caller's DE.\nError: NZ, A = the error code; BC = the count, DE = the address.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"Function $0F: read bytes"},
        "2247": {"synopsis":"The write block entry of both devices (table words at $069D and $06B7): DSK_BLOCK with\nfunction $10 (write bytes).\nEntry: A = the channel number; BC = the byte count; DE = the address; IX = its RAM; IY = the\ndevice's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z; BC = the bytes not written; DE = the address after the last byte; IX = the\ncaller's DE.\nError: NZ, A = the error code; BC = the count, DE = the address.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"Function $10: write bytes"},
        "2249": {"synopsis":"Moves a block through function H ($0F read, $10 write): makes the channel current, writes\nthe waiting bytes, gives back the bytes read ahead, then calls the function with IX = the\ncaller's address, BC = the count and DE = the control block. Its count done becomes the\ncount not done.","comment":"The function number on the stack"},
        "2250": {"comment":"Make the channel current"},
        "2253": {"comment":"Keep the caller's BC, DE, HL in the alternates"},
        "2254": {"comment":"Write the waiting bytes"},
        "2257": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "2259": {"comment":"Give back the bytes read ahead"},
        "2262": {"comment":"The caller's registers back"},
        "2263": {"comment":"IX = the caller's address"},
        "2266": {"comment":"DE = the control block"},
        "2269": {"comment":"A = the function"},
        "2270": {"comment":"The address on the stack"},
        "2272": {"comment":"Count the call at IY-$80"},
        "2275": {"comment":"The count on the stack"},
        "2276": {"comment":"Run the function: BC = the bytes moved"},
        "2279": {"comment":"HL = the count asked for"},
        "2280": {"comment":"All moved?"},
        "2282": {"comment":"Moved in part ($E4)?"},
        "2286": {"comment":"DE = the address: nothing moved"},
        "2289": {"synopsis":"BC = the bytes not moved, DE = the address after the last, IX = the caller's address.","comment":"HL = the bytes not moved"},
        "2291": {"comment":"IX = the caller's address, the function's IX on the stack"},
        "2293": {"comment":"DE = the address after the last byte"},
        "2294": {"synopsis":"BC = HL."},
        "2297": {"synopsis":"The waiting writes failed: drops the function number, the caller's registers back."},
        "2298": {"comment":"The caller's BC, DE, HL"},
        "2300": {"synopsis":"The read status entry of both devices (table words at $069F and $06B9): C = 0 when a byte\ncan be read (bytes left in the buffer, or the position below the length), $FF at the end of\nthe file.\nEntry: A = the channel number; IX = its RAM; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0; C = 0 or $FF.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, all alternates.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Keep the channel number in A'"},
        "2301": {"comment":"Bytes left in the buffer?"},
        "2305": {"comment":"Then readable"},
        "2309": {"comment":"Make the channel current"},
        "2312": {"comment":"Write the waiting bytes"},
        "2316": {"comment":"DE = the position, HL = the length"},
        "2319": {"comment":"Their high bytes"},
        "2325": {"comment":"4 bytes, high byte first"},
        "2327": {"synopsis":"Compares the position with the length, high byte first."},
        "2328": {"comment":"Bytes differ?"},
        "2335": {"synopsis":"C = 0 when carry (readable), else $FF (end of file).","comment":"A = 0 without touching carry"},
        "2338": {"comment":"Position below the length?"},
        "2339": {"comment":"C = $FF: end of file"},
        "2341": {"synopsis":"The set status entry of both devices (table words at $06A1 and $06BB). DE points at the\ncaller's 16-byte status block (paged into page 1 through the caller's page map at $BFFC):\nwith bit 0 of C set its first 4 bytes become the file's position, else the position is\nwritten there. Then bytes 4-7 get the file's length and 8-15 are cleared.\nEntry: A = the channel number; C = the flags; DE = the block; IX = its RAM; IY = the\ndevice's pointer.\nExit: A = 0; C = 3.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'; page 1.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Make the channel current"},
        "2344": {"comment":"Keep the caller's BC, DE, HL in the alternates"},
        "2345": {"comment":"Write the waiting bytes"},
        "2349": {"comment":"Give back the bytes read ahead"},
        "2352": {"comment":"The caller's registers back"},
        "2353": {"comment":"The caller's page map at $BFFC"},
        "2355": {"comment":"A = DE's segment, DE = its page-1 address"},
        "2358": {"comment":"Page the block in"},
        "2360": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "2362": {"comment":"DE = the position, HL = the length"},
        "2365": {"comment":"HL = the block, the length's address on the stack"},
        "2366": {"comment":"Bit 0 of C set?"},
        "2369": {"comment":"No: copy the position into the block"},
        "2370": {"synopsis":"Copies the 4 bytes of the position one way or the other."},
        "2375": {"comment":"Position read?"},
        "2377": {"comment":"DE = the block +4"},
        "2378": {"synopsis":"Bytes 4-7 = the file's length, 8-15 = 0, C = 3.","comment":"HL = the length"},
        "2381": {"comment":"Copy it into the block"},
        "2386": {"comment":"Clear 8 bytes: one, then 7 more"},
        "2395": {"synopsis":"CHAN_SELECT for a device entry: IY to EXDOS's base first. Also the buffer-moved entry of\nboth devices (table words at $06A7 and $06C1): noting the channel's place again is all a\nmove needs. ($06A7 is the drive-letter device's interrupt word too, which a device without\ninterrupts never has called.)\nEntry: A = the channel number; IX = its RAM; IY = the device's pointer.\nExit: A = 0, Z when the channel's open was completed.\nError: A = $E4, NZ, for a channel whose open did not complete.\nChanges: AF, IY, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2398": {"synopsis":"Makes channel A the current one. The current channel's 48-byte control block is worked on at\nIY+$0724; IY+$0720 holds that channel's number (0: none), IY+$0721 the segment and IY+$0722\nthe address of the channel's own copy (at IX-$34 in its RAM). For a new channel the old\none's block is copied back into its RAM (its segment paged into page 1 for the copy) and the\nnew one's copied in. Then the copy's place is noted again, which also serves after the\nchannel's RAM has moved. Works in the alternate set, so BC, DE and HL are kept.\nEntry: A = the channel number; IX = its RAM; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z when the channel's open was completed (the byte at IX-1 is $FF).\nError: A = $E4, NZ, for a channel whose open did not complete.\nChanges: AF, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2402": {"comment":"DE' = IX-$34: the channel's copy of its block"},
        "2410": {"comment":"HL' = IY+$0720: the current channel's number"},
        "2414": {"comment":"Note the new channel"},
        "2418": {"comment":"Already the current one?"},
        "2422": {"comment":"48 bytes"},
        "2425": {"comment":"No channel was current?"},
        "2428": {"comment":"Keep page 1's segment"},
        "2431": {"comment":"Page in the old channel's segment"},
        "2436": {"comment":"DE = the old channel's copy"},
        "2441": {"comment":"Copy the block back from IY+$0724"},
        "2446": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "2450": {"synopsis":"Copies the new channel's block from its RAM to IY+$0724.","comment":"HL = IY+$0724"},
        "2455": {"comment":"Copy the channel's block in"},
        "2459": {"synopsis":"Notes where the current channel's copy lives (segment, address), then tests the open mark.","comment":"The segment in page 1: the channel RAM's"},
        "2463": {"comment":"And the copy's address"},
        "2467": {"comment":"The open mark: $FF once the open completed"},
        "2471": {"comment":"Open completed?"},
        "2472": {"comment":"Error $E4"},
        "2475": {"synopsis":"Moves IY from the device's own pointer to EXDOS's base: IY += the word at IY-5. Every device\nentry starts with it.\nEntry: IY = the pointer the device was entered with.\nExit: IY = EXDOS's base.\nChanges: F, IY, DE'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Work in the alternate set"},
        "2476": {"comment":"DE' = the word at IY-5"},
        "2508": {"synopsis":"Moves buffer HL to the end of the chain at IY+$22, the end used last; a buffer whose link is\nalready 0 stays.\nEntry: HL = the buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: HL = the buffer, now last.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Link 0: last already?"},
        "2516": {"comment":"DE = the next buffer"},
        "2520": {"comment":"Its link 0: it will be the last"},
        "2524": {"comment":"BC = the buffer"},
        "2529": {"comment":"HL = IY+$22: the chain's first link"},
        "2533": {"comment":"DE = the link to the buffer"},
        "2537": {"comment":"DE = the next buffer"},
        "2538": {"comment":"Take the buffer out of the chain"},
        "2542": {"comment":"DE = the last link"},
        "2545": {"synopsis":"Stores BC in the link at DE, then takes the registers back."},
        "2546": {"comment":"The link = BC"},
        "2551": {"synopsis":"DE back, return."},
        "2553": {"synopsis":"Writes buffer HL back when changed (BUF_WRITE_BACK), then moves it to the head of the chain.\nEntry: HL = the buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: HL = the buffer, now first.\nChanges: AF, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2556": {"synopsis":"Moves buffer HL to the head of the chain at IY+$22: the first buffer to be reused.\nEntry: HL = the buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: HL = the buffer, now first.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2557": {"comment":"DE = the word at IY+$22, the chain's head"},
        "2561": {"synopsis":"CALL $00F2 returns here, past its byte: unlinks buffer HL and puts it first."},
        "2562": {"comment":"Already first?"},
        "2569": {"comment":"The buffer is the head from now on"},
        "2575": {"comment":"BC = the buffer's next one"},
        "2579": {"comment":"Link it to the old head"},
        "2582": {"comment":"HL = the old head, DE = the buffer"},
        "2583": {"comment":"BC = the buffer"},
        "2585": {"comment":"DE = the link that still points to it"},
        "2588": {"comment":"BC = its next one: the link skips it"},
        "2591": {"synopsis":"Follows a chain of links (each node's first word links to the next, 0 ends it) from the link\nat HL to node BC.\nEntry: HL = the first link's address; BC = the node.\nExit: NZ, carry 0: DE = the address of the link to node BC; HL = BC.\nError: Z: BC is not in the chain; DE = the last link's address, HL = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY."},
        "2595": {"comment":"HL = the next node, DE = its link's address"},
        "2598": {"comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "2599": {"comment":"Node BC?"},
        "2606": {"synopsis":"Writes buffer HL back to its disk when it is in use (+2 nonzero) and changed (bit 7 of +3,\ncleared now). A buffer is an 11-byte header and 512 data bytes: +0 the link, +2 the unit\nkey, +3 flags, +4 the sector, +6 the number of copies, +7 the distance between copies, +8\nthe drive record's segment, +9 its address. Every copy (a FAT has one per FAT) is written by\ndriver request 5 or 6; when none could be written DISK_ERROR asks, and Z from it tries\nagain. Bit 6 of +3 writes only the one sector copies x distance further on.\nEntry: HL = the buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: bit 2 of IY+$63 is set; page 1 as it was.\nChanges: AF, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Bit 2 of IY+$63: a buffer was looked at"},
        "2613": {"comment":"Unit key 0: buffer not in use?"},
        "2618": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "2622": {"comment":"Not changed from now on"},
        "2626": {"comment":"Keep page 1's segment"},
        "2631": {"synopsis":"Takes the sector and the copies from the header."},
        "2632": {"comment":"Only the one copy further on?"},
        "2635": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "2639": {"comment":"B = the number of copies"},
        "2644": {"synopsis":"Adds the distance between copies B times.","comment":"Add the distance (+7)"},
        "2648": {"synopsis":"Next copy; at the end one sector is written."},
        "2651": {"comment":"Write one copy"},
        "2653": {"synopsis":"Pages in the drive's record and points IX at the data."},
        "2655": {"comment":"The record's segment"},
        "2656": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "2659": {"comment":"DE = the record's address"},
        "2664": {"comment":"The data's address in page 1"},
        "2669": {"comment":"IX = the data"},
        "2671": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "2672": {"comment":"C = 1: no copy written yet"},
        "2674": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "2675": {"synopsis":"Writes one copy: driver request 5 or 6 for one sector ($01FF)."},
        "2677": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "2680": {"comment":"A = the write request"},
        "2683": {"comment":"Write sector DE from IX"},
        "2688": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "2690": {"comment":"One more copy written"},
        "2691": {"synopsis":"Error $BF ends the copies at once.","comment":"Error $BF?"},
        "2695": {"comment":"Then stop: last copy, none written"},
        "2698": {"synopsis":"Steps DE to the next copy."},
        "2699": {"comment":"The distance between copies (header +7)"},
        "2707": {"synopsis":"After the last copy: done when one was written, else DISK_ERROR (carry set unless bit 1 of\nthe flags is set)."},
        "2708": {"comment":"Next copy"},
        "2710": {"comment":"At least one copy written?"},
        "2713": {"comment":"Header flag 1 present?"},
        "2719": {"comment":"Carry for DISK_ERROR (IY+$2A = $FF)"},
        "2720": {"synopsis":"Reports the failed write (DISK_ERROR); Z comes back to try again."},
        "2723": {"synopsis":"The end of a buffer write (the flush that starts at $0A2E): after the error prompt, Z\n(Retry) writes the buffer again from $0A47; otherwise, and after a write that worked, puts\npage 1's segment and the caller's registers back.","comment":"HL = the buffer's flags byte (+3)"},
        "2724": {"comment":"Retry: write it again"},
        "2728": {"comment":"B = page 1's segment on entry"},
        "2730": {"comment":"Back in page 1"},
        "2734": {"synopsis":"Returns with the caller's HL: the buffer was free or unchanged, or the write is done.","comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "2735": {"comment":"Done"},
        "2736": {"synopsis":"The driver request for a write: 5 when the byte at IY-$58 is nonzero, else 6.\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 5 or 6.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The byte at IY-$58 set?"},
        "2740": {"comment":"Request 5"},
        "2743": {"comment":"Request 6"},
        "2745": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 30: with B = $FF gets a buffer for sector A x $101 tagged $80 (a scratch\nbuffer, read in when bit 0 of A is set) and returns its data's address; with any other B\ngets it and frees it (tag 0). The drive record GET_SECTOR_BUF reads is the code at $0AC9,\nso its fields are this code's bytes (+8 = $80, the tag).\nEntry: A = the sector byte (also the flags); B = $FF to keep the buffer; IY = the\nworkspace.\nExit: A = 0; with B = $FF, HL = the buffer's data (+$0B) and Z; else HL = the buffer's\ntag, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "2746": {"comment":"IX = $0AC9: a record made of code bytes"},
        "2750": {"comment":"DE = A x $101: the sector"},
        "2752": {"comment":"B = the flags"},
        "2753": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "2757": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "2758": {"comment":"B = $FF? Keep it"},
        "2761": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's tag"},
        "2763": {"comment":"Free it"},
        "2765": {"synopsis":"The end of $0AB9 when B was $FF: returns HL = the buffer's data, 11 bytes past its header.","comment":"BC = $000B (B is 0 here)"},
        "2767": {"comment":"HL = the data"},
        "2769": {"comment":"Data: $80, read as IX+8 when $0AB9 sets IX = $CAC9"},
        "2770": {"synopsis":"Gets FAT sector DE of the drive whose record is at IX into a buffer and returns it. The\nnumber of FAT copies to try goes to IY+$68: the byte at record+$0E, one fewer when bit 0 of\nrecord+$18 is set (at least 1). The code from $0AE0 (shared, A = 1 there) looks for a buffer\nthat holds the sector (the one used last, IY+$24, first), else reuses the head of the chain\n(or the one after it when the head's +2 has bit 7 set), writes that back and reads the\nsector in, trying copy after copy.\nEntry: DE = the sector; IX = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL = the buffer (its data from HL+$0B).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, all alternates.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY.","comment":"B = 1: read the sector in"},
        "2772": {"comment":"A = the number of FATs"},
        "2775": {"comment":"One copy fewer for this drive?"},
        "2781": {"comment":"Then one fewer"},
        "2784": {"synopsis":"Finds or loads a sector into a buffer with one sector (IY+$68 = 1); $0AE2 continues.\n1. The tag is the record's +8 (C): the most recent buffer (IY+$24) or one in the list at\n   IY+$22 that holds the same tag and sector is used as it is.\n2. Otherwise the first buffer of the list (the second when the first is a scratch one,\n   tag bit 7) is written back if changed and filled in: +2 the tag, +3 bit 1 of B, +4/+5\n   the sector, +6 the count, +7 the record's +$11, +8 page 1's segment.\n3. With bit 0 of B set the sector is read through the driver (function 4); a failed read\n   goes to the error handler ($0ED5), which retries, goes on or abandons the call.\n4. The buffer becomes the most recent one (IY+$24).\nEntry: IX = the drive's record; DE = the sector; B = the flags (bit 0: read it); IY = the\nworkspace.\nExit: HL = the buffer; A = 0, Z.\nError: a failed read reaches the error handler, which may abandon the EXDOS call.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE.","comment":"One sector"},
        "2786": {"synopsis":"Finds the buffer for sector DE of the drive whose parameter block is IX, reading the sector\nin when no buffer holds it.\n1. The buffer used last (IY+$24) is tried first; a match returns at once.\n2. Otherwise the chain from IY+$22 is searched (BUF_SEARCH_LOOP); a buffer found there\n   becomes the last used and moves to the chain's end ($09CC).\n3. Otherwise the chain's first buffer is taken (the second when the first is kept aside, bit\n   7 of its drive) and filled for this sector (BUF_CLAIM), which writes it out first if\n   changed.\nEntry: A = the number of copies (IY+$68), B = flags (bit 0 read the sector in, bit 1 Ignore\nallowed in the prompt), DE = the sector, IX = the drive's parameter block.\nExit: HL = the buffer header (data at HL+$0B), A = 0 and Z.","comment":"Copies of this sector (FAT copies)"},
        "2789": {"comment":"C = the drive's number (parameter block +8)"},
        "2792": {"comment":"HL = the buffer used last"},
        "2799": {"comment":"None yet (H = 0)? Then carry skips the test"},
        "2804": {"comment":"It holds the sector: done"},
        "2805": {"comment":"HL = the chain's first buffer"},
        "2812": {"synopsis":"Walks the buffer chain for the sector; the chain's head is on the stack. A match goes to\n$0B7F with HL = the buffer; the end of the chain picks a buffer to reuse."},
        "2815": {"comment":"Found: $0B7F drops the head and keeps HL"},
        "2817": {"comment":"HL = the next buffer"},
        "2821": {"comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "2824": {"comment":"HL = the chain's first buffer"},
        "2827": {"comment":"Is it kept aside (bit 7 of its drive)?"},
        "2830": {"comment":"A = the link's high byte"},
        "2832": {"comment":"No: reuse the first buffer"},
        "2834": {"comment":"Yes: reuse the second one"},
        "2836": {"synopsis":"Fills buffer HL's header for sector DE (the layout is at the top of this file) after writing\nout what it held ($0A2E). Bit 0 of B clear: returns at once (the caller fills the data);\nelse the sector is read in (BUF_READ_SECTOR).","comment":"Writes the buffer out if it was changed"},
        "2839": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer"},
        "2842": {"comment":"+2 = the drive"},
        "2845": {"comment":"+3 = flags: only Ignore allowed (bit 1) is kept"},
        "2849": {"comment":"+4/+5 = the sector"},
        "2853": {"comment":"+6 = the number of copies"},
        "2858": {"comment":"+7 = sectors between copies (parameter block +$11)"},
        "2863": {"comment":"+8 = the segment in page 1, which holds the buffer"},
        "2867": {"comment":"HL = the data (+$0B)"},
        "2871": {"comment":"IX = the data; the parameter block goes on the stack"},
        "2873": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "2874": {"comment":"+9/+10 = the parameter block"},
        "2880": {"comment":"IX = the data seen through page 1 ($C000 = minus $4000)"},
        "2886": {"comment":"Read the sector in?"},
        "2888": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "2890": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector into the buffer: tries each copy in turn (B = the number of copies).","comment":"Keeps the flags and the drive"},
        "2892": {"comment":"B = copies to try"},
        "2897": {"synopsis":"The next copy: C sectors further on.","comment":"E + C: the same sector in the next copy"},
        "2900": {"comment":"No carry into D?"},
        "2903": {"synopsis":"Reads one copy: the disk call at $0C1E with A = 4 (read) and BC = $01FF."},
        "2905": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "2908": {"comment":"Read"},
        "2915": {"comment":"Read: $0B79 drops the saved registers and goes on"},
        "2917": {"comment":"Error $BF?"},
        "2919": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the prompt"},
        "2921": {"comment":"Try the next copy"},
        "2923": {"synopsis":"Every copy failed: asks the user (error prompt at $0ED5), offering Ignore only when bit 1\nof the flags is set."},
        "2925": {"comment":"No carry: Ignore is offered"},
        "2926": {"comment":"Ignore allowed?"},
        "2930": {"comment":"No: carry takes Ignore out of the prompt"},
        "2931": {"synopsis":"Shows the error prompt for error A: Retry reads again; Ignore goes on with the buffer as it\nis. Abort does not come back.","comment":"Error prompt: Z = Retry, NZ = Ignore"},
        "2934": {"comment":"Retry"},
        "2936": {"comment":"Never taken (Z tested above): hides POP DE/POP BC ($0B79)"},
        "2939": {"synopsis":"The buffer is ready: puts the drive's parameter block back in IX, makes the buffer the last\nused (IY+$24), sets bit 2 of IY+$63 and moves the buffer to the end of the chain ($09CC).\nBUF_GET_SECTOR enters at $0B7F, inside CP $C1, to drop the chain's head instead.\nExit: HL = the buffer header, A = 0 and Z.","comment":"HL = the buffer; the parameter block comes off the stack"},
        "2940": {"comment":"IX = the drive's parameter block"},
        "2942": {"comment":"Its result is not used: the byte $C1 is POP BC, entry $0B7F"},
        "2948": {"comment":"The buffer used last"},
        "2954": {"comment":"Moves it to the end of the chain (most recent last)"},
        "2957": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "2959": {"synopsis":"Marks the buffer used last (IY+$24) as changed (bit 7 of its flags), so it is written out\nbefore reuse.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: HL = the buffer's flags byte (+3).\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"HL = the buffer used last"},
        "2965": {"comment":"HL+3 = its flags"},
        "2968": {"comment":"Changed"},
        "2971": {"synopsis":"Does buffer HL hold sector DE of drive C?\nEntry: HL = a buffer header, C = the drive, DE = the sector.\nExit: Z = it does.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2972": {"comment":"HL+2 = the buffer's drive"},
        "2975": {"comment":"Same drive?"},
        "2978": {"comment":"HL+4 = the sector, low byte first"},
        "2981": {"comment":"Same low byte?"},
        "2986": {"comment":"Same high byte?"},
        "2987": {"synopsis":"BUF_MATCH's exit: puts the buffer's address back in HL.","comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "2988": {"comment":"Z = a match"},
        "2989": {"synopsis":"Writes out every changed buffer of a drive. Entered here, the drive is that of the parameter\nblock HL (+8); entered at $0BAE (the SCF inside OR $37) it is A, $FF for every drive.\nBUF_MARK_DRIVE marks the drive's buffers, then each marked one is written out ($0A2E).\nEntry: HL = a parameter block, or A = the drive with entry at $0BAE.\nExit: Z.\nChanges: AF, DE', L' (the last two only when the error prompt writes a number).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY (the disk call at $0470 restores IY and the alternates).","comment":"Clears carry: the drive comes from HL; its $37 is SCF ($0BAE)"},
        "2991": {"comment":"Marks the drive's buffers"},
        "2995": {"synopsis":"Writes out each marked buffer until none is left.","comment":"Next marked buffer (its mark is cleared)"},
        "2998": {"comment":"None left: done"},
        "3000": {"comment":"Writes it out if changed"},
        "3005": {"synopsis":"Drops a drive's buffers: marks them (BUF_MARK_DRIVE), then unlinks each marked buffer\nthrough $09FC and frees it (tag 0). Entered here the tag is the record's +8 (HL); entered\nat $0BBE (SCF) it is A.\nEntry: HL = the drive's record, or A = the tag at $0BBE; IY = the workspace.\nExit: Z; HL kept.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL.","comment":"Carry clear: the tag from the record; $0BBE: SCF"},
        "3007": {"comment":"Mark the drive's buffers"},
        "3011": {"synopsis":"The loop of $0BBD (and of $0BBE, the SCF inside its OR $37): frees each marked buffer\nwithout writing it: moves it to the chain's head ($09FC) and sets its drive to 0.","comment":"Next marked buffer"},
        "3014": {"comment":"None left: done"},
        "3016": {"comment":"Moves it to the head of the chain"},
        "3019": {"comment":"HL+2 = its drive"},
        "3021": {"comment":"0: the buffer is free"},
        "3025": {"synopsis":"Marks the buffers of one drive: bit 0 of each buffer's flags (+3) is set when its tag (+2)\nis the drive's, and cleared otherwise. Tag $FF marks every buffer in use whose tag is\nbelow $80; free buffers (tag 0) are never marked.\nEntry: carry set: A = the tag; carry clear: HL = the drive's record (the tag at +8); IY =\nthe workspace.\nExit: A = 0; Z, carry clear.\nError: none.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Tag given in A?"},
        "3027": {"synopsis":"Marks the buffers of the drive whose parameter block is HL: A = its drive number (+8), then\nBUF_MARK_DRIVE.\nEntry: HL = a parameter block.\nExit: Z; bit 0 of each buffer's flags set for the drive's buffers, clear for the others.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3029": {"comment":"HL+8 = the drive's number"},
        "3036": {"synopsis":"Marks (bit 0 of the flags) every buffer of drive A and clears the mark on all others; A =\n$FF marks the buffers of every drive except those kept aside (bit 7 of the drive).\nEntry: A = the drive, or $FF.\nExit: Z.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3039": {"comment":"B = the drive to mark"},
        "3040": {"comment":"HL = the chain's first buffer"},
        "3046": {"synopsis":"One buffer of the walk: DE = the next one; clears its mark and sets it again if it belongs\nto the drive.","comment":"DE = the next buffer"},
        "3050": {"comment":"A = this buffer's drive"},
        "3052": {"comment":"Not marked"},
        "3054": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "3057": {"comment":"The drive asked for?"},
        "3060": {"comment":"Kept aside (bit 7)?"},
        "3063": {"comment":"Every drive ($FF) asked for?"},
        "3067": {"synopsis":"Marks this buffer.","comment":"Mark"},
        "3069": {"synopsis":"Goes on with the next buffer until the chain ends, then returns with the caller's BC, DE and\nHL.","comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "3071": {"comment":"HL = the next buffer"},
        "3076": {"synopsis":"Returns with the caller's HL (the flush, free and mark walks end here).","comment":"HL = the caller's HL"},
        "3077": {"comment":"Z"},
        "3078": {"synopsis":"Finds the first buffer of the chain whose mark (bit 0 of the flags) is set, and clears it.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: NZ and HL = that buffer; Z when none is marked.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"HL = the chain's first buffer"},
        "3084": {"synopsis":"Tests and clears one buffer's mark; else goes on along the chain."},
        "3085": {"comment":"HL+3 = the flags"},
        "3088": {"comment":"Marked?"},
        "3093": {"comment":"Yes: NZ, HL = the buffer"},
        "3094": {"comment":"HL = the next buffer"},
        "3098": {"comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "3101": {"comment":"Z: none marked"},
        "3102": {"synopsis":"Runs driver request A on unit HL ($0470) after UNIT_CHECK_DISK; the code from $0C24 then\nsets the disk-change timer (record+9) to 100 and returns the driver's status.\nEntry: A = the request; HL = the drive's record; the request's registers (BC, DE, IX);\nIY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = the status, Z when 0; carry 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: IY."},
        "3105": {"comment":"The unit's driver"},
        "3108": {"synopsis":"Sets byte +9 of the parameter block HL to 100 ($64) and returns A unchanged with carry\nclear. Below 3 that byte makes the next access check the disk ($0C30).\nEntry: HL = a parameter block, A = the result to return.\nExit: carry clear.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3109": {"comment":"IX = the parameter block (IX kept on the stack)"},
        "3111": {"comment":"+9 = 100"},
        "3115": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3118": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "3120": {"synopsis":"Makes sure the disk in unit HL is the one its record describes, before a driver request. A\ntimer (record+9) above 2 means the disk was used lately, and nothing is checked; at 2 the\ndriver is asked (UNIT_CHANGED). Otherwise the disk's identity is read ($0C69) and compared\nwith the record ($0C7F); while it differs, error $B3 (Wrong disk) is reported and asked\nagain.\nEntry: HL = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: the right disk is in the unit.\nChanges: HL, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, IY."},
        "3123": {"comment":"HL = record+9: the disk-change timer"},
        "3127": {"comment":"Above 2: used lately?"},
        "3134": {"comment":"At 2: ask the driver"},
        "3137": {"comment":"Not changed?"},
        "3141": {"synopsis":"Loop: asks for the drive's disk (error $B3) until the check at $0C7F finds it in."},
        "3156": {"synopsis":"The right disk is in: restores IX, then falls into the common exit."},
        "3158": {"synopsis":"Restores BC, then falls into the common exit."},
        "3159": {"synopsis":"The common exit: restores DE and AF."},
        "3162": {"synopsis":"Asks the driver of unit HL (request 2) whether its disk was changed. B = 1 back: Z (not\nchanged); B = 0: decided by the byte at IY-$54 (Z when it is $FF, carry set); any other B:\nNZ.\nEntry: HL = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: Z: the disk is the same one; NZ: it may have changed.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Request 2"},
        "3167": {"comment":"Answer 1?"},
        "3169": {"comment":"Answer other than 0?"},
        "3171": {"comment":"0: the byte at IY-$54 decides"},
        "3177": {"synopsis":"Reads the drive's boot sector: the disk call at $0465 with A = 3, which fills the buffer at\nIY-$3B5F. A failure asks the user (error prompt without Ignore) and reads again; Abort does\nnot come back.\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block, IY.\nExit: IX = the boot sector (IY-$3B5F plus $4000, IY+$04A1).\nChanges: AF, IX, DE', L' (the last two only when the error prompt writes a number).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IY (the disk call at $0470 saves and restores HL, IY and the alternates).","comment":"Keeps BC, DE for the exit"},
        "3179": {"synopsis":"One read; on an error the prompt, then again.","comment":"Disk call 3: read the boot sector"},
        "3184": {"comment":"Read"},
        "3186": {"comment":"Error prompt (no Ignore): returns only for Retry"},
        "3191": {"synopsis":"The read worked: moves IX $4000 up to the buffer's address in the page it is used from.","comment":"IX + $4000"},
        "3196": {"comment":"The caller's DE, BC"},
        "3199": {"synopsis":"Is the disk in the drive the one parameter block HL describes? Compares the boot sector's\n4-byte volume serial (DSK_VOL_SERIAL) with the block's +$19-$1C, then boot sector byte $15\nwith the block's +$1D.\nEntry: HL = the parameter block, IX = the boot sector.\nExit: Z = the same disk.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "3200": {"comment":"HL = the serial (four $FF bytes when the disk has none)"},
        "3203": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "3206": {"comment":"HL = the block's serial (+$19)"},
        "3210": {"comment":"The 4 bytes match?"},
        "3213": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "3215": {"comment":"A = the block's +$1D"},
        "3216": {"comment":"Matches the boot sector's byte $15?"},
        "3219": {"synopsis":"Returns with the block's address in HL.","comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3221": {"synopsis":"Finds the boot sector's volume serial: when the 6 bytes at its +$40 are \"VOL_ID\" ($113D)\nreturns HL = its +$47 (the serial, 4 bytes); else HL = $0CB0, four $FF bytes.\nEntry: IX = the boot sector.\nExit: HL = the serial; Z when the disk has one.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY."},
        "3224": {"comment":"HL = boot sector +$40"},
        "3228": {"comment":"DE = \"VOL_ID\""},
        "3231": {"comment":"6 letters"},
        "3233": {"synopsis":"Compares the 6 letters; on a match HL skips the byte after them."},
        "3234": {"comment":"Same letter?"},
        "3235": {"comment":"No: no serial"},
        "3241": {"comment":"HL = +$47, the serial"},
        "3243": {"synopsis":"The disk has no \"VOL_ID\": HL = $0CB0, four $FF bytes taken as its serial ($0CAF, before\nthem, is 0).","comment":"HL = four $FF bytes"},
        "3252": {"synopsis":"Compares 4 bytes at DE with 4 at HL.\nEntry: DE, HL = the two.\nExit: Z = equal (DE, HL past them); NZ at the first byte that differs.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY.","comment":"4 bytes"},
        "3254": {"synopsis":"One byte of CMP4."},
        "3256": {"comment":"Different: NZ"},
        "3262": {"synopsis":"Selects drive C for a call that wants its record (B = 0): IX = IY+$06A1, then the code from\n$0CC9 (shared with $0608, which enters with B = 2) finds the drive's unit through $02D1,\nstores it at IY+$2B, pages the unit's segment into page 1 and checks the disk in it.\nEntry: C = the drive number (0 = the default drive, 1-26 = A-Z); IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, HL = the drive's record (in page 1).\nError: A = $AF (Invalid drive) with Z set when the drive has no unit; callers test A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; page 1.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"B = 0: the caller wants the record"},
        "3264": {"comment":"IX = IY+$06A1, a work block"},
        "3273": {"synopsis":"Selects drive C for an operation: maps it to its unit (kept in IY+$2B) and pages the unit's\nrecord in. The byte at IY+$234 + record +7 names the unit that last used that physical\nunit; when it is another one, that one's changed buffers are written back and the error\nhandler is called with $B1 for it. The unit then takes the physical unit over. B says\nwhat follows ($0CFD on): 2 writes back the drive's changed buffers and returns A = 0,\nHL = the record.\nEntry: C = the drive; B = the operation; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0; HL = the record (B = 2).\nError: A = $AF, Z when the drive has no unit.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"A = the drive"},
        "3274": {"comment":"HL = its unit's slot"},
        "3277": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "3278": {"comment":"Kept in IY+$2B"},
        "3281": {"comment":"A = the record's segment"},
        "3282": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "3284": {"comment":"No unit?"},
        "3285": {"comment":"Error $AF"},
        "3288": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "3293": {"comment":"Its +7: the physical unit"},
        "3300": {"comment":"HL = IY+$234 + that"},
        "3308": {"comment":"A = the unit that used it last"},
        "3309": {"comment":"This one? Go on"},
        "3312": {"comment":"None? Go on"},
        "3315": {"comment":"Write back the other one's buffers"},
        "3318": {"comment":"Code $B1 for the error handler"},
        "3320": {"comment":"HL = the record, the stacked HL kept"},
        "3321": {"comment":"Report it for that record"},
        "3325": {"synopsis":"Part of $0CC9 (log drive C in): records drive C as the one now using its unit (the table at\nIY+$234). Then B says what else to do: 1 goes on to check the disk against the caller's file\n(DRV_CHK_FILE); any other value to DRV_CHK_FLUSH.","comment":"The unit now belongs to drive C"},
        "3326": {"comment":"B = 1?"},
        "3327": {"comment":"No"},
        "3329": {"synopsis":"Checks that the disk in the drive is the one the caller's file is on: the serial kept at\nIX+$2C. The parameter block is on the stack.\n1. A block whose disk was never read (+9 = 0) reads the boot sector (DRV_CHK_FRESH).\n2. When the block's serial is not the file's, the drive's changed buffers are written out\n   first, then the boot sector is read too.\n3. Otherwise DRV_CHK_KNOWN decides from +9 whether to look at the disk at all.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "3332": {"comment":"IX+$2C = the file's disk serial"},
        "3336": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "3337": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3341": {"comment":"C = 9"},
        "3343": {"comment":"HL+9 = the block's disk state"},
        "3345": {"comment":"0: no disk read yet?"},
        "3348": {"comment":"HL = the block's serial (+$19)"},
        "3351": {"comment":"C = the state"},
        "3353": {"comment":"The file's disk?"},
        "3357": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "3359": {"comment":"A = the drive (IY+$2B)"},
        "3362": {"comment":"Writes out its changed buffers (entry $0BAE: A = the drive)"},
        "3365": {"synopsis":"Reads the boot sector and compares its serial with the file's (C = 1: a match rereads the\nlayout).","comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3366": {"comment":"IX = the boot sector"},
        "3370": {"comment":"A match rereads the layout"},
        "3374": {"synopsis":"The block describes the file's disk; its +9 (C) decides: 1 reads the boot sector to compare;\n2 asks the drive whether the disk changed ($0C5A), reading it only if so; 3 or more trusts\nthe block."},
        "3376": {"comment":"State 1?"},
        "3379": {"comment":"State 2?"},
        "3380": {"comment":"3 or more: nothing to check"},
        "3383": {"comment":"Disk changed? (disk call 2)"},
        "3387": {"comment":"Z: not changed"},
        "3389": {"synopsis":"Reads the boot sector to compare its serial; C = H, not 1 (blocks are not at $01xx), so a\nmatch keeps the layout.","comment":"IX = the boot sector"},
        "3392": {"comment":"C = H: not 1, so a match does not reread the layout"},
        "3393": {"synopsis":"Compares the boot sector's serial with the file's (DE). A match ends the check, rereading\nthe layout and freeing the drive's buffers when C = 1; another disk asks for the file's disk\n(DRV_CHK_WRONG)."},
        "3394": {"comment":"HL = the disk's serial"},
        "3398": {"comment":"The file's?"},
        "3401": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block (kept on the stack)"},
        "3403": {"comment":"No: the wrong disk"},
        "3405": {"comment":"C = 1?"},
        "3408": {"comment":"Rereads the layout from the boot sector"},
        "3411": {"comment":"Frees the drive's buffers"},
        "3414": {"synopsis":"The disk is the right one: on to the exit.","comment":"Done"},
        "3416": {"synopsis":"Error $B2 (Wrong disk for file), Ignore offered: Ignore takes the disk in the drive (layout\nreread, buffers freed); Retry checks again from DRV_CHK_FILE.","comment":"Carry clear: Ignore is offered"},
        "3417": {"comment":"Error $B2: Wrong disk for file"},
        "3419": {"comment":"Error prompt: Z = Retry"},
        "3423": {"comment":"Ignore: take this disk"},
        "3425": {"comment":"IX = the caller's"},
        "3427": {"comment":"The block back on the stack"},
        "3428": {"comment":"Retry: check again"},
        "3430": {"synopsis":"The B other than 1 path of $0CC9: writes out the drive's changed buffers. B = 2 ends there.\nOtherwise the disk is checked from the block's +9: below 2 (or a changed disk at 2) the boot\nsector is read (DRV_CHK_BOOT); above 2 the block is trusted.","comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3431": {"comment":"Writes out the drive's changed buffers"},
        "3435": {"comment":"B = 2 on entry: only that"},
        "3437": {"comment":"IX kept for the exit"},
        "3440": {"comment":"HL+9 = the disk state"},
        "3445": {"comment":"D = state - 2"},
        "3449": {"comment":"Below 2: read the boot sector"},
        "3451": {"comment":"Above 2: nothing to check"},
        "3454": {"comment":"Disk changed? (disk call 2)"},
        "3458": {"comment":"Cannot tell: read the boot sector"},
        "3460": {"comment":"Not changed: nothing to do"},
        "3462": {"synopsis":"Reads the boot sector; the layout is read again when the block's state is 0, when the disk\nis another one, or when bit 7 of its serial's last byte is set (always for a disk without\nVOL_ID); else the block is kept.","comment":"IX = the boot sector"},
        "3465": {"comment":"D = the state again"},
        "3467": {"comment":"State 0: read the layout"},
        "3469": {"comment":"The same disk?"},
        "3472": {"comment":"No: read the layout"},
        "3474": {"comment":"DE = the serial's last byte"},
        "3476": {"comment":"Serial's last byte below $80: keep the layout"},
        "3480": {"synopsis":"Reads the layout from the boot sector and frees the drive's buffers (a new disk).","comment":"Layout from the boot sector"},
        "3483": {"comment":"Frees the drive's buffers"},
        "3486": {"synopsis":"Copies the block's serial (+$19, 4 bytes) to IX+$2C, the caller's record of the disk.","comment":"DE = the caller's IX"},
        "3489": {"comment":"HL = the block's serial"},
        "3494": {"comment":"DE = IX+$2C"},
        "3498": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "3502": {"synopsis":"Ends the log-in: HL = the parameter block, IX the caller's; its +9 = 100 and A = 0\n(DRV_SET_COUNT).","comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3503": {"comment":"IX = the caller's"},
        "3505": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "3509": {"comment":"Not reached by a jump on this page: error $A2"},
        "3510": {"comment":"Error $A2 (Invalid MAPDISK)"},
        "3513": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 25: makes drive B use drive C's unit. Copies the first 8 bytes of C's record\n(the driver call: segments, IY, routine, unit number, physical unit) to IY+$6A1, writes\nback and drops drive B's buffers, copies the 8 bytes over B's record and resets it (+9 =\n0, +$1E = $FF at $0DE6).\nEntry: C = the drive to copy; B = the drive that becomes a copy; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = $A2 (Z) when either drive has no unit.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; page 1.","comment":"HL = IY+$6A1, an 8-byte store"},
        "3521": {"comment":"A = the drive to copy"},
        "3522": {"comment":"DE = its record"},
        "3525": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "3526": {"comment":"DE = the store"},
        "3527": {"comment":"Error $A2: no unit"},
        "3531": {"comment":"A = the drive to change"},
        "3532": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "3538": {"comment":"Write back its changed buffers"},
        "3541": {"comment":"Drop them"},
        "3544": {"comment":"A = the drive to change"},
        "3545": {"comment":"DE = its record"},
        "3548": {"comment":"HL = the store"},
        "3549": {"comment":"Error $A2: no unit"},
        "3553": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "3557": {"comment":"HL = the changed record"},
        "3558": {"synopsis":"Marks the parameter block HL as holding no known disk: +9 = 0 (the next access reads the\nboot sector) and +$1E = $FF.\nEntry: HL = a parameter block.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3559": {"comment":"D = 0, E = 9"},
        "3563": {"comment":"+9 = 0: disk not read"},
        "3564": {"comment":"D is still 0"},
        "3566": {"comment":"HL+$1E"},
        "3572": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 26: maps drive B to the unit of drive C (C = 0: to its own), then links\ndrive B's letter device if it does not answer (ENSURE_DRIVE_DEV). B = 0 maps every drive\nto itself.\nEntry: B = the drive (0: all); C = the drive whose unit it takes (0: its own); IY = the\nworkspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z (ENSURE_DRIVE_DEV's result when B is not 0).\nError: A = $AF, carry clear, for a drive above 26.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the drive map, IY+$2A0"},
        "3579": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "3580": {"comment":"0: map every drive to itself"},
        "3583": {"comment":"Above 26?"},
        "3585": {"comment":"Error $AF"},
        "3588": {"comment":"HL = the drive's entry"},
        "3592": {"comment":"A = the unit's drive"},
        "3593": {"comment":"0: its own"},
        "3596": {"comment":"Above 26?"},
        "3598": {"comment":"Error $AF"},
        "3601": {"comment":"B = the new unit"},
        "3602": {"synopsis":"Part of $0DF4: stores B in the drive map's entry for drive E (IY+$2A0 + E) and goes on at\n$036C with A = that drive.","comment":"The map entry"},
        "3603": {"comment":"A = the drive changed"},
        "3607": {"synopsis":"Part of $0DF4 when B = 0: resets the drive map from its entry A on: entry n = n, up to 26.\nExit: A = 0, Z.","comment":"Entry n = n"},
        "3610": {"comment":"Past the last (26)?"},
        "3614": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "3616": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function $16 (table entry at $057C): the physical unit and number of drive B. B with\nbit 7 clear goes through the drive map first ($02D1); bit 7 set takes the drive as given.\nEntry: B = the drive.\nExit: A = 0; C = the unit (parameter block +7), B = +8, D = the segment holding the block\n(now in page 1), E = the block's address low byte.\nError: A = $AF (Invalid drive) when there is no such drive.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "3617": {"comment":"Through the drive map?"},
        "3622": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "3624": {"comment":"DE = the parameter block; Z: none"},
        "3627": {"comment":"Error $AF: Invalid drive"},
        "3630": {"comment":"HL = DE + 7"},
        "3634": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "3636": {"comment":"B = the drive number"},
        "3637": {"comment":"D = page 1's segment (the block's)"},
        "3642": {"synopsis":"Reads a disk's layout from its boot sector (IX) into the parameter block HL:\n+$0A sectors per cluster - 1, +$0B its power of 2, +$0C/$0D the reserved sectors (the first\nFAT), +$0E the number of FATs, +$0F/$10 the root entries' remainder and count in sectors\n(16 to a sector), +$11 sectors per FAT, +$12/$13 the root directory's first sector, +$14/$15\nthe first data sector, +$16/$17 the number of clusters + 2, +$18-$1C boot byte $46 and the\nserial (0, $FF x 4 without VOL_ID), +$1D boot byte $15. Ends at DRV_CLEAR_1E.\nEntry: HL = the parameter block, IX = the boot sector.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "3643": {"comment":"HL+$0A"},
        "3647": {"comment":"Sectors per cluster (boot +$0D)"},
        "3650": {"comment":"As a mask"},
        "3653": {"comment":"C counts the mask's 1 bits"},
        "3655": {"synopsis":"Counts the mask's bits (the cluster size as a power of 2), then copies the reserved sectors\nand the FAT count, and starts on the root directory's size."},
        "3657": {"comment":"Another 1 bit?"},
        "3659": {"comment":"+$0B = cluster size as a shift"},
        "3661": {"comment":"Reserved sectors (boot +$0E)"},
        "3671": {"comment":"Kept: the first FAT's sector"},
        "3672": {"comment":"The number of FATs (boot +$10)"},
        "3677": {"comment":"DE = root directory entries (boot +$11)"},
        "3684": {"comment":"Entries over whole sectors"},
        "3687": {"comment":"Divides by 16 (entries to a sector)"},
        "3689": {"synopsis":"Shifts DE right 4 times; a partly used last sector adds one."},
        "3696": {"comment":"Carry: some entries over (A = 0 here)"},
        "3698": {"comment":"+$10 = whole root sectors"},
        "3700": {"comment":"No remainder?"},
        "3702": {"comment":"One more sector"},
        "3703": {"synopsis":"Copies the sectors per FAT and starts the root directory's first sector: reserved + FATs x\nFAT size.","comment":"Sectors per FAT (boot +$16)"},
        "3708": {"comment":"HL = the first FAT; the block's pointer goes on the stack"},
        "3709": {"comment":"Root directory sectors"},
        "3710": {"comment":"E = sectors per FAT"},
        "3712": {"comment":"DE: the FAT area's size, added up B times"},
        "3713": {"synopsis":"One FAT's sectors added."},
        "3714": {"comment":"No carry into D?"},
        "3717": {"synopsis":"Stores the root directory's first sector and the first data sector, then works out the\nnumber of clusters.","comment":"Once for each FAT"},
        "3720": {"comment":"HL = the root directory's first sector"},
        "3722": {"comment":"HL = its size in sectors"},
        "3723": {"comment":"HL = the first data sector"},
        "3724": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the block's pointer"},
        "3725": {"comment":"+$12/$13 = the root directory's first sector"},
        "3729": {"comment":"DE = the first data sector"},
        "3730": {"comment":"+$14/$15 = it"},
        "3735": {"comment":"HL = total sectors (boot +$13)"},
        "3742": {"comment":"HL = data sectors"},
        "3744": {"comment":"C = the shift + 1"},
        "3745": {"synopsis":"Divides the data sectors by the cluster size.","comment":"Shifted enough?"},
        "3748": {"comment":"HL / 2"},
        "3754": {"synopsis":"Stores the clusters + 2, then the serial (with the byte before it) and boot byte $15.","comment":"HL = clusters + 2 (they are numbered from 2)"},
        "3758": {"comment":"+$16/$17"},
        "3763": {"comment":"HL = the serial (or the four $FF)"},
        "3767": {"comment":"From the byte before it"},
        "3768": {"comment":"5 bytes to +$18-$1C"},
        "3774": {"comment":"Boot byte $15 (the media byte)"},
        "3777": {"comment":"+$1D"},
        "3778": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3779": {"synopsis":"Zeroes the parameter block's +$1E and +$1F unless bit 7 of +$1F is set.\nEntry: HL = a parameter block.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3784": {"comment":"HL+$1F"},
        "3787": {"comment":"+$1F at $80 or more: keep both"},
        "3791": {"comment":"+$1F = 0"},
        "3793": {"comment":"+$1E = 0"},
        "3794": {"synopsis":"Returns with the caller's HL.","comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "3796": {"synopsis":"The drive error handler entered with carry set (IY+$2A = $FF); $0ED5 takes the carry from\nthe caller. It reports code A for the drive record at HL (through the error hook at IY-$3A\nwhen one is set) and acts on the answer: it returns Z to retry, NZ to go on, or abandons\nthe EXDOS call through FUNC_RETURN.\nEntry: A = the code; HL = the drive's record; IY = the workspace.\nExit: Z: retry; NZ: go on.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"IY+$2A will be $FF"},
        "3797": {"synopsis":"Reports disk error A on the drive whose record is at HL and returns the answer; $0ED4 enters\nwith carry set. IY+$2A = $FF with carry, else 0. A set unit flag at record+9 becomes 1.\nError $E5 (or bit 3 of IY-$37 set) aborts at once, error $BF is retried at once; otherwise\nthe handler at the word at IY-$39 asks (when the byte at IY-$3A is nonzero), else $0F3F.\nAnswer 1 aborts: the drive's buffers are dropped and the call ends with error $A4 (Disk\noperation aborted) through the word at IY-$5C; it does not come back here.\nEntry: A = the error code; HL = the drive's record; F: carry, kept as IY+$2A = $FF for the\nquestion; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: Z: try again; NZ: carry on.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3803": {"comment":"A = $FF with carry, else 0"},
        "3807": {"comment":"HL = record+8"},
        "3811": {"comment":"C = the unit key"},
        "3813": {"comment":"The disk-change timer"},
        "3814": {"comment":"Already 0?"},
        "3817": {"comment":"Then 1"},
        "3819": {"synopsis":"Part of the error prompt at $0ED5 (B = the error, C = the drive): decides who answers.\n1. Error $E5 (the STOP key, $04B2) aborts at once; error $BF retries without asking; bit 3\n   of IY-$37 set aborts without asking.\n2. When IY-$3A is not 0, the routine in RAM at IY+$205 is called with DE = the word at\n   IY-$39 ($00F2's byte $C7), B = the error, C = the drive. Its A = 0 leaves the answer to\n   the prompt; else its B is the answer.\n3. Otherwise ERR_PROMPT asks the user. The answer (1 Abort, 2 Retry, 3 Ignore; 4 or more\n   counts as 1) is handled at ERR_ANSWER.","comment":"A = the error"},
        "3820": {"comment":"Error $E5 (STOP pressed)?"},
        "3822": {"comment":"Yes: abort"},
        "3824": {"comment":"Error $BF?"},
        "3826": {"comment":"Answer 2 (Retry)"},
        "3828": {"comment":"Yes: retry without asking"},
        "3830": {"comment":"Abort without asking?"},
        "3836": {"comment":"HL = IY+$205: the RAM routine"},
        "3843": {"comment":"A = IY-$3A: call it?"},
        "3847": {"comment":"DE = the word at IY-$39 (the byte after the call)"},
        "3851": {"synopsis":"Calls the RAM routine (NZ), or asks the user when it was not called or returned A = 0.","comment":"The error and the drive"},
        "3852": {"comment":"Calls the RAM routine at HL"},
        "3855": {"comment":"H = the error, L = the drive"},
        "3856": {"comment":"A = 0?"},
        "3857": {"comment":"Then ask the user: B = the answer"},
        "3860": {"comment":"A = the answer"},
        "3861": {"comment":"1-3?"},
        "3865": {"synopsis":"Answer 1: abort.","comment":"Abort"},
        "3867": {"synopsis":"Handles the answer: 1 aborts (ERR_ABORT); 2 and 3 return to the caller of $0ED5 with its\nregisters: Z for Retry, NZ for Ignore.","comment":"Abort?"},
        "3868": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "3870": {"comment":"The caller's IX, BC, DE, HL"},
        "3875": {"comment":"A = 0 and Z for Retry; 1 and NZ for Ignore"},
        "3877": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL here calls the address in HL.","comment":"To the routine at HL"},
        "3878": {"synopsis":"Abort: frees every buffer without writing it ($0BBE with A = $FF), stores H at IY-$4D (the\nerror code when the prompt was asked; HL holds other values on the paths from $0EEE and\n$0EFA), and leaves the EXDOS function with error $A4 (Disk operation aborted) from the stack\nit saved at entry (IY+$28).","comment":"A = $FF: every drive"},
        "3879": {"comment":"Frees their buffers (entry $0BBE)"},
        "3882": {"comment":"H = the error code (on the prompt path)"},
        "3885": {"comment":"Error $A4: Disk operation aborted"},
        "3887": {"comment":"DE = the stack at the function's entry (byte $28)"},
        "3891": {"synopsis":"Puts SP back to the function's entry stack, clears HL, BC and DE, and leaves through the\nfunction exit at $052F with the status in A."},
        "3892": {"comment":"SP = the entry stack"},
        "3893": {"comment":"HL, BC, DE = 0"},
        "3900": {"comment":"The EXDOS function exit"},
        "3903": {"synopsis":"Asks the user what to do about an error, on the channel in IY-$52, through the prompt's own\noutput buffer (IY+$620):\n1. \"<the error's text> -- drive X:\" or, for error $B1, \"Insert disk for drive X:\".\n2. \"Press ENTER to continue...\" for error $B1, else \"Ignore, retry or abort (I/R/A)?\", or\n   \"Retry or abort (R/A)?\" when IY+$2A is not 0 (no Ignore). German texts have W, not R.\n3. Reads the answer (ERR_READ_KEY) until it is one, then puts the output channel back.\nEntry: H = the error code, L = the drive (1 = A), IY.\nExit: B = the answer: 1 Abort, 2 Retry, 3 Ignore.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, DE', L'.\nKeeps: F, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The prompt's buffer in use"},
        "3907": {"comment":"The output channel, kept"},
        "3911": {"comment":"The channel for the prompt"},
        "3917": {"comment":"B = the error code"},
        "3918": {"comment":"HL = IY; the error and drive go on the stack"},
        "3921": {"comment":"HL = the prompt's buffer"},
        "3925": {"comment":"Empty"},
        "3927": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "3930": {"comment":"Error $B1?"},
        "3933": {"comment":"Message $49: \"Insert disk for\""},
        "3937": {"comment":"A = the error"},
        "3938": {"comment":"HL = the place for its digits"},
        "3939": {"comment":"Its text in the buffer"},
        "3942": {"comment":"Message $45: \" --\"; NZ"},
        "3945": {"synopsis":"Writes the first line's end: the message in A, \" drive \" and the drive's letter.","comment":"H = the error, L = the drive"},
        "3946": {"comment":"Z kept: error $B1"},
        "3947": {"comment":"Message $45 or $49"},
        "3950": {"comment":"Message $46: \" drive \""},
        "3955": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "3956": {"comment":"Its letter and a colon"},
        "3959": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "3962": {"synopsis":"Picks the question: Z (error $B1) \"Press ENTER to continue...\" ($44); else \"Ignore, retry or\nabort (I/R/A)?\" ($48), or \"Retry or abort (R/A)?\" ($47) when IY+$2A is not 0.","comment":"Z = error $B1"},
        "3964": {"comment":"Message $44: \"Press ENTER to continue...\""},
        "3968": {"comment":"Ignore allowed (IY+$2A = 0)?"},
        "3972": {"comment":"Message $48: \"Ignore, retry or abort (I/R/A)? \""},
        "3976": {"comment":"Message $47: \"Retry or abort (R/A)? \""},
        "3978": {"synopsis":"Writes the question and reads the answer; another key asks again.","comment":"The question"},
        "3981": {"comment":"Reads a key: B = the answer"},
        "3984": {"comment":"Not an answer: ask again"},
        "3986": {"comment":"Drops the saved flags"},
        "3987": {"comment":"A = the output channel"},
        "3988": {"comment":"Put back"},
        "3991": {"comment":"The normal output buffer again"},
        "3996": {"synopsis":"Reads the prompt's answer: writes code $8E, sends the buffer out, reads a key from the\nchannel in IY-$53 (EXOS 5), or from the first keyboard channel when that is $FF, and writes\nthe codes at $1000. A read error counts as A. The key is echoed when printable, followed by\na new line; then the STOP key (FLAG_SOFT_IRQ = $20), A, ESC and Ctrl-C give 1 (Abort); R (W\nin German) and ENTER 2 (Retry); I 3 (Ignore).\nEntry: IY.\nExit: Z and B = the answer; NZ for any other key.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "3997": {"comment":"Code $8E"},
        "4002": {"comment":"Sends the buffer out"},
        "4005": {"comment":"The key channel"},
        "4009": {"comment":"None ($FF)?"},
        "4010": {"comment":"Then the first keyboard channel"},
        "4013": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4017": {"comment":"Z: B = the key"},
        "4018": {"comment":"The codes at $1000"},
        "4025": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "4027": {"comment":"No: take it as A (Abort)"},
        "4029": {"synopsis":"Echoes the key when printable ($20-$7F), writes a new line, then classifies it: STOP pressed\nor A gives B = 1 with Z (at $0FD6).","comment":"A = the key"},
        "4032": {"comment":"Printable?"},
        "4035": {"comment":"Yes: echo it"},
        "4038": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "4041": {"comment":"STOP pressed (FLAG_SOFT_IRQ)?"},
        "4046": {"comment":"Yes: Z, answer 1"},
        "4049": {"comment":"In capitals"},
        "4052": {"comment":"\"A\": Abort?"},
        "4054": {"synopsis":"The tail of the Abort/Retry/Ignore prompt ($0F9C): classifies the key in A. Entered with Z\nset (from $0FCE, FLAG_SOFT_IRQ = $20) it answers Abort at once.\n1. Z on entry, \"A\", ESC or code 3: Abort, B = 1.\n2. B = 2; reads EXOS variable $90: when it is 0 (German) \"W\" is Retry, else \"R\"; ENTER is\nRetry too.\n3. B = 3; \"I\" is Ignore.\nEntry: A = the key (upper case), Z = abort already.\nExit: Z with B = 1 (Abort), 2 (Retry) or 3 (Ignore); NZ for any other key (B = 3).\nChanges: AF, B.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"B = 1: Abort"},
        "4056": {"comment":"Abort already (Z)?"},
        "4057": {"comment":"ESC?"},
        "4060": {"comment":"Code 3?"},
        "4063": {"comment":"B = 2: Retry"},
        "4064": {"comment":"Keeps the answer number"},
        "4066": {"comment":"Keeps the key"},
        "4067": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90 (the message language)"},
        "4073": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "4074": {"comment":"0 (German)?"},
        "4076": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "4078": {"comment":"No: English, Retry is \"R\""},
        "4080": {"comment":"German: Retry is \"W\""},
        "4084": {"synopsis":"Part of KEY_ARI_ANSWER: the English Retry key \"R\".","comment":"Retry (\"R\")?"},
        "4086": {"synopsis":"Part of KEY_ARI_ANSWER: answers Retry for the language's key or ENTER, then Ignore for \"I\".","comment":"Puts DE back"},
        "4087": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "4088": {"comment":"Retry key: Z, B = 2"},
        "4089": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "4092": {"comment":"B = 3: Ignore"},
        "4093": {"comment":"\"I\"? Z for Ignore, NZ for any other key"},
        "4101": {"synopsis":"The RAM disk's driver entry: its address ($D005) is what $01CA passes to $03DF with C = 1,\nas $01B2 passes FLOPPY_DRIVER with C = 4. The disk lives in RAM segments; the first one,\nkept at IY+$1D, holds the boot sector at $4000 and the list of the disk's segments at $4100,\nand stays in page 1 while the driver runs.\n1. Pages the RAM disk's segment into page 1 (A' = the caller's page-1 segment).\n2. Function $FF: create (B = segments) or remove (B = 0) the disk (RD_CREATE).\n3. No RAM disk (IY+$1D = 0): error $BE.\n4. Functions 0-2: nothing to do. 3: reads sector 0. 4: reads, 5 and 6: write B sectors from\nsector DE, IX being the 512-byte buffers (in the caller's page-1 segment's view). 7 and up:\nerror $BD.\nEntry: A = the function; B = the sector count (or segment count); DE = the first sector;\nIX = the buffer; IY = EXDOS's variables.\nExit: A = 0; B = the sectors transferred (1 for functions 0-2); page 1 = the RAM disk's\nsegment.\nError: A = $BE (no RAM disk), $BD (no such function), $BB (sector past the end, B = the\nsectors done), or RD_CREATE's.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"Keeps the function"},
        "4102": {"comment":"H = the caller's page-1 segment"},
        "4105": {"comment":"L = the RAM disk's segment (0: none)"},
        "4109": {"comment":"Page 1 = the RAM disk's segment"},
        "4112": {"comment":"A' = the caller's page-1 segment; A = the function"},
        "4113": {"comment":"Function $FF?"},
        "4117": {"comment":"RAM disk present?"},
        "4119": {"comment":"No"},
        "4121": {"comment":"Function 0-2?"},
        "4123": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to do"},
        "4125": {"comment":"Not function 3"},
        "4127": {"comment":"Function 3: sector 0 ..."},
        "4129": {"comment":"... one sector"},
        "4131": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: functions 3-6 go on to the transfer; 7 and up fail with $BD.","comment":"A = function - 7 ($FD-$FF for 3-6)"},
        "4133": {"comment":"Function 3-6: transfer"},
        "4135": {"comment":"Error $BD: no such function"},
        "4138": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: no RAM disk exists; error $BE.","comment":"Error $BE: no RAM disk"},
        "4141": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: functions 0-2 need nothing on a RAM disk; returns A = 0, B = 1.","comment":"One unit of work done"},
        "4143": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "4145": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: sets up the sector transfer. L counts the sectors done; the\ndirection (bit 1 of the function - 7: functions 5 and 6 write) is kept in F'.","comment":"L = sectors done"},
        "4147": {"comment":"H = function - 7"},
        "4149": {"comment":"F' = Z for a read (3, 4), NZ for a write (5, 6)"},
        "4152": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER, once per sector: locates sector DE (RD_LOCATE_SECTOR), stops with\n$BB past the end, disables interrupts (INT_DISABLE) and sets HL and DE for the copy: from\nthe buffer at IX to the segment for a write, the other way for a read.","comment":"DE' = the sector number ..."},
        "4153": {"comment":"... (the alternate set does the copy)"},
        "4155": {"comment":"B = its segment, DE = its offset there"},
        "4158": {"comment":"Past the end: error $BB"},
        "4160": {"comment":"Interrupts off while page 0 is swapped"},
        "4163": {"comment":"Keeps the interrupt state"},
        "4164": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "4167": {"comment":"Keeps it"},
        "4168": {"comment":"A = the caller's page-1 segment; F = the direction"},
        "4169": {"comment":"A write: copy buffer to segment"},
        "4171": {"comment":"A read: copy segment to buffer"},
        "4172": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: copies one 512-byte sector with the caller's segment in page 1\n(where the buffer is) and the RAM disk's data segment in page 0, then puts both pages back,\nmoves IX on by 512 and enables interrupts again if they were on.","comment":"Page 1 = the caller's segment (the buffer)"},
        "4174": {"comment":"Keeps it in A' again"},
        "4175": {"comment":"C = page 0's segment"},
        "4178": {"comment":"Page 0 = the sector's segment"},
        "4181": {"comment":"A = page 0's own segment"},
        "4182": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "4187": {"comment":"Page 0 back"},
        "4189": {"comment":"Page 1 = the RAM disk's segment again"},
        "4194": {"comment":"HL = the buffer ..."},
        "4195": {"comment":"... plus 512"},
        "4197": {"comment":"IX = the next buffer"},
        "4200": {"comment":"The interrupt state"},
        "4201": {"comment":"Were interrupts off before?"},
        "4203": {"comment":"No: enable them again"},
        "4204": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: counts the sector done and goes on with the next one until B sectors\nare done; then A = 0.","comment":"The counting set"},
        "4205": {"comment":"One more sector done"},
        "4206": {"comment":"Next sector number"},
        "4207": {"comment":"More to do?"},
        "4209": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "4211": {"synopsis":"Part of RAMDISK_DRIVER: returns B = the sectors transferred (A = 0, or $BB from\nRD_SECTOR_LOOP).","comment":"The counting set"},
        "4212": {"comment":"B = the sectors done"},
        "4214": {"synopsis":"Finds where a RAM disk sector lives: 32 sectors of 512 bytes fill each 16K segment, and the\nsegment list at $4100 gives the segment of each run of 32.\nEntry: DE = the sector number; the RAM disk's segment in page 1.\nExit: NC; A = 0; B = the segment holding the sector; DE = its offset in the segment.\nError: Carry and A = $BB when DE is not below the total sector count ($4013).\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY.","comment":"HL = the total sectors (the boot sector's word at +$13)"},
        "4218": {"comment":"HL = total - sector - 1"},
        "4220": {"comment":"Error $BB"},
        "4222": {"comment":"Sector DE past the end?"},
        "4224": {"comment":"HL = sector x 2"},
        "4225": {"comment":"A = (sector x 2) low byte"},
        "4226": {"comment":"HL = sector x 8"},
        "4228": {"comment":"L = sector / 32: the segment list's index"},
        "4231": {"comment":"B = the segment"},
        "4232": {"comment":"A = (sector mod 32) x 2"},
        "4234": {"comment":"D = the offset's high byte (512 bytes a sector)"},
        "4235": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "4236": {"comment":"E = 0"},
        "4238": {"synopsis":"RAMDISK_DRIVER's function $FF, create or remove the RAM disk: B = 0 removes it; a new disk\nof B segments may be made only when none exists, else error $9D.","comment":"Remove (B = 0)?"},
        "4241": {"comment":"A disk already there?"},
        "4242": {"comment":"Error $9D: it exists"},
        "4245": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: opens a channel to \"DISK:\" ($0329), whose special functions give and take\nback segments; B = 0 goes on to RD_REMOVE.","comment":"Keeps the segment count"},
        "4249": {"comment":"H = the DISK: channel"},
        "4253": {"comment":"Could not open it"},
        "4254": {"comment":"Remove?"},
        "4257": {"comment":"The segment list (entry 0 at $4100)"},
        "4260": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE, once per segment: asks the DISK: channel for a segment (special function\n$F0). The first one becomes the RAM disk's own (page 1, IY+$1D). On failure the segments got\nso far are given back (RD_FREE_LOOP) with error $F7.","comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4262": {"comment":"Special function $F0: give a segment"},
        "4266": {"comment":"A = the segment"},
        "4268": {"comment":"Failed: give them back, error $F7"},
        "4270": {"comment":"The first segment?"},
        "4273": {"comment":"Yes: page it in ..."},
        "4275": {"comment":"... as the RAM disk's segment"},
        "4278": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: lists each segment at $4100 + n, then closes the channel and writes the\nboot sector: the 11-byte parameter template and the 11-byte volume text from $1132 at $400B\nand $4040, the root directory entries ((segments / 4 + 2) x 16) at $4011, the total sectors\n(segments x 32) at $4013, two sectors a cluster at $400D for 128 segments and more, and the\nsectors of one FAT (RD_SET_FAT_SIZE).","comment":"List entry n = the segment"},
        "4280": {"comment":"L = the segments listed"},
        "4282": {"comment":"More to get?"},
        "4284": {"comment":"Keeps the list's end"},
        "4288": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4291": {"comment":"A = the segment count"},
        "4292": {"comment":"The boot sector's parameters ..."},
        "4295": {"comment":"... from the template"},
        "4303": {"comment":"The volume text"},
        "4310": {"comment":"L = segments / 4 ..."},
        "4315": {"comment":"... + 2"},
        "4317": {"comment":"HL x 16"},
        "4322": {"comment":"Root directory entries"},
        "4325": {"comment":"HL = segments x 32"},
        "4332": {"comment":"Total sectors"},
        "4335": {"comment":"HL = 3 x total - 1 ..."},
        "4340": {"comment":"... / 1024: the sectors of a 12-bit FAT, less one"},
        "4344": {"comment":"128 segments or more?"},
        "4347": {"comment":"Yes: two sectors a cluster ..."},
        "4352": {"comment":"... and half the FAT"},
        "4354": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: stores the sectors of one FAT ($4016) and returns A = 0.","comment":"L = the FAT's sectors less one"},
        "4356": {"comment":"Plus one"},
        "4357": {"comment":"Sectors a FAT"},
        "4360": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "4362": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE, B = 0: removes the RAM disk. With none, just closes the channel; else\ngives every listed segment but the first back to the DISK: channel (RD_FREE_LOOP), closes it\nand forgets the disk (IY+$1D = 0).","comment":"A RAM disk at all?"},
        "4365": {"comment":"No: close the channel only"},
        "4367": {"comment":"DE = the list's end"},
        "4371": {"comment":"A = 0: the result"},
        "4372": {"comment":"Never jumps: its operand is LD A,$F7 at $1115 (from $10AC)"},
        "4375": {"comment":"Keeps the result (0, or $F7 from $1115)"},
        "4376": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: gives the listed segments back from the last to entry 1 (special function\n$F1), then goes on to RD_CLOSE_EXIT.","comment":"Back to entry 0?"},
        "4377": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "4379": {"comment":"Special function $F1: take a segment back"},
        "4381": {"comment":"The previous entry"},
        "4382": {"comment":"C = its segment"},
        "4384": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4385": {"comment":"Keeps the list pointer"},
        "4392": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: no RAM disk to remove; keeps the result and closes the channel.","comment":"Keeps the result"},
        "4393": {"synopsis":"Part of RD_CREATE: closes the DISK: channel and marks the RAM disk gone (IY+$1D = 0);\nreturns the result kept on the stack.","comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4396": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "4397": {"comment":"No RAM disk now"},
        "4424": {"synopsis":"Reads the FAT entry of cluster DE. A value above $0FF7 (the end-of-chain marks), and a\ncluster past the last one (after error $A3 through DISK_ERROR), come back as DE = $FFFF.\nEntry: DE = the cluster; HL = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: DE = the entry's value or $FFFF; carry 0 for a value up to $0FF7.\nChanges: AF, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"DE = the entry's bytes, carry = odd"},
        "4427": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "4429": {"synopsis":"Part of $1148 (read a FAT entry): the cluster number is past the disk's last; reports error\n$A3 through $0ED5, again while it returns Z, then answers the end-of-chain value $FFFF.","comment":"Error $A3"},
        "4431": {"comment":"NC for $0ED5"},
        "4432": {"comment":"Reports it"},
        "4435": {"comment":"Report again?"},
        "4439": {"synopsis":"Part of $1148: takes the 12-bit entry out of its two bytes at DE: the low 12 bits for an\neven cluster (NC), the high 12 bits for an odd one (carry, from $11ED).","comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "4440": {"comment":"L = the first byte"},
        "4443": {"comment":"A = the second byte"},
        "4444": {"comment":"An even cluster?"},
        "4446": {"comment":"Odd: H = the second byte"},
        "4447": {"comment":"A = its high nibble"},
        "4450": {"comment":"L = the middle 8 bits"},
        "4451": {"synopsis":"Part of $1148: DE = the entry; a value above $FF7 (end of chain or bad) becomes $FFFF.","comment":"The entry's top 4 bits"},
        "4454": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "4455": {"comment":"Above $FF7?"},
        "4461": {"comment":"No: NC, DE = the next cluster"},
        "4462": {"synopsis":"Part of $1148: answers DE = $FFFF, the end of the chain.","comment":"End of chain"},
        "4466": {"synopsis":"Gives the disk sector of a sector within a cluster: (cluster - 2) shifted left by the\ndrive's sectors-a-cluster power, plus the sector, plus the first data sector.\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block (+$09 the first data sector, +$0B the power of 2 of\nthe sectors a cluster); DE = the cluster; A = the sector within the cluster.\nExit: DE = the sector number.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4468": {"comment":"HL = the block + $0B"},
        "4472": {"comment":"B = the shift count ..."},
        "4473": {"comment":"... + 1 for the DJNZ"},
        "4474": {"comment":"HL = the cluster ..."},
        "4475": {"comment":"... - 2"},
        "4477": {"comment":"Its operand byte ($29) is the loop's ADD HL,HL at $117E"},
        "4479": {"comment":"Shifts HL left the count times"},
        "4481": {"comment":"Plus the sector in the cluster"},
        "4484": {"comment":"HL = the block + $09"},
        "4487": {"comment":"HL = the first data sector"},
        "4491": {"comment":"Plus the cluster's sector"},
        "4492": {"comment":"DE = the sector number"},
        "4496": {"synopsis":"Writes a cluster's FAT entry: first ends the single-FAT mode (FAT_SYNC_COPIES), then stores\nthe 12-bit value in the FAT's buffer ($1193 on, FAT_SET_STORE) and marks it to be written. A\nvalue of $1000 or more is stored as $FFF.\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block; DE = the cluster; BC = the value.\nExit: the entry set in the buffer.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: DE, IX.","comment":"Writes go to every FAT copy again"},
        "4499": {"synopsis":"Writes the 12-bit FAT entry of cluster DE: B >= $10 writes $FFF (end of chain), else BC.\nThe code from $119C finds the entry (FAT_ENTRY_ADDR), merges the value with the neighbouring\nentry's nibble, marks the FAT sector changed and, for an entry that straddles two sectors,\nwrites both halves back. A cluster past the end is reported as error $A3 through\nDISK_ERROR, and nothing is written.\nEntry: DE = the cluster; BC = the value; HL = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: the entry is set, its sector's buffer marked changed.\nChanges: AF, BC, all alternates.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4500": {"comment":"Value $1000 or more?"},
        "4505": {"comment":"Then the end-of-chain mark $FFF"},
        "4508": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: finds the entry's two bytes ($11ED); a cluster past the disk's end goes to\nFAT_SET_BADCL.","comment":"DE = the entry's bytes, carry for an odd cluster"},
        "4511": {"comment":"Found"},
        "4513": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: the cluster number is past the disk's last; reports error $A3 through\n$0ED5, again while it returns Z, and writes nothing.","comment":"Error $A3"},
        "4515": {"comment":"NC for $0ED5"},
        "4516": {"comment":"Reports it"},
        "4519": {"comment":"Report again?"},
        "4523": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: an even cluster takes the low 12 bits of the two bytes: C in the first, B's\nlow nibble under the second byte's high nibble.","comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "4524": {"comment":"An odd cluster?"},
        "4526": {"comment":"First byte = the value's low byte"},
        "4529": {"comment":"Second byte: keeps its high nibble ..."},
        "4532": {"comment":"... and takes the value's top 4 bits"},
        "4536": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: an odd cluster takes the high 12 bits: the value x 16 goes in under the\nfirst byte's low nibble.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "4538": {"comment":"HL = the value x 16"},
        "4541": {"comment":"First byte: keeps its low nibble ..."},
        "4544": {"comment":"... and takes the value's low 4 bits"},
        "4547": {"comment":"Second byte = the value's top 8 bits"},
        "4549": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: marks the buffer to be written. When the entry straddles two sectors\n(IY+$63 bit 0, its bytes kept at IY+$66), the second byte goes to the first data byte of the\nsecond sector's buffer and the first byte to the last of the first sector's ($11D9, the\nsector kept at IY+$64).","comment":"Mark the buffer changed (HL = its flags)"},
        "4552": {"comment":"Did the entry straddle two sectors?"},
        "4556": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "4558": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's first data byte"},
        "4562": {"comment":"The second byte goes there"},
        "4563": {"comment":"A = the first byte"},
        "4565": {"comment":"DE = IY+$64: the first sector (byte $64 follows)"},
        "4569": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET (after the inline byte at $11D8): puts the first byte of a straddling entry\nin the last data byte of its sector's buffer.","comment":"IX = the parameter block (saved on the stack)"},
        "4571": {"comment":"Keeps the byte"},
        "4572": {"comment":"HL = the sector's buffer"},
        "4575": {"comment":"Mark it changed"},
        "4578": {"comment":"HL = its last data byte"},
        "4583": {"comment":"The first byte goes there"},
        "4584": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "4586": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: puts HL back and returns through FAT_SET_RET.","comment":"HL back"},
        "4587": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SET: puts the caller's DE back and returns.","comment":"DE back (the cluster)"},
        "4589": {"synopsis":"Finds the 12-bit FAT entry of cluster DE: its byte offset is DE x 3 / 2, so the sector is\nthe FAT's first (record+$0C) + offset / 512. An entry that straddles two sectors is copied\nto IY+$66 (bit 0 of IY+$63 set, the first sector at IY+$64) and DE points there.\nEntry: DE = the cluster; HL = the drive's record; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: Z; DE = the entry's two bytes; carry = the cluster is odd (the entry is the high 12\nbits).\nError: NZ, carry: the cluster is past the last one (record+$16 - 1).\nChanges: AF, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4593": {"comment":"IX = the record"},
        "4596": {"comment":"No straddling entry yet"},
        "4600": {"comment":"HL = record+$16: the cluster limit"},
        "4606": {"comment":"The last cluster"},
        "4608": {"comment":"Cluster DE past it?"},
        "4614": {"comment":"HL = DE x 3"},
        "4616": {"comment":"HL = DE x 3 / 2: the byte offset, carry = odd"},
        "4620": {"comment":"The odd bit on the stack"},
        "4622": {"comment":"E = offset / 512"},
        "4626": {"comment":"HL = the FAT's first sector"},
        "4632": {"comment":"DE = the sector that holds the entry"},
        "4634": {"comment":"HL = its buffer"},
        "4637": {"comment":"Past the buffer's header"},
        "4642": {"comment":"BC = the offset within the sector"},
        "4647": {"comment":"Its last byte ($1FF)?"},
        "4650": {"comment":"A = the entry's first byte"},
        "4654": {"comment":"HL = IY+$63"},
        "4658": {"comment":"The entry straddles two sectors"},
        "4661": {"comment":"Note the first sector"},
        "4665": {"comment":"And the first byte"},
        "4668": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "4676": {"comment":"A = the entry's second byte"},
        "4678": {"comment":"Next to the first one"},
        "4679": {"comment":"DE will point at the two bytes"},
        "4680": {"synopsis":"Part of $11ED (find a FAT entry): DE = the entry's two bytes; Z, with carry for an odd\ncluster (the half byte of cluster x 1.5).","comment":"DE = the entry's bytes"},
        "4681": {"comment":"Carry = the odd half"},
        "4682": {"comment":"A = 0 or $FF"},
        "4683": {"comment":"Z: found"},
        "4684": {"comment":"Carry = odd cluster"},
        "4685": {"synopsis":"Part of $11ED: puts HL, BC and IX back and returns (NZ, from $1202, when the cluster is past\nthe last).","comment":"HL back"},
        "4690": {"synopsis":"Shifts HL left by 4 bits into A: A:HL = HL x 16.\nEntry: HL = the value.\nExit: HL = the value x 16 (low 16 bits); A = the 4 bits shifted out (entry H's high nibble).\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "4691": {"comment":"Bit 15 out ..."},
        "4692": {"comment":"... into A, 4 times"},
        "4700": {"synopsis":"Ends the single-FAT mode of the drive whose parameter block is HL: when its +$18 bit 0 is\nset, marks every sector of the first FAT to be written to all the copies (bit 6 of each\nbuffer's flags, through $0AD2/$0B8F), then sets +$18 to 0 and stores the 0 in the boot\nsector (data byte $46) too (FAT_MODE_SET).\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block.\nExit: the mode cleared; IX as on entry.\nChanges: AF, HL, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX.","comment":"IX = the block (its own IX kept on the stack)"},
        "4703": {"comment":"Single-FAT mode on?"},
        "4707": {"comment":"No: nothing to do"},
        "4709": {"comment":"A = 0: write to all copies, mode 0"},
        "4712": {"synopsis":"Starts the single-FAT mode of the drive whose parameter block is HL, unless its +$19 bit 7\nis set or the mode is on already: goes over every sector of the first FAT through $0AE0 and\n$09F9 with one copy, then sets +$18 to 1 and stores the 1 in the boot sector (FAT_MODE_SET).\nFrom then on FAT writes go to the first copy only, until FAT_SYNC_COPIES.\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block.\nExit: the mode on; IX as on entry.\nChanges: AF, HL, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX.","comment":"IX = the block (its own IX kept on the stack)"},
        "4715": {"comment":"Drive barred from single-FAT mode?"},
        "4719": {"comment":"Yes: leave the mode alone"},
        "4721": {"comment":"Single-FAT mode on already?"},
        "4727": {"comment":"A = 1: one copy, mode 1"},
        "4729": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SYNC_COPIES and FAT_SINGLE_ON (A = the new mode, 0 or 1): with more than one\nFAT, goes over the first FAT's sectors (FAT_MODE_LOOP); then records the mode\n(FAT_MODE_MARK).","comment":"Keeps BC"},
        "4730": {"comment":"Keeps DE"},
        "4731": {"comment":"B = the number of FATs"},
        "4734": {"comment":"Only one?"},
        "4735": {"comment":"Yes: just record the mode"},
        "4737": {"comment":"DE = the first FAT sector"},
        "4743": {"comment":"B = the sectors of one FAT"},
        "4746": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_MODE_SET, once per FAT sector: mode 1 takes its buffer through $0AE0 (one copy);\nmode 0 through $0AD2, then marks it changed and to be written to all copies (bit 6).","comment":"Keeps the sector count"},
        "4747": {"comment":"Keeps the mode"},
        "4748": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "4749": {"comment":"B = 0 for $0AE0"},
        "4751": {"comment":"Mode 1: the buffer, one copy"},
        "4754": {"comment":"Mode 1"},
        "4756": {"comment":"Mode 0: the buffer, every copy"},
        "4760": {"comment":"Mark it changed (HL = its flags)"},
        "4763": {"comment":"Write it to all the copies"},
        "4766": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_MODE_SET: passes the buffer to $09F9, clears its byte +2 and goes on with the\nnext FAT sector; then B = the mode."},
        "4769": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's byte +2"},
        "4773": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "4774": {"comment":"B = the sectors left"},
        "4775": {"comment":"The next FAT sector"},
        "4778": {"comment":"B = the mode"},
        "4779": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_MODE_SET: when the mode changes, records it in +$18 and in the boot sector\n(sector 0's buffer, data byte $46).","comment":"A = the new mode"},
        "4780": {"comment":"Is it the mode already?"},
        "4783": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to record"},
        "4786": {"comment":"Sector 0 ..."},
        "4789": {"comment":"... one copy"},
        "4797": {"comment":"Mark it changed (HL = its flags)"},
        "4800": {"comment":"HL = data byte $46"},
        "4805": {"comment":"The mode in the boot sector"},
        "4806": {"comment":"And in the parameter block"},
        "4809": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_MODE_SET: puts DE and BC back.","comment":"DE back"},
        "4811": {"synopsis":"Part of FAT_SYNC_COPIES, FAT_SINGLE_ON and FAT_MODE_SET: puts IX and HL back and returns.","comment":"IX back; the parameter block on the stack"},
        "4813": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"Selects the directory a search runs in, and starts it at its first entry (DIR_FIRST):\n1. DE's first byte $FF: the directory is the path text at HL (DIR_SELECT_PATH).\n2. Else DE is an open file's descriptor: its entry is fetched again (DIR_REOPEN_ENTRY), must\n   be a directory (attribute bit 4) and becomes the one to search.\nEntry: DE = the descriptor or $FF; HL = the path text or the block with the position; B, C\nas PATH_PARSE takes them.\nExit: Z; the search started.\nError: NZ, A = $A1 (not a directory), $A8 (the path text does not end the path) or the error\nof DIR_REOPEN_ENTRY or PATH_PARSE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"The first byte"},
        "4816": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "4817": {"comment":"Yes: a path"},
        "4819": {"comment":"A = the entry's attributes"},
        "4822": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "4823": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "4827": {"comment":"Error $A1: not a directory"},
        "4830": {"comment":"Search this directory"},
        "4835": {"synopsis":"Part of DIR_SELECT: reads the path text (PATH_PARSE with flags $81: look it up, the last\nelement too); anything left after the path is error $A8.","comment":"IX = the parse block"},
        "4838": {"comment":"Keeps BC"},
        "4839": {"comment":"DE = the text, HL = the block"},
        "4840": {"comment":"Look up every element"},
        "4842": {"comment":"Read and walk the path"},
        "4845": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "4847": {"comment":"Anything after the path?"},
        "4848": {"comment":"Error $A8"},
        "4850": {"synopsis":"Part of DIR_SELECT: puts BC back; returns an error (NZ).","comment":"BC back"},
        "4852": {"synopsis":"Part of DIR_SELECT: starts the search at the directory's first entry; Z.","comment":"Start at the first entry"},
        "4855": {"comment":"Z: done"},
        "4857": {"synopsis":"Goes back to the directory entry of an open file: the descriptor at DE must start with $FE;\nthe position kept in the block at HL is restored (DIRPOS_RESTORE), the 4 bytes at the\ndescriptor's +$19 are copied to +$2C, and the entry is fetched again (DIR_REFETCH).\nEntry: DE = the file's descriptor (first byte $FE); HL = the block with the position.\nExit: Z; A = the entry's attributes (its byte $0B); DE = the entry; IX = the descriptor.\nError: NZ, A = $A0 (not a $FE descriptor) or DIRPOS_RESTORE's error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"The descriptor's first byte"},
        "4858": {"comment":"$FE?"},
        "4860": {"comment":"Error $A0"},
        "4863": {"comment":"Keeps the descriptor"},
        "4864": {"comment":"DE = the position's block"},
        "4865": {"comment":"Restore the position"},
        "4869": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "4873": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor + $19 ..."},
        "4878": {"comment":"... DE = + $2C"},
        "4882": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "4886": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor"},
        "4887": {"comment":"DE = the directory entry"},
        "4891": {"comment":"HL = its byte $0B ..."},
        "4895": {"comment":"... A = the attributes"},
        "4897": {"comment":"IX = the descriptor"},
        "4900": {"comment":"Z: done"},
        "4902": {"synopsis":"Makes the directory position kept in a descriptor the current one: selects its drive ($0CC9)\nand copies its 12 bytes from +$17 to IY+$30. Sets IY+$63 bit 2 either way (the sector buffer\nmust be found again).\nEntry: DE = the descriptor (+$07 the drive).\nExit: Z, A = 0; IX = the descriptor; the position copied.\nError: NZ, A = the error from $0CC9.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "4903": {"comment":"IX = the descriptor"},
        "4906": {"comment":"C = its drive"},
        "4911": {"comment":"Select the drive"},
        "4914": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "4918": {"comment":"Set up the copy"},
        "4921": {"comment":"The position is current"},
        "4924": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "4925": {"synopsis":"Part of DIRPOS_RESTORE: puts BC back and marks the buffer to be found again (IY+$63 bit 2).","comment":"BC back"},
        "4926": {"comment":"The entry's buffer must be found again"},
        "4931": {"synopsis":"Sets up the copy of a 12-byte directory position between a file's descriptor (from +$17) and\nthe current one at IY+$30.\nEntry: IX = the descriptor.\nExit: DE = IY+$30; HL = IX+$17; BC = 12.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, IX, IY."},
        "4934": {"comment":"DE = IY+$30: the current position"},
        "4942": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor's position"},
        "4946": {"comment":"12 bytes"},
        "4950": {"synopsis":"PATH_PARSE_BLK with drive 0 (the default).\nEntry: A = the parse flags (IX+6); C = PATH_PARSE's flags; DE = the text.\nExit: as PATH_PARSE.\nError: as PATH_PARSE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"Drive 0: the default"},
        "4952": {"synopsis":"PATH_PARSE with EXDOS's own parse block (IY+$6A1): its flags = A, its drive = B.\nEntry: A = the parse flags (IX+6); B = the drive (0 = the default); C = PATH_PARSE's flags;\nDE = the text.\nExit: as PATH_PARSE; IX = the parse block.\nError: as PATH_PARSE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"IX = IY ..."},
        "4957": {"comment":"... + $6A1: the parse block"},
        "4963": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "4966": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "4969": {"synopsis":"Reads a path: \"[drive:][\\]dir\\...\\name.ext\". Swaps the register sets (the caller's are the\nalternates while it runs, the text read through DE') and leaves them swapped. The flags are\nthe caller's C.\n1. A letter and \":\" give the drive (1 = A); else IX+7, or the default drive IY-$57 when that\nis 0. IX+7 = the drive.\n2. Flag bit 7: selects the drive ($0CC9, HL = its parameter block) and sets the start\ndirectory (PATH_START_DIR): the root after a \"\\\" (or with IX+6 bit 3), else the drive's\ncurrent one.\n3. IX+6 bit 3: the rest is one raw 11-character name up to \"/\" (PATH_RAW_NAME). Else each\n   element is read into the name buffer (PARSE_NAME_ELEM) and, when a \"\\\" follows, looked up\n   and entered (PATH_FIND_ELEM); the last one too when flag bit 0 is set and it has a name.\n4. PATH_FINISH writes 0 at the text position kept at IY+$5B (where the last directory\n   element ended) and, with flag bit 7, clears the word at the caller's HL.\nEntry: DE = the text; C = the flags; HL = the word to clear; IX = the parse block (+6 flags,\n+7 drive or 0).\nExit: the sets swapped; Z, A = 0; DE = the text after the path; C = the character that\nstopped it (0 at the end); B = the last element's flags; the name buffer (IY+$6D1) holds it.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($0CC9's, or a lookup's).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"Text not in view ..."},
        "4971": {"comment":"... and folded to upper case"},
        "4973": {"comment":"The text goes to the alternate set"},
        "4974": {"comment":"B = flags: bit 2, a drive was given"},
        "4976": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "4981": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "4984": {"comment":"No: no drive"},
        "4986": {"comment":"C = the drive number (1 = A)"},
        "4989": {"comment":"Anything after it?"},
        "4994": {"comment":"\":\"?"},
        "4996": {"comment":"Yes: a drive"},
        "4998": {"comment":"No: back to the letter"},
        "5001": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: steps the text back by one character, then takes the default drive.","comment":"Back to the start"},
        "5004": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: no drive in the text: the parse block's drive, or the default (IY-$57)\nwhen that is 0.","comment":"A = the block's drive"},
        "5007": {"comment":"C = the default drive"},
        "5010": {"comment":"None in the block?"},
        "5014": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: no drive was given (B bit 2 cleared).","comment":"No drive given"},
        "5016": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: stores the drive in the block, selects it when C' bit 7 is set ($0CC9),\nand reads a leading \"\\\" (B bits 0 and 1); IX+6 bit 3 forces the root.","comment":"The block's drive"},
        "5019": {"comment":"Keeps the flags"},
        "5021": {"comment":"B = 0 for $0CC9"},
        "5023": {"comment":"Look the path up?"},
        "5026": {"comment":"Yes: select the drive"},
        "5030": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5032": {"comment":"A raw name (from the root)?"},
        "5036": {"comment":"Keeps the answer"},
        "5039": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "5042": {"comment":"End of text"},
        "5044": {"comment":"\"\\\"?"},
        "5046": {"comment":"No: put it back"},
        "5048": {"comment":"Yes: B bit 0, a \"\\\" was read"},
        "5050": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: B bit 1, start at the root; A = 0 so nothing is put back.","comment":"Start at the root"},
        "5053": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: puts a non-\"\\\" character back, sets the start directory when C' bit 7 is\nset (PATH_START_DIR), keeps the text position at IY+$5B and goes on with the raw name\n(PATH_RAW_NAME) or the elements (PATH_ELEM_LOOP).","comment":"Not a \"\\\": put it back"},
        "5057": {"comment":"Look the path up?"},
        "5060": {"comment":"Yes: set the start directory"},
        "5064": {"comment":"Keeps the text position"},
        "5071": {"comment":"The raw-name answer"},
        "5072": {"comment":"A raw name"},
        "5074": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: reads each element; one followed by \"\\\" is a directory, looked up and\nentered (PATH_FIND_ELEM), and the \"\\\" is skipped.","comment":"Reads an element"},
        "5077": {"comment":"A \"\\\" after it?"},
        "5079": {"comment":"No: the last element"},
        "5081": {"comment":"Enter the directory"},
        "5084": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5087": {"comment":"Skips the \"\\\""},
        "5092": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: the last element is looked up too when C' bit 0 is set and it has a name\nor an extension (B bits 3, 4).","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5094": {"comment":"Look the last element up?"},
        "5099": {"comment":"A name or a \".\"?"},
        "5102": {"comment":"Yes: look it up"},
        "5105": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: C = the character after the path (0 at the end); clears the word at the\ncaller's HL when flag bit 7 is set, then PATH_CUT_TEXT.","comment":"Keeps the result"},
        "5106": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5109": {"comment":"Not the end: put it back"},
        "5112": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5113": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "5114": {"comment":"The caller's set"},
        "5117": {"comment":"Look the path up?"},
        "5121": {"comment":"Yes: clear the word at HL"},
        "5124": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE: writes 0 at the address kept in IY+$5B, returns the text pointer in DE\nwith the sets left swapped, and Z for A = 0.","comment":"HL = the address kept"},
        "5130": {"comment":"0 there"},
        "5131": {"comment":"DE = the text ..."},
        "5132": {"comment":"... in the parser's set"},
        "5134": {"comment":"Z for A = 0"},
        "5136": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_PARSE, IX+6 bit 3: the rest of the text, case kept, is one raw 11-character\nname up to a \"/\" or the end, padded with spaces; characters past 11 are skipped.","comment":"Keep the case"},
        "5140": {"comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "5141": {"comment":"HL = the name buffer"},
        "5144": {"comment":"11 characters (C counts 12)"},
        "5146": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_RAW_NAME: the buffer is full; C goes back to 1 so further characters are\nskipped.","comment":"C = 1 again (full)"},
        "5147": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_RAW_NAME: reads each character into the buffer (B bits 0 and 3).","comment":"The next character"},
        "5150": {"comment":"End: pad"},
        "5152": {"comment":"\"/\"?"},
        "5154": {"comment":"Yes: put it back, pad"},
        "5156": {"comment":"Something stored ..."},
        "5158": {"comment":"... a name"},
        "5160": {"comment":"Buffer full?"},
        "5163": {"comment":"Stores it"},
        "5167": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_RAW_NAME: puts the \"/\" back.","comment":"Puts the \"/\" back"},
        "5170": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_RAW_NAME: fills the rest of the buffer with spaces.","comment":"Filled?"},
        "5173": {"comment":"A space"},
        "5178": {"synopsis":"Part of PATH_RAW_NAME: A = 0, then PATH_FINISH.","comment":"HL back"},
        "5179": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "5182": {"synopsis":"Reads one path element into the name buffer (NAME_BUFFER) as 8 + 3 characters padded with\nspaces: \".\" and \"..\" are taken whole; else the name part up to a \".\" or a character not\nallowed in a name, then the extension after a \".\".\nEntry: the text at DE' (C' its flags); B = the flags (bits 0-2 kept).\nExit: A = the character that stopped it (unread; 0 at the end); B bit 0 = something stored,\nbit 3 = a name part, bit 4 = a \".\" before an extension, bit 5 = wildcards, bit 6 = \".\" or\n\"..\", bit 7 = \"..\".\nChanges: AF, BC, DE'.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5184": {"comment":"HL = the name buffer"},
        "5187": {"comment":"8 characters of name"},
        "5189": {"comment":"Keeps the low 3 flags"},
        "5193": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "5196": {"comment":"End: an empty name"},
        "5198": {"comment":"\".\"?"},
        "5200": {"comment":"No: put it back, read a name"},
        "5202": {"comment":"One dot"},
        "5204": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "5207": {"comment":"End: \".\""},
        "5209": {"comment":"Allowed in a name?"},
        "5212": {"comment":"Yes: put both back, read a name"},
        "5214": {"comment":"A second \".\"?"},
        "5216": {"comment":"No: put it back, \".\""},
        "5218": {"comment":"\"..\""},
        "5220": {"comment":"Two dots"},
        "5221": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "5224": {"comment":"End: \"..\""},
        "5226": {"comment":"Allowed in a name?"},
        "5229": {"comment":"Yes: put them back, read a name"},
        "5231": {"comment":"A third \".\"?"},
        "5233": {"comment":"Yes: put them back, read a name"},
        "5235": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: the character after \".\" or \"..\" is not a dot: puts it back.","comment":"Puts it back"},
        "5238": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: stores the dots (\".\" or \"..\") and marks B bits 0, 3 and 6.","comment":"A dot"},
        "5241": {"comment":"One less to pad"},
        "5242": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Something stored, a name, dots"},
        "5251": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: puts back three characters (two dots and the next).","comment":"Puts one back"},
        "5254": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: puts back two characters.","comment":"Puts one back"},
        "5257": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: puts back one character.","comment":"Puts one back"},
        "5260": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: copies the name part (8 characters); B bit 3 when it has one.","comment":"The name part"},
        "5263": {"comment":"Anything taken?"},
        "5266": {"comment":"Yes: a name"},
        "5268": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: a \".\" starts the extension (B bit 4) and is skipped.","comment":"\".\"?"},
        "5272": {"comment":"Yes: an extension"},
        "5274": {"comment":"Skips it"},
        "5277": {"synopsis":"Part of PARSE_NAME_ELEM: copies the extension (3 characters) and returns.","comment":"3 characters"},
        "5279": {"comment":"The extension"},
        "5285": {"synopsis":"Copies a name part from the path text to HL: at most C characters, upper case as\nPATH_GET_CHAR gives them; \"*\" fills the rest with \"?\"; characters past C are skipped; the\nrest is padded with spaces. Stops at the end or at a character not allowed in a name, which\nis put back.\nEntry: C = the part's length; HL = where it goes; the text at DE' (C' its flags); B = the\nflags.\nExit: Z; HL past the part; D = 1 when a character was taken, else 0; B bit 0 set for one,\nbit 5 for \"?\" or \"*\"; A = the character that stopped it (0 at the end).\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL, DE'.\nKeeps: E, IX, IY.","comment":"Nothing taken yet"},
        "5287": {"synopsis":"The field is full: C goes back to 1, so the characters that follow are read and dropped.","comment":"C = 1: the next stored character only counts down"},
        "5288": {"synopsis":"Takes the next character of the name text into the field at HL.","comment":"A = the next character (upper case); Z at the end"},
        "5291": {"comment":"End of the text? Pad the field"},
        "5293": {"comment":"A separator?"},
        "5296": {"comment":"Yes: give it back and pad the field"},
        "5298": {"comment":"\"*\"?"},
        "5302": {"comment":"\"?\"?"},
        "5306": {"synopsis":"Marks the name as holding a wildcard (B bit 5)."},
        "5308": {"synopsis":"Stores the character, unless the field is full.","comment":"B bit 0: the name has a character"},
        "5310": {"comment":"D = 1: this field has a character"},
        "5312": {"comment":"Field full? Drop the character"},
        "5315": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "5319": {"synopsis":"\"*\": fills the rest of the field with \"?\" and marks a wildcard."},
        "5320": {"synopsis":"Writes \"?\" until one position is left in C's count."},
        "5321": {"comment":"Last position? Mark the wildcard and go on"},
        "5324": {"comment":"Fill with \"?\""},
        "5329": {"synopsis":"Gives the separator back to the text, then pads the field.","comment":"Step the text pointer back over it"},
        "5332": {"synopsis":"Pads the rest of the field with spaces and returns Z."},
        "5333": {"comment":"Field done: return Z"},
        "5339": {"synopsis":"Tests for a capital letter.\nEntry: A = the character.\nExit: Z (NC) for \"A\"-\"Z\"; NZ otherwise, with carry below \"A\".\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Below \"A\"?"},
        "5342": {"comment":"Above \"Z\"?"},
        "5346": {"comment":"Z: a letter"},
        "5348": {"synopsis":"Not an upper-case letter: returns NZ and NC (A is not 0 here)."},
        "5350": {"synopsis":"Tests whether a character may not be part of a file name: a control code, or one of the 19\nin the table at $1500 (space, tab and : ; . , = + # \\ ! ' < > | / \" [ ]).\nEntry: A = the character.\nExit: Z when it may not; NZ when it may.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A control code?"},
        "5352": {"comment":"No: search the table"},
        "5354": {"comment":"Z: not allowed"},
        "5356": {"synopsis":"Searches all 19 separator characters at $1500 for A."},
        "5358": {"comment":"The 19 characters"},
        "5363": {"comment":"No caller: the same search for space and tab only"},
        "5365": {"comment":"Space and tab, the table's first two"},
        "5368": {"synopsis":"Searches the separator table at $1500 for A; Z when A is in it.","comment":"HL = the separator characters"},
        "5371": {"comment":"Z when found"},
        "5395": {"synopsis":"Reads the next character of the path text at DE' (the alternate set): from segment IY+$2D\npaged into page 1 unless C' bit 3 is set (the text is in view). Unless C' bit 1 is set, a-z\nbecome upper case and \"!\" and \"'\" are taken as \"\\\".\nEntry: DE' = the text; C' = the flags.\nExit: NZ, A = the character, DE' past it; Z, A = 0 at the end (DE' stays).\nChanges: AF, DE'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The text's set"},
        "5397": {"comment":"Text in view?"},
        "5401": {"comment":"Keeps BC'"},
        "5404": {"comment":"B = page 1's segment"},
        "5406": {"comment":"Page 1 = the text's segment"},
        "5411": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5412": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "5414": {"comment":"BC' back"},
        "5415": {"synopsis":"The next character of the text: 0 ends it (Z); C bit 1 asks for it unchanged; otherwise\nlower case becomes upper case and \"!\" or \"'\" become \"\\\".","comment":"End of the text?"},
        "5418": {"comment":"Step past the character"},
        "5419": {"comment":"Raw characters wanted?"},
        "5423": {"comment":"Below \"a\"?"},
        "5427": {"comment":"Above \"z\"?"},
        "5431": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "5433": {"synopsis":"\"!\" and \"'\" stand for the \"\\\" separator.","comment":"\"!\"?"},
        "5437": {"comment":"\"'\"?"},
        "5441": {"synopsis":"Replaces the character with \"\\\"."},
        "5443": {"synopsis":"Returns the character with NZ and NC."},
        "5444": {"synopsis":"Back to the caller's register set."},
        "5446": {"synopsis":"Steps the path text back by one character: DE' - 1.\nEntry: DE' = the text.\nExit: DE' = the text - 1.\nChanges: DE'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5447": {"comment":"Back one character"},
        "5450": {"synopsis":"Sets the directory a path starts in (IY+$30): the root when B bit 1 is set or the drive has\nno current directory (+$1E bit 7 of its parameter block); else walks the drive's\ncurrent-directory path, kept as text at +$20, from the root through PARSE_NAME_ELEM and\n$15D4. When that walk fails, the path text is cleared (+$20 = 0) and the root is used.\nEntry: HL = the drive's parameter block; B = the flags; the path text at DE' (C' its flags).\nExit: A = 0; IY+$30 = the start directory's cluster.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', HL'.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"Keeps the parameter block"},
        "5451": {"comment":"From the root?"},
        "5455": {"comment":"HL = the current directory's cluster ..."},
        "5462": {"comment":"None (bit 7)?"},
        "5466": {"comment":"Z when it is cluster 0"},
        "5468": {"comment":"HL = the block; its +$1F on the stack"},
        "5469": {"comment":"The text's set"},
        "5470": {"comment":"HL = the block + $1F"},
        "5472": {"comment":"Keeps the caller's flags and text"},
        "5474": {"comment":"DE = the kept path text (+$20)"},
        "5476": {"comment":"Text in view"},
        "5478": {"comment":"Look each element up ..."},
        "5482": {"comment":"... unless the start cluster is 0"},
        "5484": {"synopsis":"Starts at the root and walks the drive's stored path text component by component, with the\ndisk searched when no cluster was stored.","comment":"Save the caller's BC and DE"},
        "5487": {"comment":"Begin at the root, the path text empty"},
        "5491": {"synopsis":"One component: parse it, find it, and go on while the text has more.","comment":"Parse the next component into the 11-byte name"},
        "5494": {"comment":"Append it to the path text and find it"},
        "5497": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5500": {"comment":"Text left?"},
        "5503": {"comment":"Yes: the next component"},
        "5505": {"comment":"Never jumps (Z here): hides LD D,$FF at $1582, reached from $157A"},
        "5508": {"comment":"Restore the caller's BC"},
        "5510": {"comment":"Restore the other set's DE and BC"},
        "5513": {"comment":"HL = the drive block's directory word + 1"},
        "5514": {"comment":"Store the directory's cluster in the drive block"},
        "5517": {"comment":"Walked it all? Make it the current directory"},
        "5519": {"comment":"Failed: empty the stored path text"},
        "5523": {"comment":"Then start again at the root"},
        "5524": {"synopsis":"Makes the root the current directory and empties the path text being built.\n1. Puts \":\" after the 64-byte path text at IY+$06DE (the end mark) and points HL' one byte\n   before the text.\n2. Sets the current directory word (IY+$30) to $FF00 + E: the root.\n3. When C' bit 2 is set and that word equals IY+$5E's, sets IY+$5D bit 6.\nEntry: E = the low byte for the directory word; C' bit 2 = compare with IY+$5E.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL' = IY+$06DD; IY+$30-$31 = $FF00 + E.\nError: none (every path returns A = 0).\nChanges: AF, D, HL'.\nKeeps: BC, E, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5525": {"synopsis":"The body of DIR_SET_ROOT; $154D and $1558 also enter here, with HL pushed."},
        "5527": {"comment":"HL' = IY + $071E: the byte after the path text"},
        "5534": {"comment":"\":\" marks the end of the path text"},
        "5536": {"comment":"HL' = IY + $06DD: the text's start - 1"},
        "5542": {"synopsis":"D = $FF: the directory word names the root."},
        "5544": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the current directory (IY+$30) and returns A = 0.","comment":"The current directory's cluster"},
        "5551": {"comment":"Compare it with IY+$5E?"},
        "5556": {"comment":"HL = the word at IY+$5E"},
        "5563": {"comment":"The same directory?"},
        "5567": {"comment":"Yes: IY+$5D bit 6"},
        "5571": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0 and Z."},
        "5574": {"synopsis":"Remembers where an element ended (IY+$5B) and marks B bit 1; when C' bit 7 is set, looks the\nelement up in the directory being searched and enters it ($15D4 on).\nEntry: B = the element's flags; DE' = the text; C' = the flags.\nExit: A = 0 (not looked up, or found).\nError: A = $A8 or $AA from the lookup.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5575": {"comment":"B bit 1"},
        "5578": {"comment":"Look it up?"},
        "5580": {"comment":"Keeps the text position"},
        "5587": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "5588": {"synopsis":"Adds one parsed path component to the path text and, when asked, finds it on the disk.\n1. \".\" keeps the directory, \"..\" cuts the text back to the separator before the last name,\n   any other name is appended as \"\\\" + name, then \".\" + extension when it has one.\n2. A name with a wildcard, or without B bit 3, is refused.\n3. When C' bit 7 is set, the current directory is searched for a directory of that name,\n   which becomes the current directory (IY+$30).\nEntry: B = the component's flags from the parse (bit 3 a name, bit 4 an extension, bit 5 a\nwildcard, bit 6 \".\" or \"..\", bit 7 \"..\"); the name at IY+$06D1 (11 bytes); HL' = the end of\nthe path text; C' bit 7 = search the disk; HL = the drive parameter block.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL' = the new end of the path text; when searched, DE = the found entry.\nError: A = $A8 (\"Invalid pathname string\": the text is full, or the name is not allowed)\nor $AA (\"Directory not found\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, DE, all alternates; the scan state IY+$30-$3B.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5589": {"comment":"HL = the 11-byte name"},
        "5593": {"comment":"Keep the caller's DE, restore HL"},
        "5594": {"comment":"Skips PUSH DE at $15DB, an entry from $3C65"},
        "5596": {"comment":"A = the component's flags"},
        "5598": {"comment":"Save the text pointers"},
        "5600": {"comment":"DE' = the end of the path text"},
        "5601": {"comment":"C' = the flags"},
        "5602": {"comment":"\".\" or \"..\"?"},
        "5606": {"comment":"\"..\"?"},
        "5610": {"synopsis":"\"..\": steps back through the path text to the separator before the last name."},
        "5613": {"comment":"A = the separator character"},
        "5618": {"comment":"Reached it?"},
        "5621": {"comment":"The start of the text?"},
        "5624": {"synopsis":"The path text is full: error $A8."},
        "5625": {"comment":"Restore the text pointers"},
        "5627": {"synopsis":"Returns error $A8 (\"Invalid pathname string\")."},
        "5630": {"comment":"Restore the caller's DE"},
        "5632": {"synopsis":"Appends \"\\\" + the name (spaces dropped), then \".\" + the extension when there is one."},
        "5635": {"comment":"HL = the 11-byte name"},
        "5636": {"comment":"The separator and up to 8 name characters"},
        "5638": {"comment":"A = the separator character"},
        "5644": {"comment":"The text full?"},
        "5646": {"comment":"An extension?"},
        "5648": {"comment":"\".\" and up to 3 extension characters"},
        "5655": {"comment":"The text full?"},
        "5658": {"synopsis":"Checks the component's flags and, when asked, searches the disk for it.","comment":"HL' = the end of the path text"},
        "5659": {"comment":"A = the component's flags"},
        "5660": {"comment":"Restore DE' and C' (bit 7: search the disk)"},
        "5662": {"comment":"A name (bit 3) without a wildcard (bit 5)?"},
        "5668": {"comment":"Search the disk?"},
        "5672": {"comment":"No: done, A = 0"},
        "5673": {"comment":"Start the scan of the current directory"},
        "5676": {"synopsis":"Compares each entry with the name until a directory of that name is found.","comment":"The end of the directory?"},
        "5680": {"comment":"HL = the 11-byte name"},
        "5683": {"comment":"Does the entry match?"},
        "5690": {"comment":"A directory (attribute bit 4)?"},
        "5694": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next entry; C at the end of the directory."},
        "5699": {"synopsis":"Returns error $AA (\"Directory not found\")."},
        "5702": {"synopsis":"Makes the directory whose entry DE points at the one to search: its start cluster (the\nentry's word at +$1A) goes to IY+$30; cluster 0 means the root ($FF00). With C' bit 2 set, a\nstart cluster equal to IY+$5E sets IY+$5D bit 6 ($15A8 on).\nEntry: DE = the directory entry.\nExit: Z, A = 0; IY+$30 = the directory's start cluster.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps HL (popped at $15C4)"},
        "5703": {"comment":"HL = the entry's start cluster"},
        "5710": {"comment":"0 (the root)?"},
        "5712": {"comment":"No: that cluster"},
        "5715": {"comment":"Yes: the root"},
        "5718": {"synopsis":"Copies the name's next character, skipping spaces."},
        "5720": {"comment":"Spaces are dropped"},
        "5724": {"synopsis":"Stores A and copies up to B - 1 more characters from the name at HL into the path text at\nDE, skipping spaces; stops when the text is full (the \":\" end mark is next).\nEntry: A = the first character to store; B = 1 + the characters to copy; HL = the name;\nDE = where the text goes.\nExit: NZ, NC; DE = past the copied text; HL = past the name.\nError: Z, A = 0 when the text is full.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY."},
        "5726": {"comment":"The next text byte the \":\" end mark?"},
        "5730": {"synopsis":"Counts the name character; the end returns NZ (A is not 0 here)."},
        "5734": {"synopsis":"Gives the 11-byte name buffer (8 + 3 characters).\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's variables.\nExit: HL = IY+$6D1.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "5738": {"comment":"HL = IY+$6D1"},
        "5744": {"synopsis":"Compares the directory entry at DE with the 11-byte name at HL: \"?\" in the name matches any\ncharacter, letters match in either case, and bit 7 is ignored. When IX+6 bit 3 asks for the\nvolume label, any name matches. The entry's volume bit (attribute bit 3) must agree with\nIX+6 bit 3.\nEntry: DE = the directory entry; HL = the name; IX = the request block.\nExit: C set when it matches: A = the entry's attribute byte, HL = the entry + $0B.\nError: NC: Z when the entry is free (A = 0, the end of the directory, or $E5, deleted), NZ\nwhen it does not match.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY.","comment":"The end of the directory?"},
        "5747": {"comment":"A deleted entry?"},
        "5751": {"comment":"11 characters"},
        "5753": {"comment":"C = the request's flags (bit 3: volume label)"},
        "5756": {"comment":"$05 in an entry stands for a first character $E5"},
        "5760": {"comment":"Compare $E5 then"},
        "5762": {"synopsis":"Compares one character.","comment":"Volume label: any name"},
        "5766": {"comment":"The same, bit 7 aside?"},
        "5771": {"comment":"Only the case differs?"},
        "5775": {"comment":"And a letter?"},
        "5779": {"synopsis":"\"?\" in the name matches anything.","comment":"\"?\"?"},
        "5784": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next character; after 11 checks the volume bit."},
        "5789": {"comment":"HL = the entry's attribute byte"},
        "5791": {"comment":"Both volume labels, or neither?"},
        "5796": {"comment":"A = the attribute; C: a match"},
        "5798": {"comment":"Skips OR A at $16A7, the no-match exit (NC)"},
        "5802": {"synopsis":"Starts a search of the directory whose start cluster is at IY+$30 (bit 7 of the high byte\nset: the root): DE = that cluster, then on at $16AE.\nEntry: IY+$30 = the directory's start cluster; HL = the drive's parameter block.\nExit: as $16AE on.","comment":"DE = IY+$30 (byte $30 follows)"},
        "5806": {"synopsis":"The rest of the scan start at $16AA, with DE = the current directory's word (IY+$30): the\nroot ($FFxx) takes its place from the drive parameter block, another directory is walked\nfrom its cluster.","comment":"The root?"},
        "5812": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block + $0F"},
        "5816": {"comment":"C = the root's last part-sector entries (+$0F)"},
        "5818": {"comment":"A = the root's whole sectors (+$10)"},
        "5821": {"comment":"DE = the root's first sector (+$12)"},
        "5825": {"comment":"$FF + C for both cluster words: no next cluster"},
        "5831": {"synopsis":"Gives the current directory entry again after the position was restored: counts one more\nentry left in the sector (IY+$39) and takes a step of 0 bytes through the stepping code at\n$16D4, which comes back with DE = the entry in its sector buffer.\nEntry: DE = the current entry; IY+$30 on, the directory position.\nExit: DE = the entry (from $16D4 on).","comment":"Undoes the step's count of one entry"},
        "5834": {"comment":"Keeps BC"},
        "5835": {"comment":"A step of 0 bytes ($16D0's is $20)"},
        "5840": {"synopsis":"Steps the directory scan to the next 32-byte entry, reading the next sector, and the next\ncluster from the FAT, when needed.\nEntry: DE = the current entry; HL = the drive parameter block; IY+$32-$3B = the scan state.\nExit: NC; DE = the next entry; A = its first byte, Z when 0 (the end mark).\nError: C set (NZ) when the directory has no more entries (its sectors or chain ended).\nChanges: AF, DE, all alternates; the scan state.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5841": {"comment":"The next entry: 32 bytes on"},
        "5844": {"synopsis":"Moves DE on by BC and loads the current sector number."},
        "5845": {"comment":"HL = the entry + BC"},
        "5847": {"comment":"DE = the sector (IY+$36)"},
        "5851": {"synopsis":"Counts the entry; the sector's last one moves on to the next sector.","comment":"A = the entries left in the sector - 1"},
        "5855": {"comment":"The sector done?"},
        "5857": {"comment":"The sector buffer still valid (IY+$63 bit 2 clear)?"},
        "5864": {"comment":"No: read the sector again"},
        "5866": {"synopsis":"Releases the sector buffer and moves to the next sector of the cluster, then of the chain.","comment":"IX = the drive parameter block"},
        "5876": {"comment":"HL = the drive parameter block"},
        "5877": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "5878": {"comment":"Sectors left in the cluster?"},
        "5884": {"comment":"A last part-sector (the root)?"},
        "5889": {"comment":"DE = the next cluster (IY+$34)"},
        "5893": {"synopsis":"$FFxx as the next cluster ends the directory: C set.","comment":"No next cluster?"},
        "5895": {"comment":"C: the end of the directory"},
        "5898": {"synopsis":"Enters cluster DE: finds the one after it in the FAT and its first sector."},
        "5900": {"comment":"DE = the next cluster from the FAT"},
        "5903": {"comment":"BC = the next cluster"},
        "5908": {"comment":"DE = the cluster's first sector"},
        "5913": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block + $0A"},
        "5917": {"comment":"A = the sectors in a cluster (the byte + 1)"},
        "5922": {"comment":"No last part-sector"},
        "5924": {"synopsis":"Stores the part-sector count, the next cluster and the cluster.","comment":"The last part-sector's entries"},
        "5928": {"comment":"The next cluster"},
        "5935": {"comment":"The cluster"},
        "5941": {"synopsis":"A whole sector: 16 entries."},
        "5943": {"synopsis":"No whole sectors left: the last part-sector, counted once.","comment":"Whole sectors left?"},
        "5946": {"comment":"B = the part-sector's entries"},
        "5949": {"comment":"Counted once"},
        "5952": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "5953": {"synopsis":"Stores the sector count, the sector and its entry count, then reads the sector.","comment":"The sectors left"},
        "5956": {"comment":"The sector"},
        "5962": {"comment":"The entries in the sector"},
        "5967": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector and points DE at the entry the count gives.","comment":"IX = the drive parameter block"},
        "5969": {"comment":"Keep the entries left"},
        "5970": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Read it: HL = the buffer, the data at HL + $0B"},
        "5975": {"comment":"B = the entries left"},
        "5978": {"comment":"Back $15: the first entry is $20 on"},
        "5982": {"comment":"A = the entry's place in the sector, from 1"},
        "5990": {"synopsis":"Steps HL on $20 bytes per entry."},
        "5999": {"synopsis":"Stores the entries left and returns the entry.","comment":"The entries left in the sector"},
        "6002": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "6005": {"comment":"A = its first byte; Z when 0 (the end mark)"},
        "6008": {"synopsis":"Function 1 (table $0552): parses a file specification (drive, path and name) for the request\nblock at DE without reading the disk (C bits 2 and 7 cleared), and unless C bit 0 is set\ncopies the parsed 11-byte name into the block at +8.\nEntry: HL = the specification text (in the caller's segment); DE = the request block; C bit\n0 = do not copy the name.\nExit: A = 0; IX = the block.\nError: A = the parse's error code, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "6010": {"comment":"IX = the request block"},
        "6013": {"comment":"No IY+$5E check, no disk"},
        "6017": {"comment":"HL = the block, DE = the text"},
        "6018": {"comment":"Parse the specification"},
        "6021": {"comment":"L = the caller's C"},
        "6024": {"comment":"Name wanted?"},
        "6029": {"comment":"DE = the block's name (+8)"},
        "6037": {"comment":"HL = the parsed 11-byte name"},
        "6046": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0."},
        "6047": {"synopsis":"Restores HL and returns."},
        "6049": {"synopsis":"Function 2 (table $0554): resolves a path on the disk and makes it the drive's current\ndirectory: its cluster word goes to the drive block's +$1E and its path text to +$20.\nEntry: HL = the path text (in the caller's segment).\nExit: A = 0; HL = the path text at IY+$06DE.\nError: A = the parse's error code, or $A8 (\"Invalid pathname string\") when C is not 0 after\nthe parse, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.","comment":"DE = the path text"},
        "6051": {"comment":"Search the disk (bit 7), flag bit 0"},
        "6053": {"comment":"Parse and walk the path with the work block"},
        "6057": {"comment":"Anything left in C?"},
        "6061": {"comment":"HL = the drive block + $1E"},
        "6065": {"comment":"DE = the current directory's word (IY+$30)"},
        "6069": {"synopsis":"Stores the directory word and copies the path text after it."},
        "6073": {"comment":"DE = the drive block's path text (+$20)"},
        "6074": {"comment":"HL = the path text just built"},
        "6077": {"synopsis":"Copies the path text up to and with its 0."},
        "6080": {"comment":"The 0 copied?"},
        "6083": {"synopsis":"Points HL at the path text buffer (IY+$06DE, 64 bytes, ended by 0).\nEntry: IY = the work area.\nExit: HL = IY + $06DE.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "6093": {"synopsis":"Function 3 (table $0556): walks drive B's stored current directory again (an empty path) and\nreturns its path text.\nEntry: B = the drive.\nExit: A = 0; HL = the path text at IY+$06DE.\nError: A = $AF (\"Invalid drive\") with Z; or the walk's error code, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates."},
        "6094": {"comment":"A = the drive, 0 when there is none"},
        "6099": {"comment":"No such drive?"},
        "6103": {"comment":"Search the disk"},
        "6105": {"comment":"An empty path text"},
        "6108": {"comment":"Walk the drive's stored path"},
        "6114": {"synopsis":"Function 7 (table $055E): creates a directory (attribute $10) through DIR_CREATE_ENT.\nEntry: DE = the request block (the name at +8); BC = the result buffer.\nExit: as DIR_CREATE_ENT.\nError: A = $A1 (\"Invalid file attributes\") for a volume label request (IX+6 bit 3), NZ; or\nDIR_CREATE_ENT's errors.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates."},
        "6117": {"comment":"A volume label?"},
        "6124": {"comment":"The directory attribute, Z"},
        "6126": {"synopsis":"Function 6 (table $055C) and the body of 4, 5 and 7: finds the name of the request block in\nits directory and, when IY+$5D bit 7 is clear, creates an entry for it.\n1. Checks the name (CHECK_FILENAME) and stores the mode in IY+$5D: the attribute ($00 a\n   file, $10 a directory), or $80 to find only (function 4 enters at $17F8, function 5 at\n   DIR_SEARCH_ON).\n2. Resolves the path and starts the scan ($12CF), then searches (DIR_FIND_ENT).\n3. An existing entry is refused, or a file taken over (DELETE_ENTRY); a new one goes in the\n   first free slot seen, or a new cluster of the directory; a directory gets a cleared\n   cluster of its own.\n4. Writes $FE, the block's bytes 1-7 and the 32-byte entry to the result buffer (BC), saves\n   the scan state at the block's +$17 and returns HL = the path text.\nEntry: A = the attribute and Z (the dispatcher passes A = 0); DE = the request block; BC =\nthe result buffer (40 bytes).\nExit: A = 0; DE = the block; HL = the path text at IY+$06DE.\nError: A = $A6 (\"Invalid file name\"), $97 (\"File exists\"), $98 (\"Directory exists\"), $99\n(\"System file exists\"), $A7, $95, $AC (\"Disk full\"), $AD (\"Root directory full\"), $CF (not\nfound, finding only), or the parse's error, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.","comment":"Keep the attribute and its Z in AF'"},
        "6128": {"comment":"IX = the request block"},
        "6130": {"comment":"A file name without wildcards?"},
        "6134": {"comment":"A = the attribute, Z"},
        "6135": {"comment":"Never jumps (Z here): hides LD A,$80 at $17F8, function 4's entry"},
        "6138": {"comment":"The mode: the attribute, or $80 to find only"},
        "6141": {"comment":"Resolve the path and start the scan"},
        "6145": {"comment":"NC: the scan goes on from the current entry"},
        "6146": {"comment":"Keep the result buffer's address"},
        "6149": {"synopsis":"Function 5 (table $055A): goes on with the search that the request block's saved scan state\n(+$17) describes, from the entry after the last one found.\nEntry: DE = the request block; BC = the result buffer.\nExit: A = 0; the next matching entry in the result buffer (as DIR_CREATE_ENT).\nError: A = $CF when no more entries match, or the disk's error, NZ.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"The mode: find only"},
        "6153": {"comment":"Restore the saved scan state"},
        "6157": {"comment":"Keep the result buffer's address"},
        "6158": {"comment":"The entry after the last one found"},
        "6161": {"synopsis":"Searches the directory; a match goes to FIND_FOUND, no match finds a free slot or fails.","comment":"C: a match"},
        "6166": {"comment":"Finding only?"},
        "6170": {"comment":"Not found when finding only"},
        "6172": {"comment":"Creating: back to the free slot"},
        "6175": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6179": {"synopsis":"The name exists: when finding, return it; when creating, refuse it or take the file over.","comment":"Finding only? Return the entry"},
        "6185": {"comment":"A system file (attribute bit 2)?"},
        "6189": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "6191": {"comment":"\"Directory exists\""},
        "6195": {"comment":"Creating a directory?"},
        "6199": {"comment":"\"File exists\""},
        "6201": {"comment":"Never jumps (NC here): hides LD A,$99 at $183A, reached from $182B"},
        "6204": {"comment":"A file: delete the old entry to reuse it"},
        "6207": {"comment":"Refused?"},
        "6209": {"synopsis":"Builds the attribute; a directory gets a new cleared cluster.","comment":"A directory being made?"},
        "6214": {"comment":"BC = 0: no cluster for a file"},
        "6216": {"comment":"The archive bit"},
        "6220": {"comment":"A cluster for the directory, cleared"},
        "6227": {"synopsis":"Fails when the allocation (or the free slot) failed."},
        "6229": {"comment":"The directory attribute"},
        "6231": {"synopsis":"Writes the new entry: the block's name, the attribute (the volume bit from IX+6), the\ncluster and the time."},
        "6232": {"comment":"Read the current entry again: DE"},
        "6235": {"comment":"HL = the request block"},
        "6241": {"comment":"The volume bit from the request"},
        "6247": {"comment":"HL = the block's name (+8)"},
        "6252": {"comment":"Write the directory entry"},
        "6255": {"synopsis":"Success: A = 0."},
        "6256": {"synopsis":"Fills the result buffer: $FE, the block's bytes 1-7, then the 32-byte entry.","comment":"HL = the result buffer"},
        "6260": {"comment":"DE = the request block"},
        "6263": {"comment":"$FE first"},
        "6267": {"comment":"The block's bytes 1-7"},
        "6274": {"comment":"The entry's first byte"},
        "6275": {"comment":"$05 stands for $E5"},
        "6281": {"synopsis":"Copies the first byte and the other 31."},
        "6284": {"comment":"The other 31 bytes"},
        "6289": {"synopsis":"Saves the scan state at the block's +$17 and returns with the path text.","comment":"HL = IY+$30, DE = IX+$17, BC = 12"},
        "6295": {"comment":"DE = the request block"},
        "6298": {"comment":"Restore BC"},
        "6299": {"comment":"HL = the path text"},
        "6302": {"synopsis":"Checks the request block's 8.3 name: the name may not start with a space, and no field may\nhold a separator, \"?\" or \"*\", or a character after a space. A volume label is not checked.\nEntry: IX = the request block (+6 bit 3 volume label, +8 the 11-byte name).\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = $A6 (\"Invalid file name\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A volume label?"},
        "6309": {"comment":"HL = the block's name (+8)"},
        "6316": {"comment":"8 name characters; it may not start with a space"},
        "6323": {"comment":"3 extension characters, which may all be spaces"},
        "6331": {"synopsis":"Checks one field of B characters at HL.\nEntry: A = the character the field may not start with; B = the field length; HL = the field.\nExit: A = 0, Z; HL = past the field.\nError: A = $A6 (\"Invalid file name\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"The first character not allowed?"},
        "6334": {"synopsis":"Checks one character."},
        "6336": {"comment":"A space: only spaces may follow"},
        "6340": {"comment":"A separator?"},
        "6345": {"comment":"\"?\"?"},
        "6349": {"comment":"\"*\"?"},
        "6355": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0, Z."},
        "6357": {"synopsis":"Takes the next character after a space."},
        "6359": {"synopsis":"The rest of the field must be spaces.","comment":"Not a space?"},
        "6366": {"synopsis":"Returns error $A6 (\"Invalid file name\")."},
        "6370": {"synopsis":"Writes a new directory entry: the 11-byte name (a first byte $E5 stored as $05), the\nattribute, zeros, the start cluster, then the time and date; marks the sector buffer\nchanged.\nEntry: DE = the entry; HL = the name; A = the attribute; BC = the start cluster (bit 7 of B\nset: none, 0 is written).\nExit: AF and AF' swapped ($190C).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, AF'.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY."},
        "6372": {"comment":"B = the attribute"},
        "6374": {"comment":"$E5 would read as deleted?"},
        "6378": {"comment":"It is stored as $05"},
        "6380": {"synopsis":"Stores the name and the attribute."},
        "6384": {"comment":"The other 10 name bytes"},
        "6389": {"comment":"The attribute (+$0B)"},
        "6391": {"comment":"20 bytes, +$0C to +$1F"},
        "6393": {"synopsis":"Clears the rest of the entry (C = 0 after the copy)."},
        "6404": {"synopsis":"Stores the start cluster at +$1A and stamps the time.","comment":"HL = the entry + $1B"},
        "6408": {"comment":"The start cluster"},
        "6411": {"comment":"Restore DE"},
        "6412": {"comment":"Swap in AF'"},
        "6413": {"synopsis":"Writes the current time (+$16) and date (+$18) into the directory entry at DE and marks the\nsector buffer changed.\nEntry: DE = the directory entry.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "6416": {"comment":"HL = the entry's time field"},
        "6423": {"comment":"The sector buffer changed"},
        "6430": {"synopsis":"Reads the clock (EXOS 32 and 34) and writes the time and the date in the disk's packed\nform: hours x 2048 + minutes x 32 + seconds / 2, then (year - 1980) x 512 + month x 32 +\nday, each least significant byte first.\nEntry: HL = 4 bytes.\nExit: the 4 bytes written; HL = the last.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "6432": {"comment":"C = the hours, binary"},
        "6437": {"comment":"A = the minutes, binary"},
        "6441": {"comment":"Minutes x 4"},
        "6443": {"comment":"Three more shifts into C"},
        "6445": {"synopsis":"Shifts the minutes' top bits into C: C:A = hours x 2048 + minutes x 32; then the seconds\nand the date."},
        "6450": {"comment":"D = the low byte so far"},
        "6451": {"comment":"A = the seconds, binary"},
        "6455": {"comment":"Seconds / 2"},
        "6458": {"comment":"The time, low byte first"},
        "6461": {"comment":"HL = the date's place"},
        "6466": {"comment":"C = the years, binary"},
        "6471": {"comment":"A = the month, binary"},
        "6475": {"comment":"Month bits 0-2 to bits 5-7, bit 3 to carry"},
        "6479": {"comment":"C = years x 2 + month bit 3"},
        "6482": {"comment":"A = the day, binary"},
        "6487": {"comment":"The date, low byte first"},
        "6491": {"synopsis":"Turns a BCD byte into binary: tens x 10 + units.\nEntry: A = the BCD byte.\nExit: A = its value.\nChanges: AF, B.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "6492": {"comment":"B = tens x 8"},
        "6496": {"comment":"Tens x 2"},
        "6498": {"comment":"+ tens x 8"},
        "6501": {"comment":"+ the units"},
        "6505": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next entry first."},
        "6508": {"synopsis":"Searches the rest of the directory for the request block's name, remembering the first free\nslot (a deleted entry, or the end mark) when none is saved yet.\nEntry: C set when the directory has already ended; DE = the current entry; HL = the drive\nparameter block; IX = the request block.\nExit: C set: DE = the matching entry, A = its attribute.\nError: NC, A = 0, Z: no match before the end.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates; the scan state; IY+$3C-$47 and IY+$5D bit 0.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The end of the directory?"},
        "6512": {"comment":"HL = the block's name (+8)"},
        "6517": {"comment":"Does the entry match?"},
        "6521": {"comment":"Yes: C"},
        "6522": {"comment":"An entry in use: the next"},
        "6524": {"comment":"A free slot saved already?"},
        "6528": {"comment":"No: save this one"},
        "6531": {"comment":"A deleted entry: go on; 0 is the end"},
        "6534": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0, NC: not found."},
        "6536": {"synopsis":"Saves the scan state (IY+$30-$3B) at IY+$3C as the free slot and sets IY+$5D bit 0.\nEntry: IY = the work area.\nExit: none.\nChanges: F, BC.\nKeeps: A, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "6541": {"comment":"HL = IY+$30, DE = IY+$3C"},
        "6554": {"synopsis":"Moves the scan back to the saved free slot; without one, adds a cluster to the directory\nand moves into it. The sector buffer must be read again (IY+$63 bit 2).\nEntry: HL = the drive parameter block; IX = the request block.\nExit: A = 0, Z; the scan state at the free slot (or at the new cluster's first entry).\nError: A = $AD (\"Root directory full\") or $AC (\"Disk full\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "6558": {"comment":"A free slot saved?"},
        "6568": {"comment":"HL = IY+$3C, DE = IY+$30"},
        "6576": {"synopsis":"No free slot: the directory needs a new cluster.","comment":"DE = the directory's cluster (IY+$32)"},
        "6580": {"synopsis":"The root cannot grow; another directory gets a cleared cluster linked after this one.","comment":"The root?"},
        "6585": {"comment":"A cleared cluster: BC"},
        "6590": {"comment":"Link it after cluster DE in the FAT"},
        "6594": {"comment":"The next cluster"},
        "6600": {"comment":"Step into it"},
        "6603": {"synopsis":"Allocates one cluster and clears it (IY+$48 bit 1), through ALLOC_CLUSTERS.\nEntry: HL = the drive parameter block.\nExit: A = 0; BC = the new cluster.\nError: A = $AC (\"Disk full\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, all alternates.\nKeeps: DE, IX.","comment":"One cluster"},
        "6606": {"comment":"Clear it"},
        "6610": {"synopsis":"Allocates BC free clusters as a chain, the search starting from the cluster that FAT entry 1\nholds (the search goes on at $19DD); IY+$48 bit 1 asks for each to be cleared.\nEntry: BC = the clusters wanted; HL = the drive parameter block.\nExit: A = 0; BC = the new chain's first cluster.\nError: A = $AC (\"Disk full\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, all alternates.\nKeeps: DE, IX."},
        "6611": {"comment":"FAT entry 1"},
        "6614": {"comment":"DE = its value"},
        "6621": {"synopsis":"Allocation loop: keeps the clusters still to allocate and the last cluster of the chain on\nthe stack, then searches for the next free cluster (CHAIN_FIND_FREE).","comment":"Clusters still to allocate"},
        "6622": {"comment":"Last cluster of the chain (1 at the start)"},
        "6623": {"synopsis":"Scans the FAT upwards from cluster DE + 1 for a free entry (0), links it to the last cluster\nof the chain, clears it when bit 1 of IY+$48 is set, and goes on until the count on the\nstack is used up; then ends the chain with $FFF. A run that reaches the disk's last cluster\ngoes to CHAIN_DISK_FULL.","comment":"Next cluster to try"},
        "6624": {"comment":"HL = the drive's parameter block"},
        "6625": {"comment":"HL+$16 = the cluster count + 2 (one past the last)"},
        "6633": {"comment":"Past the last cluster?"},
        "6636": {"comment":"Yes: the disk is full"},
        "6639": {"comment":"DE = the cluster's FAT entry"},
        "6642": {"comment":"Entry 0 (free)?"},
        "6645": {"comment":"No: try the next cluster"},
        "6647": {"comment":"BC = the free cluster"},
        "6649": {"comment":"DE = the last cluster of the chain"},
        "6651": {"comment":"Link it to the free cluster"},
        "6654": {"comment":"DE = the new cluster, now the chain's last"},
        "6658": {"comment":"Clear new clusters?"},
        "6662": {"comment":"Yes: zero its sectors"},
        "6666": {"comment":"BC = clusters still to allocate"},
        "6667": {"comment":"One less"},
        "6670": {"comment":"More to allocate: search on from this cluster"},
        "6672": {"comment":"End of chain mark"},
        "6675": {"comment":"Ends the chain at the last new cluster"},
        "6678": {"comment":"FAT entry 1 holds the chain's first cluster"},
        "6681": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6684": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "6687": {"synopsis":"The disk ran out of free clusters: frees every cluster this call allocated (the chain hung\non FAT entry 1) and leaves with error $AC (Disk full) through CHAIN_RESTORE_1.","comment":"Drops the last cluster of the chain"},
        "6688": {"comment":"Drops the count still to allocate"},
        "6689": {"comment":"The chain starts at FAT entry 1"},
        "6692": {"comment":"Frees entry 1 and the clusters linked from it"},
        "6695": {"comment":"Error code $AC (Disk full)"},
        "6697": {"synopsis":"The end of the allocation that starts at $19CB: puts back FAT entry 1, which the allocation\nused as the head of the new chain, and returns. BC = the value entry 1 held (the first new\ncluster on success), A = 0 with Z on success or the error code with NZ; DE = the caller's\nDE.","comment":"BC = entry 1's value before the allocation"},
        "6698": {"comment":"Keeps the result code"},
        "6699": {"comment":"DE = entry 1's value now (the chain's head)"},
        "6700": {"comment":"FAT entry 1"},
        "6703": {"comment":"Puts its old value back"},
        "6706": {"comment":"BC = the chain's first cluster"},
        "6708": {"comment":"Z when A = 0 (done), NZ for an error"},
        "6709": {"comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "6711": {"synopsis":"Zeroes every sector of a newly allocated cluster, last sector first, through the sector\nbuffers (each one marked changed). When bit 2 of IY+$48 is set (a directory is being made)\nit then writes the \".\" entry (pointing at the cluster itself) and the \"..\" entry (pointing\nat the cluster held at IY+$30/$31) into the cluster's first sector, both with attributes\n$12.\nEntry: BC = the cluster; HL = the drive's parameter block (+$0A sectors per cluster); IY =\nEXDOS's variables.\nExit: the cluster's sectors are zero in the buffers.\nChanges: AF, DE, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the sector buffers.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the cluster"},
        "6712": {"comment":"DE = the cluster"},
        "6715": {"comment":"HL+$0A = sectors per cluster"},
        "6719": {"comment":"B = sectors per cluster"},
        "6721": {"comment":"A = sector offset: one past the cluster's last"},
        "6722": {"comment":"DE = that sector's number"},
        "6725": {"comment":"A = sectors per cluster"},
        "6726": {"comment":"A = sectors to clear + 1; NZ, so the first pass reads nothing"},
        "6727": {"comment":"BC = the cluster"},
        "6728": {"synopsis":"Clears A sectors of a drive, from sector DE downwards: each gets a buffer without being read\n($0AE0 with B = 0), 512 zero bytes and the changed mark. After the first, each buffer is\nmoved to the head of the chain first (BUF_TO_HEAD). When bit 2 of IY+$48 is set (a new\ndirectory), the lowest sector then gets the \".\" entry and the \"..\" entry, whose cluster is\nthe word at IY+$30, through $18E2.\nEntry: A = the sector count; DE = the highest sector; HL = the drive's record; F: Z moves\nthe first sector's buffer to the head too; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: DE = the lowest sector - 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"IX = the parameter block, the caller's IX on the stack"},
        "6729": {"comment":"IX = the drive's record, its own IX on the stack"},
        "6731": {"comment":"Keeps the cluster"},
        "6732": {"comment":"B = the sector count"},
        "6733": {"synopsis":"Gets a buffer for sector DE (after the first pass, through $09FC) and zeroes its 512 data\nbytes.","comment":"Keeps the count"},
        "6734": {"comment":"Not the first pass: calls $09FC first"},
        "6737": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "6739": {"comment":"HL = the buffer for sector DE"},
        "6742": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer"},
        "6743": {"comment":"The data starts after the buffer's 11-byte header"},
        "6747": {"comment":"A = 0, B = 0: 256 passes of 2 bytes"},
        "6748": {"synopsis":"Zero-fill loop for the buffer's 512 bytes; then moves to the previous sector, and after the\nlast writes the \".\" and \"..\" entries when a directory is being made.","comment":"Zeroes two bytes"},
        "6752": {"comment":"512 bytes in all"},
        "6754": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "6757": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "6758": {"comment":"B = sectors still to clear"},
        "6759": {"comment":"The previous sector"},
        "6760": {"comment":"Z: later passes call $09FC"},
        "6761": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "6763": {"comment":"BC = the cluster"},
        "6764": {"comment":"Making a directory?"},
        "6768": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "6770": {"comment":"DE = the first entry of the first sector"},
        "6775": {"comment":"HL = the name \".\" padded with spaces"},
        "6778": {"comment":"Attributes $12"},
        "6780": {"comment":"Writes the \".\" entry, cluster BC"},
        "6783": {"comment":"DE = the second entry"},
        "6788": {"comment":"HL = the name \"..\" padded with spaces"},
        "6791": {"comment":"BC = the parent directory's cluster"},
        "6797": {"comment":"Attributes $12"},
        "6799": {"comment":"Writes the \"..\" entry"},
        "6802": {"synopsis":"Puts back the caller's IX and HL and returns.","comment":"IX = the caller's IX"},
        "6804": {"comment":"HL = the drive's parameter block"},
        "6818": {"synopsis":"Frees a cluster chain: sets the FAT entry of DE and of every cluster linked from it to 0.\nStops at an entry that was 0 or at the end-of-chain mark ($FFFF from $1148).\nEntry: DE = the first cluster; HL = the drive's parameter block.\nExit: Z with A = 0 when the last entry was 0; NZ when the chain ended with an end mark.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the FAT.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the cluster"},
        "6819": {"comment":"DE = its FAT entry (the next cluster)"},
        "6822": {"comment":"BC = the cluster"},
        "6823": {"comment":"Keeps the next cluster"},
        "6826": {"comment":"Free"},
        "6829": {"comment":"Sets the cluster's FAT entry to 0"},
        "6832": {"comment":"DE = the next cluster"},
        "6833": {"comment":"Was the entry 0?"},
        "6836": {"comment":"End mark ($FFFF)?"},
        "6838": {"comment":"No: free the next one"},
        "6841": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 8 (table $0550): deletes the file or the empty directory whose descriptor is\nat DE.\n1. Finds its directory entry ($12F9).\n2. A directory: refuses \".\" and \"..\", enters it and checks every entry is \".\", \"..\" or\n   empty, then finds the entry again.\n3. Refuses a read-only file, and a file whose first cluster and drive match the ones\n   recorded at IY+$60-$62 while bit 1 of IY-$37 is set.\n4. Frees the cluster chain, keeps the name's first character at entry+$0C and marks the\n   entry deleted ($E5).\nEntry: DE = the file's descriptor (first byte $FE); HL = passed on to $12F9 and $1268.\nExit: A = 0 with Z.\nError: NZ (or C from the \".\" check) with A = the error code: $9E (Invalid . or ..\noperations), $A5 (Directory not empty), $A7 (Read only file), $95 (File cannot be copied\nonto itself), or one from $12F9.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the directory, the FAT.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"BC = HL, kept for finding the entry again"},
        "6843": {"comment":"DE = the entry, IX = the descriptor, A = attributes"},
        "6846": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "6847": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "6849": {"comment":"No: delete the file"},
        "6851": {"comment":"Is it \".\" or \"..\"?"},
        "6854": {"comment":"Yes: error $9E"},
        "6855": {"comment":"Enters the directory"},
        "6858": {"comment":"Its first entry"},
        "6861": {"synopsis":"Walks the directory being deleted: any entry other than \".\", \"..\" or an empty one stops with\nerror $A5 (Directory not empty).","comment":"End of the directory: it is empty"},
        "6863": {"comment":"Empty, \".\" or \"..\"?"},
        "6866": {"comment":"Error code $A5 (Directory not empty)"},
        "6868": {"comment":"No: the directory has a file"},
        "6869": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "6872": {"comment":"Not past the end: check it"},
        "6874": {"synopsis":"The directory is empty: finds its own entry again from the descriptor and clears the word at\nHL+$1E ($0EC3).","comment":"DE = the descriptor"},
        "6877": {"comment":"HL = the caller's HL again"},
        "6879": {"comment":"Finds the entry again"},
        "6882": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "6883": {"comment":"Clears the word at HL+$1E"},
        "6886": {"synopsis":"Deletes the entry: refuses a read-only file, frees the chain and marks the entry deleted.","comment":"Calls $1268 with HL"},
        "6889": {"synopsis":"Deletes the current directory entry: frees its cluster chain and marks it deleted ($E5,\nits first byte kept at +$0C).\nEntry: DE = the current entry; HL = the drive parameter block.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = $A7 (\"Read only file\") for attribute bit 0; A = $95 (\"File cannot be copied onto\nitself\") when IY-$37 bit 1 is set and its drive (IY+$2B) and start cluster are those at\nIY+$60-$62; NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Read the entry again: DE"},
        "6893": {"comment":"HL = the attribute byte"},
        "6898": {"comment":"Read only?"},
        "6900": {"comment":"Error code $A7 (Read only file)"},
        "6903": {"comment":"Yes: refused"},
        "6906": {"comment":"HL = the start cluster's place (+$1A)"},
        "6910": {"comment":"DE = the start cluster"},
        "6913": {"comment":"The file open for a copy?"},
        "6917": {"comment":"No"},
        "6919": {"comment":"The same drive?"},
        "6925": {"comment":"No"},
        "6927": {"comment":"The same start cluster?"},
        "6933": {"comment":"The same cluster?"},
        "6935": {"comment":"Yes: error $95"},
        "6937": {"synopsis":"Frees the file's cluster chain (when it has one) and marks the entry deleted, the old first\ncharacter kept at entry+$0C.","comment":"HL = the caller's HL"},
        "6938": {"comment":"Any cluster?"},
        "6940": {"comment":"Yes: frees the chain"},
        "6943": {"comment":"DE = the entry pointer kept at $1AF8"},
        "6944": {"comment":"DE = the directory entry"},
        "6948": {"comment":"HL = entry+$0C"},
        "6952": {"comment":"Keeps the name's first character there"},
        "6954": {"comment":"Deleted mark"},
        "6957": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "6963": {"synopsis":"The file matches the one recorded at IY+$60-$62: leaves with error $95 (File cannot be\ncopied onto itself), NZ.","comment":"Error code $95"},
        "6967": {"comment":"NZ: an error"},
        "6969": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the directory entry at DE is \".\" or \"..\", comparing it with the names at $1A97\nand $1A96 through $1670 (whose matching takes bit 3 of IX+$06 into account).\nEntry: DE = the directory entry; IX = the descriptor.\nExit: A = $9E (Invalid . or .. operations); C when the entry is \".\" or \"..\", else NC. Z when\nit matched or is empty (first byte 0 or $E5), NZ for any other entry.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "6971": {"comment":"HL = \".\" padded with spaces"},
        "6974": {"comment":"Is the entry \".\"?"},
        "6977": {"comment":"HL = \"..\" padded with spaces"},
        "6980": {"comment":"Not \".\": is it \"..\"?"},
        "6985": {"comment":"Error code $9E, for a caller that refuses them"},
        "6988": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 9 (table $0550): renames a file. The new name is taken from the descriptor at\nBC into the file's descriptor (a \"?\" keeps the old character), checked, and written into the\nfile's directory entry.\n1. Finds the entry ($12F9), clears the word at HL+$1E for a directory ($0EC3), refuses \".\"\n   and \"..\".\n2. Refuses a second descriptor on another drive (byte +7).\n3. Copies the 11 name characters (+8 on) and checks the new name ($189E).\n4. Refuses a name that exists already, then finds the entry again and stores the name.\nEntry: DE = the file's descriptor (first byte $FE); BC = the descriptor holding the new\nname; HL = passed on to $12F9.\nExit: A = 0 with Z.\nError: NZ, or C with A = $AB, with A = the error code: $9E (Invalid . or .. operations), $AF\n(Invalid drive), $AB (Duplicate filename), one from $189E or $12F9.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the directory.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "6989": {"comment":"DE = the entry, IX = the descriptor, A = attributes"},
        "6992": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "6994": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "6996": {"comment":"Yes: clears the word at HL+$1E"},
        "6999": {"comment":"Is it \".\" or \"..\"?"},
        "7002": {"comment":"Yes: error $9E"},
        "7004": {"comment":"The new name's descriptor"},
        "7006": {"comment":"HL' = the file's descriptor"},
        "7009": {"comment":"Its byte +7 (the drive)"},
        "7013": {"comment":"DE' = the file's descriptor +7"},
        "7014": {"comment":"HL' = the new name's descriptor"},
        "7015": {"comment":"+7"},
        "7016": {"comment":"The same drive?"},
        "7018": {"comment":"Error code $AF (Invalid drive)"},
        "7020": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "7022": {"comment":"11 name characters"},
        "7024": {"synopsis":"Copies one character of the new name over the old one, except a \"?\" which keeps the old one."},
        "7026": {"comment":"A = the new character"},
        "7027": {"comment":"A \"?\"?"},
        "7029": {"comment":"Yes: keep the old one"},
        "7031": {"comment":"No: store it"},
        "7032": {"synopsis":"The next character; then checks the new name and its uniqueness and finds the entry again.","comment":"Next character"},
        "7035": {"comment":"Is the new name valid?"},
        "7038": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "7040": {"comment":"Starts at the directory's first entry"},
        "7043": {"comment":"Searches it for the new name"},
        "7046": {"comment":"HL = the caller's HL"},
        "7047": {"comment":"Error code $AB (Duplicate filename)"},
        "7049": {"comment":"Found: refused"},
        "7050": {"comment":"DE = the file's descriptor"},
        "7053": {"comment":"Finds its entry again"},
        "7054": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "7057": {"comment":"HL = the new name in the descriptor"},
        "7064": {"comment":"Its first character"},
        "7065": {"comment":"$E5?"},
        "7067": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "7069": {"comment":"$E5 is stored as $05 in an entry"},
        "7071": {"synopsis":"Stores the name's first character in the entry, then the other 10 through ENTRY_COPY_N.","comment":"The first character"},
        "7074": {"comment":"10 more"},
        "7076": {"comment":"Copies them and marks the buffer changed"},
        "7079": {"synopsis":"Leaves with error $A1 (Invalid file attributes).","comment":"Error code $A1"},
        "7081": {"synopsis":"The common error exit of functions 9 and 10: drops the HL kept on the stack and returns with\nthe error code in A.","comment":"Drops the kept HL"},
        "7083": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 10 (table $0550): moves a file or a directory to another directory on the\nsame drive. The entry is copied to $06A1 above IY, deleted ($E5) where it is, and written to\na free entry of the destination; a moved directory's \"..\" entry is then pointed at its new\nparent. Volume labels and descriptors with bit 3 of +$06 set are refused.\nEntry: DE = the descriptor of what moves (first byte $FE); BC = the destination's path\ndescriptor, read by $1369; HL = passed on to $12F9.\nExit: A = 0 with Z.\nError: NZ with A = the error code: $A1 (Invalid file attributes), $9E (Invalid . or ..\noperations), $A8 (Invalid pathname string), $AF (Invalid drive), $A9 (Invalid directory\nmove), $AB (Duplicate filename), or one from $12F9, $1369 or $199A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the directories.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "7084": {"comment":"DE = the entry, IX = the descriptor, A = attributes"},
        "7087": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "7089": {"comment":"Descriptor bit 3 set?"},
        "7091": {"comment":"Yes: error $A1"},
        "7095": {"comment":"A volume label?"},
        "7097": {"comment":"Yes: error $A1"},
        "7099": {"comment":"Keeps the destination"},
        "7100": {"comment":"C = $81, the flags passed to $1369"},
        "7102": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "7104": {"comment":"No"},
        "7106": {"comment":"Adds flag bit 2 for a directory"},
        "7109": {"comment":"HL = the directory's first cluster"},
        "7114": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$5E/$5F"},
        "7123": {"comment":"Clears the word at HL+$1E"},
        "7126": {"synopsis":"Function 10, after the source: refuses \".\" and \"..\", reads the destination path ($1369) and\nchecks it (a plain path, the same drive, not inside the directory being moved, no entry of\nthe same name), takes a free entry there, then moves the entry and fixes a moved directory's\n\"..\".","comment":"Is the source \".\" or \"..\"?"},
        "7129": {"comment":"DE = the destination's descriptor"},
        "7130": {"comment":"Yes: error $9E"},
        "7132": {"comment":"Clears the flags at IY+$5D"},
        "7136": {"comment":"A' = the source's drive"},
        "7140": {"comment":"Reads the destination path"},
        "7143": {"comment":"Bad path"},
        "7145": {"comment":"Anything left in C?"},
        "7146": {"comment":"Error code $A8 (Invalid pathname string)"},
        "7148": {"comment":"Yes: refused"},
        "7150": {"comment":"A = the destination's drive"},
        "7151": {"comment":"The same drive?"},
        "7154": {"comment":"Error code $AF (Invalid drive)"},
        "7156": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "7158": {"comment":"Destination inside the moved directory?"},
        "7162": {"comment":"Error code $A9 (Invalid directory move)"},
        "7164": {"comment":"Yes: refused"},
        "7166": {"comment":"Starts at the destination's first entry"},
        "7169": {"comment":"Searches it for the name"},
        "7172": {"comment":"Error code $AB (Duplicate filename)"},
        "7174": {"comment":"Found: refused"},
        "7176": {"comment":"Finds a free entry"},
        "7179": {"comment":"None"},
        "7181": {"comment":"Records where the free entry is"},
        "7184": {"comment":"HL = the caller's HL"},
        "7185": {"comment":"DE = the source's descriptor"},
        "7188": {"comment":"Finds the source entry again"},
        "7191": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "7192": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "7194": {"comment":"Kept for after the move"},
        "7195": {"comment":"Yes: clears the word at HL+$1E"},
        "7198": {"comment":"HL = IY, the caller's HL kept on the stack"},
        "7201": {"comment":"$06A1 above IY: a 32-byte copy of the entry"},
        "7207": {"comment":"HL = the source entry"},
        "7208": {"comment":"One entry"},
        "7211": {"comment":"Copies it"},
        "7213": {"comment":"HL = the source entry"},
        "7214": {"comment":"Deleted mark"},
        "7216": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "7219": {"comment":"DE = the copy"},
        "7220": {"comment":"HL = the caller's HL"},
        "7222": {"comment":"Back to the free entry found at $1C08"},
        "7225": {"comment":"DE = the free entry"},
        "7228": {"comment":"HL = the copy, the caller's HL on the stack"},
        "7229": {"comment":"One entry"},
        "7233": {"comment":"Writes it there"},
        "7235": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "7240": {"comment":"Z: not a directory"},
        "7241": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7242": {"comment":"A file: done"},
        "7243": {"comment":"BC = the destination directory's cluster"},
        "7250": {"comment":"IX+8 = \"..\", a descriptor for the search"},
        "7254": {"comment":"Enters the moved directory"},
        "7257": {"comment":"Its first entry"},
        "7260": {"comment":"Searches it for \"..\""},
        "7263": {"comment":"BC = the new parent's cluster"},
        "7264": {"comment":"Not found: done"},
        "7265": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "7267": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7268": {"comment":"HL = the \"..\" entry's first cluster"},
        "7272": {"comment":"Points it at the new parent"},
        "7275": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "7277": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 11 (table $0550): stores a file's attributes and its time and date from its\ndescriptor (attributes at +$13, time and date at +$1E-$21) into its directory entry. Some\nbits may not change: none of a volume label's, all but bit 1 (hidden) of a directory's, and\nbits 7, 6, 4 and 3 of a file's.\nEntry: DE = the file's descriptor (first byte $FE); HL = passed on to $12F9.\nExit: A = 0 with Z.\nError: NZ with A = $A1 (Invalid file attributes), or the error from $12F9.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF', BC', DE', HL'; the directory.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Keeps the descriptor"},
        "7278": {"comment":"DE = the entry, A = its attributes"},
        "7281": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor"},
        "7282": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "7283": {"comment":"+$13: the new attributes"},
        "7287": {"comment":"DE = them, HL = the entry"},
        "7290": {"comment":"HL = the entry's attributes"},
        "7291": {"comment":"B = $FF: no bit may change"},
        "7292": {"comment":"A volume label?"},
        "7294": {"comment":"Yes: B = $FF"},
        "7296": {"comment":"Only bit 1 may change"},
        "7298": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "7300": {"comment":"Yes: B = $FD"},
        "7302": {"comment":"A file: bits 0, 1, 2 and 5 may change"},
        "7304": {"synopsis":"Refuses attributes that change a bit outside the allowed ones (B = the fixed bits); stores\nthem, then copies the time and date.","comment":"A = the new attributes"},
        "7306": {"comment":"Which bits change?"},
        "7307": {"comment":"Any fixed one?"},
        "7308": {"comment":"Error code $A1 (Invalid file attributes)"},
        "7310": {"comment":"Yes: refused"},
        "7311": {"comment":"Stores the attributes"},
        "7315": {"comment":"HL = the entry's time"},
        "7316": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "7317": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor's time, +$1E"},
        "7318": {"comment":"Time and date: 4 bytes"},
        "7320": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to DE into the directory entry, then marks the buffer changed."},
        "7322": {"synopsis":"Marks the current sector buffer changed and returns A = 0 with Z.","comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "7325": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "7327": {"synopsis":"The floppy controller driver: runs one operation on a drive of the disk card. The\ncontroller's ports are found from the segment this ROM runs in (port $B3, page 3's segment,\nhalved; $10 when bit 1 of that is set): base+0 command/status, +1 track, +2 sector, +3 data,\nbase+8 the drive latch (selects, side, bit 5 from H; reads back DRQ in bit 7, INTRQ in bit\n1, a disk change in bit 6). Each drive's track is kept at IY-$1B+n (n = 0-3), $FF when not\nknown. A = 0: forgets the tracks of the drives in B (B = 0: also stops a busy command and\nresets the latch). 1 reads sectors, 2 writes sectors, 3 verifies sectors against the buffer,\n4 writes a track, 5 reads a track, 6 reads an address field, 7 only reports a disk change, 8\nrestores the drive in B and counts its tracks. Another code gives $80.\nEntry: A = the operation; B bits 0-3 = the drive (its lowest set bit); C bit 0 = the side; D\n= the track ($FF: stay); E = the first sector; H bits 0-1 = the step rate, bit 2 = write\nprecompensation, bit 3 = double step, bit 5 = to the latch; L = the sector count; IX = the\nbuffer.\nExit: A = 0 with Z when done; L = the sectors done; B as on entry except after a disk\nchange; for operation 8 A = 0 with L = $FF (49 or more\nsteps back to track 0) or 0, A = 1 when track 0 was not found.\nError: NZ with A = 1 (time-out), 2 (verify mismatch), $20 (the disk was changed: B = the\ndrives marked changed), $80 (bad operation or no drive), or the controller's error bits\n(status AND $5C: $40 write protected, $10 not found, $08 CRC, $04 lost data).\nChanges: AF, B, L; IY-$1F to IY-$13, the 4 bytes at IY-$4A, IY-$5F.\nKeeps: C, DE, H, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the operation"},
        "7330": {"comment":"Keeps the side"},
        "7333": {"comment":"Keeps the sector"},
        "7336": {"comment":"Keeps the track"},
        "7340": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "7343": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer as the exit's IX"},
        "7345": {"comment":"Port $B3: page 3's segment"},
        "7347": {"comment":"C = this ROM's segment"},
        "7349": {"comment":"Halved: the controller's port base"},
        "7351": {"comment":"Segment bit 2 set?"},
        "7355": {"comment":"Yes: base $10"},
        "7357": {"synopsis":"Runs the operation in A: 0 (DIO_RESET), 1-7 (DIO_TRANSFER), 8 (DIO_COUNT_TRK), others fail.","comment":"Operation 0?"},
        "7360": {"comment":"Restarts the count at IY-$5F"},
        "7364": {"comment":"1-7?"},
        "7369": {"comment":"8?"},
        "7371": {"synopsis":"An operation above 8 (or no drive given): A = $80, L = 0.","comment":"Result $80"},
        "7373": {"comment":"No sectors done"},
        "7375": {"synopsis":"The exit: puts back BC, IX and DE, and sets the flags from the result in A.","comment":"The caller's BC"},
        "7376": {"synopsis":"The exit that keeps B as set (a disk change): puts back IX and DE, flags from A.","comment":"The caller's IX"},
        "7378": {"comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "7379": {"comment":"Z when A = 0"},
        "7381": {"synopsis":"Operation 0: sets the track of every drive in B's low 4 bits to $FF (not known).","comment":"A = the drives"},
        "7384": {"comment":"IY is stepped per drive"},
        "7386": {"synopsis":"One drive bit per pass, drive 0 first.","comment":"This drive's bit"},
        "7388": {"comment":"Not given"},
        "7390": {"comment":"Its track is not known"},
        "7394": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next drive while bits are left; then stops a busy command when B = 0.","comment":"The next drive's track byte"},
        "7396": {"comment":"More drives"},
        "7400": {"comment":"Controller status"},
        "7402": {"comment":"Busy?"},
        "7403": {"comment":"No"},
        "7405": {"comment":"Force interrupt"},
        "7407": {"comment":"Stops the command"},
        "7409": {"synopsis":"With drives given, returns A = 0. With B = 0 also clears the latch copy at IY-$1C, writes\nthe latch (drive 0 selected only while the motor runs) and sets the count at IY-$5F to $0A.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "7410": {"comment":"Drives given?"},
        "7411": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7413": {"comment":"No latch value"},
        "7416": {"comment":"Controller status"},
        "7418": {"comment":"Motor on?"},
        "7420": {"comment":"A = 1 when it is"},
        "7421": {"comment":"The drive latch"},
        "7423": {"comment":"Selects drive 0 only while the motor runs"},
        "7425": {"comment":"The count at IY-$5F"},
        "7429": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "7432": {"synopsis":"Operation 8: restores the drive in B, steps in 50 tracks and counts the steps out back to\ntrack\n0. 49 or more gives L = $FF, fewer L = 0; no track 0 within 256 steps gives A = 1. With no\n   drive in B it restores drive 0, and drive 1 too when drive 0 reports track 0\n   (DIO_RESTORE_0_1).","comment":"Flags: the motor counts as running"},
        "7436": {"comment":"A = the lowest drive bit"},
        "7442": {"comment":"None: restore drives 0 and 1"},
        "7444": {"comment":"Selects and restores the drive"},
        "7447": {"comment":"Waits"},
        "7450": {"comment":"50 steps in"},
        "7452": {"synopsis":"Steps in one track per pass, then waits.","comment":"Step in, update track"},
        "7454": {"comment":"Issues it and waits"},
        "7460": {"comment":"Waits"},
        "7463": {"synopsis":"Steps out one track per pass until track 0, counting the steps in D; A = 1 after 256 steps.","comment":"Step out, update track"},
        "7465": {"comment":"Issues it; NZ at track 0"},
        "7468": {"comment":"Track 0"},
        "7470": {"comment":"One more step"},
        "7471": {"comment":"Up to 256"},
        "7473": {"comment":"Track 0 not found"},
        "7477": {"synopsis":"Track 0 reached after D steps out: L = $FF for 49 or more, L = 0 for fewer; A = 0.","comment":"L = 0: few tracks"},
        "7479": {"comment":"49 or more steps?"},
        "7482": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7483": {"comment":"No: L = 0"},
        "7485": {"comment":"Yes: L = $FF"},
        "7488": {"synopsis":"Operation 8 with no drive given: restores drive 0, then drive 1 when drive 0 reports track\n0.","comment":"A = 1: drive 0"},
        "7489": {"comment":"Restores it; A = 2 at track 0"},
        "7492": {"comment":"At track 0?"},
        "7494": {"comment":"A = 2: drive 1"},
        "7496": {"comment":"Yes: restores drive 1"},
        "7499": {"synopsis":"Waits (DIO_DELAY), then returns through DIO_EXIT.","comment":"The return goes to DIO_EXIT"},
        "7502": {"comment":"Pushed as the return address"},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"A wait of $1A x 256 turns of a DEC/JR loop.\nEntry: E = the first inner count (0 for 256).\nExit: B = 0, E = 0.\nChanges: F, B, E.\nKeeps: A, C, D, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Outer count"},
        "7505": {"synopsis":"The inner and outer loops of DIO_DELAY."},
        "7511": {"synopsis":"Operations 1-7: notes whether the motor is running, finds the drive (its lowest bit in B)\nand selects it with the side and H's bit 5 on the latch.","comment":"Controller status"},
        "7513": {"comment":"Motor on?"},
        "7515": {"comment":"Flags: bit 7 = the motor runs"},
        "7518": {"comment":"A = the lowest drive bit"},
        "7524": {"comment":"None: result $80"},
        "7527": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer"},
        "7528": {"comment":"E = the drive's bit"},
        "7529": {"comment":"IX steps to the drive's track byte"},
        "7533": {"synopsis":"Finds the drive's number: IX = IY + the number + 1."},
        "7535": {"comment":"This drive?"},
        "7538": {"comment":"D = the drive's track"},
        "7549": {"synopsis":"Writes the latch: the drive, the side and bit 5 of H. A change of drive is noted in bit 0 of\nthe flags at IY-$16 (the head loads again).","comment":"H's bit 5"},
        "7552": {"comment":"With the drive and side"},
        "7554": {"comment":"The drive latch"},
        "7556": {"comment":"Selects the drive"},
        "7558": {"comment":"The same drive as before?"},
        "7563": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7565": {"comment":"Notes the new drive"},
        "7568": {"comment":"The latch's new value"},
        "7571": {"synopsis":"Reads the latch's disk-change bit and clears it with a pulse of bit 6; a drive whose change\nis new is reported (DIO_CHANGED), one already seen goes on to the seek.","comment":"B = the drives seen since a change"},
        "7574": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7576": {"comment":"Disk change bit clear?"},
        "7578": {"comment":"Yes: no change"},
        "7580": {"comment":"Pulses bit 6"},
        "7585": {"comment":"To clear the change"},
        "7587": {"comment":"Still set?"},
        "7591": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7593": {"comment":"Already seen?"},
        "7595": {"comment":"Yes: go on"},
        "7597": {"comment":"Records the drive as seen"},
        "7602": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "7603": {"synopsis":"The disk was changed: result $20.","comment":"Result $20"},
        "7605": {"synopsis":"Adds the drive bits in A to the changed drives at IY-$1E, returns B = this drive's bit if it\nis among them, A = the result in B on entry, L = 0.","comment":"Adds to the changed drives"},
        "7611": {"comment":"This drive changed?"},
        "7614": {"comment":"D = the result"},
        "7615": {"comment":"Drops the kept buffer"},
        "7616": {"comment":"Drops the caller's BC"},
        "7617": {"comment":"B = this drive's changed bit"},
        "7618": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "7619": {"comment":"No sectors done"},
        "7624": {"synopsis":"No change on the latch: the drive is taken off the seen drives at IY-$1D.","comment":"Every other drive"},
        "7627": {"comment":"Updated"},
        "7630": {"synopsis":"Operation 7 ends here, reporting the drive's change bit with A = 0. Others restore the head\nwhen the track is not known, then seek to track D.","comment":"A = the operation"},
        "7633": {"comment":"7?"},
        "7635": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "7636": {"comment":"Yes: report only"},
        "7638": {"comment":"The command register"},
        "7640": {"comment":"Track known?"},
        "7643": {"comment":"No: track 0 after the restore"},
        "7644": {"comment":"Restores the head"},
        "7647": {"comment":"Waits"},
        "7650": {"synopsis":"E = the track asked for, or the current one when $FF was asked.","comment":"D = the current track"},
        "7651": {"comment":"The track asked for"},
        "7655": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "7658": {"comment":"Yes: stay"},
        "7659": {"synopsis":"For double stepping, both tracks are doubled for the controller.","comment":"Keeps the tracks"},
        "7660": {"comment":"Double step?"},
        "7668": {"synopsis":"Loads the track, sector and data registers (the target track) and notes a head move in bit 2\nof IY-$16.","comment":"The track register"},
        "7669": {"comment":"= the current track"},
        "7671": {"comment":"The sector register"},
        "7675": {"comment":"= the sector"},
        "7677": {"comment":"The data register"},
        "7678": {"comment":"= the target track"},
        "7680": {"comment":"Back to the command register"},
        "7683": {"comment":"Does the head move?"},
        "7687": {"comment":"Yes: the next command waits for it to settle"},
        "7691": {"synopsis":"Seeks, then sets the track register and the drive's track byte to the logical track; one\nsector for operations 4 and 5.","comment":"Seek"},
        "7693": {"comment":"Issues it and waits"},
        "7696": {"comment":"E = the logical track"},
        "7698": {"comment":"The track register"},
        "7701": {"comment":"The drive's track"},
        "7707": {"comment":"D = the operation"},
        "7708": {"comment":"Operations 4 and 5?"},
        "7714": {"comment":"Yes: one pass"},
        "7716": {"synopsis":"Starts the transfer: B = the sector count, E = the flags in H, HL = the buffer (the caller's\nHL kept on the stack), and disables interrupts ($1FC5, the old state kept).","comment":"B = the sector count"},
        "7717": {"comment":"E = the flags"},
        "7718": {"comment":"HL = the buffer, the caller's HL kept"},
        "7719": {"comment":"Disables interrupts, C if they were off"},
        "7722": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "7723": {"synopsis":"Picks the controller command for the operation in D, once per sector: 1 read sector ($88), 2\nwrite sector ($A8), 3 verify (a read, $88), 4 write track ($F8), 5 read track ($E8), 6 read\naddress ($C8).","comment":"Read?"},
        "7724": {"comment":"Read sector"},
        "7728": {"comment":"Write?"},
        "7731": {"comment":"Verify?"},
        "7735": {"comment":"Write track?"},
        "7736": {"comment":"Write track"},
        "7740": {"comment":"Read track?"},
        "7741": {"comment":"Read track"},
        "7745": {"comment":"Read address"},
        "7747": {"synopsis":"Issues a read command and waits on the latch for the first data byte.","comment":"Settle bit and wait count"},
        "7750": {"comment":"Issues the command"},
        "7752": {"comment":"The latch: DRQ and INTRQ"},
        "7754": {"synopsis":"A jump to the poll that follows."},
        "7756": {"synopsis":"Polls the latch for DRQ (bit 7) while counting DE down; a count that ends is a time-out."},
        "7758": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7760": {"comment":"DRQ: a byte"},
        "7763": {"comment":"Counts the wait"},
        "7768": {"comment":"DRQ: a byte"},
        "7771": {"comment":"Waited too long?"},
        "7773": {"comment":"Yes: time-out"},
        "7778": {"comment":"No DRQ: poll again"},
        "7781": {"synopsis":"Reads a data byte into the buffer.","comment":"The data register (a mirror)"},
        "7782": {"comment":"Reads the byte"},
        "7784": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "7786": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7787": {"synopsis":"Waits for DRQ (another byte) or INTRQ (the command ended).","comment":"The latch"},
        "7789": {"comment":"DRQ or INTRQ?"},
        "7791": {"comment":"Neither: wait"},
        "7793": {"comment":"DRQ: the next byte"},
        "7796": {"comment":"INTRQ: the command ended"},
        "7798": {"synopsis":"Write sector command.","comment":"Write sector"},
        "7800": {"synopsis":"Turns write precompensation off (command bit 1) unless bit 2 of H asks for it.","comment":"Precompensation asked for?"},
        "7804": {"comment":"No: disable it"},
        "7806": {"synopsis":"Issues the write command and waits for the first DRQ."},
        "7807": {"comment":"Settle bit and wait count"},
        "7810": {"comment":"Issues the command"},
        "7812": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7814": {"comment":"Wait count"},
        "7817": {"synopsis":"Polls the latch for DRQ; INTRQ first, or the end of the count, ends the command.","comment":"Counts the wait"},
        "7820": {"comment":"Waited too long"},
        "7822": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7824": {"comment":"DRQ: write"},
        "7827": {"comment":"INTRQ?"},
        "7829": {"comment":"Yes: ended early"},
        "7833": {"synopsis":"E = the data register's port.","comment":"The data register (a mirror)"},
        "7834": {"comment":"E = its port"},
        "7835": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte from the buffer.","comment":"The latch"},
        "7836": {"comment":"D = the next byte"},
        "7838": {"synopsis":"Waits for DRQ or INTRQ and writes the byte on DRQ.","comment":"The latch"},
        "7840": {"comment":"DRQ or INTRQ?"},
        "7842": {"comment":"Neither: wait"},
        "7844": {"comment":"The data register"},
        "7845": {"comment":"Writes the byte"},
        "7847": {"comment":"DRQ: the next byte"},
        "7850": {"comment":"INTRQ: the latch again"},
        "7851": {"comment":"The last byte was not written"},
        "7854": {"synopsis":"Issues a read sector command and compares the data with the buffer.","comment":"Settle bit and wait count"},
        "7857": {"comment":"Issues the command"},
        "7859": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7861": {"synopsis":"A jump to the poll that follows."},
        "7863": {"synopsis":"Polls the latch for DRQ while counting DE down; a count that ends is a time-out."},
        "7865": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7867": {"comment":"DRQ: a byte"},
        "7870": {"comment":"Counts the wait"},
        "7875": {"comment":"DRQ: a byte"},
        "7878": {"comment":"Waited too long?"},
        "7880": {"comment":"Yes: time-out"},
        "7884": {"comment":"No DRQ: poll again"},
        "7887": {"synopsis":"Compares a data byte with the buffer.","comment":"The data register (a mirror)"},
        "7888": {"comment":"Reads the byte"},
        "7890": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7891": {"comment":"The same as the buffer?"},
        "7892": {"comment":"No: mismatch"},
        "7895": {"synopsis":"Waits for DRQ (another byte) or INTRQ (the command ended).","comment":"The latch"},
        "7897": {"comment":"DRQ or INTRQ?"},
        "7899": {"comment":"Neither: wait"},
        "7901": {"comment":"DRQ: the next byte"},
        "7904": {"synopsis":"The read or verify ended: checks the status."},
        "7906": {"synopsis":"The write waited too long or ended early: drops the kept DE.","comment":"Drops the kept command flags"},
        "7907": {"synopsis":"Result 1 (time-out) unless INTRQ shows the command ended; a command still running is\nstopped.","comment":"Result 1: time-out"},
        "7909": {"comment":"The latch"},
        "7911": {"comment":"INTRQ?"},
        "7913": {"comment":"Yes: check the status"},
        "7917": {"synopsis":"Result 2: the data differs from the buffer.","comment":"Result 2"},
        "7919": {"synopsis":"Stops the command with a force interrupt and ends with the result in D.","comment":"The command register"},
        "7921": {"comment":"Force interrupt"},
        "7923": {"comment":"Stops the command"},
        "7927": {"synopsis":"The write ended: drops the kept DE.","comment":"Drops the kept command flags"},
        "7928": {"synopsis":"Result 0 so far: the status decides.","comment":"Result 0"},
        "7930": {"synopsis":"A sector command ended: the status's error bits ($5C) or an earlier result in D end the\noperation; else, while sectors are left in B, the sector register is advanced and the next\nsector's command is issued (DIO_OP_CMD) with the flags at IY-$16 = $80.","comment":"The command/status register"},
        "7932": {"comment":"The status"},
        "7934": {"comment":"Write protect, not found, CRC or lost data?"},
        "7936": {"comment":"Yes: the result"},
        "7938": {"comment":"An earlier result (time-out, mismatch)?"},
        "7941": {"comment":"One sector fewer: none left?"},
        "7944": {"comment":"The sector register"},
        "7946": {"comment":"The sector just done"},
        "7949": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Back to the command register"},
        "7953": {"comment":"Flags: motor on, no head move, same drive"},
        "7957": {"comment":"D = the operation"},
        "7960": {"comment":"Its command for the next sector"},
        "7963": {"synopsis":"The result is the status's error bits (0 when the count ran out).","comment":"D = the result"},
        "7964": {"synopsis":"After a write (2) or a track write (4), a short wait of 256 DEC/JR passes before the end.","comment":"A = the operation"},
        "7967": {"comment":"Write?"},
        "7971": {"comment":"Write track?"},
        "7973": {"comment":"No: no wait"},
        "7975": {"synopsis":"The 256-pass wait after a write."},
        "7978": {"synopsis":"Sets the count at IY-$5F to $6E and enables interrupts again unless INT_DISABLE (called at\n$1E27) found them disabled.","comment":"The count at IY-$5F"},
        "7982": {"comment":"The state kept at $1E2A: C if they were off"},
        "7983": {"comment":"Were off: leave them"},
        "7985": {"comment":"Were on"},
        "7986": {"synopsis":"L = the sectors done (the count asked for less those left in B); stores R in the next of the\n4 bytes at IY-$4A (IY-$1F counts the stores) and leaves through DIO_EXIT with A = the\nresult.","comment":"HL = the caller's HL (L = the sector count)"},
        "7988": {"comment":"Less the sectors not done"},
        "7989": {"comment":"L = the sectors done"},
        "7990": {"comment":"A = the store count"},
        "7993": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "7996": {"comment":"0-3: which byte"},
        "8001": {"comment":"IX = IY + that"},
        "8007": {"comment":"A = R"},
        "8009": {"comment":"Into one of IY-$4A to IY-$47"},
        "8012": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "8013": {"comment":"Puts back BC, IX, DE; flags from A"},
        "8016": {"synopsis":"Adds the settle bit (bit 2) to the command in A when the head moved, and sets the wait\ncount: DE = $9331 when the motor runs, else 0 (65,536 passes).\nEntry: A = the command; IY-$16 = the flags.\nExit: A = the command; DE = the wait count.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Did the head move?"},
        "8022": {"comment":"Yes: wait for it to settle"},
        "8024": {"synopsis":"Part of FDC_CMD_FLAGS: the wait count is $9331 while the motor runs, else 0 (65,536).","comment":"The wait while the motor runs"},
        "8027": {"comment":"Motor running (flags bit 7)?"},
        "8032": {"comment":"No: the longest wait"},
        "8036": {"synopsis":"Forgets the track of the drives in A (DISK_IO operation 0), selects them on the latch and\nrestores the head (FDC_RESTORE).\nEntry: A = the drive bits; C = the controller's port base; H bits 0-1 = the step rate.\nExit: A = 2 (NZ) when the head is at track 0, else 0.\nChanges: AF, B, E; IY-$17 to IY-$13 (the nested DISK_IO call), IY-$16, IY-$5F.\nKeeps: C, D, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"B = the drives"},
        "8037": {"comment":"Operation 0"},
        "8038": {"comment":"Forgets their tracks"},
        "8041": {"comment":"The drive latch"},
        "8043": {"comment":"Selects the drives"},
        "8045": {"comment":"The command register"},
        "8047": {"synopsis":"Issues a restore (command $08) and waits for it (FDC_TYPE1_CMD).\nEntry: as FDC_TYPE1_CMD.\nExit: as FDC_TYPE1_CMD.\nChanges: AF, B, E.\nKeeps: C, D, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Restore"},
        "8049": {"synopsis":"Issues a head command (restore, seek, step) with the step rate from H, waits for the head to\nload when the drive changed and for the motor to spin up when it was off (index pulses on\nlatch bit 0, bounded), then waits while the controller is busy.\nEntry: B = the command; C = the controller's port base; H bits 0-1 = the step rate; IY-$16 =\nthe flags, IY-$17 = the operation.\nExit: A = 2 (NZ) when the head is at track 0, else 0; IY-$16 = the flags, motor bit 7 set.\nChanges: AF, B, E; IY-$16, IY-$5F.\nKeeps: C, D, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps HL"},
        "8050": {"comment":"The step rate"},
        "8053": {"comment":"Issues the command"},
        "8056": {"comment":"E = the flags"},
        "8059": {"comment":"A = the operation"},
        "8062": {"comment":"Operations 1 and 3 become 1"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Read or verify?"},
        "8065": {"comment":"Yes: no waits"},
        "8067": {"comment":"A new drive?"},
        "8071": {"comment":"Clears the mark"},
        "8073": {"comment":"Waits for the head to load"},
        "8075": {"synopsis":"Part of FDC_TYPE1_CMD: a new drive was selected, so waits $2C x 256 passes for the head to\nload."},
        "8078": {"comment":"$2C rounds"},
        "8080": {"synopsis":"When the motor was off, marks it running and waits for it: up to $E935 passes, cut short\nonce index pulses (the latch's bit 0) come in.","comment":"Motor already running?"},
        "8082": {"comment":"Yes: no wait"},
        "8084": {"comment":"Marks it running"},
        "8086": {"comment":"The drive latch"},
        "8088": {"comment":"B = the latch now"},
        "8090": {"comment":"The longest wait"},
        "8093": {"synopsis":"Each change of the index bit cuts the passes left to at most $0CFF.","comment":"The latch"},
        "8095": {"comment":"Index bit changed?"},
        "8097": {"comment":"No"},
        "8099": {"comment":"B = the latch now"},
        "8101": {"comment":"More than $0CFF passes left?"},
        "8104": {"comment":"No: count on"},
        "8106": {"comment":"Yes: $0Cxx"},
        "8107": {"synopsis":"Counts the motor wait down."},
        "8110": {"comment":"Not run out: watch the index bit"},
        "8112": {"synopsis":"Stores the flags in E at IY-$16. Operations 1 and 3 (read, verify) enter at $1FB1, inside\nthe LD HL, which is RES 2,E: they skip the waits and clear the head-moved mark, so their\ncommand does not wait for the head to settle.","comment":"Hides RES 2,E at $1FB1, the entry for reads and verifies"},
        "8115": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "8118": {"synopsis":"Waits while the controller is busy (the count at IY-$5F held at $6E), then returns A = 2\nwhen the status shows track 0, else 0.","comment":"The count at IY-$5F"},
        "8122": {"comment":"The command/status register"},
        "8124": {"comment":"The status"},
        "8126": {"comment":"Busy?"},
        "8129": {"comment":"The caller's HL"},
        "8130": {"comment":"A = 2 at track 0 (status bit 2)"},
        "8133": {"synopsis":"Disables interrupts and says whether they were enabled. LD A,R copies IFF2 into P/V, but an\ninterrupt accepted during the instruction can leave it 0, so a 0 is checked again: the word\njust below SP still holds the AF pushed at the start (A = 0) unless an interrupt's return\naddress overwrote it.\nEntry: none.\nExit: interrupts disabled; NC when they were enabled, carry when they were not.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A = 0, NC"},
        "8134": {"comment":"Leaves A = 0 in the word below SP"},
        "8136": {"comment":"P/V = IFF2"},
        "8139": {"comment":"Were enabled: NC"},
        "8140": {"comment":"Back to the word pushed at the start"},
        "8142": {"comment":"A = its high byte"},
        "8143": {"comment":"Not 0: an interrupt came in between, so they were enabled"},
        "8145": {"comment":"Carry: interrupts were disabled"},
        "8147": {"synopsis":"The floppy driver's entry: its address ($DFD3) is what $01B2 passes to $03DF with C = 4, as\n$01CA passes RAMDISK_DRIVER. Keeps the function at IY-$12 and dispatches it: 0 and 1 to\n$1FEB, 2 to $2013, 3 to $2032, 4-6 to $2231, 8 to $241D; others (7 among them) fail with\n$BD.\nEntry: A = the function.\nError: A = $BD (no such function).","comment":"Keeps the function"},
        "8152": {"comment":"Function 0 or 1?"},
        "8154": {"comment":"Function 2?"},
        "8157": {"comment":"Function 3?"},
        "8161": {"comment":"Function 4-6?"},
        "8165": {"comment":"Function 7?"},
        "8168": {"comment":"Error $BD: no such function"},
        "8171": {"synopsis":"FLOPPY_DRIVER functions 0 and 1: forgets every drive's track (DISK_IO 0, B = $0F), asks\ndrives 3 to 0 for a disk change (DISK_IO 7), which takes a pending change off the latch, and\nstores the select bits 1, 2, 4, 8 at IY-$0B to IY-$08. Function 1 then returns A = 0;\nfunction 0 restores drive 0, and drive 1 when drive 0 is at track 0 (DISK_IO 8 with B = 0,\nstep rate 0). IY is 4 higher when it leaves (the select-bit loop steps it); DRIVER_CALL\ngives the driver its IY afresh on every call.","comment":"A' = function - 2: $FE for 0, $FF for 1"},
        "8173": {"comment":"All four drives"},
        "8175": {"comment":"Forgets their tracks"},
        "8178": {"comment":"Drive 3 first"},
        "8180": {"synopsis":"One drive per pass, 3 down to 0.","comment":"B = the drive's bit"},
        "8181": {"comment":"Disk change report"},
        "8188": {"comment":"Not past drive 0: the next one"},
        "8190": {"comment":"4 drives; drive 0's bit first"},
        "8193": {"synopsis":"Stores each drive's select bit, then ends the function.","comment":"The drive's select bit"},
        "8196": {"comment":"The next drive's bit"},
        "8198": {"comment":"The next drive's slot"},
        "8202": {"comment":"A = function - 2"},
        "8203": {"comment":"Function 1: done, A = 0"},
        "8205": {"comment":"Count tracks; B = 0: drives 0 and 1"},
        "8207": {"comment":"H = 0: step rate 0"},
        "8208": {"comment":"Function 0 returns DISK_IO's result"},
        "8211": {"synopsis":"FLOPPY_DRIVER function 2: has the disk in the drive changed? B = $FF when the drive's\nparameters are not known or DISK_IO 7 reports a new change (or fails); B = 0 when the drive\nhas no change mark; with a change mark B = 1 when IY-$45 is not 0, else 0. A = 0 every time.","comment":"IX = the drive's slot, B = its select bit"},
        "8214": {"comment":"Parameters known?"},
        "8218": {"comment":"No: changed"},
        "8220": {"comment":"Disk change report"},
        "8225": {"comment":"A new change (or a failure)"},
        "8227": {"comment":"B = the drive's change mark"},
        "8229": {"comment":"None: B = 0"},
        "8231": {"comment":"IY-$45 = 0?"},
        "8234": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "8235": {"comment":"Yes: B = 0"},
        "8236": {"comment":"No: B = 1"},
        "8238": {"synopsis":"B = $FF: the disk may have changed; A = 0.","comment":"Changed or not known"},
        "8242": {"synopsis":"FLOPPY_DRIVER function 3: reads the disk's layout and sets the drive's parameters.\n1. Marks the parameters not known, forgets the track and reads track 0 sector 1 into the\n   caller's buffer (FD_XFER_RETRY).\n2. Takes the BPB at +$0B, or the record at +$50 (BOOT_BPB_FIND); failing both, reads sector\n   2 and builds the BPB from the media byte that starts the FAT (FD_TRY_FAT_ID).\n3. Stores the geometry in the drive's slot (FD_SET_PARAMS), checking side 1 of a two-sided\n   disk, and the double step for a new disk of more than 50 tracks.","comment":"IX = the drive's slot, B = its select bit, HL' = buffer"},
        "8245": {"comment":"Parameters not known"},
        "8249": {"comment":"DISK_IO 0"},
        "8250": {"comment":"Forgets the drive's track"},
        "8253": {"comment":"Track 0, sector 1"},
        "8256": {"comment":"Side 0"},
        "8257": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "8259": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer"},
        "8261": {"comment":"Reads it"},
        "8264": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8265": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "8269": {"comment":"A usable BPB in it?"},
        "8273": {"comment":"No: try the FAT's media byte"},
        "8275": {"comment":"Drops the buffer"},
        "8276": {"comment":"Z: the drive's parameters from it"},
        "8279": {"synopsis":"No usable BPB in the boot sector: reads sector 2 (the FAT's first sector) into the buffer; a\nmedia byte of $F0 or more followed by $FF, $FF gives a BPB built from it (BPB_FROM_MEDIA),\nelse error $B4.","comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8282": {"comment":"HL' = the buffer"},
        "8285": {"comment":"Track 0, sector 2"},
        "8288": {"comment":"Side 0"},
        "8289": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "8291": {"comment":"Reads it"},
        "8294": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8295": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "8297": {"comment":"C = the first byte (the media byte)"},
        "8301": {"comment":"The next two bytes"},
        "8302": {"comment":"Both $FF?"},
        "8303": {"comment":"No: not a DOS disk"},
        "8306": {"comment":"Media byte $F0 or more?"},
        "8308": {"comment":"No: not a DOS disk"},
        "8310": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8312": {"comment":"The BPB at +$0B from the media byte"},
        "8315": {"comment":"NC: the drive's parameters from it"},
        "8318": {"synopsis":"The boot sector could not be read. A time-out or a disk change is mapped to its error; else\nan address field is read on the track: if one is found the disk is formatted ($B4 Not a DOS\ndisk); if not, a second try with the latch's bit 5 set decides between $B4 and $B5.","comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "8320": {"comment":"Yes: map it"},
        "8322": {"comment":"Reads an address field here"},
        "8325": {"comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "8329": {"comment":"Record not found?"},
        "8331": {"comment":"No: a formatted disk, not DOS"},
        "8333": {"comment":"Stay on the track; bit 5 to the latch"},
        "8336": {"comment":"Tries again"},
        "8339": {"synopsis":"A read of sector 2 failed (D = 0 here: $B4 unless a time-out or change), or the second\naddress-field read ended (D = its result).","comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "8341": {"synopsis":"Maps a time-out or a disk change; else a record not found gives $B5 (Unformatted disk) and\nanything else $B4.","comment":"Yes: map it"},
        "8344": {"comment":"Record not found?"},
        "8346": {"comment":"Error $B5 (Unformatted disk)"},
        "8349": {"synopsis":"Error $B4 (Not a DOS disk).","comment":"Error $B4"},
        "8352": {"synopsis":"Looks for a usable BPB in the boot sector: the one at +$0B (BPB_CHECK, then 1-128 sectors\nper track and 1 or 2 sides), else the record at +$50 when byte +8 is 1 (BOOT_ALT_BPB).\nEntry: HL = the boot sector.\nExit: Z. NC with HL = the boot sector +$0B; or C with HL = the boot sector +$50, its 15\nbytes copied over +$0B to +$19 and A = its +$0D byte (taken as the sides).\nError: NZ when neither passes.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"The BPB at +$0B"},
        "8356": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8357": {"comment":"Passes the first checks?"},
        "8360": {"comment":"No: try the record at +$50"},
        "8362": {"comment":"Sectors per track 1-128?"},
        "8367": {"comment":"D = its high byte"},
        "8369": {"comment":"A = the sides' low byte"},
        "8371": {"comment":"1 or 2 sides: 0"},
        "8374": {"comment":"With the high bytes"},
        "8376": {"comment":"Not 0: try the record at +$50"},
        "8378": {"comment":"HL = the BPB"},
        "8380": {"synopsis":"The BPB at +$0B failed: when the boot sector's byte +8 is 1, checks the record at +$50 the\nsame way (with its +$0D byte below 3) and copies its 15 bytes over the BPB at +$0B.","comment":"HL = the boot sector +$0B"},
        "8383": {"comment":"HL = +$08"},
        "8384": {"comment":"Byte +8 = 1?"},
        "8386": {"comment":"No: NZ, refused"},
        "8387": {"comment":"The record at +$50"},
        "8391": {"comment":"Passes the checks?"},
        "8395": {"comment":"Its +$0D byte (sides) below 3?"},
        "8397": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "8400": {"comment":"DE = the boot sector +$19"},
        "8405": {"comment":"15 bytes, +$5E down to +$50"},
        "8408": {"comment":"Over +$19 down to +$0B"},
        "8410": {"comment":"HL = the record at +$50"},
        "8411": {"comment":"Z"},
        "8412": {"comment":"C: the record at +$50 was taken"},
        "8414": {"synopsis":"A refused BPB: NZ (A OR H, H being the buffer's high byte).","comment":"NZ: refused"},
        "8416": {"synopsis":"Checks a BPB: 512 bytes per sector, a power of 2 sectors per cluster, 1-7 FATs, 1-12 sectors\nper FAT.\nEntry: HL = the BPB (the bytes-per-sector word, boot sector +$0B).\nExit: Z when it passes: A = the sectors per track's low byte, HL = BPB+$0E (its high byte).\nError: NZ when a field is out of range (BPB_BAD makes it NZ with OR H).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY.","comment":"D = bytes per sector, low"},
        "8418": {"comment":"A = high"},
        "8420": {"comment":"$0200?"},
        "8423": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "8424": {"comment":"Sectors per cluster"},
        "8425": {"comment":"0: refused"},
        "8427": {"comment":"A power of 2?"},
        "8432": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "8433": {"comment":"BPB+$05: the number of FATs"},
        "8436": {"comment":"1-7?"},
        "8439": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "8441": {"comment":"DE = 6 (D = 0 from the check)"},
        "8443": {"comment":"BPB+$0B: sectors per FAT"},
        "8446": {"comment":"1-12?"},
        "8449": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "8451": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "8453": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "8454": {"comment":"A = sectors per track, low"},
        "8457": {"synopsis":"Builds a BPB at +$0B of the buffer from a FAT media byte (bit 0: two sides, bit 1: 8 sectors\nper track, bit 2: 40 tracks): 512 bytes per sector; 1 sector per cluster when the bits 0 and\n2 give 4 ($FC, $FE), else 2; 1 reserved sector; 2 FATs; $40 root entries (with 1 per\ncluster) or $70; 320 or 360 sectors, doubled for two sides and again for 80 tracks; 1 sector\nper FAT for $FA, $FE, $FF, 3 for $F9, else 2. Bytes +$0B to +$63 are cleared first.\nEntry: A = C = the media byte; HL = the buffer.\nExit: HL = the buffer +$0B; NC.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "8460": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +$64"},
        "8461": {"comment":"$59 bytes: +$0B to +$63"},
        "8463": {"synopsis":"Clears the bytes, then fills in the sector size and the cluster size.","comment":"One byte lower"},
        "8464": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "8467": {"comment":"Keeps the BPB"},
        "8468": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "8470": {"comment":"+$0C: bytes per sector $0200"},
        "8472": {"comment":"+$0D: sectors per cluster 1"},
        "8474": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 2 of the media byte"},
        "8476": {"comment":"Both give 4?"},
        "8480": {"comment":"No: 2 per cluster"},
        "8481": {"synopsis":"One reserved sector, 2 FATs, $40 root entries, $70 when a cluster is 2 sectors."},
        "8482": {"comment":"+$0E: 1 reserved sector"},
        "8485": {"comment":"+$10: 2 FATs"},
        "8487": {"comment":"+$11: $40 root entries"},
        "8489": {"comment":"1 sector per cluster?"},
        "8492": {"comment":"No: $70 entries"},
        "8494": {"synopsis":"Works out the total sectors (HL), the sectors per track (D) and the sides (E): 8 or 9 per\ntrack from bit 1."},
        "8496": {"comment":"Keeps +$13 (the total sectors)"},
        "8497": {"comment":"A = the media byte"},
        "8498": {"comment":"40 tracks x 8 sectors"},
        "8501": {"comment":"40 more for 9 sectors per track"},
        "8504": {"comment":"8 sectors per track, 1 side"},
        "8507": {"comment":"8 sectors per track (bit 1)?"},
        "8511": {"comment":"No: 9 per track"},
        "8512": {"comment":"360 sectors"},
        "8513": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 set: two sides, twice the sectors.","comment":"Two sides?"},
        "8517": {"comment":"Yes: 2"},
        "8518": {"comment":"Twice the sectors"},
        "8519": {"synopsis":"Bit 2 clear: 80 tracks, twice the sectors.","comment":"40 tracks?"},
        "8523": {"comment":"No: twice the sectors"},
        "8524": {"synopsis":"Stores the total sectors and the media byte, and the sectors per FAT: 1 for $FA, $FE, $FF,\n3 for $F9, else 2.","comment":"DE = the total sectors"},
        "8525": {"comment":"HL = +$13; the track geometry on the stack"},
        "8526": {"comment":"+$13: the total sectors"},
        "8530": {"comment":"+$15: the media byte"},
        "8532": {"comment":"+$16: 1 sector per FAT"},
        "8533": {"comment":"$FE or $FF?"},
        "8535": {"comment":"Yes: 1"},
        "8537": {"comment":"$FA?"},
        "8539": {"comment":"Yes: 1"},
        "8541": {"comment":"2"},
        "8542": {"comment":"$F9?"},
        "8545": {"comment":"Yes: 3"},
        "8546": {"synopsis":"Stores the sectors per track and the sides, and returns NC with HL = the BPB."},
        "8548": {"comment":"D = sectors per track, E = sides"},
        "8549": {"comment":"+$18: sectors per track"},
        "8552": {"comment":"+$1A: sides"},
        "8553": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +$0B"},
        "8554": {"comment":"NC"},
        "8556": {"synopsis":"Takes the drive's parameters from the BPB at HL: the total sectors (IX+$09/$0D), the sectors\nper track and the sides. The record at +$50 (carry) gives 9 sectors per track and 2 sides\nwhen its +$0D byte is 2, else 1.","comment":"Keeps C: the record at +$50 was taken"},
        "8560": {"comment":"HL = BPB+$08: the total sectors"},
        "8565": {"comment":"The drive's total sectors, low"},
        "8568": {"comment":"... and high"},
        "8571": {"comment":"B = the media byte"},
        "8575": {"comment":"C = sectors per track"},
        "8578": {"comment":"The record at +$50?"},
        "8581": {"comment":"A = the sides"},
        "8583": {"comment":"HL = BPB+$11: the hidden sectors"},
        "8586": {"synopsis":"The record at +$50: 2 sides when its byte says 2, else 1.","comment":"2 sides?"},
        "8590": {"comment":"No: 1"},
        "8592": {"synopsis":"The record at +$50: 9 sectors per track.","comment":"9 sectors per track"},
        "8594": {"synopsis":"Stores the sectors per track; a disk with as many sides as the drive's last one, or with one\nside, goes on; otherwise side 1 is checked (FD_SIDE1_TRY), H counting the tries.","comment":"The drive's sectors per track"},
        "8597": {"comment":"The other set: B' = select bit, HL' = BPB"},
        "8598": {"comment":"Same sides as before?"},
        "8603": {"comment":"One side?"},
        "8607": {"comment":"H = the tries"},
        "8608": {"synopsis":"Reads an address field on side 1 of the current track. A time-out or change is mapped to its\nerror; a record not found gives $96 (Incompatible disk); other failures are tried again.","comment":"Stay on the track; flags 0"},
        "8611": {"comment":"Side 1"},
        "8613": {"comment":"B = the drive's select bit"},
        "8616": {"comment":"Reads an address field, side C"},
        "8619": {"comment":"Read: is it side 1?"},
        "8621": {"comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "8623": {"comment":"Yes: map it"},
        "8625": {"comment":"Record not found?"},
        "8627": {"comment":"Yes: incompatible"},
        "8629": {"comment":"Another try?"},
        "8632": {"synopsis":"Error $96 (Incompatible disk). $21BB, inside the LD HL, is LD A,$B4: the entry for error $B4\n(Not a DOS disk).","comment":"Error $96"},
        "8634": {"comment":"Hides LD A,$B4 at $21BB: error $B4 (Not a DOS disk)"},
        "8637": {"synopsis":"Returns the error in A with NZ."},
        "8639": {"synopsis":"The field was read: its side byte (IY-$10) must be 1, else the disk is incompatible.","comment":"The field's side"},
        "8642": {"comment":"1?"},
        "8643": {"comment":"No: incompatible"},
        "8645": {"comment":"2 sides"},
        "8647": {"synopsis":"Stores the sides and the first sector's offset (the BPB's hidden sectors), then finds the\nlast sector's track (LSN_TO_CHS): it must be 1-253. A media byte the drive had before keeps\nthe flags; else a disk of fewer than 51 tracks clears bit 2, a larger one sets it and,\nunless bit 1 is set, has the double step checked (FD_CHECK_STEP).","comment":"The drive's sides"},
        "8650": {"comment":"HL = BPB+$11 again"},
        "8651": {"comment":"The hidden sectors"},
        "8654": {"comment":"The drive's first sector offset, low"},
        "8657": {"comment":"... and high"},
        "8660": {"comment":"DE = the last sector"},
        "8661": {"comment":"Its track, side and sector"},
        "8664": {"comment":"Offset overflow: not a DOS disk"},
        "8666": {"comment":"Track above 255?"},
        "8668": {"comment":"Yes: NZ, A = the track's high byte"},
        "8669": {"comment":"Track 1-253?"},
        "8673": {"comment":"No: not a DOS disk"},
        "8675": {"comment":"The drive's last track"},
        "8678": {"comment":"The media byte"},
        "8679": {"comment":"The drive's media byte before?"},
        "8682": {"comment":"Yes: keep the flags"},
        "8684": {"comment":"51 tracks or more?"},
        "8687": {"comment":"A = the drive's flags"},
        "8690": {"comment":"Not over 50 tracks"},
        "8692": {"comment":"Fewer: store them"},
        "8694": {"comment":"Over 50 tracks"},
        "8696": {"comment":"Double step known?"},
        "8698": {"comment":"Yes: store them"},
        "8700": {"comment":"C = the new flags"},
        "8702": {"comment":"B = the drive's select bit"},
        "8705": {"comment":"Checks the head steps on this disk"},
        "8709": {"comment":"C: incompatible ($96)"},
        "8711": {"synopsis":"A failed check is mapped to its error; else the flags worked out before the check (C) are\nstored, not those the check wrote.","comment":"Failed: map it"},
        "8713": {"comment":"A = the new flags"},
        "8714": {"synopsis":"Stores the drive's flags and media byte.","comment":"The drive's flags"},
        "8717": {"comment":"The drive's media byte"},
        "8720": {"synopsis":"Marks the parameters known and returns A = 0.","comment":"Parameters known"},
        "8724": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "8726": {"synopsis":"Turns DISK_IO's error bits in A into EXDOS error codes from the table at $2229, by the\nlowest set bit: 0 time-out $BA (Not ready), 1 mismatch $B9 (Verify error), 2 lost data and\n3 CRC $B8 (Data error), 4 not found $B7 (Sector not found), 5 disk changed $BF, 6 write\nprotected $B6 (Write protected disk), 7 no drive or bad operation $BD. $BF also marks the\ndrive's parameters not known. Exchanges the register sets (EXX) and returns NZ.","comment":"One before the table"},
        "8729": {"synopsis":"Steps through the table until the lowest set bit."},
        "8730": {"comment":"This bit set?"},
        "8733": {"comment":"A = its error code"},
        "8734": {"comment":"Swaps the register sets"},
        "8735": {"comment":"Disk changed?"},
        "8739": {"comment":"Yes: parameters not known"},
        "8743": {"synopsis":"Returns A with NZ."},
        "8753": {"synopsis":"FLOPPY_DRIVER functions 4 (read), 5 (write) and 6 (write and verify): B sectors from logical\nsector DE, the caller's IX being the buffer.\n1. No count: A = 0. Parameters not known: A = $BF.\n2. The double step is checked when it was not yet (FD_CHECK_STEP).\n3. Refuses a run past the disk's end ($BB).\n4. Works a track (and side) at a time (FD_XFER_TRACK, FD_XFER_RETRY).\nIt returns with the register sets exchanged, so the caller gets the counters kept in the\nalternates: B = the sectors done, C = those not done, HL = past the last one done. The flags\ndo not always match A; DRIVER_CALL sets them with OR A.","comment":"IX = drive's slot, A = count, B = select bit"},
        "8757": {"comment":"B' = 0: done"},
        "8759": {"comment":"C' = the count: left"},
        "8761": {"comment":"Parameters known?"},
        "8765": {"comment":"No: error $BF"},
        "8767": {"comment":"L = the count"},
        "8769": {"comment":"None: A = 0"},
        "8772": {"comment":"Step checked?"},
        "8776": {"comment":"No: check it now"},
        "8779": {"comment":"C: incompatible ($96)"},
        "8782": {"comment":"Failed: map it"},
        "8784": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "8785": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "8786": {"comment":"HL = the last sector"},
        "8787": {"comment":"Past $FFFF"},
        "8790": {"comment":"BC = the disk's total sectors"},
        "8796": {"comment":"The last sector inside the disk?"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Yes: go"},
        "8801": {"synopsis":"The run ends past the disk: error $BB (a code with no message). $2264, inside the LD HL, is\nLD A,$BF: the entry for parameters not known.","comment":"Error $BB"},
        "8803": {"comment":"Hides LD A,$BF at $2264: parameters not known"},
        "8806": {"synopsis":"Exchanges the register sets for the caller and returns.","comment":"B = sectors done, C = not done, HL = buffer"},
        "8808": {"synopsis":"The first sector's track, side and sector.","comment":"DE = track, C = side, A = sector"},
        "8811": {"comment":"D = the track"},
        "8812": {"comment":"E = the sector"},
        "8813": {"synopsis":"L = the sectors to do on this track and side: those left on it, or fewer when the count left\n(C') is smaller.","comment":"Sectors per track"},
        "8816": {"comment":"Less the first sector"},
        "8817": {"comment":"+ 1: those left on the track"},
        "8818": {"comment":"C' = the count left"},
        "8819": {"comment":"More than that?"},
        "8822": {"comment":"No: all that is left"},
        "8823": {"synopsis":"Transfers them (FD_XFER_RETRY); then goes on at sector 1 of the next side, or of the next\ntrack after the last side, until the count is done.","comment":"L = sectors this pass"},
        "8825": {"comment":"Transfers them"},
        "8828": {"comment":"Failed: map it"},
        "8830": {"comment":"A = 0 OR the count left"},
        "8832": {"comment":"Done: A = 0 with the sets exchanged"},
        "8834": {"comment":"Sector 1"},
        "8836": {"comment":"Next side"},
        "8837": {"comment":"Past the last side?"},
        "8841": {"comment":"No"},
        "8843": {"comment":"Side 0"},
        "8844": {"comment":"Next track"},
        "8845": {"synopsis":"The next pass."},
        "8847": {"synopsis":"Turns a logical sector into its track, side and sector: adds the drive's first sector\noffset, divides by the sectors per track, and for two sides takes the low bit of the\nquotient as the side.\nEntry: DE = the logical sector; IX = the drive's slot.\nExit: DE = the track; C = the side; A = the sector (from 1); NC.\nError: C with A = 0 when the offset takes it past $FFFF.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.\nKeeps: B, IX, IY.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "8848": {"comment":"HL = the drive's first sector offset"},
        "8854": {"comment":"Plus the sector"},
        "8856": {"comment":"Past $FFFF"},
        "8857": {"comment":"C = sectors per track"},
        "8860": {"comment":"DE = the quotient, A = the sector - 1"},
        "8863": {"comment":"C = the sides"},
        "8866": {"comment":"NC: side 0 for one side"},
        "8867": {"comment":"One side?"},
        "8868": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8870": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "8871": {"comment":"DE = the track, carry = the side"},
        "8875": {"synopsis":"C = the side from the carry, A = the sector from 1.","comment":"C = the side"},
        "8877": {"comment":"The sector, from 1"},
        "8879": {"synopsis":"Divides DE by C, bit by bit.\nEntry: DE = the dividend; C = the divisor (1-128).\nExit: DE = the quotient; A = the remainder.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "8880": {"comment":"16 bits"},
        "8882": {"comment":"The remainder starts at 0"},
        "8883": {"synopsis":"Shifts the next bit into the remainder and subtracts the divisor when it fits.","comment":"Next bit of DE ..."},
        "8887": {"comment":"... into the remainder"},
        "8888": {"comment":"Does the divisor fit?"},
        "8891": {"comment":"Yes: take it off"},
        "8892": {"comment":"Quotient bit 1"},
        "8893": {"synopsis":"The next bit."},
        "8895": {"comment":"The caller's BC"},
        "8897": {"synopsis":"Every function's start: checks the unit's drive number in C and points IX at the drive's\nslot in the per-drive arrays (IY + the drive), keeping the caller's IX (the buffer) in HL'.\nA drive number of 4 or more leaves the driver function at once with error $BC (FD_UNIT_BAD).\nEntry: C = the drive (0-3); B = the caller's value (a count or a media byte); IX = the\nbuffer; IY = the driver's variables.\nExit: IX = IY + C; A = the entry B; B = the drive's select bit; HL' = the entry IX; DE' = C.\nError: drops its return address and returns from the driver function with A = $BC, B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, IX, DE', HL'.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"A = the drive"},
        "8898": {"comment":"Drive 0-3?"},
        "8900": {"comment":"No: error $BC"},
        "8903": {"comment":"DE' = the drive"},
        "8906": {"comment":"IX = IY, the caller's IX on the stack"},
        "8910": {"comment":"IX = the drive's slot"},
        "8912": {"comment":"HL' = the caller's IX (the buffer)"},
        "8914": {"comment":"A = the caller's B"},
        "8915": {"comment":"B = the drive's select bit"},
        "8919": {"synopsis":"No such drive: returns from the driver function with A = $BC (a code with no message) and\nB = 0.","comment":"Drops the return into the function"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Error $BC"},
        "8922": {"comment":"Nothing done"},
        "8925": {"synopsis":"Reads an address field on side 0 of the track the head is on (ADDR_READ with D = $FF).\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; IY = the driver's variables.\nExit: as ADDR_READ.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Stay on the track"},
        "8927": {"synopsis":"Reads an address field on side 0 of track D, with no extra flags (ADDR_READ with E = 0).\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; D = the track; IY = the driver's variables.\nExit: as ADDR_READ.\nChanges: AF, E, D.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"No extra flags"},
        "8929": {"synopsis":"Reads one address field (DISK_IO 6) on side 0 into IY-$11 to IY-$0C: track, side, sector,\nsize, CRC. $22E5 (inside LD A,$C5) is the entry that keeps the caller's C as the side.\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; D = the track ($FF: stay); E = flags for DISK_IO's H (bit\n5 to the latch, bit 3 double step), added to the step rate in bits 0-1 of IY-$55; IY.\nExit: A = D = DISK_IO's result (0 with Z when a field was read).\nChanges: AF, D; IY-$11 to IY-$0C.\nKeeps: BC, E, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps BC"},
        "8930": {"comment":"Side 0"},
        "8932": {"comment":"Hides PUSH BC at $22E5, the entry with C = the side"},
        "8935": {"comment":"IX = IY, the caller's IX on the stack"},
        "8940": {"comment":"-$11"},
        "8943": {"comment":"IX = IY-$11: the field goes there"},
        "8946": {"comment":"The step rate"},
        "8951": {"comment":"With the flags"},
        "8952": {"comment":"H = DISK_IO's flags"},
        "8953": {"comment":"One field"},
        "8955": {"comment":"Read address"},
        "8960": {"comment":"The caller's IX"},
        "8964": {"comment":"D = the result"},
        "8966": {"synopsis":"One DISK_IO transfer for the function at IY-$12 (4 read, 5 write, 6 write then verify,\n8 write a track): double step when the drive's flags say so, write precompensation on tracks\npast half the last; then moves the counters on by the sectors done.\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; C = the side; D = the track; E = the sector; L = the\ncount; H = the sectors done so far; HL' = the buffer; B' = done, C' = left; IX = the drive's\nslot.\nExit: A and the flags = DISK_IO's result (function 6: the verify's when it failed); E = the\nnext sector; H = done so far + done now; L = the count less done now; HL' advanced 512 bytes\na sector; B' + done, C' - done; E' = done now.\nChanges: AF, B, E, HL, AF', BC', E', H'.\nKeeps: C, D, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the done and count"},
        "8967": {"comment":"The step rate"},
        "8972": {"comment":"H = DISK_IO's flags"},
        "8973": {"comment":"The drive's flags"},
        "8976": {"comment":"Double step, not over 50 tracks?"},
        "8982": {"comment":"Yes: double step"},
        "8984": {"synopsis":"Write precompensation past half the last track.","comment":"The last track"},
        "8987": {"comment":"Half of it"},
        "8988": {"comment":"Track past that?"},
        "8992": {"comment":"Yes: precompensation"},
        "8994": {"synopsis":"Puts the buffer in IX and picks DISK_IO's operation: function 8 writes a track (4)."},
        "8995": {"comment":"The buffer ..."},
        "8996": {"comment":"... in IX, the drive's slot on the stack"},
        "8999": {"comment":"The function"},
        "9002": {"comment":"Format (8)?"},
        "9006": {"comment":"Yes: 4, write a track"},
        "9009": {"synopsis":"Function 4 reads (1), functions 5 and 6 write (2).","comment":"Function 4?"},
        "9011": {"comment":"Read"},
        "9015": {"comment":"Write"},
        "9016": {"synopsis":"Runs the operation; for function 6 after sectors were written, verifies them (DISK_IO 3) and\nreturns the verify's result when it failed, else the write's.","comment":"Runs it"},
        "9019": {"comment":"AF' = the result"},
        "9020": {"comment":"The function"},
        "9023": {"comment":"Write and verify?"},
        "9027": {"comment":"Any sectors written?"},
        "9030": {"comment":"Verify them"},
        "9035": {"comment":"Verified: the write's result"},
        "9037": {"comment":"The verify's result goes back"},
        "9038": {"synopsis":"Moves the counters on by the sectors done (L) and returns DISK_IO's result.","comment":"IX = the drive's slot"},
        "9042": {"comment":"E = the next sector"},
        "9045": {"comment":"A = the sectors done"},
        "9047": {"comment":"E' = done now"},
        "9048": {"comment":"512 bytes a sector ..."},
        "9050": {"comment":"... H' = the buffer past them"},
        "9051": {"comment":"B' = done in all"},
        "9054": {"comment":"C' = left"},
        "9058": {"comment":"A = done now"},
        "9059": {"comment":"H = done so far, L = the count"},
        "9060": {"comment":"H = done in all"},
        "9062": {"comment":"L = the count ..."},
        "9064": {"comment":"... less done now"},
        "9067": {"comment":"A = DISK_IO's result"},
        "9069": {"synopsis":"Transfers sectors with up to 4 tries' worth of retries (D'), each failure costing by kind: 5\nfor a time-out, a disk change or write protection (no retry), 1 for a mismatch, lost data or\nCRC error, 2 for others. A first record not found reads an address field: a wrong track has\nthe double step checked again. A retry goes on from the sector that failed.\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; C = the side; D = the track; E = the first sector; L =\nthe count; HL' = the buffer; B' and C' the counters (FD_XFER_ONCE); IX = the drive's slot;\nIY-$12 = the function.\nExit: A = 0 with Z; L = the sectors done; E = the next sector; HL', B', C' moved on.\nError: NZ with A = the error bits that ended it (masked by kind; $20 for a change found by\nthe address read).\nChanges: AF, B, E, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: C, D, IX, IY."},
        "9070": {"comment":"D' = the tries"},
        "9073": {"comment":"H = done so far"},
        "9075": {"synopsis":"One transfer; a failure is weighed by its bits.","comment":"One transfer"},
        "9078": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "9079": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9081": {"comment":"Keeps done and count"},
        "9082": {"comment":"L = the error bits"},
        "9083": {"comment":"Time-out, change, write protect?"},
        "9085": {"comment":"Yes: no retry"},
        "9088": {"comment":"Mismatch, lost data, CRC?"},
        "9090": {"comment":"Yes: cost 1"},
        "9092": {"comment":"A = the tries left"},
        "9095": {"comment":"Retried before?"},
        "9097": {"comment":"A = the error bits"},
        "9098": {"comment":"Yes: cost 2"},
        "9101": {"comment":"Stay on the track, no flags"},
        "9104": {"comment":"Reads an address field, side C"},
        "9108": {"comment":"Read: right track?"},
        "9110": {"comment":"Disk change?"},
        "9112": {"comment":"Yes: no retry"},
        "9114": {"comment":"No field: check the steps"},
        "9116": {"synopsis":"The head is on the right track: a retry at cost 2; on the wrong one the double step is\nchecked again.","comment":"The track found"},
        "9119": {"comment":"The one asked for?"},
        "9120": {"comment":"Yes: retry"},
        "9122": {"synopsis":"Checks the double step again (FD_CHECK_STEP).","comment":"Checks the steps"},
        "9125": {"comment":"Z when it worked"},
        "9126": {"synopsis":"Retry at cost 2 when the check worked, else no retry.","comment":"A = the error bits"},
        "9127": {"comment":"Worked: cost 2"},
        "9129": {"synopsis":"H = the failure's cost (5 here; $23AC is LD H,1, $23AF LD H,2, entries inside the JPs, which\nnever jump: Z is clear). Takes the cost off the tries (D'); while they do not go below 0,\ntransfers again. Before that, a try other than the first calls DISK_IO with A = tries - 4\n($FC-$FF), an operation it refuses with $80.","comment":"Cost 5: no retry"},
        "9131": {"comment":"Hides LD H,1 at $23AC: cost 1"},
        "9134": {"comment":"Hides LD H,2 at $23AF: cost 2"},
        "9137": {"comment":"Keeps the error bits"},
        "9139": {"comment":"A = the tries left"},
        "9142": {"comment":"The first try?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No: DISK_IO refuses A = $FC-$FF"},
        "9147": {"comment":"A = the tries left"},
        "9148": {"comment":"Less the cost"},
        "9150": {"comment":"D' = the tries left"},
        "9152": {"comment":"H = the error bits"},
        "9153": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "9154": {"comment":"H = done so far, L = the count"},
        "9155": {"comment":"Tries left: again"},
        "9157": {"synopsis":"L = the sectors done; flags from A.","comment":"L = the sectors done"},
        "9158": {"comment":"Z when A = 0"},
        "9160": {"synopsis":"Checks how the head steps on this disk: forgets the track, seeks 8 steps and reads an\naddress field (two tries). Track 8 found: single steps (for a disk of at most 50 tracks, bit\n1 is cleared). Track 4: double steps (bit 2 cleared, bit 1 set). Track 16: error $96. Sets\nbit 0 of the drive's flags (checked), and forgets the track again at the end.\nEntry: B = the drive's select bit; IX = the drive's slot; IY.\nExit: A = 0 with Z; bits 0-2 of IX-$07 set as above.\nError: Z and C with A = $96 (Incompatible disk); NZ with DISK_IO's bits: $01/$20/$21 for a\ntime-out or change, else the last read's result ($10 when another track was found).\nChanges: AF; IX-$07, the drive's track (forgotten).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps BC"},
        "9162": {"comment":"Two tries"},
        "9164": {"comment":"Not checked"},
        "9168": {"comment":"No double step"},
        "9172": {"synopsis":"Forgets the track and reads an address field 8 steps in.","comment":"DISK_IO 0"},
        "9173": {"comment":"Forgets the drive's track"},
        "9176": {"comment":"Track 8, single steps"},
        "9178": {"comment":"Reads an address field there"},
        "9181": {"comment":"Read"},
        "9183": {"comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "9185": {"comment":"Yes: fail"},
        "9187": {"synopsis":"Another try, or fails with the last result in D.","comment":"Another try?"},
        "9190": {"comment":"A = the result"},
        "9191": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "9194": {"synopsis":"Judges the track the field gives: 4 double steps, 8 single steps, 16 incompatible; another\nis tried again with D = $10.","comment":"E = the flags ..."},
        "9197": {"comment":"... marked double step"},
        "9199": {"comment":"The track found"},
        "9202": {"comment":"4?"},
        "9204": {"comment":"Yes: double steps"},
        "9206": {"comment":"8?"},
        "9208": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9210": {"comment":"16?"},
        "9212": {"comment":"D = $10, not found, for another"},
        "9214": {"comment":"Neither: again"},
        "9216": {"comment":"Error $96 (Incompatible disk)"},
        "9218": {"comment":"C"},
        "9221": {"synopsis":"Track 8: single steps; bit 1 is kept for a disk over 50 tracks, else cleared.","comment":"Over 50 tracks?"},
        "9223": {"comment":"Yes: keep bit 1"},
        "9225": {"comment":"No double step"},
        "9227": {"comment":"Never jumps (Z); hides RES 2,E at $240C, the entry for track 4"},
        "9230": {"synopsis":"Marks the drive checked and stores the flags; A = 0.","comment":"Checked"},
        "9232": {"comment":"The drive's flags"},
        "9235": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "9236": {"synopsis":"Forgets the drive's track and returns the result.","comment":"Keeps the result"},
        "9237": {"comment":"DISK_IO 0"},
        "9238": {"comment":"Forgets the drive's track"},
        "9242": {"comment":"The caller's DE and BC"},
        "9245": {"synopsis":"FLOPPY_DRIVER function 8: formats the disk for media byte B ($F8-$FF, else error $B4).\nCounts the drive's tracks (DISK_IO 8): an 80-track drive gives the disk over 50 tracks\nunless the media byte's bit 2 asks for 40 (then double steps); a 40-track drive forces bit 2\non. Then checks the drive answers on track 0 and builds the track image (FMT_BUILD_IMAGE).","comment":"IX = the drive's slot, A = the media byte"},
        "9248": {"comment":"C = the media byte"},
        "9249": {"comment":"$F8 or more?"},
        "9251": {"comment":"Error $B4 (Not a DOS disk)"},
        "9253": {"comment":"No: refused"},
        "9254": {"comment":"H = the step rate"},
        "9257": {"comment":"Count the drive's tracks"},
        "9262": {"comment":"Failed: map it"},
        "9265": {"comment":"Flags: checked, double step"},
        "9267": {"comment":"An 80-track drive (L = $FF)?"},
        "9268": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9270": {"comment":"40-track drive: single steps"},
        "9272": {"comment":"A 40-track media byte"},
        "9274": {"synopsis":"An 80-track disk (media bit 2 clear) is marked over 50 tracks.","comment":"A 40-track media byte?"},
        "9278": {"comment":"No: over 50 tracks"},
        "9280": {"synopsis":"Stores the drive's flags and reads an address field on track 0: a time-out, change or no\ndrive gives $BA (Not ready). Then writes the track image into the buffer from the pairs at\n$2553 (FILL_PAIRS): the track's header, then a sector at a time (FMT_IMG_SECTOR).","comment":"The drive's flags"},
        "9283": {"comment":"Track 0 (A = 0 from DISK_IO)"},
        "9284": {"comment":"Reads an address field there"},
        "9287": {"comment":"Time-out, change, no drive?"},
        "9289": {"comment":"Error $BA (Not ready)"},
        "9292": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "9293": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9294": {"comment":"The track's header"},
        "9297": {"comment":"5 pairs"},
        "9302": {"comment":"9 sectors"},
        "9304": {"comment":"A' = sector 1"},
        "9307": {"synopsis":"One sector's part of the image: the pairs at $255D for the address field (its track and side\n0, filled in later), the sector number, then 10 pairs for the size code 2, the gaps and 512\nbytes of $E5. After 9 sectors, the 2 pairs that follow give the track's end.","comment":"The sector's pairs"},
        "9310": {"comment":"4: up to the track and side"},
        "9315": {"comment":"A = the sector number"},
        "9316": {"comment":"Into the address field"},
        "9318": {"comment":"The next sector's number"},
        "9320": {"comment":"10 pairs: size, data field, gaps"},
        "9325": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "9328": {"comment":"The track's end: 2 pairs"},
        "9333": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "9334": {"comment":"Back to the caller's set"},
        "9335": {"synopsis":"The format's passes, entered with the track image built at HL': FMT_ALL_TRACKS writes every\ntrack (IY-$12 = 8), then a second pass with IY-$12 = 0 reads every track back. Then the boot\nsector is built in the same buffer and written to track 0, side 0, sector 1:\n1. BPB_FROM_MEDIA fills in the BPB from the media byte C.\n2. +0 gets the 3 bytes and \"EXDOS1.3\" at $24C2, +$1E a RET ($C9).\n3. +$40 gets \"VOL_ID\" ($113D), +$47 the 4 bytes at IY-$4A as the disk's serial.\n4. FD_XFER_RETRY writes it with IY-$12 = 5 (one sector, no verify).\nA double-sided format that finds side 1 missing on track 0 comes back here with the media\nbyte one lower (FMT_ONE_SIDED): the one-sided type.","comment":"Pass 1: every track, the function at IY-$12"},
        "9338": {"comment":"A = 0: pass 2 reads the tracks back"},
        "9341": {"comment":"Pass 2"},
        "9344": {"comment":"A = the media byte"},
        "9346": {"comment":"Keeps the buffer"},
        "9347": {"comment":"C = the media byte"},
        "9348": {"comment":"The BPB at +$0B; HL = the buffer +$0B"},
        "9351": {"comment":"DE = the buffer +$0B"},
        "9352": {"comment":"From the last byte of \"EXDOS1.3\""},
        "9355": {"comment":"The jump bytes and the name: 11 bytes"},
        "9358": {"comment":"DE = the buffer +$0A"},
        "9359": {"comment":"Down to the buffer +0"},
        "9363": {"comment":"HL = the buffer - 1"},
        "9364": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +$1E"},
        "9365": {"comment":"A RET"},
        "9369": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +$40"},
        "9370": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "9371": {"comment":"\"VOL_ID\""},
        "9374": {"comment":"6 letters"},
        "9378": {"comment":"DE = the buffer +$47 (+$46 stays 0)"},
        "9379": {"comment":"HL = IY"},
        "9382": {"comment":"IY-$4A"},
        "9386": {"comment":"4 bytes: the serial"},
        "9391": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "9393": {"comment":"Keeps the media byte"},
        "9394": {"comment":"Track 0, sector 1"},
        "9397": {"comment":"Side 0"},
        "9398": {"comment":"One sector"},
        "9399": {"comment":"Function 5: write"},
        "9403": {"comment":"Writes the boot sector"},
        "9407": {"comment":"Failed: map the error"},
        "9409": {"comment":"A = 0, Z: formatted"},
        "9421": {"synopsis":"One pass over every track of the disk for function 8: takes its return address into HL (the\npass returns with JP (HL) at $2544), starts at track 0 and goes on at $24D0: per track and\nside 8 or 9 sectors by the media byte, through FD_XFER_RETRY with the function at IY-$12 (8\nwrites the track image, its address fields given the track and side first).\nEntry: C = the media byte (bit 0 two sides, bit 1 8 sectors, bit 2 40 tracks); B = the\ndrive's select bit; IX = the drive's slot; HL' = the track image; IY-$12 = the function.\nExit: A = 0 when every track is done.\nError: a failure leaves function 8 itself through FD_ERR_MAP; $C4B2 giving Z leaves it too.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Track 0"},
        "9424": {"synopsis":"One track: D = the last side (1 for a double-sided media byte), sides done downwards.","comment":"A = the media byte"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Bit 0: two sides"},
        "9427": {"comment":"D = the side"},
        "9428": {"synopsis":"One side of track E: keeps the return address and the track and side, then (pass 1, IY-$12\nbit 3) writes the track and side into the 9 address fields of the image (FMT_PATCH_IDS).","comment":"Keeps the pass's return address"},
        "9429": {"comment":"Keeps the side and the track"},
        "9431": {"comment":"B' = the side, C' = the track"},
        "9432": {"comment":"Keeps the image's address"},
        "9433": {"comment":"Writing the tracks (function 8)?"},
        "9437": {"comment":"No: the image is not used"},
        "9439": {"comment":"9 address fields"},
        "9441": {"comment":"The first one's track byte: the image +$98"},
        "9444": {"synopsis":"Writes the track and the side into one address field, then steps to the next ($290 bytes\non)."},
        "9445": {"comment":"The track"},
        "9447": {"comment":"The side"},
        "9448": {"comment":"One sector's bytes in the image, less 1"},
        "9451": {"comment":"Next address field"},
        "9454": {"synopsis":"The transfer for one side: L = 9 sectors, or 8 for a media byte with bit 1 set.","comment":"HL = the image"},
        "9455": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "9456": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "9457": {"comment":"Keeps the media byte"},
        "9458": {"comment":"Keeps the side and the track"},
        "9459": {"comment":"9 sectors"},
        "9461": {"comment":"A media byte for 8 sectors a track?"},
        "9465": {"comment":"8"},
        "9466": {"synopsis":"Runs the side's transfer (FD_XFER_RETRY) from sector 1, then takes the registers back: the\npass's return address goes to HL for JP (HL) at the end.","comment":"C = the side"},
        "9467": {"comment":"D = the track"},
        "9468": {"comment":"From sector 1"},
        "9470": {"comment":"Writes or reads the side"},
        "9473": {"comment":"The side and the track"},
        "9474": {"comment":"The media byte"},
        "9476": {"comment":"HL' = the image again"},
        "9478": {"comment":"HL = the pass's return address"},
        "9479": {"synopsis":"After a side: a failure leaves the format through FD_ERR_MAP; Z from $C4B2 leaves it at\nonce; else the next side down. After side 0, a double-sided pass 1 on track 0 reads an\naddress field on side 1: a time-out or a disk change fails, any other failure, or a field\nwhose side byte is not 1, makes the disk one-sided (FMT_ONE_SIDED).","comment":"Failed: map the error and leave"},
        "9482": {"comment":"$C4B2 says stop?"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Yes: leave the format with Z"},
        "9486": {"comment":"The next side down"},
        "9487": {"comment":"Another side"},
        "9490": {"comment":"Two sides?"},
        "9492": {"comment":"No"},
        "9494": {"comment":"Pass 1 (writing the tracks)?"},
        "9498": {"comment":"No"},
        "9500": {"comment":"Track 0?"},
        "9502": {"comment":"No"},
        "9504": {"comment":"Keeps the track and the side"},
        "9505": {"comment":"Keeps the media byte"},
        "9506": {"comment":"Side 1"},
        "9508": {"comment":"Reads an address field there (ADDR_READ's $22E5)"},
        "9511": {"comment":"The media byte"},
        "9512": {"comment":"The track and the side"},
        "9513": {"comment":"Read: check its side byte"},
        "9515": {"comment":"Time-out or disk change?"},
        "9517": {"comment":"Yes: fail"},
        "9519": {"synopsis":"Formats again with the media byte one lower: bit 0 clear, the one-sided type.","comment":"Media byte - 1: one side"},
        "9520": {"comment":"Formats the disk again"},
        "9523": {"synopsis":"An address field was read on side 1: its side byte (IY-$10) must be 1.","comment":"The field's side byte"},
        "9526": {"comment":"Side 1?"},
        "9527": {"comment":"No: the drive has one head"},
        "9529": {"synopsis":"The track count by the media byte: 40 for bit 2 set, else 80.","comment":"40 tracks"},
        "9531": {"comment":"A 40-track media byte?"},
        "9535": {"comment":"80 tracks"},
        "9536": {"synopsis":"The next track; after the last one the pass returns through its return address in HL.","comment":"The next track"},
        "9537": {"comment":"Tracks left"},
        "9538": {"comment":"More: the next track"},
        "9540": {"comment":"Pass done: back to its caller, A = 0"},
        "9541": {"synopsis":"Writes B runs of bytes from a list of (count, byte) pairs; a count of 0 is 256.\nEntry: B = the pairs; DE = the list; HL = where to write.\nExit: DE past the list; HL past the bytes; B = 0.\nChanges: A, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: F, C, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the pairs left"},
        "9543": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "9545": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "9547": {"synopsis":"FILL_PAIRS' inner loop: writes byte A count times, then takes the next pair.","comment":"One byte of the run"},
        "9549": {"comment":"Rest of the run"},
        "9551": {"comment":"B = the pairs left"},
        "9552": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "9597": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 13 (table word at $056A), the call close makes on a file. A file the control\nblock marks changed (bit 6 of +$20) gets its directory entry brought up to date:\n1. The directory's cluster (+$1F/$20, flag bits cleared) goes to IY+$30; the file's drive\n   (+$07) is selected, its disk checked against the file's.\n2. The entry is searched for again (DIR_FIRST, SEARCH_DIR): missing gives $CF; one with\n   attribute bits 0-2 set gives $A1.\n3. STAMP_ENTRY writes the time and date; the archive bit (5) is set; the first cluster\n   (+$21) and the size (+$17) are copied in. The drive's changed buffers are written out.\n4. FCB_FROM_ENTRY reloads the block from the entry (position 0).\nEvery return goes through $264A: DE = the control block.\nEntry: A = 0 (the dispatcher's); DE = the file's control block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z (also for an unchanged file); DE = IX = the control block.\nError: NZ, A = $CF (the entry is gone), $A1 (Invalid file attributes) or SELECT_DRIVE's\nerror.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; the directory sector's buffer; IY+$30,\nIY+$60-$62.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"IX = the control block"},
        "9600": {"comment":"Every return: DE = IX"},
        "9604": {"comment":"DE = the directory's cluster and flags"},
        "9610": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "9612": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9613": {"comment":"Clears the changed bit"},
        "9615": {"comment":"And the read-only bit"},
        "9617": {"comment":"The directory to search"},
        "9623": {"comment":"C = the file's drive"},
        "9626": {"comment":"B = 1: check it holds the file's disk"},
        "9628": {"comment":"Selects the drive; HL = its record"},
        "9631": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9633": {"comment":"Starts on the directory"},
        "9636": {"comment":"Searches it for the name"},
        "9639": {"comment":"Not found: error $CF"},
        "9641": {"comment":"Attribute bits 0-2 set?"},
        "9643": {"comment":"Error $A1 (Invalid file attributes)"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Time and date into the entry"},
        "9649": {"comment":"Keeps the entry"},
        "9650": {"comment":"HL = the control block, the record kept"},
        "9653": {"comment":"The size at +$17"},
        "9657": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the entry"},
        "9658": {"comment":"Entry +$0B: the attributes"},
        "9661": {"comment":"The archive bit"},
        "9663": {"comment":"Entry +$1A: the first cluster"},
        "9666": {"comment":"From the block's +$21"},
        "9676": {"comment":"HL = the block's +$17, DE = the entry's +$1C"},
        "9677": {"comment":"4 bytes: the size"},
        "9681": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "9682": {"comment":"Writes the drive's changed buffers out"},
        "9685": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "9686": {"comment":"The entry again (its buffer may have moved)"},
        "9689": {"comment":"No attributes for the block"},
        "9691": {"comment":"Reloads the block from the entry"},
        "9693": {"synopsis":"The file's name is no longer in its directory: error $CF.","comment":"Error $CF"},
        "9696": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 12 (table word at $0568): fills a file's control block from its directory\nentry. DIR_REOPEN_ENTRY goes back to the entry; a directory or a volume label (attribute bit\n4 or 3) gives $A1; then FCB_FROM_ENTRY copies it in, the position set to 0. Every return\ngoes through $264A: DE = the control block.\nEntry: DE = the control block (first byte $FE); HL = the block with the directory position;\nIY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; DE = IX = the control block; BC = the file's first cluster; IY+$60 = the\nunit (IY+$2B), IY+$61/$62 = the first cluster.\nError: NZ, A = $A1 (Invalid file attributes) or DIR_REOPEN_ENTRY's error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Every return: DE = IX"},
        "9700": {"comment":"Back to the entry; A = its attributes"},
        "9703": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9704": {"comment":"B = the attributes"},
        "9705": {"comment":"A directory or a volume label?"},
        "9707": {"comment":"Error $A1 (Invalid file attributes)"},
        "9710": {"synopsis":"Copies the directory entry DE into the control block IX: the size, date and time, the first\ncluster (also kept as the cluster of index 0), the directory's cluster (IY+$30) with bit 5\nset for a read-only file (bit 0 of the attributes in B), and position 0. IY+$60-$62 keep the\nunit and the first cluster.","comment":"Keeps the attributes"},
        "9711": {"comment":"HL = the control block"},
        "9714": {"comment":"+$17: the size"},
        "9718": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the entry"},
        "9719": {"comment":"Entry +$1C: its size"},
        "9722": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "9724": {"comment":"Keeps the entry's +$1C"},
        "9728": {"comment":"HL = entry +$1B"},
        "9729": {"comment":"BC = the first cluster (+$1A)"},
        "9732": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "9733": {"comment":"IY+$61/$62 = the first cluster"},
        "9739": {"comment":"The unit being used"},
        "9742": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$60"},
        "9745": {"comment":"HL = entry +$18: the date"},
        "9747": {"comment":"Into the block's +$1B"},
        "9751": {"comment":"HL = entry +$16: the time"},
        "9755": {"comment":"Into the block's +$1D"},
        "9759": {"comment":"HL = the block's +$1F"},
        "9760": {"comment":"BC = the first cluster"},
        "9761": {"comment":"DE = IY+$30: the directory's cluster"},
        "9765": {"synopsis":"Clears the flag bits of the directory's cluster and sets bit 5 for a read-only file.","comment":"Not changed"},
        "9767": {"comment":"Not read only"},
        "9769": {"comment":"A = the attributes"},
        "9770": {"comment":"Read only?"},
        "9774": {"comment":"Yes: mark the block"},
        "9776": {"synopsis":"Writes the rest of the block from +$1F: the directory's cluster and flags, the first cluster\ntwice (+$21 and +$23, the cluster kept for index 0), the index 0 (+$25) and the position 0\n(+$28-$2B); +$27 is left as it was. Returns A = 0, Z.","comment":"+$1F/$20: the directory and the flags"},
        "9780": {"comment":"+$21/$22: the first cluster"},
        "9784": {"comment":"+$23/$24: the cluster kept"},
        "9788": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "9789": {"comment":"+$25/$26: its index, 0"},
        "9793": {"comment":"Skips +$27"},
        "9794": {"comment":"+$28-$2B: the position, 0"},
        "9801": {"comment":"Returns through $264A"},
        "9806": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 18 (table word at $0574): reads whole sectors into memory. A = 1, then\nFN19_WRITE_SECT's code.\nEntry: A = 0 (the dispatcher's); DE = the first sector; H = the count; L = the drive; IX =\nthe address; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as FN19_WRITE_SECT.\nError: as FN19_WRITE_SECT.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H, IX, all alternates; IY+$48-$4A, IY+$57/$58.\nKeeps: L, IY.","comment":"A = 1: read"},
        "9807": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 19 (table word at $0576), and function 18's body: moves H whole sectors\nbetween memory at IX and drive L from sector DE, past the sector buffers (RAW_SECTORS), bit\n0 of IY+$48 saying which way (1 reads). A block that would pass $FFFF gives $9B. The drive's\nchanged buffers are written out and all its buffers dropped first, and dropped again after.\nEntry: A = 0 (write), 1 from FN18_READ_SECT (read); DE = the first sector; H = the count; L\n= the drive (0 the default, 1-26 A-Z); IX = the address in the caller's pages; IY = EXDOS's\nbase.\nExit: A = 0; H = the count; L = the drive; IX = the address after the last sector; DE = the\nsector after it.\nError: A = $9B (the block passes $FFFF) or SEL_DRIVE_REC's error; H = 0; IX, DE as on entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H, IX, all alternates; IY+$48-$4A, IY+$57/$58.\nKeeps: L, IY.","comment":"The direction"},
        "9810": {"comment":"The first sector"},
        "9816": {"comment":"Keeps the count and the drive"},
        "9817": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "9820": {"comment":"IY+$49/$4A = the address"},
        "9826": {"comment":"A = the address's high byte"},
        "9827": {"comment":"Plus 2 x count pages ..."},
        "9828": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "9830": {"comment":"... (512 bytes a sector)"},
        "9831": {"synopsis":"Fails with $9B when the block passes $FFFF; selects drive L and empties its buffers, then\nmoves the sectors (RAW_SECTORS).","comment":"Error $9B (with carry)"},
        "9833": {"comment":"Past $FFFF: fail"},
        "9835": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "9836": {"comment":"Selects it; HL = its record"},
        "9839": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9842": {"comment":"Writes its changed buffers out"},
        "9845": {"comment":"Drops all its buffers"},
        "9848": {"comment":"B = the count, C = the drive"},
        "9850": {"comment":"Moves the sectors"},
        "9853": {"comment":"Drops the buffers again"},
        "9856": {"comment":"HL = the caller's count and drive"},
        "9857": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "9858": {"comment":"Skips $2683 (POP HL, LD H,0): the error entry, H = 0"},
        "9862": {"comment":"DE = IY+$49: the address after the last sector"},
        "9866": {"synopsis":"IX = the address after the last sector; DE = the next sector.","comment":"IX = it"},
        "9869": {"comment":"DE = IY+$57: the next sector"},
        "9873": {"synopsis":"Returns with the function's results."},
        "9874": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 17 (table word at $0572): FN16_WRITE with IY+$48 = 2 (bit 1), so every\nsector written in part is read in first, whatever the file's size.\nEntry: A = 0 (the dispatcher's); as FN16_WRITE.\nExit: as FN16_WRITE.\nError: as FN16_WRITE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; the control block's position.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"A = 2 (with the next)"},
        "9875": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 15 (table word at $056E): reads bytes from a file, FN16_WRITE's code with\nIY+$48 = 1.\nEntry: A = 0 (the dispatcher's); as FN16_WRITE.\nExit: as FN16_WRITE; A = $E4, NZ when the file ended first (BC = the bytes read).\nError: as FN16_WRITE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; the control block's position.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"A = 1: read"},
        "9876": {"synopsis":"EXDOS function 16 (table word at $0570), also the body of 15 and 17: moves BC bytes between\nmemory at IX and the file DE at its position, IY+$48 the mode (bit 0: 1 reads). Sets up the\ncounts and runs XFER_BYTES; then adds the bytes moved to the position (+$28-$2B). A read\nthat met the file's end returns $E4 with the bytes it got.\nEntry: A = 0 (the dispatcher's; 1 from $2693, 2 from $2692); BC = the count; DE = the file's\ncontrol block; IX = the address in the caller's pages; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; BC = the bytes moved; DE = the control block; IX = HL = the address after\nthe last byte.\nError: NZ, A = $E4 (a read met the file's end) or the error code ($9B the block passes\n$FFFF, $A7 Read only file, $AC Disk full, $9A, the drive's errors).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates; the control block's position.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"The mode"},
        "9879": {"comment":"No bytes moved yet"},
        "9886": {"comment":"The bytes left: the count"},
        "9892": {"comment":"IX = the control block"},
        "9895": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "9896": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$49/$4A"},
        "9902": {"comment":"Moves the bytes"},
        "9905": {"comment":"BC = the bytes moved"},
        "9911": {"comment":"HL = the address after them"},
        "9917": {"comment":"IX = it, DE = the control block"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Keeps the result"},
        "9923": {"comment":"The block's +$28: the position"},
        "9927": {"comment":"Plus the bytes moved"},
        "9934": {"comment":"No carry?"},
        "9936": {"comment":"Carry into byte 3"},
        "9938": {"comment":"No carry?"},
        "9940": {"comment":"Carry into byte 4"},
        "9942": {"synopsis":"The position is moved on: the result, or $E4 when a read met the file's end.","comment":"HL = the address after"},
        "9943": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "9944": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9946": {"comment":"A read cut at the file's end?"},
        "9950": {"comment":"No: A = 0"},
        "9951": {"comment":"$E4: fewer bytes than asked for"},
        "9954": {"synopsis":"Moves the bytes of a read or write ($2694) for the file IX:\n1. Checks the block does not pass $FFFF, selects the file's drive (checking it holds the\n   file's disk), and works out where the transfer starts and ends (XFER_SETUP).\n2. Finds the cluster of the start (FILE_CLUSTER_N) and moves the part of the first sector\n   from the offset (XFER_PART_SECT).\n3. Moves runs of whole sectors straight between memory and disk (RAW_SECTORS), each run as\n   many sectors as lie in consecutive clusters (XFER_LOOP).\n4. Moves the part of the last sector and keeps the cluster reached and its index in the\n   block (+$23-$26) for the next call.\nEntry: BC = the count; HL = the address; IX = the control block; IY = EXDOS's base with\nIY+$48-$4E set by $2694.\nExit: A = 0, Z; IY+$49/$4A = the address after the last byte; IY+$4D/$4E = the bytes moved.\nError: NZ, A = the error code; carry with A = $9B when the block passes $FFFF.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, all alternates; IY+$4B-$5A; the control block's +$17-$26.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"No bytes?"},
        "9956": {"comment":"Done: A = 0"},
        "9957": {"comment":"BC = the count - 1"},
        "9958": {"comment":"HL = the last byte's address"},
        "9959": {"comment":"Error $9B"},
        "9961": {"comment":"Past $FFFF: fail"},
        "9962": {"comment":"C = the file's drive"},
        "9965": {"comment":"B = 1: check it holds the file's disk"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Selects the drive; HL = its record"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9972": {"comment":"Where the transfer starts and ends"},
        "9975": {"comment":"DE = IY+$4F: the start's cluster index"},
        "9979": {"synopsis":"Finds the start's cluster, then moves the first sector's part when the start is not at a\nsector's beginning.","comment":"Set up: the start's cluster"},
        "9982": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$55"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9989": {"comment":"BC = the offset in the sector"},
        "9995": {"comment":"Not at a sector's beginning?"},
        "9997": {"comment":"Then that sector's part first"},
        "10000": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "10001": {"synopsis":"The whole sectors left (the bytes left / 512): with none, the last sector's part\n(XFER_LAST_PART). Otherwise steps to the next sector, and gathers a run: the rest of this\ncluster, then whole clusters while the next one in the chain follows on (XFER_RUN_GROW).","comment":"C = the bytes left / 256"},
        "10004": {"comment":"C = the whole sectors left"},
        "10006": {"comment":"None: the last sector's part"},
        "10008": {"comment":"Steps on when the last sector was used"},
        "10011": {"comment":"Failed (the chain ended)?"},
        "10012": {"comment":"A = - the sector in the cluster"},
        "10015": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "10016": {"comment":"DE = IY+$55: the cluster"},
        "10020": {"synopsis":"The disk sector to start from (XFER_SECT_NUM).","comment":"IY+$57 = the run's first sector"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"B = the run's sectors up to the end of cluster DE. Ends the run when it covers the sectors\nleft; else reads the next cluster and grows the run by a cluster while it is DE + 1.","comment":"Plus the sectors per cluster"},
        "10027": {"comment":"B = the run up to this cluster's end"},
        "10028": {"comment":"Enough for the sectors left?"},
        "10029": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10031": {"comment":"Keeps the cluster"},
        "10032": {"comment":"DE = the next cluster"},
        "10035": {"comment":"HL = the cluster, the record kept"},
        "10037": {"comment":"HL = the cluster + 1"},
        "10038": {"comment":"The next one?"},
        "10040": {"comment":"No: the run ends here"},
        "10042": {"comment":"Yes: the cluster index + 1"},
        "10045": {"comment":"No carry?"},
        "10047": {"comment":"Carry into the high byte"},
        "10050": {"synopsis":"Takes the next cluster into the run.","comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10051": {"comment":"Grows the run"},
        "10053": {"synopsis":"The chain jumps: the run ends at the last sector of cluster DE.","comment":"HL = the cluster + 1"},
        "10054": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10055": {"comment":"DE = the cluster"},
        "10056": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10057": {"comment":"A = the sectors per cluster: its last sector"},
        "10062": {"synopsis":"The run ends inside this cluster: B = the sectors left.","comment":"A = the sectors per cluster"},
        "10065": {"comment":"Less the run up to the cluster's end"},
        "10066": {"comment":"Plus the sectors left: past the run's last sector"},
        "10067": {"comment":"B = the sectors left"},
        "10068": {"synopsis":"Records where the run ends (the sector in the cluster, the cluster), moves the run\n(RAW_SECTORS), counts its bytes and goes on.","comment":"The run's last sector in the cluster"},
        "10072": {"comment":"The run's last cluster"},
        "10078": {"comment":"Keeps the run's sectors"},
        "10079": {"comment":"Moves the run past the buffers"},
        "10083": {"comment":"B = the bytes / 256"},
        "10085": {"comment":"BC = the bytes"},
        "10087": {"comment":"Counts them"},
        "10090": {"comment":"The last sector is used: step on next"},
        "10094": {"comment":"More sectors?"},
        "10096": {"synopsis":"The last sector's part from offset 0 (XFER_PART_SECT); then keeps the cluster reached and\nits index in the control block, so the next call starts its walk there.","comment":"From the sector's beginning"},
        "10099": {"comment":"Moves the part"},
        "10102": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "10103": {"comment":"DE = IY+$55: the cluster reached"},
        "10107": {"synopsis":"The control block's +$23/$24 = the cluster reached."},
        "10113": {"comment":"DE = IY+$4F: its index"},
        "10117": {"synopsis":"The control block's +$25/$26 = its index; returns A = 0."},
        "10124": {"synopsis":"Moves the part of one sector from offset BC: to the sector's end, or the bytes left when\nfewer, through a sector buffer (SECT_VIA_BUF). Steps to the next sector first when bit 6 of\nIY+$48 says the current one was used; then sets that bit and counts the bytes.\nEntry: BC = the offset in the sector; HL = the drive's record; IY+$48-$58, the transfer\nstate.\nExit: A = 0, Z (also when no bytes are left).\nError: NZ, A = $9A (the cluster chain ended).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates; IY+$48-$58.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "10125": {"comment":"A sector's bytes"},
        "10129": {"comment":"Less the offset: the room in the sector"},
        "10131": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "10132": {"comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "10138": {"comment":"More left than room?"},
        "10140": {"comment":"Yes: the room"},
        "10142": {"comment":"No: HL = the bytes left"},
        "10143": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "10145": {"synopsis":"Moves DE bytes of the sector, unless there are none.","comment":"No bytes?"},
        "10147": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10148": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "10149": {"comment":"Steps on when the last sector was used"},
        "10152": {"comment":"Failed (the chain ended)?"},
        "10153": {"comment":"IY+$57 = the sector"},
        "10156": {"comment":"Moves the bytes through a buffer"},
        "10159": {"comment":"The sector is used: step on next"},
        "10163": {"comment":"Counts the bytes"},
        "10166": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "10168": {"synopsis":"Moves B whole sectors between the disk and memory past the sector buffers, from sector\nIY+$57 and the address at IY+$49 (bit 0 of IY+$48: 1 reads, 0 writes).\n1. The address is mapped into page 1 (MAP_TO_PAGE1). The run is the sectors that fit before\n   page 1's end, at most B.\n2. The unit's driver runs request 4 (read) or WRITE_REQUEST's 5/6 on the run (UNIT_REQUEST:\n   B the sectors, C the segment, DE the sector, IX the address in page 1). A failure asks\n   DISK_ERROR: a retry runs the rest of the run again, an Ignore skips it (segment 0: no\n   request is made).\n3. RAW_SYNC_BUFS squares the buffers with the run; IY+$49 and IY+$57 move past it.\n4. A sector that would cross page 1's end goes alone through SECT_VIA_BUF.\nEntry: B = the sectors; HL = the drive's record; IY+$48, IY+$49/$4A, IY+$57/$58; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z; IY+$49/$4A and IY+$57/$58 past the sectors.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"No sectors (left)?"},
        "10170": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10171": {"comment":"DE = IY+$49: the address"},
        "10175": {"synopsis":"Maps the address into page 1 and sizes the run: the whole sectors before $8000, at most B.","comment":"A = the segment, DE = the address in page 1"},
        "10178": {"comment":"A' = the segment"},
        "10179": {"comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "10180": {"comment":"Room before $8000, less one sector"},
        "10184": {"comment":"A sector crosses page 1's end?"},
        "10186": {"comment":"Yes: that one through a buffer"},
        "10188": {"comment":"A = the room / 256"},
        "10189": {"comment":"The room in sectors ..."},
        "10191": {"comment":"... plus the last one"},
        "10192": {"comment":"Fewer than B?"},
        "10195": {"comment":"No: all B"},
        "10196": {"synopsis":"C = the run; the sectors left after it are kept with it.","comment":"C = the run"},
        "10197": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10198": {"comment":"Run - B ..."},
        "10199": {"comment":"... negated: the sectors left after it"},
        "10201": {"comment":"B = them"},
        "10202": {"comment":"Kept with the run"},
        "10203": {"comment":"B = the run"},
        "10204": {"comment":"A = the segment"},
        "10205": {"comment":"C = the segment"},
        "10207": {"synopsis":"One try at the run: B = the sectors, C = the segment, DE = the address in page 1.","comment":"The run and the segment, for the end"},
        "10208": {"comment":"And again, for this try"},
        "10209": {"comment":"The address, for the end"},
        "10210": {"comment":"IX = the address, the caller's IX kept"},
        "10212": {"comment":"Request 4: read"},
        "10214": {"comment":"A write?"},
        "10218": {"comment":"Request 5 or 6"},
        "10221": {"comment":"DE = IY+$57: the sector"},
        "10225": {"synopsis":"Runs the request (not for segment 0: a run the user chose to ignore), then works out where\nit got to: IY+$57 past the sectors done, DE past their bytes, B = the sectors not done.","comment":"Keeps the sector"},
        "10226": {"comment":"Segment 0?"},
        "10228": {"comment":"No: the driver moves the sectors"},
        "10231": {"comment":"Keeps the result"},
        "10232": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "10233": {"comment":"The caller's IX"},
        "10234": {"comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "10236": {"comment":"HL = the sectors done"},
        "10239": {"comment":"Plus the first sector"},
        "10240": {"comment":"IY+$57 = the next sector"},
        "10246": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10247": {"comment":"DE = the address"},
        "10248": {"comment":"D + 2 x the sectors done ..."},
        "10251": {"comment":"... the address after them"},
        "10252": {"comment":"A = the sectors done"},
        "10253": {"comment":"B = the run, C = the segment"},
        "10254": {"comment":"Done - run ..."},
        "10255": {"comment":"... negated: the sectors not done"},
        "10257": {"comment":"B = them"},
        "10258": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10259": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "10261": {"comment":"NC: not a format error"},
        "10262": {"comment":"Asks: Z retries, NZ goes on"},
        "10265": {"comment":"Retry?"},
        "10267": {"comment":"Ignore: the rest is skipped (segment 0)"},
        "10269": {"synopsis":"Tries the rest of the run again.","comment":"Again"},
        "10271": {"synopsis":"The run is done: squares the buffers with it, moves IY+$49 past it and goes on with the\nsectors left.","comment":"B = the run, C = the segment"},
        "10272": {"comment":"Squares the buffers with the run"},
        "10275": {"comment":"B = the sectors left, C = the run"},
        "10276": {"comment":"The address's high byte ..."},
        "10279": {"comment":"... plus 2 x the run (512 bytes a sector)"},
        "10284": {"synopsis":"The next run.","comment":"More sectors?"},
        "10286": {"synopsis":"A sector that would cross page 1's end: moved alone through a buffer, then the next sector.","comment":"HL = the record"},
        "10287": {"comment":"One sector fewer"},
        "10288": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10289": {"comment":"A whole sector"},
        "10292": {"comment":"From offset 0"},
        "10294": {"comment":"Moves it through a buffer"},
        "10297": {"comment":"The sectors left"},
        "10298": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "10301": {"comment":"No carry?"},
        "10303": {"comment":"Carry into the high byte"},
        "10306": {"synopsis":"Goes on with the sectors left.","comment":"More sectors?"},
        "10308": {"synopsis":"After a run of sectors moved past the buffers, squares the drive's buffers with it: a buffer\nwhose sector is one of the run's (the B sectors before IY+$57) is dropped after a write\n(tag 0, to the head of the chain); after a read, a changed one has its data copied over that\nsector's place in memory (segment C in page 1), so memory gets the newer data.\nEntry: B = the run's sectors; C = the segment; DE = the address after the run in page 1;\nHL = the drive's record; IY+$57 = the sector after the run; IY+$48 bit 0 the direction.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Marks the drive's buffers"},
        "10311": {"synopsis":"Takes the next marked buffer and checks whether its sector is in the run.","comment":"Keeps the run and the segment"},
        "10313": {"comment":"The next marked buffer"},
        "10316": {"comment":"None left: done"},
        "10318": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +4: its sector"},
        "10322": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "10325": {"comment":"HL = the sector, DE = the buffer +5"},
        "10326": {"comment":"BC = the sector after the run"},
        "10332": {"comment":"Sector - it (negative in the run)"},
        "10334": {"comment":"B' = the run, C' = the segment"},
        "10335": {"comment":"Less than 256 below it?"},
        "10337": {"comment":"No: not in the run"},
        "10339": {"comment":"Within the run's sectors?"},
        "10341": {"comment":"No"},
        "10343": {"comment":"DE = the buffer +3"},
        "10345": {"comment":"HL = the buffer +3, DE = the distance"},
        "10346": {"comment":"A read?"},
        "10352": {"comment":"Buffer +2 ..."},
        "10353": {"comment":"... the tag 0: free"},
        "10357": {"comment":"To the head of the chain"},
        "10360": {"synopsis":"The next buffer.","comment":"The main set again"},
        "10363": {"synopsis":"A read: a changed buffer (bit 7 of its +3) has its 512 bytes copied over the sector's place\nin memory, with the run's segment in page 1.","comment":"Changed?"},
        "10365": {"comment":"No: memory is right"},
        "10367": {"comment":"B = the segment"},
        "10370": {"comment":"A = page 1's segment"},
        "10372": {"comment":"The run's segment in page 1"},
        "10375": {"comment":"The address after the run"},
        "10377": {"comment":"The buffer's data: +$0B"},
        "10381": {"comment":"HL = the address after, the data kept"},
        "10382": {"comment":"D = the distance (negative sectors)"},
        "10383": {"comment":"E = 0"},
        "10384": {"comment":"Less 512 bytes ..."},
        "10385": {"comment":"... for each sector: the sector's place"},
        "10386": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10387": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's data"},
        "10388": {"comment":"A sector"},
        "10393": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "10397": {"synopsis":"No more marked buffers.","comment":"The main set"},
        "10398": {"comment":"The caller's BC"},
        "10400": {"synopsis":"Moves the transfer on by one sector when bit 6 of IY+$48 says the current one was used: the\nnext sector of the cluster (IY+$51), or at the cluster's end sector 0 of the next cluster in\nthe chain (IY+$55, its index IY+$4F + 1).\nEntry: HL = the drive's record; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z; bit 6 of IY+$48 clear.\nError: NZ, A = $9A when the chain ends.\nChanges: AF, all alternates.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "10401": {"comment":"The current sector used?"},
        "10405": {"comment":"No: stay"},
        "10406": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "10410": {"comment":"The next sector of the cluster"},
        "10414": {"comment":"Past the cluster's end?"},
        "10417": {"comment":"No"},
        "10419": {"comment":"Keeps DE"},
        "10420": {"comment":"DE = IY+$4F: the cluster's index"},
        "10424": {"synopsis":"The next cluster: its index + 1, then the cluster itself from the FAT.","comment":"The index + 1"},
        "10431": {"comment":"DE = IY+$55: the cluster"},
        "10435": {"synopsis":"Reads the next cluster: an end mark fails with $9A.","comment":"DE = the next cluster"},
        "10438": {"comment":"The current cluster"},
        "10444": {"comment":"The chain ended?"},
        "10447": {"comment":"Error $9A"},
        "10450": {"comment":"Sector 0 of the cluster"},
        "10451": {"synopsis":"Stores the sector in the cluster; A = 0, Z.","comment":"The sector in the cluster"},
        "10454": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "10456": {"synopsis":"IY+$57/$58 = the disk sector of sector IY+$51 of cluster DE (CLUSTER_TO_SECT).\nEntry: DE = the cluster; HL = the drive's record; IY.\nExit: IY+$57/$58 = the sector.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the cluster"},
        "10457": {"comment":"A = the sector in the cluster"},
        "10460": {"comment":"DE = IY+$55 (the cluster again)"},
        "10464": {"synopsis":"Works out the disk sector and keeps it.","comment":"DE = the disk sector"},
        "10473": {"comment":"The cluster back"},
        "10475": {"synopsis":"Moves DE bytes (up to 512) between memory at IY+$49 and sector IY+$57 from offset BC,\nthrough a sector buffer (GET_SECTOR_BUF). The sector is read in first for a read, for\nfunction 17 (bit 1 of IY+$48), and for a write that does not cover the sector's data (not\nthe whole sector, by the offset and the bytes left measured against IY+$59/$5A). The memory\nis paged into page 1 a 16K page at a time (MAP_TO_PAGE1). Then IY+$49 moves past the bytes;\na write marks the buffer changed; a buffer used to its end is written back and goes to the\nhead of the chain, to be reused first.\nEntry: BC = the offset in the sector; DE = the count; HL = the drive's record; IY+$48,\nIY+$49/$4A, IY+$4B/$4C, IY+$57/$58, IY+$59/$5A; IY.\nExit: BC = the count; IY+$49/$4A = the address after the bytes; page 1 restored.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates; the sector's buffer.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"IX = the record, the caller's IX kept"},
        "10478": {"comment":"Keeps the count"},
        "10479": {"comment":"Keeps the offset"},
        "10480": {"comment":"A read?"},
        "10484": {"comment":"Yes: read the sector in"},
        "10486": {"comment":"A whole sector?"},
        "10488": {"comment":"Yes: no need to read it"},
        "10490": {"comment":"Function 17?"},
        "10494": {"comment":"Yes: read it in"},
        "10496": {"comment":"Keeps the count"},
        "10497": {"comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "10503": {"comment":"DE = IY+$59"},
        "10507": {"synopsis":"Decides from the offset and the bytes left against IY+$59 whether the sector must be read.","comment":"Bytes left - IY+$59"},
        "10510": {"comment":"DE = the count"},
        "10511": {"comment":"Below it?"},
        "10513": {"comment":"Offset 0?"},
        "10515": {"comment":"No: read it in"},
        "10517": {"comment":"Less the count too"},
        "10519": {"comment":"Below: no need to read it"},
        "10521": {"comment":"Read it in"},
        "10523": {"synopsis":"The bytes left are below IY+$59: read in unless adding the offset carries.","comment":"Plus the offset"},
        "10524": {"comment":"No carry: no need to read it"},
        "10526": {"synopsis":"B = 3: the sector is read in (Ignore allowed); $2921, inside LD HL,$0206, is LD B,2: the\nbuffer is taken without reading.","comment":"Read it in, Ignore allowed"},
        "10528": {"comment":"$2921: LD B,2, no read"},
        "10531": {"comment":"DE = IY+$57: the sector"},
        "10535": {"synopsis":"Gets the sector's buffer and points HL at the offset in its data; DE = the address.","comment":"HL = the sector's buffer"},
        "10538": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "10539": {"comment":"Plus the buffer"},
        "10540": {"comment":"Plus its header: the data's byte"},
        "10544": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "10545": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "10547": {"comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "10549": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "10550": {"comment":"DE = IY+$49: the address"},
        "10554": {"synopsis":"Keeps the address for the end.","comment":"The address"},
        "10555": {"synopsis":"Copies what fits in the page of address DE: maps it into page 1, the count cut at $8000.","comment":"The address in the caller's pages"},
        "10556": {"comment":"The count"},
        "10557": {"comment":"The buffer's place"},
        "10558": {"comment":"A = the segment, DE = the address in page 1"},
        "10561": {"comment":"Paged into page 1"},
        "10563": {"comment":"$8000 - the address - the count"},
        "10571": {"comment":"Fits before $8000?"},
        "10573": {"comment":"No: BC = the room"},
        "10574": {"comment":"Up to $8000"},
        "10576": {"synopsis":"HL = the buffer, DE = memory for a read; swapped for a write.","comment":"HL = the buffer's place"},
        "10577": {"comment":"Keeps the part's size"},
        "10578": {"comment":"A read?"},
        "10584": {"comment":"Write: memory to the buffer"},
        "10585": {"synopsis":"Copies the part.","comment":"Copies the part"},
        "10587": {"comment":"A read? (BIT's Z still)"},
        "10589": {"comment":"Write: HL = the buffer, DE = memory"},
        "10590": {"synopsis":"The count left after the part: none ends the copy, else the next page of the address.","comment":"BC = the part's size"},
        "10591": {"comment":"HL = the count, the buffer's place kept"},
        "10593": {"comment":"Less the part"},
        "10595": {"comment":"BC = the count left"},
        "10597": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's place"},
        "10598": {"comment":"All copied?"},
        "10600": {"comment":"A = the part's address (high byte)"},
        "10601": {"comment":"Its page"},
        "10603": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "10605": {"comment":"DE = its beginning"},
        "10606": {"comment":"Copies the next part"},
        "10608": {"synopsis":"Puts page 1 back, moves IY+$49 past the bytes, marks the buffer changed for a write, and\nwrites a buffer used to its end back, to the head of the chain.","comment":"Drops the loop's address"},
        "10609": {"comment":"HL = the first address"},
        "10610": {"comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "10611": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "10613": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "10614": {"comment":"HL = the address after the bytes"},
        "10615": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$49/$4A"},
        "10621": {"comment":"A write?"},
        "10625": {"comment":"Marks the buffer changed"},
        "10628": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "10629": {"comment":"Plus the count"},
        "10630": {"comment":"Reached the sector's end?"},
        "10632": {"comment":"No"},
        "10634": {"comment":"HL = the buffer used last"},
        "10640": {"comment":"Written back, to the head of the chain"},
        "10643": {"synopsis":"The caller's IX and HL back.","comment":"IX back, HL = the record"},
        "10647": {"synopsis":"Counts BC bytes as moved: IY+$4D/$4E plus BC; IY+$4B/$4C (the bytes left) minus BC, with the\ncarry of the first sum (0 while the total stays below 64K).\nEntry: BC = the bytes; IY.\nExit: IY+$4B-$4E updated.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "10648": {"comment":"HL = the bytes moved"},
        "10654": {"comment":"Plus these"},
        "10661": {"comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "10667": {"comment":"Less these"},
        "10677": {"synopsis":"Maps an address of the caller's into page 1: A = the segment that holds address DE, from a\ntable of four page segments chosen by IY-$80 (1: the four bytes at $BFFC; 2: IY-$5D; 3:\nIY-$36; else IY+$2C) and indexed by the address's page (DE's top two bits); D is moved into\n$40-$7F, the same place in page 1.\nEntry: DE = the address; IY.\nExit: A = the segment; DE = the address in page 1.\nChanges: AF, D.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A = the table's kind"},
        "10680": {"synopsis":"Turns address DE as one of four page maps sees it into a segment and a page-1 address: A\nselects the map of four segment bytes (1: $BFFC, 2: IY-$5D, 3: IY-$36, 4 or more: IY+$2C);\nthe byte for DE's page (bits 14-15) is the segment, and D is moved into $4000-$7FFF.\nEntry: A = the map (1-4); DE = the address; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = the segment; DE = the address in page 1.\nChanges: AF, D.\nKeeps: BC, E, HL, IX, IY."},
        "10682": {"comment":"Map 1: the four bytes at $BFFC"},
        "10685": {"comment":"Map 1?"},
        "10688": {"comment":"Map 2: IY-$5D"},
        "10691": {"comment":"Map 2?"},
        "10694": {"comment":"Map 3: IY-$36"},
        "10697": {"comment":"Map 3?"},
        "10700": {"comment":"Map 4: IY+$2C"},
        "10703": {"synopsis":"HL = IY + the table's offset."},
        "10707": {"synopsis":"A = the segment of the address's page; the address moved into page 1.","comment":"A = the address's high byte"},
        "10708": {"comment":"Top two bits ..."},
        "10710": {"comment":"... the page, 0-3"},
        "10715": {"comment":"HL = its entry"},
        "10716": {"comment":"A = the segment"},
        "10717": {"comment":"The address ..."},
        "10719": {"comment":"... in page 1"},
        "10724": {"synopsis":"Prepares a transfer of IY+$4B bytes at the file's position (+$28-$2B):\n1. POS_TO_CLUSTER splits the position: the cluster's index, the sector in it and the offset\n   go to IY+$4F-$53.\n2. The same for the transfer's last byte, then for the file's last byte (the size - 1, at\n   +$17-$1A) ($2A1A on).\n3. A read of an empty file gives $E4; a read past the end is cut to the end, with bit 7 of\n   IY+$48 set to report $E4 after.\n4. A write gives $A7 for a read-only file; else it marks the file changed (bit 6 of +$20)\n   and grows the cluster chain to cover the last byte ($AC when the disk is full), with the\n   new size.\nEntry: HL = the drive's record; IX = the control block; IY+$48, IY+$4B/$4C; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z; IY+$4F-$54 and IY+$59/$5A set.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($9A, $A7, $AC or $E4).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates; the control block's +$17-$26 for a write.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "10725": {"comment":"BC = the position's low word"},
        "10731": {"comment":"DE = its high word"},
        "10737": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10739": {"comment":"Splits the start"},
        "10742": {"comment":"Too far: fail"},
        "10744": {"comment":"The start's cluster index"},
        "10750": {"comment":"The sector in the cluster"},
        "10753": {"comment":"The offset in the sector"},
        "10759": {"comment":"HL = the position's low word"},
        "10760": {"comment":"DE = IY+$4B: the bytes"},
        "10764": {"synopsis":"The position of the transfer's last byte: the position + the count - 1.","comment":"The count - 1"},
        "10765": {"comment":"Plus the low word"},
        "10766": {"comment":"HL = the high word, the sum kept"},
        "10767": {"comment":"BC = the last byte's low word"},
        "10768": {"comment":"DE = the high word, HL = the count - 1"},
        "10769": {"comment":"HL = the record, the count - 1 kept"},
        "10770": {"comment":"Carry out of the low word?"},
        "10772": {"comment":"Into the high word"},
        "10773": {"synopsis":"Splits the last byte's position (POS_TO_CLUSTER).","comment":"Keeps the last byte's position"},
        "10775": {"comment":"Splits it"},
        "10778": {"synopsis":"A failure leaves; else the file's size - 1 (DE:BC, from +$17-$1A) for the comparison at\n$2A31; an empty file gives $FFFF:$FFFF with Z.","comment":"Too far: fail"},
        "10780": {"comment":"Keeps the last byte's cluster index"},
        "10781": {"comment":"BC = the size's low word"},
        "10787": {"comment":"DE = its high word"},
        "10793": {"comment":"Low word 0?"},
        "10795": {"comment":"Low word - 1"},
        "10796": {"comment":"No: no borrow"},
        "10798": {"comment":"A = the high word (Z for an empty file)"},
        "10800": {"comment":"Borrow from the high word"},
        "10801": {"synopsis":"The file's last byte (length - 1, in DE:BC; Z when the file is empty) as a cluster index\ntoo, then the transfer checked against the file's length:\n1. The alternate HL:(stack) = (length - 1) - (the transfer's last byte); carry: the\n   transfer runs past the file's end. AF' keeps that carry and NZ for an empty file.\n2. IY+$48 bit 0 set: a read ($2AD6). Otherwise a write: error $A7 (\"Read only file\") for\n   IX+$20 bit 5; else IX+$20 bit 6 is set (the file changed) and the clusters the write\n   needs past the file's last one are added to its chain (ALLOC_CLUSTERS).","comment":"Push the file's length - 1"},
        "10803": {"comment":"Not empty: DE = its last cluster index ($2AF8)"},
        "10806": {"comment":"HL', DE' = the file's length - 1"},
        "10810": {"comment":"BC = the transfer's last cluster index"},
        "10811": {"comment":"Index too big ($9A)? Drop the three words and return"},
        "10814": {"comment":"BC' = the transfer's last byte, low word"},
        "10816": {"comment":"The file's last byte - the transfer's, low word"},
        "10818": {"comment":"Low word to the stack; HL' = the last byte's high word"},
        "10820": {"comment":"High word: carry when the transfer runs past the end"},
        "10823": {"comment":"NZ: the file has no cluster (DE = $FFFF)"},
        "10825": {"comment":"Keep those flags in AF'"},
        "10826": {"comment":"A read?"},
        "10833": {"comment":"Read-only file?"},
        "10837": {"comment":"Error $A7: Read only file"},
        "10841": {"comment":"The file has changed"},
        "10846": {"comment":"HL = the transfer's last cluster index"},
        "10848": {"comment":"DE = the clusters the file has"},
        "10852": {"comment":"BC = the clusters to add"},
        "10856": {"comment":"None to add?"},
        "10858": {"comment":"Allocate them as a chain: BC = its first cluster"},
        "10861": {"comment":"Disk full?"},
        "10863": {"comment":"DE = the file's last cluster index"},
        "10864": {"comment":"The file had no cluster?"},
        "10868": {"comment":"Keep the new chain's first cluster"},
        "10869": {"comment":"DE = the file's last cluster ($2B2E)"},
        "10875": {"comment":"Its FAT entry links on to the new chain"},
        "10880": {"synopsis":"An error: drops the three words the set-up keeps on the stack and returns A (NZ).","comment":"The transfer's last byte, low word"},
        "10881": {"synopsis":"An error: drops two words and returns A (NZ)."},
        "10884": {"synopsis":"The file had no cluster: the new chain's first cluster becomes the file's first cluster and\nits known one, with index 0 (A = 0 after ALLOC_CLUSTERS).","comment":"IX+$21: the file's first cluster"},
        "10890": {"comment":"IX+$23: the known cluster"},
        "10896": {"comment":"IX+$25: its index, 0"},
        "10902": {"synopsis":"A write: the file's length becomes the transfer's last byte + 1 when the file was empty or\nthe transfer runs past its end.","comment":"BC, DE = the transfer's last byte; HL = the high word of the gap"},
        "10903": {"comment":"The flags of step 1"},
        "10904": {"comment":"The file was empty?"},
        "10906": {"comment":"Inside the file: the length stays"},
        "10908": {"synopsis":"DE:BC = the transfer's last byte + 1."},
        "10914": {"synopsis":"Stores DE:BC as the file's length (IX+$17-$1A)."},
        "10926": {"synopsis":"HL:BC = R - 1, R being the bytes the file had after the transfer's last byte (the gap of\nstep 1, negative when the write runs past the old end).","comment":"BC = the gap's low word"},
        "10927": {"comment":"DE = the count - 1, for the caller"},
        "10930": {"comment":"Count the 32-bit gap down by one"},
        "10934": {"synopsis":"IY+$59 = the bytes the write puts past the file's old end, plus 1 (1 - R, at most $FFFF);\n0 when the file has more bytes after the write.\nExit: A = 0, Z; the register sets swapped back.","comment":"R - 1 negative: the write reaches the old end?"},
        "10938": {"comment":"HL = $FFFF?"},
        "10941": {"comment":"$FFFF when R - 1 is below -$10000"},
        "10946": {"comment":"HL = 1 - R"},
        "10949": {"comment":"Not 0: that is the count"},
        "10951": {"comment":"1 - R = $10000: $FFFF"},
        "10954": {"synopsis":"The write ends inside the old file: 0."},
        "10957": {"synopsis":"Stores HL in IY+$59 and returns A = 0."},
        "10963": {"comment":"The main registers back"},
        "10966": {"synopsis":"A read: returns at once when the transfer ends inside the file; error $E4 (end of file) for\nan empty file.","comment":"The flags of step 1"},
        "10967": {"comment":"DE = the gap's low word"},
        "10968": {"comment":"HL = the count - 1; the drive's block back on the stack"},
        "10969": {"comment":"The file has no cluster: error $E4"},
        "10971": {"comment":"Inside the file: done, A = 0"},
        "10974": {"comment":"The gap's high word $FFFF (under 64K past the end)?"},
        "10978": {"synopsis":"A read that runs past the end: when part of it is inside the file, the count (IY+$4B)\nbecomes the bytes up to the end and IY+$48 bit 7 marks the read cut short; otherwise error\n$E4 (end of file).","comment":"Error $E4: end of file"},
        "10980": {"comment":"Too far past the end?"},
        "10982": {"comment":"HL = the count - 1 + the gap"},
        "10983": {"comment":"Nothing left inside the file?"},
        "10985": {"comment":"HL = the bytes up to the end"},
        "10986": {"comment":"The new count"},
        "10992": {"comment":"Cut short: $E4 after the bytes are read"},
        "10997": {"synopsis":"Takes the drive's block back into HL and returns A with flags from it."},
        "11000": {"synopsis":"Splits a byte position of a file: the offset in its sector (position mod 512), the sector in\nthe cluster, and the cluster's index in the file; IY+$54 = the sectors per cluster.\nEntry: DE:BC = the position (DE the high word); HL = the drive's record (+$0A sectors per\ncluster - 1, +$0B their power of 2); IY.\nExit: Z; DE = the cluster's index; A = the sector in the cluster; BC = the offset in the\nsector.\nError: NZ, A = $9A when the index is above $7FFF.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.\nKeeps: C, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "11001": {"comment":"A = bits 8-15"},
        "11002": {"comment":"D:E:A = the position / 2 ..."},
        "11006": {"comment":"... / 256: the sector in the file"},
        "11007": {"comment":"B = bit 8: BC = the offset in the sector"},
        "11011": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11012": {"comment":"The record's +$0A"},
        "11016": {"comment":"Keeps the sector's low byte"},
        "11017": {"comment":"The sector in the cluster"},
        "11018": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "11019": {"comment":"The sectors per cluster - 1 ..."},
        "11020": {"comment":"... + 1"},
        "11021": {"comment":"Kept at IY+$54"},
        "11024": {"comment":"A = the sector's low byte"},
        "11025": {"comment":"The record's +$0B"},
        "11026": {"comment":"B = the power of 2 ..."},
        "11027": {"comment":"... + 1 for DJNZ"},
        "11028": {"comment":"Divides by the sectors per cluster"},
        "11030": {"synopsis":"Shifts D:E:A (the position's sector number) right by one bit."},
        "11035": {"synopsis":"The loop shifts the sector number right once per bit of the drive's sectors per cluster\n(the count at HL+11, + 1, in B); then DE = the cluster index, which must be under $8000.","comment":"Shift again"},
        "11037": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "11039": {"comment":"No: error $9A"},
        "11041": {"comment":"Index $8000 or more?"},
        "11045": {"comment":"DE = the cluster index"},
        "11047": {"comment":"A = the sector in the cluster"},
        "11048": {"comment":"Hides LD A,$9A at $2B29: error $9A, NZ, for a too big index"},
        "11051": {"comment":"BC = the byte in the sector"},
        "11052": {"comment":"HL = the drive's block back"},
        "11054": {"synopsis":"Finds the cluster of index DE in the file's chain (0: the first cluster), walking the FAT\nfrom the cluster kept at +$23 (index +$25) when that is not past it, else from the first\ncluster (+$21).\nEntry: DE = the index; HL = the drive's record; IX = the control block; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z; DE = the cluster.\nError: NZ, A = $9A when the block keeps no cluster (+$23 = 0, an empty file) or the chain\nends first.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, all alternates.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Keeps the record"},
        "11055": {"comment":"HL = the index"},
        "11056": {"comment":"DE = the cluster kept"},
        "11062": {"comment":"None?"},
        "11064": {"comment":"Error $9A"},
        "11066": {"comment":"BC = its index"},
        "11072": {"comment":"Steps from it"},
        "11074": {"comment":"Not past it: walk from there"},
        "11076": {"comment":"HL = the index again"},
        "11077": {"comment":"Walk from the first cluster"},
        "11083": {"synopsis":"BC = the steps to go (HL on entry); HL = the drive's block again."},
        "11085": {"synopsis":"Follows the chain BC steps from cluster DE. A chain that ends first is error $9A.\nExit: Z, A = 0 and DE = the cluster.\nError: A = $9A, NZ.","comment":"Steps left?"},
        "11087": {"comment":"No: DE = the cluster"},
        "11089": {"comment":"DE = the next cluster (FAT_GET_ENTRY)"},
        "11092": {"comment":"Not the end of the chain ($FFFF)? Go on"},
        "11096": {"comment":"Hides POP HL at $2B59, the way in when no cluster is known"},
        "11098": {"comment":"Error $9A"},
        "11100": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "11102": {"synopsis":"Extension action 3 (help string; $0037): HELP alone writes the version line; HELP EXDOS\nwrites the version, the copyright and the command list, and claims the action. Nothing is\ndone when the byte at IY-$46 is not 0.\nEntry: B = the length of the help word (0 for HELP alone); DE = the help string (counted);\nC = 3; IY = the workspace + $80.\nExit: C = 0 when HELP EXDOS was answered; otherwise C is kept, so the next ROM answers too.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"Commands and help off?"},
        "11107": {"comment":"A help word given?"},
        "11110": {"synopsis":"Writes message $37 (\"EXDOS version 1.3\" and a new line) to channel $FF. The EXX in front of\nMSG_TO_DEFCH's own one leaves the register sets as they were.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC', DE'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11111": {"comment":"Message $37: \"EXDOS version 1.3\\\""},
        "11113": {"synopsis":"Writes message A (MSG_TO_BUFFER: German or English) to channel $FF, then swaps the register\nsets (EXX): two calls in a row leave them as they were.\nEntry: A = the message number, IY.\nExit: A = EXOS's status; the register sets swapped.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "11116": {"comment":"DE = the text, past its count byte"},
        "11117": {"comment":"C = its length"},
        "11118": {"synopsis":"Writes C bytes from DE to channel $FF (EXOS 8), then swaps the register sets (EXX).\nEntry: C = the length (1-255), DE = the bytes.\nExit: A = EXOS's status; the register sets swapped.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "11119": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "11120": {"comment":"Channel $FF"},
        "11125": {"synopsis":"HELP with a word: only HELP EXDOS is answered.\n1. Writes the version line, message $38 (spaces), \"Enterprise disk system\" ($3A), $38\n   again, the copyright line at $2BBC (32 bytes) and \"Commands avaliable:\" ($3B).\n2. Lists the command table from $2C58: every name whose last character has bit 5 clear\n   (a letter), each followed by a space, then a new line, and C = 0.\nEach call to $2B69 or $2B6E swaps the register sets; the list runs in the other set.","comment":"The table's \"EXDOS\""},
        "11128": {"comment":"Is the help word EXDOS?"},
        "11131": {"comment":"No: leave it to other ROMs"},
        "11135": {"comment":"Message $38: spaces"},
        "11140": {"comment":"Message $3A: \"Enterprise disk system\\\""},
        "11150": {"comment":"The copyright line, 32 bytes"},
        "11158": {"comment":"Message $3B: \"\\Commands avaliable:\\\""},
        "11163": {"comment":"HL = the command table"},
        "11166": {"synopsis":"Writes the command names whose last character has bit 5 clear: a name and a space each,\nthen a new line and C = 0 (the help is answered).","comment":"C = the name's length"},
        "11167": {"comment":"DE = its characters"},
        "11172": {"comment":"HL = its last character"},
        "11173": {"comment":"A letter (bit 5 clear) is listed"},
        "11177": {"comment":"HL = the next entry; a name with bit 5 set is skipped"},
        "11180": {"comment":"Channel $FF"},
        "11183": {"comment":"A space after it"},
        "11188": {"comment":"The table's end (0)?"},
        "11192": {"comment":"C = 0: the help action is answered"},
        "11193": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "11228": {"synopsis":"Not a command of the table: a word \"X:\" (or \"X:\" followed by a space or a tab) selects the\ndefault drive through the handler at $2D92, run like a command; anything else is left to\nother ROMs.","comment":"A drive?"},
        "11231": {"comment":"No: not EXDOS's"},
        "11232": {"comment":"Just \"X:\"?"},
        "11234": {"comment":"The character after the colon"},
        "11239": {"comment":"Neither space nor tab: not EXDOS's"},
        "11242": {"synopsis":"Runs the drive handler at $2D92 with the word's length taken as 2."},
        "11244": {"comment":"The handler: drive A' becomes the default drive"},
        "11249": {"synopsis":"Extension action 2 (command string; $0033): looks the command word up in the command table\nat $2C58 (counted names in order of length, each followed by its handler's address).\n1. A name whose last character has bit 7 set runs at once (CMD_JUMP); other names run only\n   when IY-$2B bit 0 is set (no EXDOS command running) and through CMD_RUN.\n2. A word not in the table may be a drive (CMD_TRY_DRIVE).\nNothing is done when the byte at IY-$46 is not 0.\nEntry: B = the command word's length; DE = the command string (counted); C = 2; IY = the\nworkspace + $80.\nExit: as the handler leaves it; C kept when the command is not EXDOS's.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF'.\nKeeps: IY.","comment":"Commands and help off?"},
        "11254": {"comment":"HL + 2 = the table's first entry"},
        "11257": {"synopsis":"The next table entry. A word shorter than the entry's name ends the search: the names that\nfollow are no shorter.","comment":"Shorter word (from CMD_NAME_MATCH)? Try a drive"},
        "11259": {"comment":"HL = the next entry"},
        "11261": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "11265": {"comment":"This name?"},
        "11268": {"comment":"No"},
        "11270": {"comment":"The name's last character"},
        "11272": {"comment":"Bit 7 to carry: a name run at once"},
        "11276": {"comment":"An EXDOS command running? Then not this one"},
        "11281": {"synopsis":"HL = the handler's address; carry (a bit-7 name) jumps to it at once."},
        "11287": {"synopsis":"Runs a handler with CMD_FINISH ($2D41) as its return address:\n1. Clears IY-$2B bit 0 (an EXDOS command is running).\n2. Moves the text after the command word, its leading spaces and tabs (and 0 bytes)\n   dropped, to the front of the string as a counted, zero-ended text.\n3. Empties the output buffer, gives the file block at IY+$FD drive 0 ($3D10), marks the\n   channels at IY-$2C and IY-$2D as none ($FF), clears IY-$2B bit 4.\n4. Enters the handler with HL = the parameters, A = $FF and NZ.","comment":"The handler, under"},
        "11288": {"comment":"the return to CMD_FINISH"},
        "11293": {"comment":"An EXDOS command is running"},
        "11297": {"comment":"C = the characters after the word"},
        "11300": {"comment":"HL = the word's last character"},
        "11305": {"comment":"One more, for SKIP_BLANKS's count"},
        "11306": {"synopsis":"Skips the blanks (and 0 bytes) in front of the parameters."},
        "11310": {"comment":"The end: no parameters"},
        "11312": {"comment":"A 0 byte: skip it too"},
        "11314": {"synopsis":"Writes the parameters' length over the string's count byte and copies them behind it.","comment":"C = the characters left"},
        "11317": {"comment":"The parameters' start, for the handler"},
        "11318": {"comment":"None to copy?"},
        "11320": {"comment":"Move them to the front"},
        "11322": {"synopsis":"Ends the parameters with a 0 and prepares the handler's state, then \"returns\" into it."},
        "11323": {"comment":"The 0 at the end"},
        "11324": {"comment":"The output buffer at IY+$6E"},
        "11327": {"comment":"Empty (A = 0)"},
        "11328": {"comment":"IX = IY+$FD, a file block for the command"},
        "11335": {"comment":"Drive 0 (the default); A = $FF"},
        "11338": {"comment":"HL = the parameters"},
        "11339": {"comment":"No channel of the command's yet ($FF)"},
        "11349": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "11350": {"comment":"Into the handler; it returns to CMD_FINISH"},
        "11351": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the handler of a bit-7 name, without CMD_RUN's preparations."},
        "11585": {"synopsis":"Where an EXDOS command returns (CMD_RUN pushed it):\n1. Closes the command's channels at IY-$2C and IY-$2D.\n2. Has every drive's changed buffers written back and dropped (function 14, B = C = $FF).\n3. Error $E5 (STOP) puts $20 back in FLAG_SOFT_IRQ ($BFF2) for the caller to see.\n4. Goes on at CMD_READY.\nEntry: A and the flags = the command's result.\nExit: A, B, DE kept.","comment":"The command's result"},
        "11588": {"comment":"IY-$2C, then IY-$2D"},
        "11596": {"comment":"B = C = $FF: all drives, buffers dropped"},
        "11599": {"comment":"EXDOS function 14"},
        "11607": {"comment":"Error $E5 (STOP)?"},
        "11611": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ = $20: the STOP key again"},
        "11616": {"synopsis":"Accepts EXDOS commands again (IY-$2B bit 0) and puts back the byte at IY-$58 (the write mode\nof $0AB0) that $3570 parked in IY-$29: $FE gives $FF, $FF gives 0; 0 there means none.","comment":"EXDOS commands accepted again"},
        "11620": {"comment":"A parked value?"},
        "11626": {"comment":"$FE/$FF become $FF/0"},
        "11632": {"comment":"None parked now"},
        "11636": {"synopsis":"Resets EXDOS's drive state: $FF into IY-$2F, -$30, -$31 and EXDOS variables $4D and $4E\n(IY-$51, IY-$50); with A not 0 and bit 7 of IY-$2B set, also calls $2F85; then $2D60.\nEntry: A = 0 on the first initialisation; IY = the workspace.\nExit: as $2D60.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = IY-$2F"},
        "11643": {"comment":"$FF (D)"},
        "11648": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $4D = $FF"},
        "11651": {"comment":"EXDOS variable $4E = $FF"},
        "11654": {"comment":"First initialisation?"},
        "11657": {"comment":"Flag bit 7 of IY-$2B: call $2F85 first?"},
        "11674": {"synopsis":"The handler of \"**\" and \"REM\": does nothing.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 0, Z, NC.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11676": {"synopsis":"The handler of the hidden 6-character name \"EXDOS\" + $FD (bit 7 set: run at once): hands\nback the workspace's address and B = $13.\nEntry: A = the handler address's low byte ($9C), as CMD_FOUND leaves it.\nExit: DE = IY (the workspace + $80); B = $13; C = A.\nChanges: BC, DE.\nKeeps: AF, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11679": {"comment":"B = $13 (1.3, the version the help text gives?)"},
        "11683": {"synopsis":"The handler of \"EXDOS\": runs EXDOS's command interpreter.\n1. Closes the input channel an earlier run opened (IY-$31); the input is the editor's\n   channel (IY-$2F) again (IY-$2E), IY-$2B bit 3 clear.\n2. A parameter names the input instead (OPEN_PARAM_CHAN, IY-$37 bit 4 set meanwhile): \"#n\"\n   or a file of commands; IY-$2B bit 3 then marks input not from the editor. Nothing may\n   follow it ($9F, \"Wrong number of parameters\").\n3. When the interpreter is already running (IY-$2F not $FF) that is all; otherwise it\n   starts (SHELL_START).\nEntry: HL = the parameters (zero-ended), IY.\nExit: A = 0 when only the input changed; else as the interpreter ends (SHELL_CLOSE).\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.\nKeeps: IY."},
        "11684": {"comment":"Close the channel at IY-$31"},
        "11689": {"comment":"The editor's channel"},
        "11692": {"comment":"is the input"},
        "11695": {"comment":"The input is the editor's"},
        "11700": {"comment":"A parameter?"},
        "11708": {"comment":"Its channel: E"},
        "11719": {"comment":"A channel of ours (C)?"},
        "11721": {"comment":"Then the command's end closes it if anything fails"},
        "11724": {"synopsis":"The parameter's channel becomes the input (IY-$2E); one EXDOS opened is kept in IY-$31\nuntil the next run, no longer closed by CMD_FINISH.","comment":"Open failed?"},
        "11725": {"comment":"Carry: a channel of ours"},
        "11726": {"comment":"HL = the channel, DE = the text"},
        "11727": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "11731": {"comment":"The input is not the editor"},
        "11735": {"comment":"The input channel"},
        "11739": {"comment":"An open channel (\"#n\")?"},
        "11741": {"comment":"Ours: closed by the next EXDOS"},
        "11744": {"comment":"not by CMD_FINISH"},
        "11748": {"synopsis":"Starts the interpreter unless it already runs (the editor's channel at IY-$2F is open)."},
        "11749": {"comment":"The editor's channel"},
        "11752": {"comment":"Open ($FF: none)? Done, A = 0"},
        "11754": {"comment":"DE = the save area, HL = the table"},
        "11757": {"synopsis":"Sets up the interpreter's channels:\n1. Each EXOS variable of the table at $2FB7 is saved at IY+$F0 and set: 4 to 0, 22-25 (the\n   video page: MODE_VID 0, 23 0, 24 40, 25 20), VID_EDIT 0, 30 0, 31 4, FLG_EDIT $1C,\n   $4E and $4D $FF, 11 $1E, 10 3. IY-$2B bit 7 records that they need putting back.\n2. SHELL_CLOSE ($2F45) becomes the return address.\n3. The keyboard channel is the first that answers @@JOY (FIND_KBD_CHAN), else \"KEYBOARD:\"\n   opened (IY-$2B bit 2: close it at the end).","comment":"C = the variable"},
        "11760": {"comment":"Read it (B = 0)"},
        "11763": {"comment":"D = its value"},
        "11765": {"comment":"into the save area"},
        "11768": {"comment":"C = the variable again"},
        "11770": {"comment":"D = its new value"},
        "11772": {"comment":"Write it (B = 1)"},
        "11777": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "11780": {"comment":"The variables need putting back"},
        "11784": {"comment":"SHELL_CLOSE: where the interpreter returns"},
        "11788": {"comment":"A keyboard channel?"},
        "11793": {"comment":"\"KEYBOARD:\""},
        "11796": {"comment":"Open it on a free channel"},
        "11799": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "11800": {"comment":"Ours: close it at the end"},
        "11804": {"synopsis":"Gives the editor its keyboard (EXOS variable 30), opens \"VIDEO:\" (IY-$30; variable 29,\nVID_EDIT) and writes the 10 bytes at $2F3E to it, opens \"EDITOR:\" (IY-$2F; variable 4),\nwhich is the input unless a parameter named one.","comment":"IY-$32: the keyboard channel"},
        "11808": {"comment":"Variable 30 = the keyboard channel"},
        "11813": {"comment":"\"VIDEO:\""},
        "11819": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "11820": {"comment":"IY-$30: the video channel"},
        "11824": {"comment":"The 10 bytes at $2F3E (ESC \"C\" ...)"},
        "11833": {"comment":"VID_EDIT = the video channel"},
        "11838": {"comment":"\"EDITOR:\""},
        "11844": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "11845": {"comment":"IY-$2F: the editor's channel"},
        "11849": {"comment":"Variable 4 = the editor's channel"},
        "11854": {"comment":"Input named by a parameter?"},
        "11860": {"comment":"No: the editor is the input"},
        "11863": {"synopsis":"Input from the editor: a space and the version line (\"EXDOS version 1.3\") on channel $FF.","comment":"A space"},
        "11871": {"comment":"EXDOS commands accepted; the loop runs on"},
        "11875": {"synopsis":"One command line, until IY-$2B bit 1 asks to end:\n1. The status line (from the word at $BFF6, + 6) shows \" EXDOS\" (bit 7 set on the letters,\n   the 6 bytes at $2F38) and message $3E (\"command interpreter\").\n2. From the editor: a \":\" prompt, and the video page shown (EXOS 11, @@DISP)."},
        "11879": {"comment":"HL = the status line's text"},
        "11886": {"comment":"\" EXDOS\", bit 7 set on the letters"},
        "11895": {"comment":"Message $3E: \"  command interpreter      \""},
        "11900": {"comment":"Past its count byte"},
        "11905": {"comment":"Input from the editor?"},
        "11909": {"comment":"Then a \":\" prompt"},
        "11914": {"comment":"The video channel"},
        "11917": {"comment":"B = 1 (@@DISP): its first row at screen row 1"},
        "11920": {"comment":"20 rows"},
        "11925": {"comment":"Failed: end with the error"},
        "11926": {"synopsis":"Reads the command line (READ_LINE) from the input channel, FLG_EDIT set to $1C first. A line\nof 128 characters or more is error $9C (\"Command too long\")."},
        "11929": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT = $1C"},
        "11933": {"comment":"The input channel"},
        "11936": {"comment":"Read the line"},
        "11939": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "11941": {"comment":"The count: 128 or more?"},
        "11944": {"comment":"Then error $9C: Command too long"},
        "11946": {"synopsis":"The line's status, STOP included: on error, $E4 (the input ended) ends the interpreter;\nanother error goes on a new line and is reported.","comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "11951": {"comment":"Input ended ($E4)?"},
        "11955": {"comment":"A new line before the report"},
        "11960": {"synopsis":"The input has ended: the interpreter ends after this line."},
        "11964": {"synopsis":"A line from the editor ended by ESC leaves the interpreter when the keyboard channel's\nstatus (EXOS 9) gives C = 0; otherwise the line is taken as a command line.","comment":"Input from a file or channel?"},
        "11971": {"comment":"Ended by ESC?"},
        "11975": {"comment":"The keyboard channel's status"},
        "11982": {"comment":"C = 0?"},
        "11983": {"comment":"No: read the line again"},
        "11985": {"comment":"End the interpreter"},
        "11989": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "11991": {"synopsis":"Runs the line as a command string.","comment":"C = the line's length"},
        "11992": {"comment":"+ 1, for SKIP_BLANKS"},
        "11993": {"synopsis":"Skips the leading spaces, tabs and colons; an empty line is not run.","comment":"The next character"},
        "11994": {"comment":"Skip blanks"},
        "11997": {"comment":"An empty line"},
        "11999": {"comment":"\":\"? Skip it too"},
        "12003": {"comment":"The count goes in front of the first character"},
        "12005": {"comment":"DE = the command string"},
        "12006": {"comment":"To every extension (EXOS 26)"},
        "12008": {"comment":"STOP pressed meanwhile?"},
        "12011": {"comment":"Done"},
        "12013": {"comment":"Error $A4 (Disk operation aborted)?"},
        "12017": {"comment":"Or STOP ($E5)?"},
        "12021": {"synopsis":"An error from a file of commands, $A4 or STOP ends the interpreter with it.","comment":"Input from a file or channel?"},
        "12026": {"synopsis":"Reports the error: \"***\" (message $3C) on channel $FF, then the error's text through the\noutput buffer."},
        "12027": {"comment":"Message $3C: \"\\***  \""},
        "12033": {"comment":"HL = IY-$23, for the code's digits"},
        "12040": {"comment":"The error's text into the buffer"},
        "12043": {"comment":"A new line: the buffer goes out"},
        "12046": {"synopsis":"Back for the next line unless IY-$2B bit 1 asks to end.","comment":"The end?"},
        "12053": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "12055": {"synopsis":"DE = the save area for EXOS variables (IY+$F0), HL = the table of variables and their new\nvalues at $2FB7 (a variable number and a value each, 0 at the end).\nEntry: IY.\nExit: DE = IY+$F0; HL = $2FB7.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, IX, IY."},
        "12067": {"synopsis":"Takes the STOP key into a status: A = 0 becomes $E5 when FLAG_SOFT_IRQ ($BFF2) holds $20;\n$E5 (from a key or given) clears FLAG_SOFT_IRQ.\nEntry: A = a status, with flags from OR A (Z for 0).\nExit: Z, A = 0 when there is no error and no STOP.\nError: NZ, A = the status, or $E5 for STOP.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"No error: look at the STOP key"},
        "12069": {"comment":"STOP ($E5)?"},
        "12071": {"comment":"Another error: kept"},
        "12072": {"synopsis":"Clears FLAG_SOFT_IRQ and returns error $E5 (NZ)."},
        "12076": {"comment":"NZ, NC"},
        "12079": {"synopsis":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ = $20 (the STOP key)?"},
        "12086": {"comment":"No: A = 0, Z"},
        "12100": {"synopsis":"STOP during the pause: its status $E5 replaces the saved one.","comment":"Drop the saved status"},
        "12101": {"synopsis":"Where the interpreter returns (SHELL_SET_VARS pushed it). After a file of commands that ran\nto its end, a pause of 65536 STOP checks; then SHELL_RESTORE.\nEntry: A, F = the interpreter's status.","comment":"Keep the interpreter's status"},
        "12102": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "12104": {"comment":"Input from the editor?"},
        "12110": {"comment":"The pause: 65536 STOP checks"},
        "12112": {"synopsis":"B = 0: 256 checks for each count of C."},
        "12113": {"synopsis":"One STOP check of the pause (after a file of commands)."},
        "12114": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "12117": {"comment":"Yes: end at once with $E5"},
        "12124": {"synopsis":"Ends the interpreter:\n1. Blanks the status line's 32 characters.\n2. Closes the editor's, the video and the input file's channels (IY-$2F, IY-$30, IY-$31),\n   and the keyboard's when EXDOS opened it (IY-$2B bit 2).\n3. IY-$2B bit 1 set (the end), bit 2 clear; the EXOS variables saved at IY+$F0 get their\n   values back.\nExit: A, F = the interpreter's status.","comment":"HL = the status line's text"},
        "12131": {"comment":"32 spaces"},
        "12134": {"synopsis":"Writes B spaces from HL."},
        "12138": {"comment":"IY-$2F: the editor's channel"},
        "12143": {"comment":"IY-$30: the video channel"},
        "12146": {"comment":"IY-$31: the input file's channel"},
        "12149": {"comment":"The keyboard's, if EXDOS opened it"},
        "12156": {"comment":"Not to close again"},
        "12160": {"comment":"The interpreter has ended"},
        "12164": {"comment":"Hides PUSH AF at $2F85, the way in from $2D8D"},
        "12166": {"comment":"The variables are put back now"},
        "12170": {"comment":"DE = the saved values, HL = the table"},
        "12173": {"synopsis":"Puts each EXOS variable of the table back to its saved value; then A and the flags come\nback from the stack.","comment":"C = the variable"},
        "12174": {"comment":"HL = the next entry"},
        "12176": {"comment":"Its saved value"},
        "12179": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "12180": {"comment":"Write it (B = 1)"},
        "12185": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "12188": {"comment":"The status"},
        "12242": {"synopsis":"Writes CR and LF to channel $FF.\nEntry: none.\nExit: AF, C as on entry.\nChanges: B, DE.\nKeeps: AF, C, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"CR"},
        "12247": {"comment":"LF"},
        "12249": {"synopsis":"Writes character B to channel $FF (EXOS 7).\nEntry: B = the character.\nExit: AF and BC as on entry.\nChanges: DE.\nKeeps: AF, BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12258": {"synopsis":"Sends the output buffer out, sets FLG_EDIT to $1C and reads a line (READ_LINE) from the\nchannel at IY-$51.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: Z, A = 0; B = the code that ended the line; HL = the output buffer.\nError: NZ, A = the status ($E4 for code $1A).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"Send the buffer out"},
        "12262": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT = $1C"},
        "12269": {"comment":"C = the channel"},
        "12272": {"synopsis":"Reads a line from channel C (EXOS 5) into the output buffer at IY+$6E: a count byte, the\ncharacters (codes from $20; at most 128) and a 0. The line ends at CR or ESC; other codes\nbelow $20, and characters past the 128th, are dropped. Code $1A (end of text) is error $E4.\nEntry: C = the channel, IY.\nExit: Z, A = 0; B = the code that ended the line; HL = the buffer.\nError: NZ, NC, A = EXOS's status, or $E4 for code $1A.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY."},
        "12275": {"comment":"DE = the count byte"},
        "12277": {"comment":"Count 0"},
        "12278": {"synopsis":"Stores the character at DE and a 0 after it.","comment":"The character (0 at the start)"},
        "12280": {"comment":"The 0 after it"},
        "12282": {"synopsis":"Reads the next character (EXOS 5)."},
        "12284": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "12287": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12289": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "12290": {"comment":"Code $1A?"},
        "12292": {"comment":"Carry: a character"},
        "12295": {"comment":"Error $E4, NC"},
        "12298": {"synopsis":"An error returns (NC); CR and ESC end the line; codes below $20 are dropped, as is any\ncharacter once 128 are in."},
        "12300": {"comment":"An error"},
        "12301": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "12302": {"comment":"CR?"},
        "12306": {"comment":"ESC?"},
        "12310": {"comment":"A control code: drop it"},
        "12314": {"comment":"128 in?"},
        "12318": {"comment":"One more"},
        "12321": {"synopsis":"The line is complete: A = 0, Z."},
        "12323": {"synopsis":"HL = the output buffer at IY+$6E.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: HL = IY+$6E.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, IX, IY."},
        "12331": {"synopsis":"HL = the output buffer in use: IY+$6E, or IY+$620 (the error prompt's) when bit 7 of IY-$20\nis set. The buffer's first byte counts the characters in it.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: HL = the buffer.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY."},
        "12334": {"comment":"The error prompt's buffer?"},
        "12339": {"comment":"IY+$620"},
        "12344": {"synopsis":"Writes CR and LF to the output buffer (and so to the channel).\nEntry: IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12349": {"comment":"A write error: stop"},
        "12352": {"synopsis":"Writes character A to the output buffer. A full buffer (128 characters) is written out\nfirst; a control code (below $1B) writes the buffer out after it.\nEntry: A = the character, IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status of the write.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12355": {"comment":"C = the character"},
        "12359": {"comment":"128 in it?"},
        "12361": {"comment":"Yes: write it out"},
        "12364": {"comment":"The write failed: return its status"},
        "12366": {"comment":"One more"},
        "12371": {"comment":"HL = the new character's place"},
        "12375": {"comment":"Control code?"},
        "12377": {"comment":"A = $FF (carry) for one, else 0"},
        "12378": {"synopsis":"OUTBUF_CHAR's end: a character from $1B up returns; a control code first sends the buffer\nout (OUTBUF_FLUSH)."},
        "12381": {"comment":"NC: a character from $1B up"},
        "12382": {"synopsis":"Writes the output buffer's characters to the channel in IY-$50 (EXOS 8) and empties it.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: A = EXOS's status, Z = written.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12388": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "12391": {"comment":"The buffer is empty again"},
        "12394": {"comment":"DE = the characters"},
        "12395": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "12404": {"synopsis":"Writes message A from the message table ($0098: German or English by EXOS variable $90) to\nthe output buffer, then goes on as OUTBUF_TEXT.\nEntry: A = the message number, IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z; DE = the copy's end.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"DE = the message, a count byte first"},
        "12407": {"synopsis":"Steps DE to the text's next character (OUTBUF_TEXT's loop)."},
        "12408": {"synopsis":"Writes the zero-ended text at DE to the output buffer.\nEntry: DE = the text, IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z; DE = its end.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12409": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "12411": {"comment":"Writes the character"},
        "12416": {"synopsis":"Writes the drive letter and \":\" of the file block at IX (its IX+$07, OUTBUF_DRIVE).\nEntry: IX = the file block, IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12419": {"synopsis":"Writes a drive's letter (A + $40) and a colon.\nEntry: A = the drive (1 = A), IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The letter"},
        "12424": {"comment":"\":\""},
        "12428": {"synopsis":"Writes a directory entry's 8-character name and 3-character extension (from BC + 8):\n- Z: as they are, a space between (\"NAME     EXT\").\n- NZ and C: the name without its spaces, \".\" (a space when there is no extension), the\n  extension, a space.\n- NZ and NC: the same with the name's spaces in front of it (right-aligned in 8).\nEntry: BC + 8 = the name; F as above; IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY."},
        "12429": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "12434": {"comment":"Short form?"},
        "12436": {"comment":"The 8 name characters"},
        "12441": {"comment":"A space"},
        "12444": {"synopsis":"Writes 3 characters from HL (the extension).\nEntry: HL = the characters, IY.\nExit: HL past them; A = 0 and Z, or the last write's status.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "12446": {"synopsis":"Writes B characters from HL to the output buffer.\nEntry: B = the count, HL = the characters, IY.\nExit: HL past them; B = 0; A = 0 and Z, or the last write's status.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "12454": {"synopsis":"The short form; carry: the name without padding.","comment":"8 characters"},
        "12457": {"comment":"Not right-aligned?"},
        "12459": {"comment":"HL = past the name; B = 8"},
        "12461": {"synopsis":"A space for each space in the name: they go in front."},
        "12463": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "12465": {"comment":"Then one in front"},
        "12470": {"synopsis":"B = 8: the name's characters without its spaces."},
        "12471": {"synopsis":"Writes the name's characters except spaces, then picks the extension's separator."},
        "12473": {"comment":"Spaces are left out"},
        "12480": {"comment":"The extension's first character"},
        "12481": {"comment":"None (a space)?"},
        "12485": {"comment":"Else \".\""},
        "12487": {"synopsis":"Writes the separator (a space or \".\"), the extension and a space."},
        "12490": {"comment":"The 3 extension characters"},
        "12493": {"synopsis":"Writes character A for NZ (an attribute that is set), else a space.\nEntry: A = the character; F: NZ to write it; IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12495": {"synopsis":"Writes a space to the output buffer.\nEntry: IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12499": {"synopsis":"Writes the 4-byte number at HL: below 1024 as \"<n> byte(s)\" (OUTBUF_COUNTWORD); from 1024 as\n\"<n>K\", n = the number / 1024 (the number at HL is shifted in place).\nEntry: HL = the number (low byte first), IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12500": {"comment":"DE = the low word"},
        "12506": {"comment":"The high word not 0?"},
        "12509": {"comment":"1024 or more?"},
        "12514": {"comment":"HL = the number; DE = its address"},
        "12516": {"comment":"Message $36: \" byte\""},
        "12518": {"synopsis":"Writes a count and a word: HL in decimal, message A (\" byte\" or \" file\"), then the plural\nunless the count is 1: \"s\" in English; in German \"s\" for \" byte\" and \"en\" for another\nword (EXOS variable $90 = 0 chooses German).\nEntry: A = the word's message number, HL = the count, IY.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status; Z with A = the message number for a count of 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12521": {"comment":"The count in decimal"},
        "12525": {"comment":"The word"},
        "12529": {"comment":"A count of 1?"},
        "12533": {"comment":"A = the message number"},
        "12534": {"comment":"Then singular"},
        "12537": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90"},
        "12544": {"comment":"0: German"},
        "12547": {"comment":"A = the message number"},
        "12549": {"comment":"English: \"s\""},
        "12551": {"comment":"German \" byte\": \"s\""},
        "12555": {"comment":"Otherwise \"en\""},
        "12564": {"synopsis":"Writes \"s\"."},
        "12568": {"synopsis":"The number at HL (pointing at its top byte) is shifted right 10 times (divided by 1024),\nthen written in decimal and \"K\".","comment":"10 shifts"},
        "12570": {"synopsis":"One pass of the size-in-K printer begun at $3118: shifts the 4-byte number whose top byte\nis at HL one bit right; C counts the 10 passes (a divide by 1024).","comment":"Keep the top byte's address"},
        "12571": {"comment":"B = 4 bytes"},
        "12573": {"comment":"Clear carry: a 0 enters at the top"},
        "12574": {"synopsis":"Shifts one byte of the number right through carry, top byte first; after 10 passes prints\nthe quotient (PRINT_DEC32, no padding) and a \"K\"."},
        "12579": {"comment":"HL = the top byte again"},
        "12580": {"comment":"10 passes done?"},
        "12583": {"comment":"DE = the number's first byte, pushed by the caller at $30D3"},
        "12584": {"comment":"A = 0: no padding"},
        "12588": {"synopsis":"Writes \"K\" to the output buffer (a tail jump to OUTBUF_CHAR).\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as OUTBUF_CHAR: A = 0 and Z, or EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12590": {"synopsis":"Writes A to the output buffer: a shared tail jump to OUTBUF_CHAR."},
        "12593": {"synopsis":"Writes a space and the time held in a directory entry's time word (hours in bits 15-11,\nminutes in bits 10-5) as \"hh:mm\". With bit 7 of IY-$4F clear the hours run 12-11 and an \"a\"\nor \"p\" follows; with it set they run 0-23.\nThe minute bits are shifted out of the word in place: the entry's time word is changed.\nEntry: HL = the time word's high byte (its low byte at HL-1); IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 and Z.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS's status when a full buffer could not be written.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL; the time word.\nKeeps: C, IX, IY."},
        "12598": {"comment":"B = 0: no suffix yet"},
        "12599": {"comment":"A = the hours (bits 7-3 of the high byte)"},
        "12605": {"comment":"24-hour clock?"},
        "12611": {"comment":"B = \"a\""},
        "12613": {"comment":"Afternoon?"},
        "12617": {"comment":"Hours 12-23 become 0-11"},
        "12619": {"comment":"B = \"p\""},
        "12621": {"synopsis":"Hour 0 of a 12-hour clock is shown as 12.","comment":"Hour 0?"},
        "12624": {"comment":"Then 12"},
        "12626": {"synopsis":"Writes the hours as two digits, a colon, the minutes as two digits and, for the 12-hour\nclock, the \"a\" or \"p\" kept in B."},
        "12629": {"comment":"\":\""},
        "12634": {"comment":"A = the high byte; the low byte's top 3 bits are rotated in below"},
        "12635": {"comment":"HL = the low byte"},
        "12645": {"comment":"A = the minutes"},
        "12650": {"comment":"B = 0 (24-hour clock)?"},
        "12653": {"synopsis":"Writes A to the output buffer (on to OUT_A_TAIL)."},
        "12655": {"synopsis":"Writes a space and the date held in a directory entry's date word (year - 1980 in bits\n15-9, month in bits 8-5, day in bits 4-0) as three two-digit fields joined by \"-\". The order\ncomes from bits 5-0 of IY-$4F, two bits per field (1 = day, 2 = month, 3 = year); 0 there\nmeans day-month-year ($6C). The year is shown as its last two digits.\nEntry: HL = the date word (low byte first); IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: NC; A = the format byte rotated.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"C = the day"},
        "12661": {"comment":"H = the year - 1980 (bit 8 of the word goes to carry)"},
        "12664": {"comment":"A = the month, its top bit from carry"},
        "12670": {"comment":"L = the month"},
        "12671": {"comment":"A = the field order, moved to bits 7-2"},
        "12676": {"comment":"Order set?"},
        "12678": {"comment":"Else day, month, year"},
        "12680": {"synopsis":"Three fields, the first one after a space.","comment":"B = 3 fields"},
        "12682": {"comment":"E = \" \", the separator before the first field"},
        "12684": {"synopsis":"Takes the next field's two bits from the top of A and picks its value: day (C), month (L)\nor year (H + 80).","comment":"Next two bits to the bottom"},
        "12686": {"comment":"Keep the rest for the next field"},
        "12687": {"comment":"D = the field's selector"},
        "12690": {"comment":"Selector 0: the value is 0"},
        "12692": {"comment":"Selector 1: the day"},
        "12696": {"comment":"Selector 2: the month"},
        "12700": {"comment":"Selector 3: the year"},
        "12701": {"comment":"Years count from 1980"},
        "12703": {"synopsis":"Writes the separator, then the field's value below 100.","comment":"D = the value"},
        "12704": {"comment":"Separator first"},
        "12709": {"comment":"From 2000 on?"},
        "12713": {"comment":"Two digits only"},
        "12715": {"synopsis":"Writes the value as two digits; the next field is preceded by \"-\"."},
        "12718": {"comment":"A = the remaining selectors"},
        "12719": {"comment":"E = \"-\" from the second field on"},
        "12723": {"comment":"NC"},
        "12725": {"synopsis":"Writes A (0-99) as two decimal digits.\nEntry: A = the value; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 and Z.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS's status when a full buffer could not be written.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"E = \"0\" - 1"},
        "12727": {"synopsis":"Counts the tens in E, writes them, then the units.","comment":"Take off 10"},
        "12729": {"comment":"One more ten"},
        "12732": {"comment":"D = the units - 10"},
        "12733": {"comment":"The tens digit"},
        "12738": {"comment":"The units digit: units - 10 + \"0\" + 10"},
        "12742": {"synopsis":"Puts the text of error A in the output buffer (ERR_EXPLAIN). An error with no text gets\nmessage $3D (\"Error \") and the code in decimal instead ($31F4, at HL).\nEntry: A = the error code, HL = space for the number's digits, IY.\nExit: NZ when EXOS gave a text (or failed); Z when the number was written.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12745": {"comment":"A text? (count byte not 0, or an EXOS error)"},
        "12747": {"comment":"BC = the error code"},
        "12751": {"comment":"Message $3D: \"Error \""},
        "12756": {"comment":"DE = the error code"},
        "12757": {"comment":"HL = where its digits go"},
        "12760": {"synopsis":"Asks EXOS for the text of error A (EXOS 28), written straight into the output buffer: its\ncount byte, then the characters.\nEntry: A = the error code, HL = kept for the caller, IY.\nExit: A = EXOS's status, HL = the output buffer, B = the error code, DE = HL on entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12765": {"comment":"DE = the output buffer"},
        "12767": {"comment":"A = the error code"},
        "12774": {"synopsis":"Writes HL in decimal (no padding) to the output buffer: it goes into IY-$26 as a 4-byte\nnumber and $31FD writes that.\nEntry: HL = the number, IY.\nExit: Z.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12777": {"comment":"BC = the output buffer"},
        "12783": {"comment":"HL = IY-$23, the number's top byte"},
        "12788": {"synopsis":"Writes DE in decimal without padding, building the 4-byte number in the 4 bytes that end at\nHL (the caller's $31E6 and OUTBUF_ERRTEXT enter here).\nEntry: DE = the value; HL = the last of 4 free bytes; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as PRINT_DEC32.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'; the 4 bytes.","comment":"The high word is 0"},
        "12792": {"comment":"then HL"},
        "12793": {"comment":"The low word is DE"},
        "12796": {"comment":"DE = the number; A = 0: no padding"},
        "12797": {"synopsis":"Writes the 4-byte number at DE in decimal, by subtracting the powers of ten in the table at\n$3233 ($FF ends it): each power's count is one digit. Leading zeros are left out when A is\n0, or written as A (a space right-aligns the number in 10 columns); the units digit always\nshows. The number is used up: it is 0 at the end.\nEntry: A = the padding character, 0 for none; DE = the number (low byte first); IY =\nEXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 and Z.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, DE', L'; the number.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY."},
        "12798": {"comment":"E' = the padding character"},
        "12799": {"comment":"D' = \"0\""},
        "12802": {"comment":"HL = the powers of ten, 1000000000 first"},
        "12805": {"synopsis":"The next power; from the last one (1) on, a zero is written as \"0\".","comment":"The power 1?"},
        "12809": {"comment":"Then the units digit always shows"},
        "12812": {"synopsis":"C counts the subtractions; carry is clear for the first.","comment":"C = 0, NC"},
        "12814": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the power once (4 bytes).","comment":"Keep the power and the number"},
        "12816": {"comment":"B = 4 bytes"},
        "12818": {"synopsis":"Subtracts byte by byte until the number goes below 0, then adds the power back (ADD32,\nwhich also moves HL to the next power), and writes the digit: C - 1, through E' while\nit is 0. A JR into $3228 runs its operand ($B3) as OR E: the zero digit's character.","comment":"Number byte - power byte - borrow"},
        "12825": {"comment":"Back to the number's first byte"},
        "12826": {"comment":"Back to the power's first byte"},
        "12827": {"comment":"One more subtraction"},
        "12828": {"comment":"Not below 0 yet?"},
        "12830": {"comment":"Add the power back; HL = the next power"},
        "12833": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "12835": {"comment":"Digit 0?"},
        "12838": {"comment":"A = the digit's character"},
        "12839": {"comment":"Every later 0 is written as \"0\""},
        "12840": {"comment":"Its operand ($B3), entered by JR: OR E, the zero's character or 0"},
        "12842": {"comment":"Write the digit, unless a leading zero is dropped"},
        "12846": {"comment":"The $FF end mark?"},
        "12884": {"synopsis":"Adds the 4-byte number at HL to the one at DE (low bytes first).\nEntry: DE = the sum; HL = the number to add.\nExit: the sum at DE; HL = HL + 4; B = 0; carry = the carry out of the top byte.\nChanges: AF, B, HL; the sum.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "12885": {"comment":"B = 4 bytes"},
        "12888": {"synopsis":"Adds one byte with carry."},
        "12897": {"synopsis":"Finds a keyboard channel: tries EXOS 11 special function 9 (@@JOY, read the joystick, C = 0)\non channels 0, 1, 2 ... until one answers.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Z and H = that channel; NZ and H = $FF when none does.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H.\nKeeps: L, IX, IY.","comment":"From channel 0"},
        "12899": {"synopsis":"Tries channel H: EXOS 11 special function 9; channels up to $FF are tried.","comment":"A = the channel"},
        "12900": {"comment":"B = 9 (@@JOY), C = 0"},
        "12905": {"comment":"It answered: Z, H = the channel"},
        "12906": {"comment":"Next channel"},
        "12909": {"comment":"None: H = $FF, NZ"},
        "12911": {"synopsis":"Closes the channel whose number is in the byte at IY - $100 + E - 1 ($FF: none), then marks\nit $FF.\nEntry: E = the low byte of the offset (IY-$100+E points just above the byte), IY.\nExit: HL = the byte; Z, A = 0 when there was no channel, else A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12914": {"comment":"DE = $FF00 + E"},
        "12917": {"synopsis":"Closes the channel whose number is in the byte below HL ($FF: none) and marks it $FF.\nEntry: HL = one above the byte.\nExit: HL = the byte; Z, A = 0 when there was no channel, else A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "12918": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "12919": {"comment":"$FF: none"},
        "12922": {"comment":"Close it (EXOS 3)"},
        "12924": {"comment":"None now"},
        "12927": {"synopsis":"The CD and CHDIR commands: with a path, makes it the current directory (EXDOS function 2,\nCHANGE_DIR); without one, writes the drive's current directory (function 3, GET_CUR_DIR)\nas \"A:\\path\" and a new line.\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($9F for a second argument).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"C bit 0: the last element is entered too, its name not copied"},
        "12932": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "12936": {"comment":"A path given?"},
        "12938": {"comment":"Function 2: make it the current directory"},
        "12943": {"comment":"B = the drive"},
        "12946": {"comment":"Function 3: the current directory's text"},
        "12952": {"comment":"The text is followed by a new line"},
        "12956": {"comment":"DE = the path text"},
        "12957": {"synopsis":"Writes the request block's drive (IX+7) as \"A:\", the path separator and the path text at DE.\nEntry: DE = the path text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 and Z; C = the path's first character.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY."},
        "12960": {"comment":"\"\\\" or \"'\", by the language"},
        "12971": {"synopsis":"The DIR command: lists the files matching the argument (all with none), with the \"/W\"\n(wide: names only, six to a line) and \"/H\" (hidden files too) options.\n1. Takes the argument apart and reads the options (IY-$2A: bit 7 /W, bit 1 /H).\n2. Writes the volume line (VOL_LABEL), then \"Directory of \" and the path (FIND_FIRST_ARG).\n3. Each entry: its name and, in the long form, \"h\"/\"r\" marks, the size (or \"<dir>\"), the\n   date and the time; the sizes are added up at IX-$123 (IY-$26).\n4. The summary: the total size, \" in \", the number of files, and the drive's free space\n   in K (EXDOS function 21).\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates."},
        "12976": {"comment":"The options: \"/W\" and \"/H\""},
        "12982": {"comment":"Nothing else after them?"},
        "12987": {"comment":"An empty path text: the root"},
        "12990": {"comment":"Read the name raw"},
        "12994": {"comment":"The volume line"},
        "13001": {"synopsis":"The end of DIR's start: drops the kept BC and HL; an error returns."},
        "13002": {"synopsis":"Drops the kept HL (or the kept result) and returns on an error."},
        "13014": {"synopsis":"C' = 0 (the wide form's column), then \"Directory of \" and the first entry.","comment":"Column 0"},
        "13016": {"comment":"\"Directory of \""},
        "13021": {"comment":"The first entry, and the path after the text"},
        "13024": {"comment":"Found one?"},
        "13027": {"comment":"$CF (nothing found) is not an error here"},
        "13032": {"synopsis":"Ends the header line with a blank line and clears the total size (IX-$123).","comment":"F' carry: nothing found"},
        "13033": {"comment":"End the line"},
        "13036": {"comment":"And a blank line"},
        "13040": {"comment":"HL = the total size (4 bytes)"},
        "13052": {"synopsis":"One entry: its name, then the wide or the long form; the entry's size is added to the\ntotal.","comment":"No more entries?"},
        "13054": {"comment":"Z: the long form (/W not given)"},
        "13061": {"comment":"The name: padded columns, or compact with /W"},
        "13064": {"comment":"DE = the entry's size (descriptor +$24)"},
        "13070": {"comment":"DE = the total"},
        "13075": {"comment":"Add the size to the total"},
        "13078": {"comment":"DE = the size"},
        "13079": {"comment":"/W?"},
        "13085": {"comment":"C = the entry's attributes"},
        "13088": {"comment":"Read-only?"},
        "13093": {"comment":"\"h\" when hidden, else a space"},
        "13100": {"comment":"\"r\" when read-only"},
        "13108": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "13114": {"comment":"The size in 10 columns"},
        "13119": {"comment":"Z: no \"<dir>\""},
        "13120": {"synopsis":"Writes \"<dir>\" for a directory, then the entry's date and time and a new line.","comment":"\" <dir>  \""},
        "13127": {"comment":"HL = the date word (entry +$18)"},
        "13132": {"comment":"The date"},
        "13136": {"comment":"HL = the time word's high byte"},
        "13137": {"comment":"The time"},
        "13146": {"synopsis":"The wide form: counts the columns in C' and starts a new line after six names."},
        "13147": {"comment":"One more column"},
        "13149": {"comment":"Six on the line?"},
        "13153": {"comment":"Column 0 again"},
        "13158": {"synopsis":"Back to the main registers."},
        "13159": {"synopsis":"Finds the next entry and loops."},
        "13164": {"synopsis":"Ends the listing: a new line after a part-filled wide line, then the total size, \" in \",\nthe file count (\"file\" or \"files\"), and the free space: function 21's free clusters times\nthe sectors per cluster, halved (512-byte sectors), in K with \" free\".","comment":"An error ended the search?"},
        "13166": {"comment":"A partly filled wide line?"},
        "13172": {"comment":"A space"},
        "13175": {"comment":"HL = the number of files"},
        "13176": {"comment":"HL = the total size"},
        "13180": {"comment":"The total, in bytes or K"},
        "13183": {"comment":"\" in \""},
        "13189": {"comment":"The count and \" file\", with its plural"},
        "13194": {"comment":"Four spaces"},
        "13199": {"comment":"B = the drive"},
        "13202": {"comment":"Function 21: the free space"},
        "13208": {"comment":"A = $29 (unused); a JR into its operand runs ADD HL,HL"},
        "13210": {"comment":"Shift once more for each power of 2 in the sectors per cluster"},
        "13214": {"comment":"Halve: sectors to K"},
        "13218": {"comment":"The free space"},
        "13221": {"comment":"\"K\""},
        "13224": {"comment":"\" free\""},
        "13246": {"synopsis":"The RD and RMDIR commands: DEL for directories (carry set).\nEntry: as CMD_DEL.\nExit: as CMD_DEL.\nError: as CMD_DEL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"Carry: directories"},
        "13247": {"synopsis":"The DEL, ERA and ERASE commands (and RD): deletes every matching entry (EXDOS function 8),\nread-only ones left out; the \"/H\" option takes hidden ones too. A name of all \"?\" asks\n\"Erase all files (Y/N)?\" first.\nEntry: AF = the mode (carry for directories); HL = the argument text; IX = the request\nblock; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, C after the last one.\nError: C and NZ, A = the error code ($CF when nothing matched).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"The name and \"/H\""},
        "13250": {"comment":"Nothing else after them?"},
        "13254": {"comment":"Read-only entries are not taken"},
        "13258": {"comment":"The first entry"},
        "13262": {"comment":"HL = the name (+8)"},
        "13266": {"comment":"B = 11 characters"},
        "13268": {"comment":"\"?\""},
        "13270": {"synopsis":"Is every character of the name \"?\"; then asks first.","comment":"\"?\" here?"},
        "13276": {"comment":"\"Erase all files\""},
        "13281": {"comment":"Ask; not \"yes\" returns"},
        "13285": {"synopsis":"BC = the result buffer."},
        "13288": {"synopsis":"Deletes the entry found, then finds the next.","comment":"HL = the request block"},
        "13289": {"comment":"DE = the entry's descriptor"},
        "13291": {"comment":"Function 8: delete"},
        "13296": {"comment":"Then the next one"},
        "13299": {"comment":"Until the search ends"},
        "13302": {"synopsis":"Writes \" (Y/N)? \", writes out the buffer and reads a line ($2FE2); the answer is yes when it\nis one character, the yes letter: \"J\" when EXOS variable $90 is 0 (German), else \"Y\".\nEntry: the question in the output buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0; Z for yes, NZ for anything else.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"\" (Y/N)? \""},
        "13310": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "13315": {"comment":"In capitals"},
        "13319": {"comment":"Read EXOS variable $90"},
        "13325": {"comment":"D = its value"},
        "13326": {"comment":"\"J\""},
        "13328": {"comment":"German?"},
        "13332": {"comment":"Else \"Y\""},
        "13334": {"synopsis":"The answer against the yes letter."},
        "13335": {"comment":"Yes?"},
        "13336": {"synopsis":"A = 0, the flags kept."},
        "13339": {"synopsis":"The MD and MKDIR commands: makes a directory (EXDOS function 7, MAKE_DIR).\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($9F without a name or with a second argument).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates."},
        "13342": {"comment":"A name given?"},
        "13346": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "13354": {"comment":"Function 7: make the directory"},
        "13359": {"synopsis":"The MVDIR command: MOVE for directories (carry set, A = 0 after the INC).\nEntry: as CMD_REN.\nExit: as CMD_REN.\nError: as CMD_REN.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"Carry: directories"},
        "13360": {"synopsis":"The MOVE command: A = 0 (Z) makes CMD_REN move. The operand of LD B,$37 at $3431 is SCF,\nthe RNDIR command's entry ($3432: REN for directories).\nEntry: as CMD_REN.\nExit: as CMD_REN.\nError: as CMD_REN.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"A = 0: move"},
        "13361": {"comment":"Its operand ($37) is SCF, RNDIR's entry"},
        "13363": {"synopsis":"The REN and RENAME commands (A = $FF, NZ), MOVE, MVDIR and RNDIR: the first argument's\nmatching entries are renamed (EXDOS function 9) to the second argument's name, or moved\n(function 10) to the directory the second argument names. \"/H\" takes hidden entries too.\n1. Takes the first argument apart and finds its first entry; the character the parse cut\n   off is put back.\n2. A second request block (NEXT_REQ_BLOCK) on the same drive takes the second argument:\n   a name to rename to (no path: B bit 1 clear), or a directory path to move to (parsed\n   with its last element entered).\n3. Each matching entry: function 9 with BC = the second block, or 10 with BC = the path\n   text.\nEntry: AF = the mode (Z: move; carry: directories); HL = the argument text; IX = the\nrequest block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 (C) after the last one.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($AE for a path in the new name, $9F for a missing argument).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"The first name and \"/H\""},
        "13369": {"comment":"Its first entry"},
        "13372": {"comment":"HL = where the parse stopped"},
        "13375": {"comment":"Put back the character the parse replaced"},
        "13377": {"comment":"The second request block"},
        "13380": {"comment":"Its drive = the first block's"},
        "13387": {"comment":"HL' = the second block"},
        "13391": {"comment":"The second argument"},
        "13394": {"comment":"C = 0: copy the name"},
        "13396": {"comment":"Rename?"},
        "13399": {"comment":"Move: enter the path's last element"},
        "13401": {"synopsis":"Takes the second argument apart into the second block, back to the first block."},
        "13402": {"comment":"The second argument"},
        "13405": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "13409": {"comment":"IX = the first block again"},
        "13414": {"comment":"AF = the command's mode, AF' kept"},
        "13418": {"comment":"Rename?"},
        "13420": {"comment":"Move: HL' = the path text"},
        "13426": {"synopsis":"The new name may have no path (B bit 1) and must be given.","comment":"A path in the new name?"},
        "13428": {"comment":"Then $AE (Invalid parameter)"},
        "13434": {"synopsis":"BC = the result buffer, DE = the block."},
        "13437": {"synopsis":"Function 9 for REN, 10 for MOVE.","comment":"AF = the command's mode"},
        "13438": {"comment":"Function 10: move"},
        "13440": {"comment":"Move?"},
        "13442": {"comment":"Else function 9: rename"},
        "13443": {"synopsis":"Runs the function on the entry found, then finds the next."},
        "13445": {"comment":"HL = the request block"},
        "13446": {"comment":"DE = the entry's descriptor"},
        "13448": {"comment":"BC = the second block or the path text"},
        "13452": {"comment":"Rename or move it"},
        "13455": {"comment":"Then the next one"},
        "13458": {"comment":"Until the search ends"},
        "13461": {"synopsis":"The VOL command: with a name, writes it as the drive's volume label (EXDOS function 6 on\nthe raw name, IX+6 bit 3); without one, writes \"Volume in drive A: is NAME\" or \"... has no\nname\".\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"Read the name raw"},
        "13466": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "13472": {"comment":"A = the parse's flags"},
        "13473": {"synopsis":"Sets the volume label (A bit 0 set: a name given, function 6) or finds and writes it\n(function 4 on the root, from DIR too).\nEntry: A bit 0 = a name given; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"BC = the result buffer, DE = the block"},
        "13476": {"comment":"A name?"},
        "13478": {"comment":"Function 6: write it"},
        "13483": {"comment":"Function 4: find the label"},
        "13488": {"comment":"$CF: no label"},
        "13492": {"comment":"Another error?"},
        "13494": {"synopsis":"Writes \"Volume in drive A:\" and \" has no name\", or \" is \" and the 11-character name.","comment":"Keep the result"},
        "13495": {"comment":"\"Volume in drive \""},
        "13500": {"comment":"\"A:\""},
        "13504": {"comment":"No label?"},
        "13505": {"comment":"\" has no name\""},
        "13510": {"comment":"\" is \""},
        "13514": {"comment":"DE = the entry's name"},
        "13519": {"comment":"End it after 11 characters"},
        "13524": {"comment":"The name"},
        "13527": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "13530": {"synopsis":"The CLS command: writes code $1A and writes out the buffer.\nEntry: IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = EXOS's status, flags from it.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Code $1A"},
        "13538": {"synopsis":"The ECHO command: writes its argument text and a new line.\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0 and Z.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the text"},
        "13545": {"synopsis":"The TYPE command: COPY to the default channel (bit 5 of IY-$2B clear).\nEntry: as COPY_TYPE.\nExit: as COPY_TYPE.\nError: as COPY_TYPE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"Not COPY"},
        "13551": {"synopsis":"The COPY command (bit 5 of IY-$2B set); goes on at COPY_TYPE.\nEntry: as COPY_TYPE.\nExit: as COPY_TYPE.\nError: as COPY_TYPE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"COPY"},
        "13555": {"synopsis":"COPY and TYPE: a source and (for COPY) a destination, each a file specification, a\n\"#n\" channel or a device name (\"NAME:\").\n1. The source (PARSE_OPERAND) and its options from $36D4: \"/A\", and \"/H\" for a file.\n2. TYPE: the destination is channel $FF (B' bit 6 set). COPY: the second operand in the\n   next request block and its options from $36DB (\"/V\", \"/T\", \"/A\" for a file, \"/A\" else).\n3. IY-$2A = the options of both. A file source is searched for (FIND_FIRST_ARG); a device\n   is opened (OPEN_FREE_CHAN), its channel kept at IY-$2C.\n4. The copy itself from $3566 on.\nEntry: HL = the argument text; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, all alternates.","comment":"The source"},
        "13560": {"comment":"Its options"},
        "13566": {"comment":"A name given?"},
        "13571": {"comment":"B' = the source's options"},
        "13574": {"comment":"HL = the text after it"},
        "13575": {"comment":"The second request block"},
        "13578": {"comment":"The next argument"},
        "13582": {"comment":"COPY?"},
        "13589": {"comment":"TYPE: B' bit 6"},
        "13591": {"comment":"C' = 0"},
        "13593": {"comment":"The destination: channel $FF"},
        "13599": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "13601": {"synopsis":"COPY's destination: the second operand and its options.","comment":"C = 0: copy the name"},
        "13602": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "13606": {"comment":"DE' = the text after it"},
        "13609": {"comment":"Its options"},
        "13615": {"synopsis":"Nothing may follow."},
        "13618": {"synopsis":"Back to the source block; IY-$2A = the options of both; a file source is searched for.","comment":"IX = the source block"},
        "13627": {"comment":"The options of both"},
        "13633": {"comment":"D = the source's first byte: $FF for a file"},
        "13636": {"comment":"A file?"},
        "13640": {"comment":"Its first entry"},
        "13646": {"synopsis":"The source is a channel or a device: refused with an all-\"?\" destination name ($AE);\na device (D not 0) is opened, its channel kept at IY-$2C and the block's +2.","comment":"The destination's name all \"?\"?"},
        "13650": {"comment":"Then $AE (Invalid parameter)"},
        "13653": {"comment":"D = 0: a channel number"},
        "13657": {"comment":"DE = the device's name"},
        "13660": {"comment":"Open it"},
        "13664": {"comment":"Close it at the end"},
        "13670": {"synopsis":"With \"/V\" (IY-$2A bit 7), IY-$29 = $FE when IY-$58 was not 0, else $FF, and IY-$58 is\ncleared."},
        "13674": {"comment":"/V?"},
        "13680": {"comment":"A = IY-$58"},
        "13685": {"comment":"A = $FF when it was not 0"},
        "13686": {"comment":"$FE or $FF"},
        "13690": {"comment":"Clear it"},
        "13694": {"synopsis":"A device destination (first byte not $FF or 0) is created (EXOS 2, $0339); its channel\ngoes to IY-$2D and the block's +$62.","comment":"D = the destination's first byte"},
        "13698": {"comment":"A file ($FF) or a channel (0)?"},
        "13703": {"comment":"DE = the device's name"},
        "13706": {"comment":"Create the channel"},
        "13710": {"comment":"Close it at the end"},
        "13716": {"synopsis":"A file source is opened (EXDOS function 12).","comment":"BC = the result buffer, DE = the block"},
        "13719": {"comment":"HL = the block"},
        "13720": {"comment":"DE = the entry's descriptor"},
        "13722": {"comment":"A file?"},
        "13728": {"comment":"Function 12"},
        "13734": {"synopsis":"Allocates up to four segments for the copy's buffer; HL' adds up DE from each EXOS 24.","comment":"HL' = 0"},
        "13739": {"comment":"HL = the segment list (IX-$133)"},
        "13744": {"comment":"B = 4 tries"},
        "13746": {"synopsis":"One EXOS 24 (allocate a segment)."},
        "13749": {"comment":"A = the segment"},
        "13751": {"comment":"Got one?"},
        "13753": {"comment":"A shared segment: its boundary"},
        "13757": {"comment":"None: segment 0, size 0"},
        "13760": {"synopsis":"Stores the segment and adds DE to HL'.","comment":"The segment number"},
        "13778": {"synopsis":"The buffer's size, rounded down to an even page, at most $FE00; without a segment, EXDOS\nfunction 30's scratch buffer (512 bytes) is used.","comment":"L = 0"},
        "13780": {"comment":"Any space?"},
        "13784": {"comment":"No segments"},
        "13789": {"comment":"Function 30: the scratch buffer"},
        "13796": {"comment":"Its address in place of the kept word"},
        "13798": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "13801": {"synopsis":"TYPE moves at most $2000 bytes at a time.","comment":"COPY?"},
        "13807": {"comment":"$20 pages at most"},
        "13813": {"synopsis":"Writes the source's name for a copy out of a named directory ($36E2), checks the stop\n($2F23), points IX at the destination block and, for a file destination, creates it:\n$3884, code $1A at DE, with \"/A\" EXDOS function 16 ($3862), then function 13."},
        "13815": {"comment":"The name, when copying a directory's files"},
        "13818": {"comment":"Stop pressed?"},
        "13825": {"comment":"HL = IY"},
        "13829": {"comment":"DE = IY+$18D"},
        "13835": {"comment":"IX = the destination block (IY+$15D)"},
        "13838": {"comment":"A file ($FD-$FF)?"},
        "13843": {"comment":"Already open?"},
        "13853": {"comment":"C = 1"},
        "13855": {"comment":"Code $1A"},
        "13858": {"comment":"/A?"},
        "13866": {"comment":"Function 13: create the file"},
        "13871": {"synopsis":"An error goes to $3699; with the stop status kept from $2F23, the new file is deleted\n(function 8)."},
        "13873": {"comment":"The kept status"},
        "13875": {"comment":"Not stopped?"},
        "13877": {"comment":"HL = the destination block"},
        "13880": {"comment":"Function 8: delete it"},
        "13887": {"synopsis":"The destination file is written and STOP was not pressed. When the source is a disk file\ntoo, gives the destination the source's attributes plus bit 5 ($20) and a time and date\n(COPY_TIME_DATE), stores them in its directory entry (function 11) and writes the drive's\nbuffers back (function 14). Then COPY_FREE_SEGS.","comment":"Source (IX-$60) a disk file?"},
        "13891": {"comment":"No: nothing to copy over"},
        "13893": {"comment":"A = the source's attributes (descriptor +$13)"},
        "13896": {"comment":"Plus bit 5"},
        "13898": {"comment":"The destination's attributes"},
        "13901": {"comment":"Keep the destination's descriptor (IX+$30)"},
        "13906": {"comment":"DE = descriptor +$21, the date's high byte"},
        "13907": {"comment":"From the destination's own descriptor (-5)"},
        "13910": {"comment":"Destination /T switch?"},
        "13914": {"comment":"Yes: keep the destination's time and date"},
        "13916": {"comment":"Else from the source's descriptor (-$65)"},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"Copies four bytes down into the destination's descriptor +$1E-$21 (where function 11 takes\nthe time and the date): +$1B-$1C to +$20-$21 and +$1D-$1E to +$1E-$1F of the descriptor HL\npoints into. Then function 11 (FN11_SET_ATTR) and, when it succeeded, function 14\n(FN14_FLUSH) for the destination's drive with C = 0.","comment":"HL = descriptor +$1C (source or destination)"},
        "13921": {"comment":"+$1C, +$1B to the destination's +$21, +$20"},
        "13925": {"comment":"HL = descriptor +$1E"},
        "13928": {"comment":"+$1E, +$1D to the destination's +$1F, +$1E"},
        "13932": {"comment":"DE = the destination's descriptor"},
        "13933": {"comment":"HL = the destination's request block"},
        "13936": {"comment":"Function 11: attributes, time, date to the entry"},
        "13941": {"comment":"B = the destination's drive"},
        "13944": {"comment":"C = 0 after a success: keep the buffers"},
        "13945": {"comment":"Function 14: write the drive's buffers back"},
        "13947": {"comment":"Only when function 11 succeeded"},
        "13952": {"synopsis":"The destination is a channel. With the destination's /A switch, and when STOP was not\npressed, ends the text with an end-of-file mark ($1A) written with EXOS 7.","comment":"Destination /A switch?"},
        "13958": {"comment":"A = the status kept at $35FD"},
        "13960": {"comment":"STOP pressed: no end mark"},
        "13962": {"comment":"A = the destination's channel"},
        "13965": {"comment":"B = $1A, the end-of-file mark"},
        "13967": {"comment":"EXOS 7: write it"},
        "13969": {"comment":"Status, STOP check"},
        "13972": {"synopsis":"Closes the channel the command opened for the destination (its number at IY-$2D, $FF for\nnone) through $326F.","comment":"IY-$2C - 1: the destination's channel"},
        "13977": {"synopsis":"Frees the copy buffer: the four segment numbers from EXOS 24 (the list pushed at $35AF),\none by one with EXOS 25. The status kept at $35FD stays on the stack.","comment":"HL = the status (AF) kept at $35FD"},
        "13978": {"comment":"HL = the segment list; the status back on the stack"},
        "13979": {"comment":"Four segments"},
        "13981": {"synopsis":"One pass of the freeing loop. On the third pass (B = 2), when B' is not 0 (a scratch sector\nbuffer was taken instead, its address in BC'), frees that buffer with function 30 (B = 0)\nand leaves the loop.","comment":"Keep the counter"},
        "13983": {"comment":"Third pass?"},
        "13987": {"comment":"And a scratch buffer taken (B' not 0)?"},
        "13992": {"comment":"Drop the counter"},
        "13993": {"comment":"B = 0: free the scratch buffer"},
        "13995": {"comment":"Function 30"},
        "14000": {"comment":"And stop"},
        "14002": {"synopsis":"Frees the next segment of the list with EXOS 25.","comment":"C = the segment"},
        "14004": {"comment":"EXOS 25: free it"},
        "14006": {"comment":"The counter"},
        "14009": {"synopsis":"The file is done: the status of the copy (kept in F') returns when it is an error. TYPE\nends the text with CR LF. When the source name had wildcards (bit 5 of its parse flags)\nthe next matching file is searched for ($3CD4) and copied from $357E.","comment":"Drop the status kept at $35FD"},
        "14010": {"comment":"A, F = the copy's status"},
        "14011": {"comment":"Error or STOP: return it"},
        "14012": {"comment":"TYPE (not COPY)?"},
        "14016": {"comment":"Yes: CR LF after the text"},
        "14019": {"comment":"IX = the source's block"},
        "14024": {"comment":"The source name had wildcards?"},
        "14028": {"comment":"No: done (A = 0, Z)"},
        "14029": {"comment":"Search for the next matching file"},
        "14032": {"comment":"Found: copy it too"},
        "14050": {"synopsis":"When the source was a directory named on the command line (IX+$13 bit 5), writes the\nentry's name and a new line.\nEntry: IX = the source block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: NZ, A = EXOS's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', DE'."},
        "14053": {"comment":"Destination +$14 = the block's high byte"},
        "14056": {"comment":"A directory's files?"},
        "14062": {"comment":"The compact name"},
        "14070": {"synopsis":"A = 0, Z: no end of file seen yet; starts the block loop."},
        "14071": {"synopsis":"Fills the buffer from the source and writes it to the destination, block after block,\nuntil the source ends. F' carries the end-of-file mark (NZ once seen). A disk-file source\nis read with function 15 (COPY_FN_BUFFER), up to the buffer's size (HL').","comment":"F' = the end-of-file mark (NZ: seen)"},
        "14072": {"comment":"Source a disk file?"},
        "14078": {"comment":"BC = HL', the buffer's size"},
        "14082": {"comment":"Function 15: read into the buffer"},
        "14087": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14088": {"comment":"BC = the bytes read"},
        "14090": {"synopsis":"The source is a channel. Without its /A switch and with a disk file as destination, reads\nblocks with EXOS 6 (COPY_FILL_BUF with A = $80); else one character at a time.","comment":"Source /A switch?"},
        "14094": {"comment":"Yes: a character at a time"},
        "14096": {"comment":"Destination a disk file?"},
        "14100": {"comment":"No: a character at a time"},
        "14102": {"comment":"Read blocks with EXOS 6"},
        "14107": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14108": {"comment":"BC = the bytes read"},
        "14110": {"synopsis":"Reads one character from the source channel (EXOS 5) into the buffer: BC = 1.","comment":"Buffer (BC') paged in, A = the channel"},
        "14113": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "14114": {"comment":"EXOS 5: read a character"},
        "14116": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "14117": {"comment":"Status: .EOF marks the end, STOP stops"},
        "14120": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14121": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "14124": {"synopsis":"Writes the BC bytes in the buffer to the destination (IX now its block). Nothing read: on\nto COPY_BLOCK_DONE. With /A on the source or the destination the buffer is first converted\n(COPY_FILL_BUF with A = bit 6 or 5 of IY-$2A), which can shorten it at a $1A.","comment":"IX = the destination's block"},
        "14129": {"comment":"Nothing read?"},
        "14134": {"comment":"The /A switches (source $40, destination $20)"},
        "14139": {"comment":"HL' = the count, its old value on the stack"},
        "14141": {"comment":"The buffer's size to the stack, HL' = the count"},
        "14142": {"synopsis":"Converts the buffer for /A (COPY_FILL_BUF) and puts the buffer's size back in HL'. The\nJP NZ at $1114 that names this address never jumps (A = 0 there)."},
        "14143": {"comment":"/A: convert, BC = the bytes to write"},
        "14147": {"comment":"HL' = the buffer's size again"},
        "14149": {"comment":"Destination a disk file?"},
        "14153": {"comment":"No: write to the channel"},
        "14156": {"comment":"Destination file not created yet (bit 7)?"},
        "14160": {"comment":"Created: write the block"},
        "14163": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "14164": {"synopsis":"Creates the destination file before its first block. Saves the destination's 13 name bytes\n(+8 to +$14) at IY+$6F, then puts the source's character (from the source's descriptor)\nin place of every \"?\" of the destination's 11-byte name.","comment":"HL = the output buffer, IY+$6E"},
        "14168": {"comment":"DE = IY+$6F"},
        "14169": {"comment":"Kept for the restore"},
        "14170": {"comment":"HL = IY+$165, the destination's name (+8)"},
        "14174": {"comment":"Twice: for the restore and the fill"},
        "14176": {"comment":"13 bytes: the name and its flags"},
        "14179": {"comment":"Saved at IY+$6F"},
        "14181": {"comment":"DE = the destination's name"},
        "14182": {"comment":"HL = the source's descriptor name (+$38)"},
        "14186": {"comment":"11 characters"},
        "14188": {"synopsis":"A \"?\" in the destination's name takes the source's character.","comment":"A \"?\"?"},
        "14193": {"comment":"Yes: the source's character"},
        "14195": {"synopsis":"Next character; then BC = the descriptor, DE = the request block, HL = DE' for function 6,\nand bit 1 of IY-$37 set when the source is a disk file."},
        "14197": {"comment":"All 11?"},
        "14199": {"comment":"BC = IX+$30, DE = IX"},
        "14205": {"comment":"HL = DE'"},
        "14206": {"comment":"Source a disk file?"},
        "14212": {"comment":"Yes: bit 1 of IY-$37"},
        "14216": {"synopsis":"Creates the destination's directory entry with function 6 (DIR_CREATE_ENT); only the first\nfile of the command sets bit 6 of IY-$2B and takes this path. When the name is a directory\n($98, \"Directory exists\"), no name was given and the source is a disk file, the destination\nbecomes that directory: its request block is copied to IX+$60, request and descriptor are\nswapped with the name made all \"?\" (DESC_SWAP_WILD), and the name is built again from the\nsource's ($3754).","comment":"Function 6: find or create the entry"},
        "14218": {"comment":"Not the first file?"},
        "14222": {"comment":"Mark: the first file is done"},
        "14226": {"comment":"Not the first: create without the checks"},
        "14228": {"comment":"Function 6"},
        "14231": {"comment":"Made: open it"},
        "14233": {"comment":"$98 (\"Directory exists\")?"},
        "14237": {"comment":"No name given (wildcards filled)?"},
        "14243": {"comment":"Source a disk file?"},
        "14249": {"comment":"HL = IX+$60"},
        "14254": {"comment":"DE' = IX+$60: HL for function 6 next time"},
        "14257": {"comment":"HL = the request block, DE = IX+$60"},
        "14258": {"comment":"48 bytes"},
        "14261": {"comment":"Keep the destination's request at IX+$60"},
        "14263": {"comment":"The directory found becomes the request"},
        "14266": {"comment":"The saved parse flags, ORed with B"},
        "14269": {"comment":"B = $3CBA's high byte of IX+$30 (bit 7 set)"},
        "14273": {"comment":"And the saved flags at +$14"},
        "14279": {"comment":"DE = the name's save area again"},
        "14280": {"comment":"HL = the destination's name"},
        "14281": {"comment":"Fill in the source's name again"},
        "14283": {"synopsis":"A later file of the command: function 6 straight away.","comment":"Function 6"},
        "14286": {"comment":"Error: restore the name and return it"},
        "14288": {"synopsis":"Opens the new entry with function 12 for DE + $30.","comment":"DE + $30"},
        "14293": {"comment":"Function 12"},
        "14298": {"synopsis":"Puts the destination's 13 name bytes saved at IY+$6F back (the \"?\" pattern for the next\nfile) and returns an error; else the block is written (COPY_WRITE_FILE).","comment":"DE = the destination's name"},
        "14299": {"comment":"HL = the saved copy at IY+$6F"},
        "14303": {"comment":"Restore it"},
        "14305": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "14306": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "14308": {"synopsis":"The destination file exists now: writes the block with function 16 ($3862).","comment":"Created"},
        "14312": {"comment":"Function 16: write BC bytes from the buffer"},
        "14315": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14316": {"comment":"Next block"},
        "14318": {"synopsis":"The destination is a channel: writes the BC bytes from the buffer (BC') in parts of at\nmost 64 bytes.","comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "14320": {"comment":"DE = BC', the buffer"},
        "14324": {"synopsis":"Writes the next part: 64 bytes, or the rest when fewer are left.","comment":"All written?"},
        "14328": {"comment":"Keep the address"},
        "14329": {"comment":"Page the part in; A = the channel"},
        "14332": {"comment":"BC = 64"},
        "14334": {"comment":"Next part's address on the stack"},
        "14337": {"comment":"Bytes left - 64"},
        "14339": {"comment":"64 or more left: a full part"},
        "14341": {"comment":"Fewer: BC = the rest"},
        "14344": {"comment":"And nothing left after it"},
        "14347": {"synopsis":"Writes BC bytes from DE to the channel: one byte with EXOS 7, more with EXOS 8 (at $381A,\ninside the LD BC at $3819).","comment":"Only one byte?"},
        "14351": {"comment":"A = the destination's channel"},
        "14354": {"comment":"More: EXOS 8 at $381A"},
        "14357": {"comment":"B = the byte"},
        "14359": {"comment":"EXOS 7: write the character"},
        "14361": {"comment":"Hides RST 30h / EXOS 8 (write block) at $381A"},
        "14364": {"comment":"DE = the next part"},
        "14365": {"comment":"Status, STOP check"},
        "14368": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14371": {"synopsis":"Back to the source's block. With no end of file seen (F' Z) the next block; else the\nfile is done, A = 0."},
        "14374": {"comment":"IX = the source's block"},
        "14376": {"comment":"The end-of-file mark"},
        "14377": {"comment":"Not seen: next block"},
        "14380": {"comment":"Done: A = 0, Z"},
        "14382": {"synopsis":"Takes one COPY or TYPE operand apart into the request block at IX: \"#n\" is a channel\nnumber, else a file specification (PARSE_ARG), or a device when the parse stops at \":\"\n($3DFA finds the name). A file ends at $3859, inside the JP NZ at $3858 (never taken: A\nis 0): XOR A, SCF, so carry marks a file.\nEntry: HL = the text; C = function 1's flags; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: carry for a file (IX+$13 = the parse's flags), NC for a channel or a device (IX+0 =\nthe name's high byte or 0, IX+1 its low byte, IX+2 the channel, IX+$13 = 1); A = 0; IX+$14\n= D; DE = the text after it; AF' = the entry AF.\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, AF', L'.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "14383": {"comment":"A \"#\"?"},
        "14386": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "14391": {"comment":"L' = the first character"},
        "14394": {"comment":"A file specification?"},
        "14397": {"comment":"A = the character that ended it"},
        "14398": {"comment":"A device name?"},
        "14402": {"comment":"Put back the \":\""},
        "14406": {"comment":"And the first character"},
        "14407": {"comment":"Find the device's name"},
        "14410": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "14413": {"synopsis":"A channel or device operand: IX+0/IX+1 = DE (the name, or 0 and the channel), IX+2 = E.\nTYPE's destination enters here with DE = $00FF.\nEntry: DE = the device's name, or D = 0 and E = the channel; HL = the text after it; IX =\nthe request block.\nExit: A = 0, Z, NC; C = the next character; DE = the text; IX+$13 = 1; IX+$14 = D.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The channel number"},
        "14416": {"comment":"The name's high byte, 0 for a channel"},
        "14419": {"comment":"C = the next character"},
        "14420": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "14422": {"comment":"B = 1, the mark for IX+$13"},
        "14424": {"comment":"Never taken (Z): its operand ($AF $37) is the file path's XOR A, SCF"},
        "14427": {"comment":"IX+$14 = D"},
        "14430": {"comment":"IX+$13 = B"},
        "14434": {"synopsis":"Runs EXDOS function 16 ($3864 on) with IX = BC' and IY-$80 = 3; status $E4 becomes 0.\nEntry: BC = passed on; BC' = the block for IX; IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z (also for $E4, with A' = $E4 and NZ).\nError: NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, AF'.","comment":"Function 16"},
        "14436": {"synopsis":"Calls EXDOS function A on a file's block with the copy buffer: DE = its descriptor\n(IX+$30), BC = the count, IX = the buffer (BC'), whose address IY-$80 = 3 says is in the\npage map at IY-$36. Entered at $3862 with A = 16 (write); $3702 uses 15 (read). Then goes\non as COPY_STATUS.\nEntry: A = the function; BC = the byte count; IX = the file's block; BC' = the buffer; IY.\nExit: as COPY_STATUS (A = 0, Z; F' NZ on .EOF); BC, DE, HL as the function leaves them.\nError: A = the status, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF'.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "14437": {"comment":"BC = the descriptor"},
        "14440": {"comment":"DE = the descriptor"},
        "14442": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "14444": {"comment":"The buffer's address (BC')"},
        "14446": {"comment":"IX = the buffer; the block kept"},
        "14448": {"comment":"The buffer is in the map at IY-$36"},
        "14452": {"comment":"Function A"},
        "14455": {"comment":"IX = the block again"},
        "14457": {"synopsis":"Checks a status for the copy loop: a 0 status still stops for a pending STOP ($2F23); .EOF\n($E4) becomes success with the end-of-file mark left in F' (NZ, A' = $E4).\nEntry: A = the status, flags from OR A.\nExit: A = 0, Z; after .EOF also F' NZ, A' = $E4.\nError: A = the status, NZ: $E5 (.STOP) when STOP was pressed.\nChanges: AF, AF'; FLAG_SOFT_IRQ ($BFF2) cleared for STOP.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"0 becomes $E5 when STOP is pending"},
        "14461": {"comment":".EOF?"},
        "14464": {"comment":"NZ: the end-of-file mark"},
        "14465": {"comment":"Into F'"},
        "14466": {"comment":"Success"},
        "14468": {"synopsis":"DE = BC', then $3888.\nEntry: BC' = the value.\nExit: as $3888.\nChanges: AF, B, DE; as $3888."},
        "14471": {"comment":"DE = BC'"},
        "14472": {"synopsis":"Pages in the copy buffer at DE: turns the address into a segment and a page-1 address\nthrough the map at IY-$36 (ADDR_TO_PAGE1 with A = 3) and puts the segment in page 1.\nEntered at $3884 with DE = BC'.\nEntry: DE = the address in the IY-$36 map; IX = the channel's block.\nExit: page 1 = its segment; D moved into $4000-$7FFF; A = the channel (IX+2); B = 0; Z.\nChanges: AF, B, D; page 1.\nKeeps: C, E, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Map 3: the segments at IY-$36"},
        "14477": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "14481": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "14485": {"synopsis":"Fills or converts the copy buffer (BC') for HL' bytes, in parts of at most 64 bytes.\n1. A bit 7 set: reads each part from the channel IX+2 with EXOS 6 ($38F2, inside the LD DE\n   at $38F1) until HL' bytes are read or the channel ends.\n2. Bit 7 clear (an /A switch): converts the bytes already there. A $1A ends the data (F' NZ,\n   A' = $E4); TYPE also keeps CR, LF and TAB, clears bit 7 of the other bytes and shows a\n   control code as \".\"; COPY copies them unchanged.\nEntry: A = the mode; HL' = the byte count; BC' = the buffer; IX = the channel's block; IY.\nExit: A = 0; BC = the bytes in the buffer; F' NZ, A' = $E4 when the data ended.\nError: A = the status, NZ ($E5 .STOP, or EXOS 6's).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF'; page 1.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "14486": {"comment":"Keep DE'"},
        "14487": {"comment":"D' = the mode"},
        "14488": {"comment":"The buffer (BC')"},
        "14490": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "14491": {"comment":"HL = the bytes done"},
        "14494": {"comment":"F' carry: more to do"},
        "14496": {"synopsis":"The next part: stops when the count is reached; else takes 64 bytes or the rest.","comment":"Keep the part's address"},
        "14498": {"comment":"Page it in; A = the channel"},
        "14501": {"comment":"Keep the bytes done"},
        "14502": {"comment":"BC = the bytes done"},
        "14505": {"comment":"HL = the count (HL')"},
        "14508": {"comment":"Bytes left"},
        "14510": {"comment":"None: done ($3902, inside the LD BC at $3901)"},
        "14515": {"comment":"Left - 64"},
        "14517": {"comment":"64 or more: a full part"},
        "14519": {"comment":"Fewer: BC = the rest"},
        "14522": {"synopsis":"Counts the part as done and moves the address on, then reads it (mode bit 7) or converts it.","comment":"HL = the bytes done"},
        "14523": {"comment":"Plus this part"},
        "14525": {"comment":"The next part's address"},
        "14528": {"comment":"Read mode (D' bit 7)?"},
        "14531": {"comment":"Yes: EXOS 6 at $38F2"},
        "14533": {"synopsis":"Converts one byte; a $1A ends the data.","comment":"The byte"},
        "14534": {"comment":"$1A, the end-of-file mark?"},
        "14538": {"comment":"A = $E4 (.EOF), NZ"},
        "14540": {"comment":"Into F': the data ended"},
        "14541": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "14542": {"comment":"The bytes after it are dropped"},
        "14544": {"synopsis":"TYPE only: keeps CR, LF and TAB; other bytes lose bit 7, and one below a space becomes \".\".","comment":"COPY?"},
        "14548": {"comment":"Yes: copied unchanged"},
        "14550": {"comment":"CR?"},
        "14554": {"comment":"LF?"},
        "14558": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "14562": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "14564": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "14568": {"comment":"Yes: show \".\""},
        "14570": {"synopsis":"Stores the shown byte."},
        "14571": {"synopsis":"Next byte of the part; at the end skips the EXOS 6 hidden in the LD DE at $38F1."},
        "14572": {"comment":"One less"},
        "14573": {"comment":"All of the part?"},
        "14577": {"comment":"Hides RST 30h / EXOS 6 (read block) at $38F2"},
        "14580": {"comment":"Status, STOP check"},
        "14583": {"synopsis":"After a part: the bytes not read or after a $1A (BC) leave the count; loops while F' carry\nsays more is to come; else BC = the bytes in the buffer, A = 0.","comment":"DE = the next part's address"},
        "14584": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14586": {"comment":"Done -= the bytes not taken"},
        "14588": {"comment":"Carry off: the next F' says \"stop\""},
        "14589": {"comment":"F' carry: more to do?"},
        "14590": {"comment":"Yes: the next part"},
        "14592": {"comment":"The marks back into F'"},
        "14593": {"comment":"Hides POP HL / POP DE at $3902 (count reached)"},
        "14596": {"comment":"BC = the bytes in the buffer"},
        "14598": {"comment":"Success"},
        "14599": {"synopsis":"Restores DE' and returns."},
        "14600": {"comment":"DE' as on entry"},
        "14603": {"synopsis":"TIME command: sets carry (time, not date) and goes on as CMD_DATE.\nEntry: as CMD_DATE.\nExit: as CMD_DATE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "14604": {"synopsis":"DATE command (and TIME's, with carry): shows or sets the date or the time; F' carry says\nwhich (set: the time).\n1. With parameters: sets the clock from them (DT_SET).\n2. Without: writes \"Current date is \" (or time) and the value (PACK_TIME_DATE, shown by\n   $316F for the date, $3131 for the time) and CR LF; then the prompt (DT_PROMPT) and a line\n   from the keyboard. An empty answer leaves the clock; a bad value writes the error's text\n   and asks again.\nEntry: carry clear for DATE, set for TIME; HL = the parameter text; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = the error, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"F' carry: time"},
        "14605": {"comment":"Parameters given?"},
        "14607": {"comment":"Yes: set from them"},
        "14609": {"comment":"\"Current\""},
        "14614": {"comment":"\" date\" or \" time\""},
        "14617": {"comment":"\" is\""},
        "14625": {"comment":"HL = IY-$26"},
        "14629": {"comment":"The time and date packed at IY-$26"},
        "14632": {"comment":"HL = the date"},
        "14633": {"comment":"Time or date?"},
        "14635": {"comment":"Date: write it"},
        "14638": {"comment":"HL = the time's high byte"},
        "14639": {"comment":"Time: write it"},
        "14644": {"synopsis":"Ends the line and writes the prompt in the order of the message language (EXOS variable\n$90; 0 takes the German table).","comment":"CR LF"},
        "14650": {"comment":"Read"},
        "14652": {"comment":"EXOS variable $90"},
        "14656": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "14659": {"comment":"0 (German)?"},
        "14661": {"comment":"No: \"Enter new date\""},
        "14663": {"comment":"German: \"Neue\""},
        "14668": {"comment":"Time or date?"},
        "14672": {"comment":"Time: no \"s\""},
        "14674": {"comment":"Date: \"Neues\""},
        "14679": {"synopsis":"The German prompt's rest: a space, the word and \" eingeben\" (message $43).","comment":"A space"},
        "14684": {"comment":"\"Datum\" or \"Uhrzeit\""},
        "14687": {"comment":"\" eingeben\""},
        "14694": {"synopsis":"The English prompt: \"Enter new\" and \" date\" or \" time\".","comment":"\"Enter new\""},
        "14699": {"comment":"\" date\" or \" time\""},
        "14702": {"synopsis":"Ends the prompt with \": \" and reads a line from the keyboard ($2FE2); also a line ended by\n.EOF ($E4) is taken.","comment":"\":\""},
        "14707": {"comment":"A space"},
        "14710": {"comment":"Read a line into the output buffer"},
        "14713": {"comment":"HL = the text after its count"},
        "14714": {"comment":"Read: set from it"},
        "14716": {"comment":".EOF?"},
        "14718": {"comment":"Another error: return it"},
        "14719": {"synopsis":"Sets the time (TIME_FROM_TEXT) or the date (DATE_FROM_TEXT) from the text; nothing but\nblanks leaves the clock. $EB (.ITIME) writes the error's text (ERR_EXPLAIN) and prompts\nagain.","comment":"Blanks passed: the end?"},
        "14722": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to set"},
        "14723": {"comment":"HL' = the text"},
        "14724": {"comment":"Time or date?"},
        "14728": {"comment":"Date"},
        "14731": {"comment":"Time"},
        "14734": {"comment":"$EB (.ITIME)?"},
        "14736": {"comment":"Another status: return it"},
        "14737": {"comment":"Write the error's text"},
        "14740": {"comment":"And ask again"},
        "14742": {"synopsis":"Sets the date from the text: three numbers in the order the date order byte (IY-$4F) gives,\neach 1 or 2 digits (DATE_FIELD), with separators between them (DT_SEPARATOR). The bits 5-0\nof IY-$4F hold three 2-bit codes, first in bits 5-4: 1 day, 2 month, 3 year, 0 ignored; 0 in\nall of them takes $6C >> 2 (day, month, year). A year xx is stored as xx - 80 in BCD (80-99\n1980-1999, 00-79 2000-2079). A missing number keeps the clock's value. EXOS 33 sets it.\nEntry: HL' = the text (at its first character); IY.\nExit: A = EXOS 33's status ($EB .ITIME for a bad date).\nError: A = $EB (.ITIME), NZ: a bad separator or text after the third number.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"EXOS 34: C = year, D = month, E = day"},
        "14744": {"comment":"The date to BC', DE'; HL = the text"},
        "14745": {"comment":"The date order byte"},
        "14748": {"comment":"Its codes to bits 7-2"},
        "14750": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "14752": {"comment":"No: day, month, year"},
        "14754": {"synopsis":"Three fields; the codes stay on the stack.","comment":"Three numbers"},
        "14759": {"synopsis":"A separator before the second and third numbers; a bad one gives $EB ($3A0E).","comment":"Separator?"},
        "14762": {"comment":"Bad: $EB, with the codes dropped"},
        "14764": {"synopsis":"Reads a number and stores it where its code says: E' the day, D' the month, C' the year\n(minus 80, in BCD).","comment":"A = the number (BCD), carry: none"},
        "14767": {"comment":"The date's registers"},
        "14768": {"comment":"B' = the number"},
        "14769": {"comment":"$FF when there was no number"},
        "14771": {"comment":"The codes"},
        "14772": {"comment":"The next code to bits 1-0"},
        "14775": {"comment":"No number?"},
        "14776": {"comment":"Yes: keep the field"},
        "14778": {"comment":"The code"},
        "14780": {"comment":"0: ignored"},
        "14783": {"comment":"1: the day ($39CC, inside the LD B at $39CB)"},
        "14786": {"comment":"2: the month"},
        "14788": {"comment":"3: the year"},
        "14789": {"comment":"Less 80, in BCD"},
        "14792": {"comment":"C' = the year since 1980"},
        "14793": {"comment":"B' = D', for the LD D,B that follows"},
        "14794": {"synopsis":"D' = the number (the month; after a year, its own value again).","comment":"D' = the month"},
        "14795": {"comment":"Hides LD E,B at $39CC: E' = the day"},
        "14797": {"synopsis":"After the third number only blanks may follow; then EXOS 33 sets the date.","comment":"Back to the text's registers"},
        "14798": {"comment":"The next number"},
        "14800": {"comment":"Blanks passed: the end?"},
        "14803": {"comment":"No: $EB"},
        "14805": {"comment":"Drop the codes"},
        "14806": {"comment":"The date in C, D, E"},
        "14807": {"comment":"EXOS 33: set the date"},
        "14810": {"synopsis":"Sets the time from the text: hours, minutes and seconds, each 1 or 2 digits, with separators\nbetween them (DT_SEPARATOR); a missing one keeps the clock's value. An \"A\" or \"P\" (either\ncase) may end it: 12 A gives 0, 1-11 P adds 12; 0 P or an A hour above 12 is refused. EXOS\n31 sets it.\nEntry: HL' = the text (at its first character); IY.\nExit: A = EXOS 31's status ($EB .ITIME for a bad time).\nError: A = $EB (.ITIME), NZ: other text left at the end.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"EXOS 32: C = hours, D = minutes, E = seconds"},
        "14812": {"comment":"The time to BC', DE'; HL = the text"},
        "14813": {"comment":"The hours"},
        "14816": {"comment":"None: keep them"},
        "14819": {"comment":"C' = the hours"},
        "14821": {"synopsis":"A separator and the minutes (D').","comment":"Separator, then the minutes"},
        "14827": {"comment":"Bad or none: keep them"},
        "14830": {"comment":"D' = the minutes"},
        "14832": {"synopsis":"A separator and the seconds (E').","comment":"Separator, then the seconds"},
        "14838": {"comment":"Bad or none: keep them"},
        "14841": {"comment":"E' = the seconds"},
        "14843": {"synopsis":"After the numbers: \"A\" or \"P\" (TIME_AM_PM), the end (EXOS 31), or $EB.","comment":"Blanks passed"},
        "14846": {"comment":"In capitals"},
        "14849": {"comment":"\"A\"?"},
        "14853": {"comment":"\"P\"?"},
        "14857": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "14858": {"comment":"The time in C, D, E"},
        "14859": {"comment":"Yes: set it"},
        "14861": {"comment":"Hides POP AF at $3A0E (DATE_FROM_TEXT's codes)"},
        "14863": {"synopsis":"Error $EB (.ITIME): an invalid date or time.","comment":"Error $EB (.ITIME)"},
        "14865": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "14867": {"synopsis":"\"A\" or \"P\": only blanks may follow. AM: 12 becomes 0, above 12 is refused.","comment":"Keep the letter"},
        "14868": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14869": {"comment":"Blanks passed: the end?"},
        "14872": {"comment":"B = the letter"},
        "14873": {"comment":"More text: $EB"},
        "14876": {"comment":"The time's registers"},
        "14877": {"comment":"B = 12 (BCD)"},
        "14879": {"comment":"AM?"},
        "14881": {"comment":"A = the hours"},
        "14882": {"comment":"PM"},
        "14884": {"comment":"12 AM?"},
        "14885": {"comment":"Yes: hour 0 ($3A2A)"},
        "14887": {"comment":"Above 12: $EB"},
        "14889": {"comment":"Never jumps (carry); hides LD C,0 at $3A2A: 12 AM"},
        "14892": {"comment":"Set it"},
        "14894": {"synopsis":"PM: 0 is refused, 1-11 get 12 added (BCD), 12 and above stay.","comment":"Hour 0?"},
        "14897": {"comment":"12 or more: as it is"},
        "14900": {"comment":"Plus 12, in BCD"},
        "14902": {"synopsis":"C = the hours."},
        "14903": {"synopsis":"EXOS 31 sets the time from C, D, E.","comment":"EXOS 31: set the time"},
        "14906": {"synopsis":"Writes \" time\" (message $3F, with F' carry) or \" date\" (message $40) to the output buffer;\nin German \"Uhrzeit\" or \"Datum\".\nEntry: F' carry set: time; clear: date; IY.\nExit: as OUTBUF_MSG.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"F' carry"},
        "14910": {"comment":"$FF for the time, 0 for the date"},
        "14911": {"comment":"$3F \" time\" or $40 \" date\""},
        "14916": {"synopsis":"FORMAT command: formats a drive and writes an empty file system.\n1. Parses the drive ($3C96, function 1), takes the switches /1, /H and /8 (table $3A97) into\n   IY-$2A and C' ($3D3B); only blanks may follow.\n2. Function 23 (FN23_OPEN_DISK) with BC = $1964 opens a query-mode \"DISK:\" channel (H, kept\n   in IY-$2C) and returns a segment (B, paged into page 1) and an address DE: the work space\n   is DE - $1964.\n3. Asks \"Destroy data on drive X: (Y/N)? \" ($33F6); any other answer than yes ends it.\n4. Function 29 (FN29_INIT_FS) formats drive IX+7 with B = $F8, + 4 for /H, + 2 for /8, + 1\n   unless /1, and DE = the work space.\n5. When bit 0 of function 1's flags (B) is set, goes on in VOL's code at $34A1 (HL = $3A9D,\n   an empty switch table) to name the volume.\nEntry: HL = the parameter text; IX = DE = the request block; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = the error, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.","comment":"Bit 3 of the request's +6"},
        "14920": {"comment":"Parse the drive (function 1)"},
        "14923": {"comment":"Keep its flags (B)"},
        "14924": {"comment":"The switches /1, /H, /8"},
        "14927": {"comment":"Take them"},
        "14930": {"comment":"Then only blanks"},
        "14935": {"comment":"$1964 bytes of work space"},
        "14938": {"comment":"Function 23: query-mode \"DISK:\" channel"},
        "14945": {"comment":"The channel, closed at the end"},
        "14948": {"comment":"Its segment"},
        "14949": {"comment":"In page 1"},
        "14951": {"comment":"C' = the switches"},
        "14954": {"comment":"Bit 0 out: bit 1 /1, bit 2 /8, bit 3 /H"},
        "14955": {"comment":"$F8, +1 unless /1, +2 /8, +4 /H"},
        "14958": {"comment":"B = the format flags"},
        "14960": {"comment":"\"Destroy data on drive \""},
        "14965": {"comment":"The drive's letter and \":\""},
        "14968": {"comment":"\" (Y/N)? \" and the answer"},
        "14971": {"comment":"Not yes: stop"},
        "14974": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "14977": {"comment":"DE - $1964: the work space"},
        "14982": {"comment":"Function 29: format, write the file system"},
        "14987": {"synopsis":"Returns the status; with bit 0 of function 1's flags set names the volume through VOL's\ncode.","comment":"B = function 1's flags"},
        "14988": {"comment":"Error"},
        "14989": {"comment":"Bit 0?"},
        "14993": {"comment":"The end of $3A97's table: no switches"},
        "15006": {"synopsis":"ISDOS command: loads the system file \"A:\\IS-DOS.SYS\" (the counted name at $3B03) as an EXOS\nmodule and passes it the rest of the command line.\n1. An \"X:\" at the start of the parameters names the drive; it, else IY-$56 as it was, else\n   the default drive (IY-$57) goes to IY-$56.\n2. What follows must be blank or start with \"/\"; the text after the \"/\" (or nothing) is\n   copied as a counted text to IY+$6F and its address stored at IY-$7F/-$7E\n   (ISDOS_SET_TAIL).\n3. Opens the file (OPEN_FREE_CHAN, bit 5 of IY-$37 set meanwhile) and loads it with EXOS 29\n   (DE = IX); a load that returns without an error gives $EF. The stored address is then\n   cleared (ISDOS_CLR_TAIL).\nEntry: HL = the parameter text (its length at HL-1); IX = the request block; IY.\nExit: A = the status ($EF after a load that returned).\nError: A = $AE (\"Invalid parameter\") for text that does not start with \"/\", or EXOS's error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, all alternates.","comment":"HL = the length byte"},
        "15007": {"comment":"B = the length"},
        "15008": {"comment":"DE = the length byte"},
        "15009": {"comment":"\"X:\" first? A' = its drive"},
        "15012": {"comment":"A = the length"},
        "15013": {"comment":"B = the drive as it was"},
        "15016": {"comment":"No \"X:\""},
        "15018": {"comment":"A = the drive named"},
        "15020": {"comment":"A = the length"},
        "15021": {"comment":"Less the \"X:\""},
        "15023": {"comment":"DE past the \"X:\""},
        "15025": {"synopsis":"C = the characters left; no drive: the default drive (IY-$57).","comment":"C = the characters left"},
        "15026": {"comment":"A drive?"},
        "15030": {"comment":"No: the default drive"},
        "15033": {"synopsis":"Stores the drive; skips blanks; the text must end or start with \"/\".","comment":"IY-$56 = the drive"},
        "15036": {"comment":"HL = before the text"},
        "15038": {"comment":"Count for the blank skip"},
        "15039": {"comment":"Blanks passed: nothing left?"},
        "15042": {"comment":"Yes: an empty tail"},
        "15044": {"comment":"\"/\"?"},
        "15046": {"comment":"$AE: \"Invalid parameter\""},
        "15049": {"comment":"The \"/\" not counted"},
        "15050": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "15051": {"synopsis":"Copies the tail as a counted text to IY+$6F, opens \"A:\\IS-DOS.SYS\" and loads it.","comment":"HL = the length's place"},
        "15052": {"comment":"The tail's length"},
        "15054": {"comment":"HL = IY+$6E"},
        "15059": {"comment":"DE = IY+$6F"},
        "15063": {"comment":"The length and the text"},
        "15064": {"comment":"To IY+$6F"},
        "15066": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "15067": {"comment":"Kept in HL'"},
        "15068": {"comment":"Set while the file is opened"},
        "15072": {"comment":"\"A:\\IS-DOS.SYS\""},
        "15075": {"comment":"Open it; H = the channel"},
        "15082": {"comment":"Error"},
        "15084": {"comment":"IY-$7F/-$7E = the tail's copy"},
        "15088": {"comment":"BC = IX+$30, DE = IX"},
        "15091": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "15092": {"comment":"EXOS 29: load the module"},
        "15094": {"comment":"Error: keep it"},
        "15096": {"comment":"Returned: $EF"},
        "15098": {"synopsis":"HL = 0 (no carry) and stores it as the tail's address.","comment":"HL = 0 or $FFFF (carry)"},
        "15100": {"synopsis":"Stores HL at IY-$7F/-$7E: the address of the counted command tail for IS-DOS (0: none).\nEntry: HL = the address; IY.\nExit: IY-$7F/-$7E = HL.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "15121": {"synopsis":"LOAD command: loads every module from a channel with EXOS 29 until EXOS answers $EC (.NOMOD,\nno more modules), which ends it with A = 0. The parameter is \"#n\" (an open channel) or a\nname, opened here ($3DDB; the channel kept in IY-$2C); nothing may follow it. Without a\nparameter the AND (HL) bytes of $3B3D and $3B69 lead to $9F.\nEntry: A = $FF; HL = the parameter text; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = the error, NZ: $9F (\"Wrong number of parameters\"), or EXOS's.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A parameter? (A = $FF)"},
        "15122": {"comment":"No: $9F"},
        "15124": {"comment":"E = the channel; carry: opened here"},
        "15127": {"comment":"Given as \"#n\""},
        "15129": {"comment":"Opened: closed at the end"},
        "15132": {"synopsis":"Only blanks may follow the channel.","comment":"L = the channel, DE = the text"},
        "15133": {"comment":"Only blanks left?"},
        "15136": {"comment":"No: $9F"},
        "15137": {"synopsis":"Loads the next module, with the output buffer (IY+$6E) for its header.","comment":"B = the channel"},
        "15138": {"comment":"HL = IY+$6E"},
        "15141": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "15142": {"comment":"L = the channel"},
        "15144": {"comment":"EXOS 29: load a module"},
        "15146": {"comment":"Loaded: the next one"},
        "15148": {"comment":"$EC (.NOMOD): no more?"},
        "15150": {"comment":"Another error"},
        "15151": {"comment":"Done"},
        "15153": {"synopsis":"PAUSE command: writes its parameters and CR LF as ECHO does ($34E2), then \"Press ENTER to\ncontinue... \" (message $44) and waits for a line ($2FE2).\nEntry: HL = the parameter text; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z when a line ended.\nError: A = the status, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"The text and CR LF"},
        "15157": {"comment":"\"Press ENTER to continue... \""},
        "15162": {"comment":"Wait for ENTER"},
        "15165": {"synopsis":"RAMDISK command: \"RAMDISK n\" calls EXDOS function 28 (FN28_DRIVE_E) with B = n (decimal,\n0-255); the /D switch (table $3B66) first calls it with B = 0. Without a number and without\n/D: $AE; without parameters: $9F.\nEntry: A = $FF; HL = the parameter text; IY.\nExit: A = function 28's status.\nError: A = $9F or $AE, NZ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"A parameter? (A = $FF)"},
        "15166": {"synopsis":"Reads the number and the switches; only blanks may follow.","comment":"No: $9F"},
        "15168": {"comment":"C = the number"},
        "15171": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15172": {"comment":"C = the character after it"},
        "15173": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "15174": {"comment":"The switch /D"},
        "15177": {"comment":"Take it; C' = the switches"},
        "15180": {"comment":"Then only blanks"},
        "15183": {"comment":"C = the switches"},
        "15184": {"comment":"E = the number"},
        "15185": {"comment":"Error"},
        "15186": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "15187": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "15188": {"comment":"The switches"},
        "15189": {"comment":"/D to carry"},
        "15190": {"comment":"A number: make it"},
        "15192": {"comment":"$AE: \"Invalid parameter\""},
        "15194": {"comment":"Neither number nor /D"},
        "15195": {"synopsis":"/D: function 28 with B = 0 first; then function 28 with B = the number."},
        "15196": {"comment":"/D: function 28 with B = 0"},
        "15200": {"comment":"B = the number"},
        "15201": {"synopsis":"Calls EXDOS function 28 (FN28_DRIVE_E) with B.\nEntry: B = the RAM disk's number from the command (0 for /D); IY.\nExit: as FUNC_DISPATCH: A = the status, flags from OR A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Function 28"},
        "15209": {"synopsis":"VAR command: \"VAR n\" writes EXOS variable n's value (in decimal, $31E6) and CR LF; \"VAR n\nON\", \"VAR n OFF\" and \"VAR n v\" write 0, $FF or v to it (the counted names \"ON\" and \"OFF\" at\n$3BDB). Variable 0 and other text give $AE; no parameters $9F. EXOS_VAR_RW does the reading\nand the writing.\nEntry: A = $FF; HL = the parameter text; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z.\nError: A = $9F, $AE or EXOS's error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, DE', L'.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"A parameter? (A = $FF)"},
        "15210": {"synopsis":"The variable's number; with nothing after it the value is read and written out.","comment":"$9F: \"Wrong number of parameters\""},
        "15212": {"comment":"No parameter"},
        "15213": {"comment":"C = the variable"},
        "15217": {"comment":"Separator?"},
        "15221": {"comment":"Bad: $AE"},
        "15223": {"comment":"More text: a value"},
        "15225": {"comment":"B = 0: read"},
        "15230": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "15232": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "15234": {"comment":"Write it in decimal"},
        "15237": {"comment":"And CR LF"},
        "15240": {"synopsis":"The value: \"ON\" (0), \"OFF\" ($FF) or a number.","comment":"Keep the variable"},
        "15241": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "15242": {"comment":"Before it, for the compare"},
        "15243": {"comment":"The counted names \"ON\" and \"OFF\""},
        "15246": {"comment":"Two characters; C = 0 for ON"},
        "15249": {"comment":"\"ON\"?"},
        "15252": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "15254": {"comment":"Three characters; C = $FF for OFF"},
        "15256": {"comment":"\"OFF\"?"},
        "15259": {"comment":"Neither: a number"},
        "15261": {"synopsis":"Steps past the word."},
        "15264": {"synopsis":"A number when no word matched; only blanks may follow; then writes the variable."},
        "15265": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "15266": {"comment":"No word: C = the number"},
        "15270": {"comment":"Separator?"},
        "15274": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "15275": {"comment":"C = the variable"},
        "15276": {"comment":"Bad: $AE"},
        "15278": {"comment":"More text: $AE"},
        "15280": {"comment":"B = 1: write"},
        "15282": {"synopsis":"Reads or writes EXOS variable C with EXOS 16. While IY-$2F is not $FF, the variables in the\nlist at $2FB7 (two bytes an entry, the first the variable, 0 ends it) are kept in EXDOS's\nown bytes at IY+$F0 + the entry's index instead.\nEntry: B = 0 read, 1 write; C = the variable; D = the value to write; IY.\nExit: A = 0, Z; D = the value.\nError: A = $AE for variable 0 (flags Z), or EXOS 16's error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"The variable"},
        "15284": {"comment":"0: $AE"},
        "15287": {"comment":"IY-$2F"},
        "15290": {"comment":"$FF: always EXOS"},
        "15293": {"comment":"DE = IY+$F0, HL = the list at $2FB7"},
        "15297": {"synopsis":"Looks for the variable in the list.","comment":"This entry's variable?"},
        "15298": {"comment":"Yes: EXDOS's copy"},
        "15300": {"comment":"The next copy byte"},
        "15301": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "15304": {"comment":"The end (0)?"},
        "15307": {"synopsis":"Not listed: EXOS 16 reads or writes it."},
        "15308": {"comment":"EXOS 16"},
        "15311": {"synopsis":"Listed: reads or writes EXDOS's copy byte.","comment":"HL = the copy byte"},
        "15313": {"comment":"Write?"},
        "15316": {"comment":"Read: D = the copy"},
        "15317": {"synopsis":"D to the copy byte; A = 0."},
        "15320": {"synopsis":"A = $AE (\"Invalid parameter\"); the flags as the jump left them.","comment":"Error $AE"},
        "15330": {"synopsis":"Compares a typed word with a counted name of the command table: the lengths and every\ncharacter (the typed ones in capitals, TO_UPPER) must be the same.\nEntry: HL = the table entry (its count byte); DE = the word's count position (its characters\nfrom DE+1); B = the word's length.\nExit: NC, NZ and A = 1 for a match, HL past the name (at the handler's address).\nError: C and Z, HL past the name, when the name differs (or the word is longer); C and NZ,\nHL kept, when the word is shorter than the name.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "15332": {"comment":"A = the word's length"},
        "15333": {"comment":"B = the name's length"},
        "15334": {"comment":"Word shorter than the name?"},
        "15337": {"comment":"Compare the length and every character"},
        "15338": {"synopsis":"The compare step of the counted-name match at $3BE2: until a difference has set carry,\nsubtracts the name's byte at HL from A (first the lengths, then each given character in\ncapitals); ADD A,$FF turns any difference into carry.","comment":"A difference seen: skip the compare"},
        "15340": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "15341": {"comment":"Carry when they differ"},
        "15343": {"synopsis":"The compare loop's step: moves both pointers on, takes the next given character in capitals\nand loops; a mismatch seen earlier (carry) skips the compare. At the end turns the carry\ninto A: 1 (NZ, NC) when every character matched, 0 (Z, carry) when one did not.","comment":"Next character of the table's name"},
        "15344": {"comment":"Next character of the given name"},
        "15346": {"comment":"In capitals"},
        "15349": {"comment":"Compare it, unless a mismatch was already seen"},
        "15351": {"comment":"A = $FF after a mismatch, else 0"},
        "15352": {"comment":"A = 0 (Z, carry) mismatch; 1 (NZ, NC) match"},
        "15353": {"synopsis":"Restores the DE and BC pushed at $3BE3 and $3BE2 and returns A and the flags as they are.","comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "15354": {"comment":"The caller's BC"},
        "15356": {"synopsis":"Checks that the parse found something (B bit 0 or 2 set): the error otherwise is $9F\n(Wrong number of parameters).\nEntry: B = the parse's flags.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, NC.\nError: A = $9F, NZ.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "15357": {"comment":"Anything given?"},
        "15361": {"comment":"A = 0 when it was, else $FF"},
        "15362": {"comment":"A = 0 or $9F"},
        "15365": {"synopsis":"Checks that only blanks (spaces, tabs) are left before the 0 that ends the text at DE; a\ncharacter that is not blank stops it, with C = that character (a \"/\" starts an option).\nEntry: DE = the text; Z: C = the character at DE, already read; NZ: read it from DE.\nExit: A = 0, Z: only blanks were left; DE = past the 0.\nError: A = $9F (\"Wrong number of parameters\"), NZ: C = the character that is not blank,\nDE = past it.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"NZ: read the character at DE first"},
        "15367": {"synopsis":"Checks that only spaces and tabs are left after an argument: C is the character that ended\nit and DE points at it; the code from $3C08 steps over spaces and tabs to the next one. A 0\nends the command line. $3C05 enters with Z to check C first.\nEntry: C = the character; DE = its address.\nExit: A = 0 and Z, NC.\nError: A = $9F (Wrong number of parameters), NZ.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "15368": {"synopsis":"The loop: passes the character in A (and C), ends at the 0 or at a character that is not a\nspace or a tab, and reads the next one through $3C14.","comment":"Past the character"},
        "15369": {"comment":"The end (0)?"},
        "15371": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "15373": {"comment":"Yes: read the next"},
        "15375": {"comment":"A tab?"},
        "15377": {"comment":"$9F: \"Wrong number of parameters\"; flags kept"},
        "15379": {"comment":"Another character: NZ"},
        "15380": {"synopsis":"Checks that nothing but spaces and tabs is left before the text's 0.\nEntry: DE = the text.\nExit: Z, NC, A = 0, DE past the 0.\nError: A = $9F (\"Wrong number of parameters\"), NZ.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"The next character"},
        "15384": {"synopsis":"The first search ran for a caller that asked for directories (the carry kept in F' by\n$3C95): drops the BC kept at $3C2D, sets bit 4 of IY-$2A (directories let through) and\nreturns the search's status to $3CDC, the return address pushed at $3C22.","comment":"Drop the BC kept at $3C2D"},
        "15385": {"comment":"Directories pass the attribute filter"},
        "15389": {"comment":"A, F = the search's status"},
        "15390": {"comment":"To $3CDC"},
        "15391": {"synopsis":"Starts the search for the request block's name (EXDOS function 4) and returns the first\nentry its attributes allow. The search's return goes through $3CDC (pushed first), which\nfilters by attribute ($3D61) and goes on with function 5 until an entry passes, counting\nthe entries found at IY-$28.\n1. In directory mode (carry kept in F' by PARSE_ARG_MODE, see $3C18) bit 4 of IY-$2A is set\n   and the search's result returned as it is.\n2. Else, when a single name (B bit 5 clear) was found and it is a directory (entry\n   attribute bit 4, IX+$43), the name is appended to the path text at IY+$135 ($15DB) and\n   the path's text is cut there.\n3. When the output buffer already holds text (\"Directory of \"), the drive and path are\n   written after it (PRINT_DRV_PATH).\n4. For a directory found in step 2 the result becomes the request block ($3CBA, the name\n   all \"?\"), bit 5 of IX+$13 is set and the search starts again inside it (FN4_FIND).\nEntry: B = the parse's flags; IX = the request block; F' carry = directory mode; IY =\nEXDOS's base.\nExit: NC, A = 0 and Z; the entry's descriptor at IX+$30 (BC); DE = IX.\nError: C with A = $CF when nothing matched, or A = the error code; C with A = 0 when the\nsearch ran out after some matches.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'; IY-$28, IY-$27.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"The search's return: the attribute filter at $3CDC"},
        "15395": {"comment":"No entry found yet"},
        "15402": {"comment":"DE = the request block"},
        "15406": {"comment":"BC = the result buffer"},
        "15409": {"comment":"Function 4: find the first entry"},
        "15412": {"comment":"Directory mode?"},
        "15416": {"comment":"Keep the result"},
        "15417": {"comment":"HL = the path text the search returns"},
        "15418": {"comment":"A = the output buffer's count"},
        "15422": {"comment":"DE = the path text"},
        "15423": {"comment":"HL = the kept result (H = the status)"},
        "15425": {"comment":"C = the count of characters waiting"},
        "15426": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "15430": {"comment":"The name was all \"?\" (none given)?"},
        "15434": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "15440": {"comment":"Append the directory's name to the path at IY+$135"},
        "15449": {"comment":"HL' = the path text; find its 0 end"},
        "15452": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "15453": {"synopsis":"The given name is a directory: finds the 0 that ends the path text (HL', from the HL pushed\nat $3C50), adds the name to the text through PATH_STEP's entry $15DB (DE = IY+$135), ends\nthe text with two 0 bytes and goes on to $3C71 with carry, to search inside that directory.","comment":"Next character of the path text"},
        "15455": {"comment":"The end (0)?"},
        "15459": {"comment":"HL' = the 0 at the end"},
        "15460": {"comment":"Main set: DE = IY+$135, B = the parse's flags"},
        "15461": {"comment":"Add the name to the path text"},
        "15464": {"comment":"The path text's address (pushed at $3C50)"},
        "15465": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "15466": {"comment":"Yes: return the error to $3CDC"},
        "15468": {"comment":"Two 0 bytes at the text's new end (HL')"},
        "15472": {"comment":"Carry: search inside the directory"},
        "15473": {"synopsis":"Ends the first search: runs $329D when C (the byte at IY+$6E) is not 0, then returns the\nsearch's status (to $3CDC). With carry (the name is a directory, $3C70) it swaps the request\nblock and the found entry ($3CBA, which makes the name all \"?\"), sets bit 5 of IX+$13 and\nsearches again with function 4 ($3C83), inside the directory.","comment":"Keep the status and the carry"},
        "15474": {"comment":"C = the byte at IY+$6E: 0?"},
        "15476": {"comment":"No: $329D"},
        "15479": {"comment":"DE = the request block, BC = the result buffer"},
        "15483": {"comment":"No directory to enter: return the status"},
        "15484": {"comment":"Swap the blocks; the name all \"?\""},
        "15487": {"comment":"Set bit 5 of IX+$13"},
        "15491": {"synopsis":"Runs EXDOS function 4 (find the first entry) through EXDOS_FN_CALL.\nEntry: DE = the request block; BC = its result buffer; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as EXDOS_FN_CALL.\nError: as EXDOS_FN_CALL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Function 4"},
        "15493": {"synopsis":"Runs EXDOS function A through FUNC_DISPATCH, keeping IX.\nEntry: A = the function; BC, DE, HL its parameters; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z, NC; BC, DE, HL as the function left them.\nError: C and NZ, A = the error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "15500": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "15501": {"comment":"C: an error"},
        "15503": {"synopsis":"PARSE_ARG for a command that may work on directories: carry on entry (RD, MVDIR, RNDIR)\nsets bit 4 of IY-$2B (directories only); A and the flags are kept in AF' for the command\n($3C95).\nEntry: AF = the command's mode; C = function 1's flags; HL = the text; IX = the request\nblock; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as PARSE_ARG; AF' = the entry AF.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, AF'.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Directories?"},
        "15505": {"comment":"Only directories"},
        "15509": {"synopsis":"Keeps the caller's A and flags in AF' (its carry, directories only, is tested again at\n$3C34), then takes the path apart with function 1 ($3C96).","comment":"The caller's carry into F'"},
        "15510": {"synopsis":"Takes an argument apart into the request block (EXDOS function 1, FN_PARSE_SPEC). When B\ncomes back with bits 3 and 4 clear (no name in it), the block's name (+8) is filled with 11\n\"?\" and B bit 5 is set ($3CA0).\nEntry: HL = the argument text; C = function 1's flags (bit 0 = do not copy the name); IX =\nthe request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; B = the parse's flags; C = the character that ended the path, DE its\naddress; HL kept.\nError: C and NZ, A = the parse's error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IY.\nKeeps: HL, IX.","comment":"Function 1: parse the specification"},
        "15515": {"comment":"A name given?"},
        "15520": {"synopsis":"Fills the request block's 11-character name (IX+$08) with \"?\", so that a search matches\nevery entry, and marks it in bit 5 of B.\nEntry: IX = the request block.\nExit: A = 0, Z, NC; bit 5 of B set.\nChanges: AF, B.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "15522": {"comment":"DE = the request block"},
        "15525": {"comment":"DE = its name, at +$08"},
        "15532": {"synopsis":"Writes 11 \"?\" from DE.","comment":"\"?\""},
        "15534": {"comment":"The name's 8 + 3 characters"},
        "15536": {"synopsis":"The fill loop; then restores DE and BC (pushed at $3CA1 and $3CA0) and sets bit 5 of B."},
        "15540": {"comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "15541": {"comment":"The caller's BC"},
        "15542": {"comment":"Bit 5: the name was made all \"?\""},
        "15544": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0, Z, NC.","comment":"A = 0, Z, NC"},
        "15546": {"synopsis":"Swaps the 48-byte request block at IX with the descriptor at IX+$30, then fills the name at\nIX+8 with eleven \"?\" ($3CA0).\nEntry: IX = the block.\nExit: the halves swapped; IX+8-IX+$12 = \"?\"; BC = HL = IX+$30; DE = IX; A = 0, Z.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"BC = IX+$30, DE = IX"},
        "15551": {"comment":"HL = IX+$30"},
        "15553": {"comment":"48 bytes"},
        "15555": {"synopsis":"Swaps the $30 bytes at DE and HL (the request block and the result buffer), then makes the\nrequest block's name all \"?\" (NAME_ALL_WILD) and returns BC = the result buffer. The pops\ntake the DE and BC pushed at $3CBD and $3CBE.","comment":"Swap one byte of the two blocks"},
        "15562": {"comment":"$30 bytes"},
        "15564": {"comment":"HL = the result buffer (BC kept at $3CBE)"},
        "15565": {"comment":"DE = the request block (kept at $3CBD)"},
        "15566": {"comment":"Its name all \"?\""},
        "15569": {"comment":"BC = the result buffer again"},
        "15572": {"synopsis":"Goes on with the search (EXDOS function 5 from $3CD7) to the next entry that passes the\nattribute filter, as FIND_FIRST_ARG's return does.\nEntry: IX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: as FIND_FIRST_ARG.\nError: as FIND_FIRST_ARG.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"BC = the result buffer, DE = the block"},
        "15575": {"synopsis":"Searches on with function 5 until an entry passes the attribute filter (ATTR_FILTER), then\ncounts it in the word at IY-$28 and returns A = 0, Z. $3CDC is also where the first search's\nstatus arrives (the return address pushed at $3C22). A failed search goes to $3CF2.","comment":"Function 5: the next matching entry"},
        "15580": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "15581": {"comment":"Yes: test its attribute"},
        "15584": {"comment":"Not let through: search on"},
        "15586": {"comment":"HL = the count of entries found"},
        "15592": {"comment":"The search failed: $3CF2"},
        "15594": {"comment":"One more found"},
        "15601": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "15602": {"synopsis":"A search failed: an error other than $CF is returned with carry. $CF (\"File not found\", no\nmore entries) becomes A = 0, Z, carry when entries were counted before, and stays $CF, NZ,\ncarry when none was.","comment":"\"File not found\": no more entries?"},
        "15605": {"comment":"Another error: return it, carry"},
        "15606": {"comment":"Were entries found before?"},
        "15608": {"comment":"Carry when none was"},
        "15610": {"comment":"A = $FF when none, else 0"},
        "15611": {"comment":"A = $CF when none, else 0 (Z)"},
        "15613": {"comment":"Carry: the search is over"},
        "15615": {"synopsis":"DE = the request block (IX), BC = its result buffer (IX+$30).\nEntry: IX = the request block.\nExit: DE = IX; BC = IX+$30.\nChanges: F, BC, DE.\nKeeps: A, HL, IX, IY."},
        "15627": {"synopsis":"Moves IX to the next request block ($60 bytes on) and prepares it (the code from $3D10, the\none the command dispatcher runs at $2C47): flags (+6) and drive (+7) = A, first byte A - 1.\nEntry: A = the value (0); IX = the request block.\nExit: IX = DE = the new block; C = A; A = A - 1.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, IX.","comment":"The next block is $60 bytes on"},
        "15632": {"synopsis":"Gives the file block at IX drive A: IX+$06 = IX+$07 = A, IX+$00 = A - 1.\nEntry: A = the drive (0 = the default), IX = the block.\nExit: DE = IX; C = A on entry; A = A - 1.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY."},
        "15638": {"comment":"IX+$07: the drive"},
        "15642": {"comment":"A - 1 into the block's first byte"},
        "15645": {"synopsis":"Takes the first argument apart (PARSE_ARG_MODE), requires one (NEED_PARAM) and reads the\n\"/H\" option ($3D3B with the table at $33BB).\nEntry: AF = the command's mode (carry = directories); C = function 1's flags; HL = the text;\nIX = the request block; IY = EXDOS's base.\nExit: A = 0, Z; B = the parse's flags.\nError: NZ, A = the error code ($9F with no argument).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'."},
        "15652": {"comment":"The options: \"/H\" only"},
        "15660": {"synopsis":"Reads the options from the table at HL for a file operand (carry), else from the table at\nHL + 4 (the options a channel or device may take); then $3D3B.\nEntry: carry = a file operand; HL = the option table.\nExit: as $3D3B.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL, C'.","comment":"A file: every option"},
        "15662": {"comment":"Else the table's later part"},
        "15668": {"synopsis":"An option letter matched: ORs its bit (at HL) into the options at IY-$2A, steps past the\nletter and checks the rest of the text (REST_BLANK); a \"/\" goes on to the next letter.\nThe hidden entry $3D3B (from $32B3, $3A4F, $3B49, $3D27, $3D2C, $3D32), with HL = the option\ntable (letter, bit pairs, 0 ended), DE = the text and C = the character at DE, starts the\noptions at bit 0 alone. IY-$2A bits 0-4 are the attributes a search lets through (bit 0\nread-only, always set); a copy goes to C'. Returns A = 0 when the options end ($3D5D).","comment":"The options so far"},
        "15671": {"comment":"Add this option's bit"},
        "15672": {"comment":"Past the option letter"},
        "15673": {"comment":"HL = the option table (pushed at $3D44)"},
        "15674": {"comment":"C is read again; hides XOR A at $3D3B, the entry"},
        "15676": {"comment":"Read-only files always let through"},
        "15678": {"comment":"Store the options"},
        "15681": {"comment":"C' = the options too"},
        "15684": {"comment":"Keep the option table's address"},
        "15685": {"comment":"Only blanks left, or C = the next character"},
        "15688": {"comment":"A \"/\": another option?"},
        "15691": {"comment":"No: DE back on it, A = 0 ($3D5D)"},
        "15693": {"synopsis":"Looks the letter after a \"/\" up in the option table at HL, in capitals; a letter it does not\nhold returns A = $AE (\"Invalid parameter\"), NZ. The jump at $3D5C never runs: its bytes hide\nthe exit $3D5D (DEC DE, XOR A), which steps DE back and returns A = 0, Z.","comment":"The option letter, in capitals"},
        "15697": {"comment":"This entry's letter?"},
        "15699": {"comment":"Yes: add its bit"},
        "15701": {"comment":"Past its bit"},
        "15703": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "15704": {"comment":"No: try the next entry"},
        "15706": {"comment":"$AE: \"Invalid parameter\", NZ"},
        "15708": {"comment":"Never jumps (NZ); hides DEC DE, XOR A at $3D5D"},
        "15711": {"comment":"The option table's address (pushed at $3D44)"},
        "15713": {"synopsis":"Tests the attribute of the entry a search found (IX+$43) against the options: a read-only,\nhidden, system or directory bit that IY-$2A does not let through rejects it, and so does an\nentry that is not a directory when IY-$2B bit 4 asks for directories only.\nEntry: IX = the request block, the found entry's attribute at +$43; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = 0, Z, NC: the entry passes.\nError: A = $CF (\"File not found\"), NZ, carry: the entry is skipped.\nChanges: AF, L.\nKeeps: BC, DE, H, IX, IY.","comment":"The found entry's attribute"},
        "15717": {"comment":"L = the bits it does not have"},
        "15718": {"comment":"Clear the bits the options let through"},
        "15721": {"comment":"A = its bits the options do not let through"},
        "15722": {"comment":"Read-only, hidden, system or directory left?"},
        "15724": {"synopsis":"Returns A = $CF with carry when the test before it gave NZ; then the directories-only test.","comment":"$CF: \"File not found\""},
        "15727": {"comment":"A bit not let through: skip the entry"},
        "15728": {"comment":"L bit 4 set: not a directory"},
        "15729": {"comment":"Directories only (IY-$2B bit 4)?"},
        "15732": {"comment":"And this is not one?"},
        "15734": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "15736": {"comment":"A = 0, Z, NC: the entry passes"},
        "15737": {"synopsis":"Passes a separator between numbers: blanks, a separator character (SEP_CHAR) or both. With\nno blank the next character must be a separator or the end.\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: NC; A = the next character, Z at the end; HL at it.\nError: carry: no blank and no separator.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.\nKeeps: B, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"Blanks passed"},
        "15740": {"comment":"None?"},
        "15741": {"comment":"Then a separator is needed"},
        "15743": {"comment":"After blanks one is optional"},
        "15746": {"synopsis":"Returns A as it is, with carry clear and Z when A is 0.","comment":"Carry clear; Z when A is 0"},
        "15748": {"synopsis":"Passes one separator, \":\" or one of \",\", \"-\", \".\", \"/\", and the blanks after it.\nEntry: A = the character at HL.\nExit: NC; A = the next character, Z at the end; HL at it.\nError: carry: another character (HL kept).\nChanges: AF, C, HL.\nKeeps: B, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"The end?"},
        "15750": {"comment":"\":\"?"},
        "15754": {"comment":"Below \",\"?"},
        "15757": {"comment":"Above \"/\"?"},
        "15761": {"synopsis":"Steps past the separator (\":\" or \",\" to \"/\") and skips the blanks after it ($3D92).","comment":"Past the separator"},
        "15762": {"synopsis":"Steps HL over spaces and tabs (at most 255).\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: HL = the first other character, A = it; Z when it is the 0 end; NC.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.\nKeeps: B, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"C counts down from 255"},
        "15764": {"synopsis":"Steps HL over spaces and tabs, C counting the characters left.\nEntry: HL = the text, C = the characters left + 1.\nExit: NC, A = the character at HL, Z when it is 0.\nError: C and Z when the text ends.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.\nKeeps: B, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"Text used up?"},
        "15767": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "15772": {"comment":"A tab? Others end the skip"},
        "15776": {"synopsis":"Steps past a space or a tab and goes on counting blanks ($3D94).","comment":"Past the blank"},
        "15777": {"comment":"Count it, look at the next"},
        "15779": {"synopsis":"Reads the decimal digits at HL into C (modulo 256).\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: C = the number; HL = the first non-digit; carry set.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.\nKeeps: B, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"C = 0"},
        "15780": {"synopsis":"Reads decimal digits from HL into C (8 bits, C x 10 + the digit each time) until a character\nthat is not a digit: returns with carry, C = the number and HL on that character.","comment":"C = the number so far"},
        "15781": {"comment":"A = the next digit, HL past it?"},
        "15784": {"comment":"Not a digit: C = the number, carry"},
        "15786": {"comment":"C x 2"},
        "15789": {"comment":"C x 8"},
        "15791": {"comment":"C x 10"},
        "15794": {"comment":"Add the digit"},
        "15795": {"comment":"Next digit"},
        "15797": {"synopsis":"Reads one or two decimal digits as a BCD byte; after a leading 0 any more zeros are passed.\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: NC; A = the number in BCD; HL past it.\nError: carry: no digit.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY.","comment":"The first digit"},
        "15801": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "15802": {"comment":"0?"},
        "15805": {"synopsis":"The first digit was 0: skips any more \"0\" characters, leaving HL on the first other one.","comment":"Next character"},
        "15807": {"comment":"Another \"0\"?"},
        "15809": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "15811": {"comment":"HL back on the character after them"},
        "15812": {"synopsis":"Reads a second digit: with none, A = the first digit (E); with one, A = the two digits as a\nBCD byte (E x 16 + D). Carry is clear either way.","comment":"A second digit?"},
        "15815": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "15816": {"comment":"A = the first digit"},
        "15817": {"comment":"Carry now when there is a second digit"},
        "15818": {"comment":"None: A = the first digit, NC"},
        "15819": {"comment":"The first digit to the high half"},
        "15823": {"comment":"A = the two digits as BCD, NC"},
        "15825": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal digit.\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: NC; A = the digit's value; HL past it.\nError: carry: not a digit (HL kept).\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "15826": {"comment":"Below \"0\"?"},
        "15829": {"comment":"Above \"9\"?"},
        "15835": {"synopsis":"The channel a parameter names: \"#n\" is channel n, already open; any other word is a file\nname, opened on a free channel (OPEN_FREE_CHAN).\nEntry: HL = the parameter.\nExit: NC, Z: E = channel n, D = 0, A = 0, HL past it (and a \":\"); C: E = the channel\nopened, HL = past the name.\nError: NZ, A = the open's status.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"\"#\"?"},
        "15840": {"comment":"DE = the name, counted"},
        "15844": {"comment":"Open it on a free channel"},
        "15847": {"comment":"E = the channel"},
        "15849": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "15850": {"comment":"C: a channel EXDOS opened"},
        "15852": {"synopsis":"Reads a channel number written \"#n\" or \"#n:\".\nEntry: HL = the \"#\".\nExit: DE = the channel number; A = 0, Z; HL after the number (and its colon).\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Over the \"#\""},
        "15856": {"comment":"A colon after it?"},
        "15862": {"synopsis":"Returns the number read after \"#\" (in C) as DE, with A = 0, Z.","comment":"E = the channel number"},
        "15863": {"comment":"A = 0, Z, NC"},
        "15864": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "15866": {"synopsis":"Makes the word at HL a counted name: writes its length (up to a 0, space, tab or \"/\") into\nthe byte before it.\nEntry: HL = the word.\nExit: DE = the count byte; HL = the word's end; A = C = the length.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.\nKeeps: B, IX, IY.","comment":"The count goes here"},
        "15868": {"comment":"Counts from 0"},
        "15870": {"synopsis":"Counts the characters of the word at HL up to a 0, a space, a tab or a \"/\".","comment":"Next character"},
        "15872": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "15873": {"comment":"The end (0)?"},
        "15876": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "15880": {"comment":"A tab?"},
        "15884": {"comment":"A \"/\"?"},
        "15886": {"comment":"No: count on"},
        "15888": {"synopsis":"Writes the count into the byte before the word (the address pushed at $3DFB), which makes\nthe word a counted text at DE; A = its length, HL on the character that ended it.","comment":"DE = the byte before the word (pushed at $3DFB)"},
        "15889": {"comment":"A = the length"},
        "15890": {"comment":"The word is now a counted text"},
        "15892": {"synopsis":"Is the command word a drive, a letter and \":\"?\nEntry: DE = the word's count position (its characters from DE+1); B = its length.\nExit: NC: A' = the drive (1 = A), HL = past the colon; Z when the word is just \"X:\".\nError: C when the second character is not \":\" or the first is not a letter.\nChanges: AF, HL, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "15894": {"comment":"HL = the second character"},
        "15897": {"comment":"\":\"?"},
        "15899": {"comment":"C, NZ: not a drive"},
        "15902": {"comment":"The first character, in capitals"},
        "15908": {"comment":"Above \"Z\"?"},
        "15912": {"comment":"Below \"A\"?"},
        "15915": {"comment":"The drive: 1 for A"},
        "15916": {"comment":"A' = the drive"},
        "15917": {"comment":"Z: the word is two characters long"},
        "15921": {"synopsis":"Makes a letter capital: a code $60-$7F loses bit 5; others are kept.\nEntry: A = the character.\nExit: A = the character in capitals.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Above $7F: kept"},
        "15924": {"comment":"Below $40: kept"},
        "15927": {"comment":"$60-$7F to $40-$5F"},
        "15930": {"comment":"Not reached by a call or jump on this page"},
        "15931": {"comment":"Not 0: on at $3E44"},
        "15933": {"synopsis":"Part of an unreached copy of $3DBA-$3DFF, $80 bytes higher, that runs into the $FF fill at\n$3E80: the bytes match ZEROS_SKIP. Its calls still go to $3DD1 and $3DFA.","comment":"As ZEROS_SKIP, not reached"},
        "15940": {"synopsis":"The unreached copy of BCD_SECOND ($3DC4); then copies of the digit reader $3DD1 ($3E51) and\nof the \"#\" number or name reader $3DDB ($3E5B).","comment":"As BCD_SECOND, not reached"},
        "15953": {"synopsis":"The unreached copy of the digit reader at $3DD1.","comment":"As $3DD1, not reached"},
        "15963": {"synopsis":"The unreached copy of the \"#\" number or name reader at $3DDB.","comment":"As $3DDB, not reached"},
        "15980": {"synopsis":"The unreached copy of $3DEC, the \"#\" number.","comment":"As $3DEC, not reached"},
        "15990": {"synopsis":"The unreached copy of CHAN_NUM_RET; from $3E7A the start of a copy of $3DFA, cut off by the\n$FF fill at $3E80.","comment":"As CHAN_NUM_RET, not reached"},
        "15994": {"comment":"Copy of $3DFA, cut off at $3E80"},
        "16306": {"synopsis":"Offers \"EXDOS E:\", \"EXDOS F:\", \"EXDOS B:\" and \"EXDOS A:\" to the extensions in turn\n(EXDOS_DRV_CMD), building each at IY+$5DB.\nEntry: IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = the last status; EXDOS variable $47 = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"HL = IY+$5DB, the buffer"},
        "16313": {"comment":"Drive 5 (E:)"},
        "16318": {"comment":"Drive 6 (F:)"},
        "16323": {"comment":"Drive 2 (B:)"},
        "16328": {"comment":"Drive 1 (A:)"},
        "16330": {"synopsis":"Makes drive A the current one (EXDOS variable $47) and offers the command \"EXDOS\n<letter>:\" to the extensions (EXOS 26), built from the text at $0131 in the buffer at HL.\nEntry: A = the drive (1-26); HL = a 9-byte buffer; IY = the workspace.\nExit: A = EXOS 26's status; HL = the buffer.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY.","comment":"EXDOS variable $47: the current drive"},
        "16333": {"comment":"The text \"EXDOS A:\""},
        "16336": {"comment":"HL = the text, DE = the buffer"},
        "16341": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "16343": {"comment":"A = the drive's letter"},
        "16345": {"comment":"DE = the letter's place"},
        "16347": {"comment":"Over the \"A\""},
        "16350": {"comment":"Offer the command"}
      }
    },
    "1": {
      "offsetIndex": 3,
      "regions": [
        {"start":0,"end":3,"type":"words"},
        {"start":4,"end":1060,"type":"bytes","decode":"text"},
        {"start":1061,"end":2376,"type":"bytes","decode":"text"},
        {"start":2377,"end":2431,"type":"bytes","decode":"text"},
        {"start":2432,"end":16383,"type":"bytes","decode":"fill"}
      ],
      "localLabels": [
        {"name":"MSG_TABLE_EN","value":4},
        {"name":"MSG_TABLE_DE","value":1061},
        {"name":"MSG_RESIDUE","value":2377}
      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "4": {"synopsis":"The English messages: 75 entries (0-$4A), each a length byte, then that many characters;\na 0 length is an entry with no text. A \"\\\" in a text is printed as a new line.\nRead by page 0's $0098 (segment + 1 put in page 1), which takes this table when EXOS\nvariable $90 is not 0 (the pointer at $0000). Entries 0-$2A are the texts of error codes\n$95-$BF ($0051), $2B the text of $CF."},
        "1061": {"synopsis":"The German messages, laid out as the English table: 76 entries (0-$4B; $4B, \"Neue\",\nis used only by the German date and time prompt at $3947). Page 0's $0098 takes this table\nwhen EXOS variable $90 is 0 (the pointer at $0002). Umlauts are written as \"{\", \"}\", \"|\"."},
        "2377": {"synopsis":"55 bytes that no entry reaches: the tail of an older copy of German entries $47 and $48."}
      }
    }
  },
